properties.description_en:
Ralmax Properties Limited is proposing to install a new barge ramp facility adjacent to 343 Bay Street in Victoria, B.C. Activities associated with the project include dredging and the installation of piles, riprap, winches, and a steel barge ramp.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Transport Canada (TC) is reviewing the project for approval under&nbsp;the&nbsp;Public Ports and Public Port Facilities Regulations&nbsp;(PPPPFR), as the proposed project falls within lands administered by Transport Canada. TC will also be issuing a licence and amending an existing lease to enable the work. Under the Impact Assessment Act, TC is reviewing project activities that relate to physical works on federal lands, specifically&nbsp;riprap installation and dredging related to the riprap installation.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The purpose of the riprap is to provide slope stability and protection at the base of the barge ramp. Dredging of seabed sediments would take place using a crane and clamshell bucket from a barge. Dredged materials would be transported to an upland facility for disposal. Following dredging, approximately 100 m3&nbsp;of riprap will be placed on federal lands.

properties.description_fr:
Ralmax Properties Limited propose d&#39;installer une nouvelle rampe pour barges adjacente au 343 Bay Street &agrave; Victoria, en Colombie-Britannique. Les activit&eacute;s associ&eacute;es au projet incluent le dragage et l&#39;installation de pieux, d&#39;enrocheur, de treuils et d&#39;une rampe en acier pour barges.

&nbsp;

Transports Canada (TC) examine le projet pour approbation en vertu du R&egrave;glement sur les ports publics et les installations portuaires publiques (PPPPFR), puisque le projet propos&eacute; rel&egrave;ve des terres administr&eacute;es par Transports Canada.&nbsp;TC d&eacute;livrera &eacute;galement une licence et modifiera un bail existant pour permettre les travaux. En vertu de la loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation de l&#39;impact, TC examine les activit&eacute;s li&eacute;es aux travaux physiques sur les terres f&eacute;d&eacute;rales, en particulier l&#39;installation d&#39;enrochement et le dragage li&eacute;s &agrave; cette installation.

&nbsp;

Le but de l&#39;enrochement est d&#39;assurer la stabilit&eacute; et la protection des pentes &agrave; la base de la rampe de la barge. Le dragage des s&eacute;diments du fond marin serait effectu&eacute; &agrave; l&#39;aide d&#39;une grue et d&#39;un seau &agrave; coquilles provenant d&#39;une barge. Les mat&eacute;riaux dragu&eacute;s seraient transport&eacute;s vers une installation pour leur &eacute;limination. Apr&egrave;s le dragage, environ 100 m3 d&#39;enrochement seront d&eacute;pos&eacute;s sur des terres f&eacute;d&eacute;rales.

Projet : JCP0050

Le pont Jacques-Cartier, inaugur&eacute; en 1930, est un ouvrage embl&eacute;matique comportant cinq voies qui relient l&#39;&icirc;le de Montr&eacute;al au littoral Sud du fleuve Saint-Laurent &agrave; la hauteur de la ville de Longueuil. Cette infrastructure d&#39;envergure est consid&eacute;r&eacute;e comme un axe de circulation routi&egrave;re, mais aussi comme un axe de mobilit&eacute; active essentiel pour la r&eacute;gion m&eacute;tropolitaine de Montr&eacute;al.

La Soci&eacute;t&eacute; Les Ponts Jacques Cartier et Champlain Incorpor&eacute;e (PJCCI) proc&eacute;dera &agrave; la r&eacute;alisation de travaux de r&eacute;fection majeurs des piles 23 et 26 du pont Jacques-Cartier. Ces travaux permettront de prolonger la dur&eacute;e de vie du pont au-del&agrave; de son 150e anniversaire.

Les principaux travaux comprennent notamment ce qui suit&nbsp;:


	R&eacute;fection et renforcement sismique des piles 23 et 26;
	Augmentation de la fiabilit&eacute; structurale du syst&egrave;me des tirants d&#39;ancrage;
	Am&eacute;lioration de l&#39;acc&egrave;s aux puits d&#39;ancrage aux fins d&#39;inspection;
	R&eacute;paration des c&ocirc;t&eacute;s ext&eacute;rieurs du tablier central de la section 7.


Les travaux de r&eacute;paration des piles seront r&eacute;alis&eacute;s dans le respect de leur architecture d&#39;origine, sans affecter leur valeur esth&eacute;tique et embl&eacute;matique.

Les travaux d&eacute;buteront en 2026 et se prolongeront pendant quatre ans.

Le projet sera r&eacute;alis&eacute; dans deux secteurs urbains, lesquels comportent des particularit&eacute;s qui leur sont propres. D&#39;une part, les travaux &agrave; la pile 26 n&eacute;cessiteront la mise en place de fermetures partielles pr&egrave;s de l&#39;intersection entre les rues Lorimier et Notre-Dame. Pour ce faire, une coordination des interventions sera r&eacute;alis&eacute;e avec la Ville de Montr&eacute;al et le minist&egrave;re de Transport et Mobilit&eacute; Durable. D&#39;autre part, en raison de la proximit&eacute; de la pile 23 avec la rive du fleuve Saint-Laurent, des mesures de protection de l&#39;environnement seront mises en place, notamment la protection des cours d&#39;eau contre les possibles mati&egrave;res en suspension, la protection de l&#39;habitat du poisson et d&#39;autres esp&egrave;ces prot&eacute;g&eacute;es comme le faucon p&egrave;lerin et l&#39;hirondelle &agrave; front blanc.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Ce projet d&#39;entretien et de r&eacute;fection s&#39;inscrit dans la mission de PJCCI qui est d&#39;assurer la mobilit&eacute; des usagers, la s&eacute;curit&eacute;, et la p&eacute;rennit&eacute; des infrastructures en pr&eacute;conisant une gestion syst&eacute;mique selon une approche de d&eacute;veloppement durable.&nbsp;

Ce projet vise &agrave; am&eacute;liorer l&#39;acc&egrave;s aux droits en mati&egrave;re de sant&eacute; pour les enfants, les adolescentes et les femmes les plus vuln&eacute;rables au Kenya. L&#39;objectif principal de cette initiative est de contribuer aux objectifs g&eacute;n&eacute;raux du projet TOGETHER, qui consistent &agrave; am&eacute;liorer la sant&eacute;, la nutrition et l&#39;hygi&egrave;ne des populations vuln&eacute;rables, en particulier les femmes, les adolescentes et les enfants de moins de cinq ans. ADRA Kenya pr&eacute;voit de forer trois puits dans les localit&eacute;s suivantes du comt&eacute; de Turkana : 1) le village d&#39;Achumae&nbsp;dans le&nbsp;sous-comt&eacute;&nbsp;de Turkana Ouest, 2) le village d&#39;Ekaburu&nbsp;dans le&nbsp;sous-comt&eacute;&nbsp;de&nbsp;Lokichogio, et 3) le village de&nbsp;Lorus&nbsp;dans le&nbsp;sous-comt&eacute;&nbsp;de&nbsp;Lokichogio. Parmi les autres activit&eacute;s essentielles &agrave; ce projet, on peut citer :&nbsp;&nbsp;

&bull; L&#39;installation d&#39;une pompe solaire (d&#39;environ 30 m&sup2;) sur les trois sites de forage afin de garantir un acc&egrave;s constant &agrave; l&#39;eau en cas de panne d&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute;.&nbsp;

&bull; Installation d&#39;un r&eacute;servoir d&#39;eau (9 m&egrave;tres de haut) pour faciliter un approvisionnement stable en eau.&nbsp;

&bull; Construction d&#39;une station de pompage (environ 12 m&sup2;) sur les trois sites de forage.&nbsp;

&bull; Installation de canalisations (environ 300 m) pour une distribution efficace de l&#39;eau&nbsp;

&bull; Installation d&#39;une cl&ocirc;ture (environ 200 m) pour prot&eacute;ger les infrastructures et pr&eacute;venir le vandalisme.&nbsp;

La zone g&eacute;ographique (comt&eacute; de Turkana) se caract&eacute;rise par :&nbsp;

&bull; un climat chaud et aride typique des terres arides et semi-arides du Kenya (ASAL).&nbsp;&nbsp;

&bull; des pr&eacute;cipitations annuelles moyennes comprises entre 150 mm et 400 mm, certaines zones recevant encore moins de pluie pendant les p&eacute;riodes de s&eacute;cheresse prolong&eacute;es.&nbsp;

&bull; des temp&eacute;ratures annuelles moyennes comprises entre 24 &deg;C et 38 &deg;C&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
Zagime Anishinabek is proposing a mix of both large and small format commercial tenants, medium and high-density mixed-use residential areas, and additional multi-unit residential buildings on the urban reserve of Saulteaux Junction Zagime IR No. 74-6. The proposed project is called Sage Meadow Development and will cover approximately 280 acres. Sage Meadow Development will utilize the existing systems on the property and tie in new service connections. The site is currently undeveloped agricultural land and project will be completed in phases. An existing gas station and two commercial buildings are located along the east side of the subject property. The remainder of the site consists of cultivated farmland.

&nbsp;

Phase1A will require roadwork and site preparation, trench excavation and backfill, pressure pipe domestic sewer, building services, utilities. Utilities currently identified on site are: Power lines, Buried electrical cable, buried or overhead phone cable, low pressure gas utility, buried sanitary sewer, buried storm sewer, buried water line.

&nbsp;

Approximately 1,190 m of roadways, including the reconstruction of Three Sisters Avenue to an urban collector cross-section, and intersection improvements at Dewdney Avenue and Pinkie Road, including turn lanes and traffic signals.

properties.description_fr:
Zagime Anishinabek propose un m&eacute;lange de locataires commerciaux de grand et petit format, de zones r&eacute;sidentielles mixtes de moyenne et haute densit&eacute;, ainsi que d&#39;autres immeubles r&eacute;sidentiels multi-unit&eacute;s dans la r&eacute;serve urbaine de Saulteaux Junction Zagime IR no 74-6. Le projet propos&eacute; s&#39;appelle Sage Meadow Development et couvrira environ 280 acres. Sage Meadow Development utilisera les syst&egrave;mes existants sur la propri&eacute;t&eacute; et reliera de nouvelles connexions de service. Le site est actuellement un terrain agricole non d&eacute;velopp&eacute; et le projet sera compl&eacute;t&eacute; par phases. Une station-service existante et deux b&acirc;timents commerciaux se trouvent le long du c&ocirc;t&eacute; est de la propri&eacute;t&eacute; concern&eacute;e. Le reste du site est constitu&eacute; de terres agricoles cultiv&eacute;es.

&nbsp;

La phase 1A n&eacute;cessitera des travaux routiers et la pr&eacute;paration du site, l&#39;excavation de tranch&eacute;es et le remblai, des &eacute;gouts domestiques sous pression, des services de construction, des services publics. Les services publics actuellement identifi&eacute;s sur le site sont : lignes &eacute;lectriques, c&acirc;ble &eacute;lectrique enfoui, c&acirc;ble t&eacute;l&eacute;phonique enseveli ou a&eacute;rien, service de gaz basse pression, &eacute;gouts sanitaires enterr&eacute;s, &eacute;gouts pluviaux enterr&eacute;s, conduites d&#39;eau enfouies.

&nbsp;

Environ 1 190 m de routes, incluant la reconstruction de Three Sisters Avenue en section transversale urbaine, ainsi que des am&eacute;liorations aux intersections &agrave; Dewdney Avenue et Pinkie Road, incluant des voies de virage et des feux de circulation.

properties.description_en:
Star Blanket Cree Nation, Okanese First Nation, and Little Black Bear First Nation are proposing to construct a Waste Diversion Centre to serve the three member Nations.

&nbsp;

The development will include the construction of an attendant building with site equipment storage bays, along with an aggregate-surfaced pad area designed to accommodate diversion and storage bays for recyclable materials and household hazardous waste (including secondary containment). The site will also feature an elevated loading platform to facilitate transfer of refuse into waste containers. The constructed area will encompass approximately 2.5 ha.

&nbsp;

The proposed site is located within an abandoned yard site. There is no tree clearing required. Approximately 3.5 ha of topsoil stripping required, with ground disturbance activities consisting of excavation of perimeter ditching, building up the transfer pad area, and constructing the access road.

&nbsp;

Solid waste will primarily consist of packaging for building materials. Construction refuse will be confined to and collected from the site, with ultimate disposal to an off-reserve designated landfill facility. To manage surface water, perimeter ditching will be constructed around the entire site and will tie into existing natural drainage courses. Site access will be provided directly from Highway 617.

properties.description_fr:
La Nation Cree Star Blanket, la Premi&egrave;re Nation Okanese et la Premi&egrave;re Nation Little Black Bear proposent de construire un centre de d&eacute;tournement des d&eacute;chets pour desservir les trois nations membres.

&nbsp;

Le d&eacute;veloppement comprendra la construction d&#39;un b&acirc;timent annexe avec des baies d&#39;entreposage pour l&#39;&eacute;quipement sur le site, ainsi qu&#39;une zone de surface en agr&eacute;gats con&ccedil;ue pour accueillir des baies de d&eacute;tournement et d&#39;entreposage pour les mat&eacute;riaux recyclables et les d&eacute;chets m&eacute;nagers dangereux (y compris le confinement secondaire). Le site comprendra &eacute;galement une plateforme de chargement sur&eacute;lev&eacute;e pour faciliter le transfert des d&eacute;chets dans les conteneurs &agrave; d&eacute;chets. La superficie construite couvrira environ 2,5 ha.

&nbsp;

Le site propos&eacute; se trouve dans un ancien terrain de cour abandonn&eacute;. Il n&#39;y a pas besoin de d&eacute;fricher les arbres. Environ 3,5 ha de d&eacute;pouillement de terre arable ont &eacute;t&eacute; n&eacute;cessaires, les activit&eacute;s de perturbation du sol consistant en l&#39;excavation des foss&eacute;s p&eacute;rim&eacute;triques, le d&eacute;veloppement de la zone de transfert et la construction de la route d&#39;acc&egrave;s.

&nbsp;

Les d&eacute;chets solides consisteront principalement en des emballages destin&eacute;s aux mat&eacute;riaux de construction. Les d&eacute;chets de construction seront confin&eacute;s au site et collect&eacute;s sur le site, avec une &eacute;limination finale vers une installation d&#39;enfouissement d&eacute;sign&eacute;e hors r&eacute;serve. Pour g&eacute;rer l&#39;eau de surface, des foss&eacute;s p&eacute;rim&eacute;triques seront construits autour de tout le site et s&#39;int&eacute;greront aux cours de drainage naturel existants. L&#39;acc&egrave;s au site se fera directement depuis l&#39;autoroute 617.

properties.description_en:
This is a non-designated project on federal lands or outside Canada. The listed authorities are responsible for the project assessment.

The Project will consist of the construction of two berthing dolphins adjacent to Pier 23. Constructions activities, including the potential for pile driving activities from a barge, will occur within 40 meters of the exiting Pier 23.&nbsp;&nbsp; 

Each dolphin will be supported by eight (8) 91.4 cm diameter steel piles embedded in the harbour floor and filled with reinforced concrete, for a total of 16 piles installed in water. A concrete deck will be cast on the piles for each dolphin and will include a catwalk to the existing Facilities, and fenders to protect berthing vessels from damage. Handrails and bollards (or quick release mooring hooks) will be affixed to the concrete deck. 

Additionally, piles will be installed on the landside of the pier, to receive new bollards (or quick release mooring hooks). A total of 8 piles will be installed on land.&nbsp;&nbsp; 

Piping will be installed and upgraded at Pier 23 to allow for the offload of tankers servicing Irving&#39;s existing tank farm. This will occur on the landside, with no in-water works associated with this activity. 

Pending all regulatory approvals, in-water construction is anticipated to commence in Q3 of 2026, with construction completion in Q2 of 2028.

Terminal Norcan Inc. operates an oil terminal that supplies numerous service stations in Quebec and Ontario. The facilities are supplied by vessels via two marine pipelines connecting Wharf 74 to the Norcan terminal, located at 6370 Notre-Dame Street East in Montreal, across from Section 66 of the Port of Montreal.

&nbsp;

The work will take place in Section 70 of the Port of Montreal, on lots 1,773,871 and 1,773,873 of the Quebec cadastre, on federal land managed by the Montreal Port Authority.

&nbsp;

The terminal has been in operation since 1935. Over time, the marine pipelines have been relocated several times. Those targeted by the present project are underground, have a diameter of 14 inches, and were installed in 1987. The project involves replacing two underground sections, each 94 meters long, at Section 70 of the Port of Montreal, part of which will be above ground. The work is being carried out as a preventive measure. It should be noted that Terminal Norcan regularly inspects its marine pipelines using an intelligent pig.

&nbsp;

Access to the underground pipelines is constrained by their location alongside rail tracks of the Port of Montreal, as well as beneath the railway siding serving the Catelli company. To access them, it will be necessary to lower the ground level on the north side, which is currently used as a parking area by employees of the company Termont. A 2-meter-high concrete block retaining wall will need to be dismantled and then rebuilt after the work is completed.

&nbsp;

The work will be carried out in the fall of 2026.

properties.description_fr:
La compagnie Terminal Norcan inc. exploite un terminal p&eacute;trolier qui dessert de nombreuses stations-service au Qu&eacute;bec et en Ontario. Les installations sont approvisionn&eacute;es par navires via deux conduites maritimes qui relient le quai 74 au terminal Norcan, situ&eacute; au 6370, rue Notre-Dame Est &agrave; Montr&eacute;al, vis-&agrave;-vis la section 66 du Port de Montr&eacute;al.

&nbsp;

Les travaux auront lieu &agrave; la section 70 du Port de Montr&eacute;al, au droit des lots 1 773 871 et 1 773 873 du cadastre du Qu&eacute;bec, lesquels sont sous la gestion de l&#39;Administration portuaire de Montr&eacute;al.

&nbsp;

Le terminal est en op&eacute;ration depuis 1935. Au fil du temps, les conduites maritimes ont &eacute;t&eacute; relocalis&eacute;es &agrave; plusieurs reprises. Celles vis&eacute;es par le pr&eacute;sent projet sont souterraines, ont un diam&egrave;tre de 14 pouces et ont &eacute;t&eacute; mises en place en 1987. Le projet pr&eacute;voit le remplacement de deux sections souterraines de 94 m&egrave;tres chacune, au droit de la section 70 du Port de Montr&eacute;al, dont une portion sera hors terre. Ces travaux sont r&eacute;alis&eacute;s &agrave; titre pr&eacute;ventif. &Agrave; noter que Terminal Norcan fait inspecter ses conduites maritimes sur une base r&eacute;guli&egrave;re &agrave; l&#39;aide d&#39;un racleur intelligent.

&nbsp;

L&#39;acc&egrave;s aux conduites souterraines est contraint par leur localisation le long de voies ferr&eacute;es du Port de Montr&eacute;al, ainsi que sous la desserte ferroviaire de la compagnie Catelli. Pour y acc&eacute;der, il sera n&eacute;cessaire d&#39;abaisser le niveau du terrain du c&ocirc;t&eacute; nord, actuellement utilis&eacute; comme stationnement par les employ&eacute;s de la compagnie Termont. Un muret de blocs de ciment de 2 m&egrave;tres de haut devra &ecirc;tre d&eacute;mantel&eacute; puis reconstruit apr&egrave;s les travaux.

&nbsp;

Les travaux seront r&eacute;alis&eacute;s &agrave; l&#39;automne 2026.

properties.description_en:
As part of a City-wide drainage improvements project, the City of Ottawa (City) is looking to improve roadway drainage along Linden Terrace. This location, adjacent to 298 Queen Elizabeth Drive, currently discharges roadway stormwater runoff to Patterson Creek via three (3) 100mm diameter storm sewers that travel from Linden Terrace to the creek through Patterson Creek Park (NCC property). As part of this project, the City of Ottawa would like to abandon two (2) existing storm sewers, while replacing them with one (1) new storm sewer discharging to Patterson Creek. A new alignment through the park has been proposed to minimize impacts to existing vegetation and mature trees.

&nbsp;

Portions of the project would take place on National Capital Commission (NCC) lands and are &nbsp;subject to a federal land use and design approval (FLUDA) under the National Capital Act and an environmental effects determination under Section 82 of the Impact Assessment Act. Consultation with the following federal departments will also be required:


	Fisheries and Oceans Canada (DFO): as Patterson Creek is deemed fish habitat, a self-assessment will be undertaken to determine if a Letter of Review from DFO will be required.
	Parks Canada Agency (PCA): The Rideau Canal, and possibly Patterson Creek, are considered lands administered by PCA, and as such, a PCA&nbsp; In-Water or Shoreline Works Approval may be required.
	&nbsp;Transport Canada for navigable waterway self-assessment.


&nbsp;

The work along Linden Terrace would be completed within the existing roadway with a right-of-way owned by the City of Ottawa. The new 250mm diameter storm sewer is proposed to be constructed through Patterson Creek Park, which is an urban park that features mature trees, vegetation, gardens, walking paths, a bistro, and a creek (Patterson Creek) that flows into the adjacent Rideau Canal.

&nbsp;

The construction is currently scheduled to begin in fall 2027 following the seasonal lowering of the water level within the Rideau Canal and Patterson Creek. It is anticipated that the majority of construction activities will take one to two (1-2) months to complete, with landscaping reinstatement to be completed in spring 2028 over the course of one (1) week. The construction area will be accessed with light duty machines and equipment, and all work areas will be fenced accordingly. The use of hydrovac excavation equipment will be used to complete required excavations within close proximity to trees and other sensitive features. Construction work will abide by all municipal by-laws, including noise.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The proposed alignment of the new storm sewer will avoid the need to remove trees. Grass or other vegetated areas impacted by construction will be replaced with topsoil and sod following construction. The abandonment of the existing storm sewers within the park will be completed by filling them with cementitious grout, which will save trees and shrubs that have been planted within and adjacent to their alignments. Temporary detouring of traffic along the pathway north of Patterson Creek, that runs through the park, will be required to construct the storm sewer to the new outfall location. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Dans le cadre d&#39;un projet d&#39;am&eacute;lioration du r&eacute;seau de drainage &agrave; l&#39;&eacute;chelle de son territoire, la Ville d&#39;Ottawa compte am&eacute;liorer le drainage routier le long de la terrasse Linden. &Agrave; cet endroit, soit &agrave; proximit&eacute; du 298, promenade Queen Elizabeth, les eaux pluviales provenant de la chauss&eacute;e sont actuellement &eacute;vacu&eacute;es vers le ruisseau Patterson par trois &eacute;gouts pluviaux de 100&nbsp;mm de diam&egrave;tre qui relient la terrasse Linden au ruisseau en traversant le parc du ruisseau Patterson (propri&eacute;t&eacute; de la Commission de la capitale nationale). La Ville d&#39;Ottawa profitera de l&#39;occasion pour abandonner deux &eacute;gouts pluviaux et les remplacer par un nouvel &eacute;gout pluvial qui se d&eacute;versera dans le ruisseau Patterson. Un nouveau trac&eacute; &agrave; travers le parc a &eacute;t&eacute; propos&eacute; pour limiter les r&eacute;percussions sur la v&eacute;g&eacute;tation et les arbres matures.

&nbsp;

Certaines parties du projet, qui se d&eacute;rouleraient sur des terrains de la Commission de la capitale nationale, doivent faire l&#39;objet d&#39;une approbation f&eacute;d&eacute;rale de l&#39;utilisation du sol et du design en vertu de la Loi sur la capitale nationale ainsi que d&#39;une &eacute;valuation des effets environnementaux en vertu de l&#39;article&nbsp;82 de la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation des impacts. Les minist&egrave;res f&eacute;d&eacute;raux suivants devront &eacute;galement &ecirc;tre consult&eacute;s.


	P&ecirc;ches et Oc&eacute;ans Canada&nbsp;: le ruisseau Patterson &eacute;tant consid&eacute;r&eacute; comme un habitat du poisson, une auto-&eacute;valuation devra &ecirc;tre r&eacute;alis&eacute;e afin de d&eacute;terminer s&#39;il est n&eacute;cessaire d&#39;obtenir une lettre d&#39;examen de la part de P&ecirc;ches et Oc&eacute;ans Canada.
	Agence Parcs Canada&nbsp;: le canal Rideau et le ruisseau Patterson sont consid&eacute;r&eacute;s comme des terres administr&eacute;es par l&#39;Agence; &agrave; ce titre, une autorisation de l&#39;Agence pour des travaux dans l&#39;eau ou sur les berges pourrait &ecirc;tre requise.
	&nbsp;Transports Canada pour l&#39;auto-&eacute;valuation relative aux voies navigables.


&nbsp;

Les travaux le long de la terrasse Linden seraient r&eacute;alis&eacute;s dans les limites de l&#39;actuelle chauss&eacute;e, sur une emprise appartenant &agrave; la Ville d&#39;Ottawa. L&#39;&eacute;gout pluvial de 250&nbsp;mm de diam&egrave;tre propos&eacute; traverserait le parc du ruisseau Patterson, un parc urbain comprenant des arbres matures, de la v&eacute;g&eacute;tation, des jardins, des sentiers p&eacute;destres, un bistrot et un ruisseau (le ruisseau Patterson) qui se jette dans le canal Rideau adjacent.

&nbsp;

Le d&eacute;but des travaux est pr&eacute;vu pour l&#39;automne&nbsp;2027, apr&egrave;s l&#39;abaissement saisonnier du niveau d&#39;eau dans le canal Rideau et le ruisseau Patterson. On pr&eacute;voit que la majeure partie des travaux sera termin&eacute;e en un &agrave; deux mois. La remise en &eacute;tat des espaces verts devrait quant &agrave; elle &ecirc;tre effectu&eacute;e au printemps&nbsp;2028 en l&#39;espace d&#39;une semaine. Le chantier accueillera de la machinerie et des &eacute;quipements l&eacute;gers, et toutes les zones o&ugrave; des travaux seront effectu&eacute;s seront cl&ocirc;tur&eacute;es en cons&eacute;quence. De l&#39;&eacute;quipement d&#39;hydroexcavation sera utilis&eacute; &agrave; proximit&eacute; imm&eacute;diate des arbres et d&#39;autres zones sensibles. Les travaux respecteront l&#39;ensemble des r&egrave;glements municipaux, notamment en mati&egrave;re de bruit.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Le trac&eacute; propos&eacute; pour le nouvel &eacute;gout pluvial permettra d&#39;&eacute;viter l&#39;abattage d&#39;arbres. Les zones couvertes de gazon ou d&#39;autre v&eacute;g&eacute;tation touch&eacute;es par les travaux seront remises en &eacute;tat avec de la terre v&eacute;g&eacute;tale et du gazon en plaque apr&egrave;s la fin des travaux. Les &eacute;gouts pluviaux qui seront mis hors service dans le parc seront remplis de coulis, ce qui permettra de pr&eacute;server les arbres et arbustes plant&eacute;s &agrave; l&#39;int&eacute;rieur et &agrave; proximit&eacute; de leur trac&eacute;. Pendant la construction de l&#39;&eacute;gout pluvial jusqu&#39;au nouvel emplacement de l&#39;exutoire, le sentier situ&eacute; au nord du ruisseau Patterson, qui traverse le parc, devra &ecirc;tre d&eacute;tourn&eacute; temporairement.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

Le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale (MDN) a propos&eacute; un projet. Le MDN a l&#39;intention de construire un nouveau b&acirc;timent d&#39;approvisionnement dans la zone am&eacute;nag&eacute;e du d&eacute;tachement Dundurn de la 17e Escadre. Ce projet vise &agrave; combler une lacune en mati&egrave;re d&#39;approvisionnement et de soutien logistique pour le d&eacute;tachement et ses unit&eacute;s appuy&eacute;es. L&#39;emprise au sol du nouveau b&acirc;timent est d&#39;environ 1 600 m&sup2;, et les 2 500 m&sup2; environnants sont pav&eacute;s.
Les travaux comprennent ce qui suit :


	pr&eacute;paration du terrain pour la construction du b&acirc;timent et des structures de stationnement connexes;
	installation des services publics sous le niveau du sol;
	construction de la structure;
	am&eacute;nagement paysager.

properties.description_en:
Vancouver Fraser Port Authority (the Applicant) is&nbsp;proposing to conduct&nbsp;works to improve&nbsp;shipping efficiency in Burrard Inlet&#39;s Second Narrows waterway, including&nbsp;facilitating&nbsp;the potential for vessels calling at Trans Mountain&#39;s Westridge Marine Terminal to&nbsp;more fully load. They include three components:&nbsp;


	Dredging along the edges of the deep-sea navigation channel with the proposed footprint east of the Iron Workers Memorial Bridge&nbsp;
	Removal of sections of decommissioned waterlines within the proposed dredging areas&nbsp;
	Installation of new navigation aids (range lights)&nbsp;


Proposed dredging activities will occur along the northern and southern margins of the navigation channel, over an approximate surface area&nbsp;of 17,000 m2&nbsp;with a potential dredge volume of approximately 25,000&nbsp;m3, and&nbsp;achieving a maximum navigation channel depth of -13.5 m chart datum.&nbsp;The dredging&nbsp;footprint overlaps with two Metro Vancouver drinking water pipes that&nbsp;extend across the Second Narrows in a north-south direction and that&nbsp;are&nbsp;in the process of being&nbsp;decommissioned. To enable the proposed dredging, segments of decommissioned waterlines overlapping with the deep-sea navigation channel in the area&nbsp;will&nbsp;need to be removed.&nbsp;

In parallel to&nbsp;the&nbsp;dredging,&nbsp;and to&nbsp;facilitate&nbsp;the potential for cargo ships&nbsp;moving through the Second Narrows waterway to load more fully, two new range lights will be installed west of the Iron Workers Memorial Bridge, on Burrard Inlet&#39;s south shore. Range lights provide spatial reference points for cargo ships transiting through confined waters such as the Second Narrows.&nbsp;

The proposed works are&nbsp;anticipated&nbsp;to start in&nbsp;Q3 of&nbsp;2026.&nbsp;Dredging could take place within a 24-hour window, seven days per week to&nbsp;facilitate&nbsp;works during&nbsp;optimal&nbsp;tide windows. Works&nbsp;related to the navigation aids will occur during standard construction hours, Monday to Saturday, from 7:00 a.m. to 8:00 p.m.&nbsp;

Additional&nbsp;details on the proposed project can be found here&nbsp;Second Narrows dredging works | Vancouver Fraser Port Authority&nbsp;

The Department of National Defence (DND) is proposing a project. The Temporary Modular Workspaces (TMW) scope of work includes construction of new one-story, partially prefabricated trailer buildings. The objective is to provide temporary accommodations for staff currently using Buildings MA26 and MB38, during construction activities in these buildings. The planned configurations of the TMW buildings are detailed as follows:


	One (1) building with a footprint of 910 m2;
	One (1) building with a footprint of 856 m2;
	One (1) building with a footprint of 776 m2;
	Two (2) buildings each with a footprint of 307 m2.


Each TMW building will connect to utility infrastructure services existing on (or adjacent) the site. Installation of new utilities includes electricity, communications, water and sanitary/storm services. While the majority of utility infrastructure will be installed below ground, new poles will be installed for connection to electricity. A new access route (road) will be constructed from Craftsman Boulevard at the south aspect of the site, to an existing parking lot northeast of the site. Temporary walkways for employee access and snow clearing will also be created. Due to the shallow bedrock at the site location, the buildings are anticipated to be constructed upon a foundation of strip footings and rock anchors. Construction activities for the project are expected to commence Fall 2026, for completion by Fall 2027.

properties.description_fr:
Le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale (MDN) propose un projet. La port&eacute;e des travaux des espaces de travail modulaires temporaires comprend la construction de nouveaux b&acirc;timents de type roulottes de chantier d&#39;un &eacute;tage partiellement pr&eacute;fabriqu&eacute;s. L&#39;objectif est de fournir des logements temporaires aux membres du personnel qui utilisent actuellement les b&acirc;timents MA26 et MB38, durant les travaux de construction. Les configurations pr&eacute;vues des b&acirc;timents modulaires temporaires sont les suivantes :


	Un (1) b&acirc;timent avec une superficie de 910 m&sup2;;
	Un (1) b&acirc;timent avec une superficie de 856 m&sup2;;
	Un (1) b&acirc;timent avec une superficie de 776 m&sup2;;
	Deux (2) b&acirc;timents d&#39;une superficie de 307 m&sup2;;


Chaque b&acirc;timent modulaire temporaire sera branch&eacute; aux services publics existants (ou adjacents) sur les lieux. L&#39;installation de nouveaux services publics comprend l&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute;, les communications, l&#39;eau et les services sanitaires/pluviaux. Alors que la majorit&eacute; de l&#39;infrastructure des services publics sera install&eacute;e sous terre, de nouveaux poteaux seront install&eacute;s pour le raccordement au r&eacute;seau d&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute;. Une nouvelle route d&#39;acc&egrave;s sera am&eacute;nag&eacute;e du boulevard Craftsman, au versant sud du site, jusqu&#39;&agrave; un stationnement existant situ&eacute; au nord-est du site. Des all&eacute;es pi&eacute;tonnes temporaires pour les employ&eacute;s seront &eacute;galement am&eacute;nag&eacute;es et d&eacute;neig&eacute;es l&#39;hiver. En raison du substrat rocheux des lieux, on pr&eacute;voit que les b&acirc;timents seront construits sur une fondation de semelle continue avec ancrage au roc. Les travaux de construction du projet devraient commencer &agrave; l&#39;automne 2026 et se terminer &agrave; l&#39;automne 2027.

properties.description_en:
The proposed project will include the construction of a lined, mine water retention pond to aid in ongoing mine water management.&nbsp; The proposed pond will be constructed off of Hinchey Avenue in Lingan, Cape Breton Regional Municipality, in Nova Scotia.&nbsp; The project will consist of clearing and grubbing of an area of small trees and scrub brush that will measure approximately 4,000 m2 in size.&nbsp; The contractor will excavate the cleared area saving the top 0.5m of material as overburden and excavate an additional 2m-2.5m in depth and using this material to construct the earthen berms of the retention pond, complete with 2:1 side slopes. The footprint of the completed pond will measure approximately 25m x 75m (1,875m2) and will have a capacity of approximately 2,000m3 of water.&nbsp; The project will also consist of the installation and hook-up of a small existing electrical control building, the installation of 3&quot; (7.6cm) diameter PVC pipe from existing well to the proposed pond, as well as the extension of existing electrical supply lines on site to the proposed building.&nbsp; 

&nbsp;

Water will be held in the retention pond and monitored.&nbsp; Water will be monitored for metals, acidity, and general chemistry. Toxicity testing would also be completed on the water.&nbsp; If water sample results meet background conditions, the mine water would be discharged through a 500mm discharge pipe out of the wall of the pond (with a boot welded to the liner) and then into a rock lined drain to a large on-site wetland. &nbsp;The flow is estimated to be approximately 50USgpm to a maximum of 100USgpm. The wetland ultimately drains over the cliff into the Atlantic Ocean.

properties.description_fr:
Le projet propos&eacute; pr&eacute;voit la construction d&#39;un bassin de r&eacute;tention des eaux mini&egrave;res &eacute;tanche afin de faciliter la gestion des eaux de la mine. Ce bassin sera construit pr&egrave;s de l&#39;avenue Hinchey &agrave; Lingan, dans la municipalit&eacute; r&eacute;gionale du Cap-Breton, en Nouvelle-&Eacute;cosse. Les travaux comprendront le d&eacute;frichage d&#39;une zone d&#39;environ 4&nbsp;000 m&sup2; recouverte de petits arbres et de broussailles. L&#39;entrepreneur proc&eacute;dera ensuite &agrave; l&#39;excavation de la zone d&eacute;frich&eacute;e, en conservant les 0,5 m sup&eacute;rieurs comme d&eacute;blais, puis &agrave; une excavation suppl&eacute;mentaire de 2 &agrave; 2,5 m de profondeur. Les mat&eacute;riaux obtenus serviront &agrave; la construction des digues du bassin, avec des talus de 2:1. L&#39;emprise au sol du bassin termin&eacute; sera d&#39;environ 25 m x 75 m (1&nbsp;875 m&sup2;) et sa capacit&eacute; sera d&#39;environ 2&nbsp;000 m&sup3;. Le projet comprendra &eacute;galement l&#39;installation et le raccordement d&#39;un petit b&acirc;timent de contr&ocirc;le &eacute;lectrique existant, la pose d&#39;une conduite en PVC de 7,6 cm (3 pouces) de diam&egrave;tre reliant le puits existant au bassin projet&eacute;, ainsi que le prolongement des lignes &eacute;lectriques existantes jusqu&#39;&agrave; ce b&acirc;timent.

&nbsp;

L&#39;eau sera stock&eacute;e dans le bassin de r&eacute;tention et fera l&#39;objet d&#39;une surveillance. Les analyses porteront sur la pr&eacute;sence de m&eacute;taux, l&#39;acidit&eacute; et la composition chimique g&eacute;n&eacute;rale de l&#39;eau. Des tests de toxicit&eacute; seront &eacute;galement effectu&eacute;s. Si les r&eacute;sultats des analyses sont conformes aux normes, les eaux de la mine seront &eacute;vacu&eacute;es par une conduite de 500 mm fix&eacute;e &agrave; la paroi du bassin (avec un raccord soud&eacute; &agrave; la membrane d&#39;&eacute;tanch&eacute;it&eacute;) et achemin&eacute;es vers un drain rev&ecirc;tu de pierres, puis vers une grande zone humide situ&eacute;e sur le site. Le d&eacute;bit est estim&eacute; entre 50 et 100 gallons US par minute. Les eaux de cette zone humide se d&eacute;versent finalement dans l&#39;oc&eacute;an Atlantique, au-del&agrave; de la falaise.

properties.description_en:
The Waterhen Lake First Nation is proposing to construct a new school to replace the former Waweyekisik Educational Centre destroyed by fire in 2024. The proposed 14 hectare site is approximately 2 km south of the former school location within undisturbed forested land east of Highway No. 951 and south of the core community. Planned infrastructure includes the new school building, a playground, ball diamond, running track and soccer field, parking lot, water and wastewater pipelines, utilities (power, propane, and communication lines), road access, culverts, and landscaping.&nbsp;

Site preparation activities will include clearing and grubbing of the proposed site. The extent of vegetation clearing will be kept to the minimum amount necessary to construct the new school, playground, access road and parking area and to provide a fire break. Construction activities will include primary earthworks, new utility installation, sub grade construction, ditch construction, structure construction, grading and landscaping.

The project is not expected to generate hazardous waste products. Waste and refuse resulting from construction will be removed from site by the contractor as soon as practicable and taken to an approved waste management facility, sent for recycling or sold for reuse where applicable and appropriate.

properties.description_fr:
La Premi&egrave;re Nation de Waterhen Lake propose de construire une nouvelle &eacute;cole pour remplacer l&#39;ancien centre &eacute;ducatif Waweyekisik, d&eacute;truit par un incendie en 2024. Le site propos&eacute; de 14 hectares se trouve &agrave; environ 2 km au sud de l&#39;ancien emplacement de l&#39;&eacute;cole, sur un terrain forestier intact &agrave; l&#39;est de l&#39;autoroute no 951 et au sud de la communaut&eacute; centrale. Les infrastructures pr&eacute;vues comprennent le nouveau b&acirc;timent scolaire, un terrain de jeux, un terrain de balle, une piste d&#39;athl&eacute;tisme et un terrain de soccer, un stationnement, des conduites d&#39;eau et d&#39;eaux us&eacute;es, des services publics (&eacute;lectricit&eacute;, propane et lignes de communication), l&#39;acc&egrave;s routier, des ponceaux et l&#39;am&eacute;nagement paysager.&nbsp;

Les activit&eacute;s de pr&eacute;paration du site incluront le d&eacute;frichage et le d&eacute;blaiement du site propos&eacute;. L&#39;&eacute;tendue du d&eacute;frichage de la v&eacute;g&eacute;tation sera r&eacute;duite au minimum n&eacute;cessaire pour construire la nouvelle &eacute;cole, la cour de jeux, la route d&#39;acc&egrave;s et le stationnement, ainsi que pour assurer un pare-feu. Les activit&eacute;s de construction comprendront des travaux de terrassement primaires, l&#39;installation de nouveaux services publics, la construction de sous-sol, la construction de foss&eacute;s, la construction de structures, le nivellement et l&#39;am&eacute;nagement paysager.

On ne s&#39;attend pas &agrave; ce que le projet g&eacute;n&egrave;re des d&eacute;chets dangereux. Les d&eacute;chets et d&eacute;chets r&eacute;sultant de la construction seront retir&eacute;s du site par l&#39;entrepreneur d&egrave;s que possible et achemin&eacute;s vers une installation de gestion des d&eacute;chets approuv&eacute;e, envoy&eacute;s pour recyclage ou vendus pour r&eacute;utilisation lorsque cela est applicable et appropri&eacute;.

properties.description_en:
The upland owners at 315 Sasamat Lane are proposing to install a new private residential dock in North Vancouver BC. The proposed works include the construction of a platform that is supported by a concrete abutment and anchored to the existing rock above on the land side and the installation of an access ramp and mooring float. The ramp and float will be constructed off-site and then placed and secured in the proposed dock location.&nbsp;

The ramp is a prefabricated aluminum frame with composite decking, with a walkway that allows light to permeate. The float will be constructed using polystyrene foam encased HDPE, with naturally rot-resistant wood stringers and the surface will be finished with composite deck boards, space 2 inches apart. The ramp will be secured to the concrete abutment and platform and the float will be anchored by four precast concrete anchor blocks and mooring chains. No vegetation will be disturbed as part of the works and no piles are proposed to be installed. The dock meets all size requirements outlined in the Recreational Dock Guideline.

Construction would be conducted during regular hours and the overall duration of the project is approximately 2 months

The Proposed Project 

&nbsp;

Webequie First Nation is proposing the installation of 4 modular teacherages (78 sq.m each) to replace 3 existing teacherages that are in poor condition and add 1 additional teacherage.&nbsp;Activities are as follows:


	The demolition of the existing teacherages;
	Site preparation for the modular units to be delivered via winter road to be placed on permanent foundations;
	Leveling and compaction by heavy equipment with aggregate (source 13 km from community) prior to screw pile install;
	New water and sewer connections (1 per site) and electrical connections (unknown if new pole and transformer is required);
	Installation of 4 new fuel day tanks for heating;
	Designated substances surveys to be completed by a professional for existing teacherages and provide disposal plan of demolished teacherages, if required;
	Landscaping for vehicle access and positive drainage grading.


This project will help with teacher retention by improving the living conditions of resident teachers teaching at the community&#39;s school, Simon Jacob Memorial Education Centre.

properties.description_fr:
Projet propos&eacute;

&nbsp;

La Premi&egrave;re Nation de Webequie propose l&#39;installation de quatre logements modulaires pour enseignants (78 m&sup2; chacun) afin de remplacer trois logements existants en mauvais &eacute;tat et d&#39;en ajouter un. Les activit&eacute;s pr&eacute;vues sont les suivantes&nbsp;:


	D&eacute;molition des logements existants&nbsp;;
	Pr&eacute;paration du site pour la livraison des modules par une route d&#39;hiver et leur installation sur des fondations permanentes&nbsp;;
	Nivellement et compactage du terrain &agrave; l&#39;aide d&#39;engins lourds et de granulats (provenant d&#39;une source situ&eacute;e &agrave; 13 km de la communaut&eacute;) avant la pose des pieux viss&eacute;s&nbsp;;
	Nouveaux raccordements &agrave; l&#39;eau et aux &eacute;gouts (un par site) et &agrave; l&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute; (il reste &agrave; d&eacute;terminer si un nouveau poteau et un transformateur seront n&eacute;cessaires)&nbsp;;
	Installation de quatre nouvelles cuves quotidiennes au mazout pour le chauffage&nbsp;;
	R&eacute;alisation d&#39;&eacute;tudes sur les substances dangereuses dans les logements existants par un professionnel et &eacute;laboration d&#39;un plan d&#39;&eacute;limination des d&eacute;chets des logements d&eacute;molis, le cas &eacute;ch&eacute;ant&nbsp;;
	Am&eacute;nagement paysager pour l&#39;acc&egrave;s des v&eacute;hicules et cr&eacute;ation d&#39;un syst&egrave;me de drainage efficace.


Ce projet contribuera &agrave; la r&eacute;tention des enseignants en am&eacute;liorant les conditions de vie des enseignants r&eacute;sidents qui enseignent &agrave; l&#39;&eacute;cole communautaire, le Centre d&#39;&eacute;ducation Simon Jacob Memorial.

properties.description_en:
The Proposed Project 

&nbsp;

Nibinamik First Nation is proposing various upgrades to the community nursing station&#39;s fuel system. Project activities will include:


	Decommissioning and removal of the old tank from the community;
	Construction of a concrete pad and placement of 50,000 L bulk fuel tank;
	Replacement of 3 existing day tanks;
	Removal and replacement of fuel system piping;
	Installation of two non-combustible fuel kiosks;
	Installation of a new control system; And
	Installation of fencing around the tank system.

properties.description_fr:
Projet propos&eacute;

&nbsp;

La Premi&egrave;re Nation de Nibinamik propose diverses am&eacute;liorations au syst&egrave;me d&#39;approvisionnement en carburant du poste de soins infirmiers communautaire. Les activit&eacute;s pr&eacute;vues comprennent&nbsp;:


	La mise hors service et le retrait de l&#39;ancien r&eacute;servoir;
	La construction d&#39;une dalle de b&eacute;ton et l&#39;installation d&#39;un r&eacute;servoir de carburant en vrac de 50&nbsp;000&nbsp;L&nbsp;;
	Le remplacement de trois r&eacute;servoirs journaliers existants;
	Le remplacement de la tuyauterie du syst&egrave;me d&#39;approvisionnement en carburant;
	L&#39;installation de deux kiosques &agrave; carburant incombustible;
	L&#39;installation d&#39;un nouveau syst&egrave;me de contr&ocirc;le; et
	L&#39;installation d&#39;une cl&ocirc;ture autour du syst&egrave;me de r&eacute;servoirs.

properties.description_en:
Thesis Gold and Silver&nbsp;Inc. is proposing the construction, operation, and closure of a new gold-silver mine located 275&nbsp;kilometers north of Smithers, British Columbia. As proposed, the Lawyers-Ranch Project would include open-pit and underground mining facilities, an ore processing plant (metal mill), a tailings management facility, waste rock storage facilities, an accommodation complex and a 70&nbsp;kilometer&nbsp;transmission line extension. The project would have a maximum production capacity of&nbsp;5.5 million&nbsp;tonnes of ore per year (approximately 15,000&nbsp;tonnes per day) over a mine life of 14 to 20 years, and would be located on the site of the former Cheni Mine.&nbsp;


British Columbia&#39;s Environmental Assessment Office is collaborating with the Impact Assessment Agency of Canada as part of the federal impact assessment of the project. For more information on the EAO&#39;s process, please visit&nbsp;EPIC.engage.


Please note that the&nbsp;proponent was formerly known as Thesis&nbsp;Gold&nbsp;Inc.

properties.description_fr:
Thesis&nbsp;Gold and Silver&nbsp;Inc. propose la construction, l&#39;exploitation et la fermeture d&#39;une nouvelle mine d&#39;or et d&#39;argent situ&eacute;e &agrave; 275&nbsp;kilom&egrave;tres au nord&nbsp;de&nbsp;Smithers, en Colombie-Britannique.&nbsp;Tel qu&#39;il est&nbsp;propos&eacute;, le projet&nbsp;Lawyers-Ranch comprendrait des installations mini&egrave;res &agrave; ciel ouvert et souterraines, une usine de traitement du minerai (usine m&eacute;tallurgique), une installation de gestion des&nbsp;d&eacute;chets&nbsp;miniers, des installations de stockage des st&eacute;riles, un complexe d&#39;h&eacute;bergement et un&nbsp;prolongement sur&nbsp;70&nbsp;kilom&egrave;tre&nbsp;de la ligne&nbsp;de&nbsp;transport d&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute;. Le projet aurait une capacit&eacute; de production maximale de 5,5 millions&nbsp;de&nbsp;tonnes de minerai par an (environ 15 000&nbsp;tonnes par jour)&nbsp;pendant la&nbsp;dur&eacute;e de vie de la mine&nbsp;qui serait&nbsp;de 14 &agrave; 20 ans.&nbsp;Le projet&nbsp;serait situ&eacute; sur le site de l&#39;ancienne mine Cheni. &nbsp;&nbsp;


Le Bureau d&#39;&eacute;valuation environnementale de la Colombie-Britannique collabore avec l&#39;Agence d&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact du Canada dans le cadre de l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact f&eacute;d&eacute;rale du projet. Pour plus d&#39;informations sur le processus du BEE, veuillez consulter le site EPIC.engage.


Veuillez noter que le promoteur &eacute;tait pr&eacute;c&eacute;demment intitul&eacute;&nbsp;Thesis&nbsp;Gold&nbsp;Inc.

properties.description_en:
Tk&#39;eml&uacute;ps te Secw&eacute;pemc (TteS) requires a new 2,630 m3 reservoir in the East Shuswap&nbsp;pressure zone to replace the existing, aging and undersized 350 m3 East Shuswap&nbsp;Reservoir.&nbsp; This project is necessary to (1) maintain current levels of water services for&nbsp;future development along East Shuswap Rd, and (2) to upgrade the system to be able to&nbsp;achieve minimum fire flow targets to all lots in the area.&nbsp; This includes at the Tk&#39;eml&uacute;ps Healing House, which is expected to be completed in Fall 2026. The existing&nbsp;infrastructure is not able to meet fire flow targets in the majority of the pressure zone,&nbsp;and this must be rectified before the Healing House is officially opened.

&nbsp;

The site infrastructure upgrades include installation of a 2,630 m3 concrete reservoir&nbsp;(divided into two 1,315 m3 cells), 420 m of new 350 mm watermain, and related site&nbsp;drainage, electrical, and instrumentation upgrades.

&nbsp;

An archaeological overview has been completed by&nbsp;Tk&#39;eml&uacute;ps&#39; Archaeology Department, and an Environmental Assessment Scoping Report was completed to determine potential environmental impacts and mitigation measures.

properties.description_fr:
La communaut&eacute; Tk&#39;eml&uacute;ps te Secw&eacute;pemc (TteS) a besoin d&#39;un nouveau r&eacute;servoir d&#39;une capacit&eacute; de 2 630 m&sup3; dans la zone de distribution sous pression d&#39;East Shuswap afin de remplacer l&#39;actuel r&eacute;servoir d&#39;East Shuswap, d&#39;une capacit&eacute; de 350 m&sup3;, qui est vieillissant et sous-dimensionn&eacute;. &nbsp;Ce projet est n&eacute;cessaire pour (1) maintenir les niveaux actuels de services d&#39;approvisionnement en eau en vue des futurs am&eacute;nagements le long de la route East Shuswap, et (2) moderniser le r&eacute;seau afin d&#39;atteindre les objectifs minimaux de d&eacute;bit d&#39;incendie pour toutes les parcelles de la zone. Cela inclut la Maison de gu&eacute;rison Tk&#39;eml&uacute;ps, dont l&#39;ach&egrave;vement est pr&eacute;vu &agrave; l&#39;automne 2026. L&#39;infrastructure existante n&#39;est pas en mesure de r&eacute;pondre aux objectifs de d&eacute;bit d&#39;incendie dans la majeure partie de la zone sous pression, et cela doit &ecirc;tre corrig&eacute; avant l&#39;ouverture officielle de la Maison de gu&eacute;rison.

&nbsp;

Les am&eacute;liorations de l&#39;infrastructure du site comprennent l&#39;installation d&#39;un r&eacute;servoir en b&eacute;ton de 2 630 m&sup3; (divis&eacute; en deux cellules de 1 315 m&sup3;), 420 m de nouvelle conduite d&#39;eau principale de 350 mm, ainsi que les am&eacute;liorations connexes en mati&egrave;re de drainage, d&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute; et d&#39;instrumentation du site.

&nbsp;

Une &eacute;tude arch&eacute;ologique pr&eacute;liminaire a &eacute;t&eacute; r&eacute;alis&eacute;e par le d&eacute;partement d&#39;arch&eacute;ologie de Tk&#39;eml&uacute;ps, et un rapport de cadrage de l&#39;&eacute;valuation environnementale a &eacute;t&eacute; r&eacute;dig&eacute; afin de d&eacute;terminer les impacts environnementaux potentiels et les mesures d&#39;att&eacute;nuation.

properties.description_en:
The Thunder Bay Port Authority proposes to rehabilitate existing dock infrastructure at Keefer Terminal.&nbsp;&nbsp;The project is funded by Transport Canada under the the National Trade Corridors Fund (NTCF).&nbsp; &nbsp;The proposed project is split into 2 phases with different timing, as follows:&nbsp; &nbsp;

&bull; Phase 1 &ndash; Cargo Ramps No. 9 - 12:&nbsp; permanent infill and decommissioning.&nbsp; &nbsp;All work is at deck level only. There are no in-water works, no pile driving, and no disturbance to the lakebed associated with this component.&nbsp; Construction, pending required approvals, is planned for fall 2026.

&bull; Phase 2 &ndash; Cargo Ramps 1, 2, 3 &amp; 4:&nbsp; replacement of Cargo Ramps No. 1 and 2;&nbsp; structural strengthening of Cargo Ramps No. 3 and 4;&nbsp;underwater pile repairs, deck soffit repairs, and pavement replacement across Docks 1, 2 and 3, and replacement of bollards, fenders, and curbs.&nbsp; &nbsp;Construction, pending required approvals, is planned for 2027.

properties.description_fr:
Le site d&#39;&eacute;limination des d&eacute;chets (SED) de Natuashish, &agrave; Terre-Neuve-et-Labrador, arrive &agrave; la fin de sa dur&eacute;e de vie et doit &ecirc;tre modifi&eacute; et agrandi afin de pouvoir continuer &agrave; &ecirc;tre utilis&eacute; &agrave; son emplacement actuel. Le projet comprendra la r&eacute;paration et la modernisation des infrastructures existantes du SED et l&#39;am&eacute;nagement d&#39;un site d&#39;&eacute;limination des d&eacute;chets de construction et de d&eacute;molition. &nbsp;Les activit&eacute;s comprennent la r&eacute;paration des cl&ocirc;tures, le nivellement du SED existant afin d&#39;en prolonger l&#39;utilisation verticale, l&#39;entretien des coupe-feu et la gestion des eaux pluviales. Le WDS comprendra &eacute;galement une extension lat&eacute;rale du c&ocirc;t&eacute; nord-ouest d&#39;environ 100 m sur 210 m, ce qui n&eacute;cessitera l&#39;essouchement et l&#39;extension de la cl&ocirc;ture et des coupe-feu.
Les d&eacute;chets non dangereux provenant de la construction et de la d&eacute;molition seront d&eacute;tourn&eacute;s vers une ancienne carri&egrave;re qui sera cl&ocirc;tur&eacute;e et am&eacute;nag&eacute;e pour recevoir ces d&eacute;chets. &nbsp;Cela permettra &eacute;galement de prolonger la dur&eacute;e de vie du SED principal.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The Proposed Project

&nbsp;

Neskantaga First Nation is proposing various upgrades to and expansion of the community&#39;s water system. Project activities are as follows:


	Installation of approximately 600 m of watermain from a dead end watermain by the Elder&#39;s 6-plex to the dead end at the Arena to eliminate two (2) dead ends;
	Extension of approximately 500 m of road and sewer with the proposed watermain looping to create 15 new serviced lots;
	Installation at an automatic flusher at the dead end by the school to automate the flushing in this location;
	Installation of approximately 200 m of watermain and sanitary forcemain to the east intersection of Neskantaga Drive and Lakeshore Drive to create six (6) new serviced lots; And
	Replacement of the existing water treatment plant chlorine dioxide system.


This work is meant to be an interim measure to support the community&#39;s growing water usage needs until a new water treatment plant is operational.

properties.description_fr:
Projet propos&eacute;

&nbsp;

La Premi&egrave;re Nation de Neskantaga propose divers travaux d&#39;am&eacute;lioration et d&#39;agrandissement de son r&eacute;seau d&#39;aqueduc. Les activit&eacute;s pr&eacute;vues sont les suivantes&nbsp;:


	Installation d&#39;environ 600 m de conduite d&#39;aqueduc reliant un cul-de-sac pr&egrave;s de l&#39;immeuble de six logements des a&icirc;n&eacute;s au cul-de-sac de l&#39;ar&eacute;na, afin d&#39;&eacute;liminer deux impasses&nbsp;;
	Prolongement d&#39;environ 500&nbsp;m de route et d&#39;&eacute;gout, avec la boucle de conduite d&#39;aqueduc propos&eacute;e, pour cr&eacute;er 15&nbsp;nouveaux lots desservis&nbsp;;
	Installation d&#39;un syst&egrave;me de rin&ccedil;age automatique au cul-de-sac pr&egrave;s de l&#39;&eacute;cole afin d&#39;automatiser le rin&ccedil;age &agrave; cet endroit&nbsp;;
	Installation d&#39;environ 200 m de conduite d&#39;aqueduc et de conduite de refoulement des eaux us&eacute;es jusqu&#39;&agrave; l&#39;intersection est de la promenade Neskantaga et de la promenade Lakeshore, afin de cr&eacute;er six nouveaux terrains desservis&nbsp;; Et
	Remplacement du syst&egrave;me de traitement de l&#39;eau au dioxyde de chlore existant.


Ces travaux constituent une mesure transitoire visant &agrave; r&eacute;pondre aux besoins croissants en eau de la communaut&eacute; jusqu&#39;&agrave; la mise en service d&#39;une nouvelle usine de traitement.

properties.description_en:
The Proposed Project

&nbsp;

K5 Dual 1 Ltd. is proposing the development of a new dual-branded hotel, bringing job creation opportunities to drive the region&#39;s economic growth. &nbsp;The development is proposed for an undeveloped area east of YEG. When complete, the hotel will have 168 total guest suites consisting of 56 standard king rooms, 44 standard double queen rooms, and 68 extended-stay suites. Accessible suites, and pet-friendly rooms are included in the proposed plan. Amenities will include over 2,000 square feet of meeting space, fitness centre, outdoor terrace, pool, hot tub and restaurant.

properties.description_fr:
Le projet propos&eacute;

&nbsp;

K5 Dual&nbsp;1 Ltd. propose la construction d&#39;un nouvel h&ocirc;tel &agrave; double enseigne, qui contribuera &agrave; la cr&eacute;ation d&#39;emplois et stimulera la croissance &eacute;conomique de la r&eacute;gion. Le projet est pr&eacute;vu dans une zone non d&eacute;velopp&eacute;e &agrave; l&#39;est de YEG. L&#39;h&ocirc;tel comptera 168&nbsp;chambres, dont 56&nbsp;chambres standard avec lit tr&egrave;s grand, 44&nbsp;chambres standard avec deux lits grand format et 68&nbsp;appartements pour les s&eacute;jours de longue dur&eacute;e. Le projet pr&eacute;voit &eacute;galement des chambres accessibles et des chambres o&ugrave; les animaux de compagnie sont permis. L&#39;&eacute;tablissement comprendra plus de 185&nbsp;m&sup2; d&#39;espace am&eacute;nag&eacute; pour les r&eacute;unions, un centre de conditionnement physique, une terrasse ext&eacute;rieure, une piscine, un bain &agrave; remous et un restaurant.

properties.description_en:
This project involves the installation of three, 75,000 litres new double-walled diesel storage tanks within the existing tank farm site. Tanks will be shop fabricated in line with applicable regulations and standards for fuel storage. The initiative is being undertaken to address an immediate and critical need for reliable fuel supply in preparation for the upcoming winter season, ensuring uninterrupted operation of the power plant during peak demand periods.&nbsp;

Scope of Work Includes:


	Site preparation
	Delivery and installation of double-walled storage tanks at the existing Tank Farm Site within the existing berm
	Testing and commissioning of the new tanks&nbsp;
	Tank Registration with the Federal Identification Registry for Storage Tank Systems (FIRSTS)

Dene Tha&#39; First Nation is proposing to construct and operate a Waste Transfer Station in Bushe River to receive and sort the community&#39;s residential waste streams including&nbsp;large items, recyclables, residential renovation waste, tires, household hazardous materials, electronics, whitegoods, propane tanks,&nbsp;and derelict vehicles. The waste will be hauled from the new transfer station by Dene Tha&#39; First Nation to third-party operated landfills.&nbsp;The transfer station will have a 30-year service life with provision for future&nbsp;expansion to accommodate community growth.&nbsp;

The Transfer Station will be located in a natural area with no previous land use requiring clearing of forest vegetation. The Project will involve the construction of an elevated platform for disposal of residential waste, a designated household hazardous waste collection site with appropriate environmental protections envisioned as a set of&nbsp;modified &quot;sea-can&quot; shipping containers equipped with secondary containment, holding tanks, collection and storage areas&nbsp;for safe temporary storage of household recyclables, derelict vehicles, and bulky items, and an attendant&#39;s shelter.&nbsp;

A wildlife sweep and biophysical assessment support an initial application for review, and will support due-diligence environmental management objectives.

Public Services and Procurement Canada (PSPC) is proposing to replace the existing Portage Channel Bridge, which was constructed in 1987 and has reached the end of its service life. Structural evaluations have identified load restrictions and geometric limitations that affect the safe and reliable movement of vehicles, including emergency and service vehicles, within the Dokis First Nation community.

The purpose of the project is to maintain safe, reliable, and unrestricted access across the Portage Channel by replacing the existing bridge with a new structure designed to meet current engineering standards and long-term service requirements.

The bridge is located within the Dokis First Nation Reserve and crosses the Portage Channel at the eastern outlet of Lake Nipissing into the French River system. The surrounding area includes Indigenous community lands and is adjacent to lands managed as part of the French River Provincial Park. Keso Bay Road is a low-volume access road and serves as the sole road connection across the Portage Channel.

The project involves the construction of a new single-span bridge located immediately north of the existing structure. The new bridge will be designed for a 75 year service life and will provide increased roadway width to improve vehicle safety and functionality.

Components of the project include:


	Construction of new bridge abutments and superstructure;
	Reconstruction and widening of approach roadways;
	Installation of safety barriers, drainage features, and lighting;
	Removal of the existing bridge following commissioning of the new structure; and
	Site restoration following completion of construction activities.
	Construction is anticipated to occur between May 2027 and August 2028.


The existing bridge will remain in service during construction of the new bridge to maintain continuous access for the Dokis First Nation community.

The project involves the construction of a new single-span bridge located immediately north of the existing structure, followed by the removal of the existing bridge once the new crossing is operational.

The new bridge will be designed for a 75 year service life and will provide an increased roadway width to improve safety and functionality for vehicular traffic.

Construction of the project will be completed in a series of coordinated activities, including enabling works, main construction works, and site restoration.

Enabling works and early construction activities are expected to include:


	Site clearing and grubbing within approved limits;
	Installation of erosion and sediment control measures;
	Establishment of temporary construction access routes, staging areas, and laydown areas;
	Installation of environmental protection fencing and site controls;
	Utility relocations, where required;
	Temporary traffic management measures to maintain access across the existing bridge;
	Installation of temporary work platforms, cofferdams, or other isolation measures to support construction activities in and near the watercourse.


Main construction activities are expected to include:


	Excavation and construction of new bridge abutments and foundations;
	Installation of the bridge superstructure and deck;
	Reconstruction and widening of approach roadways;
	Installation of safety barriers, guiderails, drainage features, and lighting;
	Commissioning of the new bridge structure.


Post-construction activities will include:


	Removal of the existing bridge structure;
	Removal of temporary works and construction access;
	Site grading and restoration of disturbed areas.


Construction is anticipated to occur between May 2027 and August 2028. The existing bridge will remain in service during construction of the new bridge to maintain uninterrupted access for the First Nation community.

PSPC is the lead federal authority for the project and is responsible for conducting the environmental effects determination under sections 81 to 91 of the Impact Assessment Act. Other federal reviews, permits, and approvals will be obtained as required to enable the project to proceed. In addition, the engagement and collaboration between PSPC and the Dokis First Nation is already underway, as this is essential to the development and progress of the project.

properties.description_fr:
Services publics et Approvisionnement Canada (SPAC) propose de remplacer le pont du canal Portage existant, qui a &eacute;t&eacute; construit en 1987 et qui a atteint la fin de sa dur&eacute;e de vie utile. Les &eacute;valuations structurales ont permis de d&eacute;terminer les restrictions de charge et les limitations g&eacute;om&eacute;triques qui ont une incidence sur le d&eacute;placement s&ucirc;r et fiable des v&eacute;hicules, y compris les v&eacute;hicules d&#39;urgence et de service, dans la collectivit&eacute; de la Premi&egrave;re Nation des Dokis.

Le but du projet est de maintenir un acc&egrave;s s&ucirc;r, fiable et sans restriction sur le canal Portage en rempla&ccedil;ant le pont existant par une nouvelle structure con&ccedil;ue pour r&eacute;pondre aux normes techniques actuelles et aux exigences de service &agrave; long terme avec une dur&eacute;e de vie utile de 75 ans.

Le pont est situ&eacute; dans la r&eacute;serve de la Premi&egrave;re Nation des Dokis et traverse le canal &agrave; la sortie est du lac Nipissing dans le r&eacute;seau de la Rivi&egrave;re des Fran&ccedil;ais. La zone environnante comprend des terres communautaires autochtones et est adjacente &agrave; une zone territoriale g&eacute;r&eacute;e par le Parc Provincial French River. Le chemin Keso Bay est une route d&#39;acc&egrave;s &agrave; faible d&eacute;bit et sert de seul lien routier pour traverser le canal Portage.

Le projet comprend la construction d&#39;un nouveau pont &agrave; trav&eacute;e unique situ&eacute; imm&eacute;diatement au nord de la structure existante. Le nouveau pont sera con&ccedil;u pour une longue dur&eacute;e de vie utile et permettra d&#39;&eacute;largir la chauss&eacute;e afin d&#39;am&eacute;liorer la s&eacute;curit&eacute; et la fonctionnalit&eacute; des v&eacute;hicules.

Les composantes du projet comprennent :


	La construction de nouvelles cul&eacute;es et de la superstructure du pont ;
	La reconstruction et l&#39;&eacute;largissement des routes d&#39;approche ;
	L&#39;installation de barri&egrave;res de s&eacute;curit&eacute;, d&#39;ouvrages de drainage et de l&#39;&eacute;clairage ;
	Le retrait du pont existant apr&egrave;s la mise en service de la nouvelle structure ;
	La remise en &eacute;tat du site une fois les activit&eacute;s de construction termin&eacute;es.
	La construction devrait avoir lieu entre mai 2027 et ao&ucirc;t 2028.


Le pont existant demeurera en service pendant la construction du nouveau pont afin de maintenir un acc&egrave;s continu pour la communaut&eacute; de la Premi&egrave;re Nation des Dokis.

Le projet comprend la construction d&#39;un nouveau pont &agrave; trav&eacute;e unique situ&eacute; imm&eacute;diatement au nord de la structure existante, suivie de l&#39;enl&egrave;vement du pont existant une fois que le nouveau pont sera op&eacute;rationnel.

Le nouveau pont sera con&ccedil;u pour une dur&eacute;e de vie utile de 75 ans et offrira une largeur de route accrue afin d&#39;am&eacute;liorer la s&eacute;curit&eacute; et la fonctionnalit&eacute; pour la circulation automobile.

La construction du projet sera r&eacute;alis&eacute;e dans le cadre d&#39;une s&eacute;rie d&#39;activit&eacute;s coordonn&eacute;es, y compris les travaux pr&eacute;paratoires, les principaux travaux de construction et la restauration du site.

Les travaux pr&eacute;paratoires et les premi&egrave;res activit&eacute;s de construction devraient comprendre :


	Le d&eacute;frichage et le nettoyage du site dans les limites approuv&eacute;es ;
	L&#39;installation de mesures de contr&ocirc;le de l&#39;&eacute;rosion et des s&eacute;diments ;
	La mise en place d&#39;acc&egrave;s temporaires au chantier, de zones de pr&eacute;paration et d&#39;aires d&#39;entreposage ;
	L&#39;installation de cl&ocirc;tures de protection environnementale et de dispositifs de contr&ocirc;le du site ;
	Le d&eacute;placement des services publics, au besoin ;
	La mise en place de mesures temporaires de gestion de la circulation pour maintenir l&#39;acc&egrave;s sur le pont existant ;
	L&#39;installation de plateformes de travail temporaires, de batardeaux ou d&#39;autres mesures d&#39;isolation pour appuyer les activit&eacute;s de construction dans et &agrave; proximit&eacute; du cours d&#39;eau.


Les principales activit&eacute;s de construction devraient comprendre :


	L&#39;excavation et la construction de nouvelles cul&eacute;es et fondations de pont ;
	L&#39;installation de la superstructure du pont et du tablier ;
	La reconstruction et l&#39;&eacute;largissement des routes d&#39;approche ;
	L&#39;installation de barri&egrave;res de s&eacute;curit&eacute;, de glissi&egrave;res de s&eacute;curit&eacute;, d&#39;&eacute;l&eacute;ments de drainage et d&#39;&eacute;clairage ;
	La mise en service de la nouvelle structure du pont.


Les activit&eacute;s post-construction comprendront :


	Le d&eacute;mant&egrave;lement de la structure de pont existante ;
	Le retrait des ouvrages temporaires et des acc&egrave;s de chantier ;
	Le nivellement du site et la remise en &eacute;tat des zones perturb&eacute;es.


La construction devrait avoir lieu entre mai 2027 et ao&ucirc;t 2028. Le pont existant demeurera en service pendant la construction du nouveau pont afin de maintenir un acc&egrave;s ininterrompu pour la communaut&eacute; de la Premi&egrave;re Nation des Dokis.

SPAC est l&#39;autorit&eacute; f&eacute;d&eacute;rale responsable du projet et est responsable de la d&eacute;termination des effets environnementaux en vertu des articles 81 &agrave; 91 de la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact. D&#39;autres examens, permis et approbations f&eacute;d&eacute;raux seront obtenus au besoin pour permettre au projet d&#39;aller de l&#39;avant. De plus, l&#39;engagement et la collaboration entre SPAC et la Premi&egrave;re Nation des Dokis sont d&eacute;j&agrave; en cours, ceci &eacute;tant essentiel dans le d&eacute;veloppement et l&#39;avancement du projet.

La Premi&egrave;re Nation de Whitefish Lake n&deg; 128 propose d&#39;am&eacute;nager 15 parcelles r&eacute;sidentielles adjacentes &agrave; un lotissement existant situ&eacute; sur Great Plains Road. Les activit&eacute;s pr&eacute;vues dans le cadre du projet comprennent le nivellement des parcelles, le drainage de surface, l&#39;am&eacute;nagement des voies d&#39;acc&egrave;s aux parcelles et la mise en service des r&eacute;seaux d&#39;eau et d&#39;&eacute;gouts. Aucun d&eacute;boisement ne sera n&eacute;cessaire, car les parcelles ont d&eacute;j&agrave; &eacute;t&eacute; d&eacute;frich&eacute;es.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
ATCO is proposing to replace a natural gas distribution pipe at Enoch Cree Nation and complete a pressure upgrade to the distribution system. The proposed project will include the installation of 5.1km of 60mm and 114mm polyethylene distribution mains. In total, 38 service lines will be replaced, disconnected, pressure upgraded, or transferred to the newly installed distribution mains as appropriate.

&nbsp;

The new pipe will be installed by a combination of trenchless horizontal drilling and plowing. The proposed pipeline will be installed to serve existing residences and buildings so the project footprint will be mostly within previously disturbed land. No tree clearing is expected.

&nbsp;

The proposed project footprint intersects a seasonal graminoid marsh, three temporary graminoid marshes, a wooded deciduous swamp, and a wooded mixed wood swamp. No species at risk or rare plants were identified in the project area. A pre-construction wildlife and nest sweep will be conducted prior to the commencement of any ground disturbance or vegetation clearing activities.

properties.description_fr:
ATCO propose de remplacer une conduite de distribution de gaz naturel sur le territoire de la Nation crie d&#39;Enoch et de proc&eacute;der &agrave; une mise &agrave; niveau de la pression du r&eacute;seau de distribution. Le projet propos&eacute; comprendra l&#39;installation de 5,1 km de conduites principales de distribution en poly&eacute;thyl&egrave;ne de 60 mm et 114 mm de diam&egrave;tre. Au total, 38 branchements seront remplac&eacute;s, d&eacute;connect&eacute;s, soumis &agrave; une mise &agrave; niveau de pression ou raccord&eacute;s aux nouvelles conduites principales de distribution, selon le cas.

&nbsp;

La nouvelle conduite sera install&eacute;e &agrave; l&#39;aide d&#39;une combinaison de forage horizontal sans tranch&eacute;e et de labour. Le pipeline propos&eacute; sera install&eacute; pour desservir les r&eacute;sidences et les b&acirc;timents existants ; l&#39;empreinte du projet se situera donc principalement sur des terres d&eacute;j&agrave; perturb&eacute;es. Aucun d&eacute;boisement n&#39;est pr&eacute;vu.

&nbsp;

L&#39;empreinte du projet propos&eacute; traverse un marais gramino&iuml;de saisonnier, trois marais gramino&iuml;des temporaires, un mar&eacute;cage bois&eacute; &agrave; feuillus et un mar&eacute;cage bois&eacute; mixte. Aucune esp&egrave;ce en p&eacute;ril ni aucune plante rare n&#39;a &eacute;t&eacute; identifi&eacute;e dans la zone du projet. Un balayage de la faune et des nids sera effectu&eacute; avant le d&eacute;but de toute activit&eacute; de perturbation du sol ou de d&eacute;frichage de la v&eacute;g&eacute;tation.

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The proposed project involves upgrading the existing breakwater with the installation of a rock revetment on an exposed section along its seaward face at the Port La Tour Small Craft Harbour.&nbsp; The substructure of the breakwater consists of a core stone berm with a vertical stone wall along its exterior face.&nbsp; The surface includes a 6 m-wide reinforced concrete deck and spray wall.&nbsp; The deck serves as a travel surface and provides access to rigid and floating wharves and is protected by shore protection revetments on its seaward side.&nbsp; The breakwater is constructed to an elevation of approximately 3.75 m above chart datum and orientated in an ell configuration, with the stem measuring approximately 132 m long and a 58 m-long ell offset from the stem by approximately 35 degrees into the harbour basin.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The outer ell section of the breakwater, being in deeper water and more exposed, is protected by a rock revetment along its exterior face.&nbsp; The inner stem section is afforded some protection from four small islands to the southeast and is mostly unprotected along its seaward face, with the exception of a 40 m-long section of rip rap at the shoreline interface.&nbsp; The stem is completely exposed to incident waves from the east and northeast storm directions and these waves, along with long period and high-energy refraction waves from the southeast direction, result in overtopping during extreme storm events.

&nbsp;

The new rock revetment will project out from the shore end of the stem a distance of approximately 48 m to join the armour stone on the ell section.&nbsp; The new revetment will include a core stone berm with side slopes shaped at 1.5:1.&nbsp; The outer layers will be constructed using imported filter and armour stone to ensure long-term durability and protection against erosion.&nbsp; The armour stone layer will be extended and toed into the existing substrate for scour protection.&nbsp; The new rock revetment will be constructed to an elevation of 5.0 m above chart datum.

&nbsp;

The project will be delivered using a traditional design&ndash;bid&ndash;build model; however, the construction methodology will not be explicitly prescribed in the contract.&nbsp; Based on the existing harbour configuration, construction is anticipated to be carried out using land-based methods, with equipment such as loaders, excavators, and trucks operating from upland areas under dry conditions.&nbsp; The new revetment will be comprised of layers of imported core, filter, and armour stone.&nbsp; Minimal demolition or removal is expected, limited to localized modifications of the existing rip rap at the shoreline interface to allow placement of core stone for a temporary access road along the outer face of the breakwater.

&nbsp;

Construction activities are anticipated to commence in summer 2026 and be completed by the end of March 2027.&nbsp; Project commencement is, however, subject to DFO-SCH operational priorities and funding, as well as the completion of regulatory approval processes, therefore work may be delayed.&nbsp; The scope of the impact assessment (subject to the Impact Assessment Act) will, therefore, be based on the works being completed over a period of 3 months commencing within a period of 5 years following finalization of the assessment.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Port La Tour SCH has been developed to support the commercial fishery, which is a main economic driver for the community.&nbsp; The main purpose of this project is to carry out upgrades of the existing infrastructure so that the harbour can operate safely and continue to serve the fishing industry.

properties.description_fr:
Le projet propos&eacute; consiste &agrave; am&eacute;lioration du brise-lames existante au port pour petits bateaux de Port La Tour en y installant un perr&eacute; en enrochement sur une section expos&eacute;e de sa face au large. Le soubassement de la digue est constitu&eacute; d&#39;un noyau en enrochement surmont&eacute; d&#39;un mur vertical en pierre le long de sa face ext&eacute;rieure. La surface comprend une dalle en b&eacute;ton arm&eacute; de 6 m de largeur ainsi qu&#39;un mur antibrise. La dalle sert de surface de circulation et assure l&#39;acc&egrave;s aux quais rigides et flottants; elle est prot&eacute;g&eacute;e du c&ocirc;t&eacute; sous le vent par des perr&eacute;s en protection c&ocirc;ti&egrave;re. La brise-lames est construite jusqu&#39;&agrave; une &eacute;l&eacute;vation d&#39;environ 3,75 m au-dessus du z&eacute;ro des cartes et est orient&eacute;e en configuration en L, dont la section principale mesure environ 132 m de longueur et l&#39;&eacute;l&eacute;ment transversal (&laquo; ell &raquo;) 58 m de longueur, d&eacute;cal&eacute; d&#39;environ 35 degr&eacute;s vers l&#39;int&eacute;rieur du bassin portuaire.

&nbsp;

La section externe de l&#39;&eacute;l&eacute;ment transversal, situ&eacute;e en eaux plus profondes et plus expos&eacute;e, est prot&eacute;g&eacute;e par un perr&eacute; en enrochement le long de sa face ext&eacute;rieure. La section int&eacute;rieure (la &laquo; tige &raquo;) b&eacute;n&eacute;ficie d&#39;une certaine protection gr&acirc;ce &agrave; quatre petites &icirc;les situ&eacute;es au sud est et demeure en grande partie non prot&eacute;g&eacute;e sur sa face au large, &agrave; l&#39;exception d&#39;une section de 40 m en enrochement au niveau de l&#39;interface du littoral. Cette section est enti&egrave;rement expos&eacute;e aux vagues incidentes provenant des temp&ecirc;tes de l&#39;est et du nord est, et ces vagues, combin&eacute;es aux vagues de r&eacute;fraction &agrave; longue p&eacute;riode et &agrave; forte &eacute;nergie provenant du sud-est, entra&icirc;nent des franchissements par-dessus la brise-lames lors d&#39;&eacute;v&eacute;nements de temp&ecirc;te extr&ecirc;mes.

&nbsp;

Le nouveau perr&eacute; en enrochement s&#39;&eacute;tendra &agrave; partir de l&#39;extr&eacute;mit&eacute; terrestre de la tige sur une distance d&#39;environ 48 m, jusqu&#39;&agrave; rejoindre l&#39;enrochement de protection de l&#39;&eacute;l&eacute;ment transversal. Le nouveau perr&eacute; comprendra un noyau en enrochement avec des talus fa&ccedil;onn&eacute;s &agrave; 1,5:1. Les couches externes seront construites &agrave; l&#39;aide de pierres filtrantes et d&#39;enrochement de protection import&eacute;es afin d&#39;assurer une durabilit&eacute; &agrave; long terme et une protection contre l&#39;&eacute;rosion. La couche d&#39;enrochement de protection sera prolong&eacute;e et ancr&eacute;e dans le substrat existant pour assurer une protection contre le d&eacute;maigrissement. Le nouveau perr&eacute; sera construit jusqu&#39;&agrave; une &eacute;l&eacute;vation de 5,0 m au-dessus du z&eacute;ro des cartes.

&nbsp;

Le projet sera r&eacute;alis&eacute; selon un mod&egrave;le traditionnel conception&ndash;appel d&#39;offres&ndash;construction; toutefois, la m&eacute;thodologie de construction ne sera pas explicitement prescrite dans le contrat. Compte tenu de la configuration actuelle du port, on pr&eacute;voit que les travaux seront effectu&eacute;s principalement &agrave; partir de la terre ferme, &agrave; l&#39;aide d&#39;&eacute;quipements tels que chargeuses, excavatrices et camions circulant en terrain sec. Le nouveau perr&eacute; sera constitu&eacute; de couches de pierres de noyau, de filtration et de protection import&eacute;es. Tr&egrave;s peu de d&eacute;molition ou d&#39;enl&egrave;vement est pr&eacute;vu, se limitant &agrave; des modifications localis&eacute;es de l&#39;enrochement existant &agrave; l&#39;interface du littoral afin de permettre la mise en place de pierre de noyau pour cr&eacute;er une route d&#39;acc&egrave;s temporaire le long de la face ext&eacute;rieure de la digue.

&nbsp;

Les travaux de construction devraient d&eacute;buter &agrave; l&#39;&eacute;t&eacute; 2026 et &ecirc;tre achev&eacute;s d&#39;ici la fin mars 2027. Toutefois, le d&eacute;but du projet d&eacute;pendra des priorit&eacute;s op&eacute;rationnelles et du financement de PPB-MPO, ainsi que de l&#39;obtention des approbations r&eacute;glementaires; les travaux pourraient donc &ecirc;tre retard&eacute;s. La port&eacute;e de l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact (en vertu de la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact) sera donc fond&eacute;e sur l&#39;hypoth&egrave;se que les travaux seront r&eacute;alis&eacute;s sur une p&eacute;riode de trois mois d&eacute;butant dans un d&eacute;lai de cinq ans suivant la finalisation de l&#39;&eacute;valuation.

&nbsp;

Le port de Port La Tour &ndash; PPB a &eacute;t&eacute; am&eacute;nag&eacute; pour soutenir la p&ecirc;che commerciale, qui constitue un moteur &eacute;conomique important pour la communaut&eacute;. L&#39;objectif principal de ce projet est de moderniser l&#39;infrastructure existante afin que le port puisse fonctionner en toute s&eacute;curit&eacute; et continuer de servir l&#39;industrie de la p&ecirc;che.

properties.description_en:
The proposed project involves the decommissioning and clean up/closure of a former landfill site and sixteen solid waste dump sites on Beardy&#39;s and Okemasis Cree Nation reserve lands. The sites were historically used as disposal sites for solid waste produced by the community including household garbage, appliances, wood, plastics, and tires. Surficial waste, buried waste, or a combination of both were encountered on the sites. The sites are primarily surrounded by agricultural land.

Supporting studies (Phase II and III Environmental Site Assessments and a Corrective Action Plan) have been completed at all of the sites. The overall project plan is to remove waste from the sites and haul it to approved locations off reserve. &nbsp;

Site management practices for existing solid waste are recommended. These recommendations include the removal of visible debris/waste, the proper decommissioning/closure of any buried waste cells, including either removal or proper soil cover, and ongoing water monitoring. Some of the waste sites are still actively being used; therefore, administrative controls to prevent development on previous waste sites and to prevent further use of the sites for solid waste purposes will also be implemented.

properties.description_fr:
Le projet propos&eacute; comprend la d&eacute;saffectation et le nettoyage/fermeture d&#39;un ancien site d&#39;enfouissement et de seize d&eacute;charges de d&eacute;chets solides sur les terres de r&eacute;serve de la Nation crie de Beardy&#39;s et d&#39;Okemasis. Les sites &eacute;taient historiquement utilis&eacute;s comme sites d&#39;&eacute;limination des d&eacute;chets solides produits par la communaut&eacute;, notamment les ordures m&eacute;nag&egrave;res, les appareils &eacute;lectrom&eacute;nagers, le bois, les plastiques et les pneus. Des d&eacute;chets de surface, des d&eacute;chets enfouis ou une combinaison des deux ont &eacute;t&eacute; trouv&eacute;s sur les sites. Les sites sont principalement entour&eacute;s de terres agricoles.

Des &eacute;tudes connexes (&eacute;valuations environnementales de site de phase II et III et plan de mesures correctives) ont &eacute;t&eacute; r&eacute;alis&eacute;es sur tous les sites. Le plan global du projet consiste &agrave; retirer les d&eacute;chets des sites et &agrave; les transporter vers des endroits approuv&eacute;s &agrave; l&#39;ext&eacute;rieur des r&eacute;serves.&nbsp;

Des pratiques de gestion des d&eacute;chets solides existants sont recommand&eacute;es. Ces recommandations comprennent l&#39;enl&egrave;vement des d&eacute;bris et des d&eacute;chets visibles, le d&eacute;classement et la fermeture appropri&eacute;s de toutes les cellules de d&eacute;chets enfouies, y compris l&#39;enl&egrave;vement ou une couverture ad&eacute;quate du sol, et la surveillance continue de l&#39;eau. Certains des sites de d&eacute;chets sont toujours utilis&eacute;s activement; Par cons&eacute;quent, des contr&ocirc;les administratifs seront &eacute;galement mis en &oelig;uvre pour emp&ecirc;cher l&#39;am&eacute;nagement de sites de d&eacute;chets ant&eacute;rieurs et pour emp&ecirc;cher l&#39;utilisation ult&eacute;rieure des sites &agrave; des fins de d&eacute;chets solides.

Le projet propos&eacute; : bornes de recharge pour v&eacute;hicules &eacute;lectriques&nbsp; 

Dans le cadre du programme d&#39;investissement &agrave; long terme en installations et terminaux (LIFT) de la Greater Toronto Airports Authority (GTAA) &agrave; l&#39;a&eacute;roport Toronto Pearson, de nouvelles infrastructures de recharge pour v&eacute;hicules &eacute;lectriques sont pr&eacute;vues afin de soutenir l&#39;&eacute;lectrification des &eacute;quipements au sol desservant les avions et la flotte de v&eacute;hicules l&eacute;gers (LDV) de maintenance de la GTAA. Les stations de recharge et les infrastructures sont pr&eacute;vues en association avec les b&acirc;timents et infrastructures existants.&nbsp;

La construction devrait inclure le creusement de tranch&eacute;es et l&#39;excavation, la gestion des mat&eacute;riaux, l&#39;installation de nouvelles fondations, des infrastructures &eacute;lectriques, des connexions et le routage des conduits pour les b&acirc;timents existants, la s&eacute;curit&eacute; et la signalisation.&nbsp;

Plusieurs pratiques exemplaires de durabilit&eacute; seront int&eacute;gr&eacute;es dans la conception et la mise en &oelig;uvre du projet dans le cadre du programme &eacute;largi d&#39;investissement &agrave; long terme en installations et terminaux (LIFT) de l&#39;a&eacute;roport Toronto Pearson.

properties.description_en:
The Canadian Coast Guard (CCG) has proposed a project. The proposed project is the new Grand Passage Lifeboat Station at Freeport (South Cove) Small Craft Harbour (SCH) on Long Island, Digby County, Nova Scotia. The existing infrastructure at Freeport SCH will be used with the following upgrades:


	dredging of the main navigation channel between the north and south breakwaters to -2.7 m Chart Datum for an approximate quantity of 10,640 m3;
	raising the existing north and south breakwaters;
	closure of the side channel in the north breakwater;
	infilling the southwest corner of the basin to provide space for the station building and supporting laydown and parking areas;
	construction of a marginal wharf;
	and installation of pile supported floating docks.


Dredging operations may be carried out from temporary causeways or land-based equipment such as long stick excavators.

Two (2) layers of 5-7 tonne armour stone placed at a 1:2 slope along the southwest breakwater will be used to raise the crest to approximately +10.1 m Chart Datum. The northeast breakwater will be reconstructed to close the 12 m wide channel to an elevation of +7.6 m.

The dredge material from the main navigation channel will be used for infilling the southwest corner of the basin. Approximately 15,804 m3 of material will be needed to reach capacity. The proposed service area will be built up to an approximate elevation of +7.30 m by placing gravel approximately 200 mm thick on top of the dredge material. Two (2) layers of 200-600 kg rip rap at 1.2 thickness will be placed at a 1.5:1 slope on the north side of the service area.

A marginal wharf approximately 30 m wide with a 300 mm concrete deck at an elevation +7.30 m will be constructed along the seaward face of the infill area. Floating docks will be constructed adjacent to the marginal wharf.

A launching ramp will be built off the existing gravel parking lot measuring approximately 64 m in length by 6 m wide from Chart Datum elevation +1.18 m to +7.30 m. At the seaward end of the launch ramp, 2 layers of 200-500 kg rip rap 1.1 m thick will be placed at a 1.5:1 slope to provide scour protection. On the existing harbour bottom, core stone will be placed to support the pre-cast and cast in place slabs which will constitute the launch ramp. Along each side of the launching ramp, 2 layers of 200-500 kg rip-rap 1.1 m thick will be placed at a 2:1 ratio to assist with slope protection.

The construction activities will consist of the use of heavy equipment such as excavators and haul trucks.

The CCG Search and Rescue (SAR) station building project encompasses land development, including site preparation, grading and foundation construction. The project will incorporate the installation of septic and potable water systems to meet sanitation and drinking water needs compliant with provincial guidelines/regulations. Basic construction items for the building will include the erection of structural frameworks, roofing, and exterior finishes, along with interior elements such as flooring, walls, and essential utilities like electrical and plumbing systems. The objective is to deliver a SAR station building that supports the operational needs of CCG.

properties.description_fr:
La Garde c&ocirc;ti&egrave;re canadienne (GCC) a propos&eacute; un projet. Le projet propos&eacute; est la nouvelle station du canot de sauvetage de Grand Passage au port pour petits bateaux (PPB) de Freeport (South Cove), &agrave; Long Island, dans le comt&eacute; de Digby, en Nouvelle-&Eacute;cosse. L&#39;infrastructure existante &agrave; Freeport PPB sera utilis&eacute;e avec les am&eacute;liorations suivantes :


	dragage du chenal de navigation principal entre les brise-lames nord et sud jusqu&#39;&agrave; -2,7 m du z&eacute;ro des cartes pour une quantit&eacute; approximative de 10 640 m3 ;
	sur&eacute;lever les brise-lames nord et sud existants ;
	fermeture du chenal lat&eacute;ral du brise-lames nord;
	remplir le coin sud-ouest du bassin pour fournir de l&#39;espace pour le b&acirc;timent de la gare et soutenir les aires de d&eacute;p&ocirc;t et de stationnement ;
	construction d&#39;un quai longitudinal;
	et l&#39;installation de quais flottants sur pieux.


Les op&eacute;rations de dragage peuvent &ecirc;tre effectu&eacute;es &agrave; partir de chauss&eacute;es temporaires ou d&#39;&eacute;quipements terrestres tels que des excavatrices &agrave; long manche.

Deux (2) couches de pierres de carapace de 5 &agrave; 7 tonnes plac&eacute;es selon une pente de 1:2 le long du brise-lames sud-ouest seront utilis&eacute;es pour &eacute;lever la cr&ecirc;te &agrave; environ +10,1 m du z&eacute;ro des cartes. Le brise-lames nord-est sera reconstruit pour fermer le brise-lames de 12 m large canal jusqu&#39;&agrave; une altitude de +7,6 m.

Les mat&eacute;riaux de dragage du chenal de navigation principal seront utilis&eacute;s pour remblayer le coin sud-ouest du bassin. Environ 15 804 m3 de mat&eacute;riaux seront n&eacute;cessaires pour atteindre sa capacit&eacute;. La zone de service propos&eacute;e sera construite jusqu&#39;&agrave; une &eacute;l&eacute;vation approximative de +7,30 m en pla&ccedil;ant du gravier d&#39;environ 200 mm d&#39;&eacute;paisseur sur les mat&eacute;riaux de dragage. Deux (2) couches d&#39;enrochement de 200 &agrave; 600 kg d&#39;&eacute;paisseur 1,2 seront plac&eacute;es selon une pente de 1,5:1 du c&ocirc;t&eacute; nord de la zone de service.

Un quai longitudinal d&#39;environ 30 m de large avec un tablier en b&eacute;ton de 300 mm &agrave; une &eacute;l&eacute;vation +7,30 m sera construit le long de la face c&ocirc;t&eacute; mer de la zone intercalaire. Des quais flottants seront construits &agrave; c&ocirc;t&eacute; du quai longitudinal.

Une rampe de mise &agrave; l&#39;eau sera construite &agrave; partir du stationnement en gravier existant, mesurant environ 64 m de longueur sur 6 m de largeur, de +1,18 m &agrave; +7,30 m. &Agrave; l&#39;extr&eacute;mit&eacute; de la rampe de mise &agrave; l&#39;eau, 2 couches d&#39;enrochement de 200 &agrave; 500 kg de 1,1 m d&#39;&eacute;paisseur seront plac&eacute;es &agrave; une pente de 1,5:1 pour assurer une protection contre l&#39;affouillement. Sur le fond du port existant, des pierres de base seront plac&eacute;es pour soutenir les dalles pr&eacute;fabriqu&eacute;es et coul&eacute;es sur place qui constitueront la rampe de mise &agrave; l&#39;eau. De chaque c&ocirc;t&eacute; de la rampe de mise &agrave; l&#39;eau, 2 couches d&#39;enrochement de 200 &agrave; 500 kg de 1,1 m d&#39;&eacute;paisseur seront plac&eacute;es dans un rapport de 2:1 pour aider &agrave; la protection des pentes.

Les activit&eacute;s de construction consisteront &agrave; utiliser des &eacute;quipements lourds tels que des excavatrices et des camions de transport.

Le projet de construction de la station de recherche et sauvetage (SAR) de la GCC comprend l&#39;am&eacute;nagement du terrain, y compris la pr&eacute;paration du site, le nivellement et la construction des fondations. Le projet comprendra l&#39;installation de fosses septiques et de syst&egrave;mes d&#39;eau potable pour r&eacute;pondre aux besoins en mati&egrave;re d&#39;assainissement et d&#39;eau potable, conform&eacute;ment aux lignes directrices et aux r&egrave;glements provinciaux. Les &eacute;l&eacute;ments de construction de base du b&acirc;timent comprendront l&#39;&eacute;rection de charpentes, de toitures et de finitions ext&eacute;rieures, ainsi que des &eacute;l&eacute;ments int&eacute;rieurs tels que le rev&ecirc;tement de sol, les murs et les services publics essentiels comme les syst&egrave;mes &eacute;lectriques et de plomberie. L&#39;objectif est de livrer un b&acirc;timent de station de SAR qui r&eacute;pond aux besoins op&eacute;rationnels de la GCC.

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The Project is located in Degnen Bay on the southeastern side of Gabrioloa Island, British Columbia. Work to decommission the in active boat grid on the shoreside of the water lot and conduct partial remediation of the Degnen Bay Small Craft Harbour falls within the mandate of the Federal Contaminated Sites Action Plan to reduce environmental and human health risks from known federal contaminated sites.

Tidal grids were typically used for vessel maintenance during low tide periods and these maintenance activities had the potential to introduce contamination into the surrounding sediments. Previous Environmental Site Assessments found Polycyclic Aromatic Hydrocarbons, Tributyltin, Polychlorinated biphenyls and metals exceedances within ther area of the boat grid.&nbsp;

The boat grid in no longer open to users and will be disassembled with handheld power tools and excavator. Remediation will address contamination in the sediments within the area of the existing boat grid.&nbsp;The excavation footprint is anticipated to be15 cubic meters. Sediment excavation will either be completed using a small excavator or handheld shovels and hydro vacuum trucks. The sediment will be disposed of at an offsite land based disposal facility qualified to accept contaminated media above industrial provincial guidelines.

NAV CANADA has a new Digital Facility strategic initiative that will transform how air traffic services (ATS) are delivered at many airports across Canada over the next 15-20 years, driving greater resiliency and sustainability. It is being implemented through the Digital Aerodrome Air Traffic Services (DAATS) program with the goal of providing ATS to aircraft operators as they receive today but from a location independent of an airport leveraging various sensor technologies installed at the airport.

&nbsp;

NAV CANADA, in coordination with Ottawa International Airport Authority, is proposing to construct a camera mast site located airside of the Ottawa International Airport (CYOW). An approximately 625-sq metre site footprint airside will provide space for a hybrid steel-concrete camera mast structure (approximately 30-metre AGL with 22-meter platform height and another 6-to-8-metre above the platform for sensors and lightning rod) and a fibreglass equipment shelter beside the mast base. This mast site will serve as a key component of the DAATS program long-term supporting operational setups at other airports by serving as a template setup, allowing sensor technology / operational procedure research and development, testing and validating future hardware / software releases prior to operational deployment at other airports, addressing issues / deficiencies discovered over the course of the DAATS program, etc.

Nakoda Oil and Gas Inc. is proposing to expand operations at the existing Goodstoney Aggregate Pit. It is proposed that that pit will expand from its permitted 10 hectares operation of 200,000 cubic metres of extraction to a total operational area of 39.9 hectares and an estimated 3,345,104 cubic meters of recoverable extraction through 5 phases of development. The project is located on Stoney Reserves 142, 143, 144&nbsp; south of HWY 1A near the community of&nbsp;M&icirc;n&icirc; Thn&icirc;.&nbsp;

The project activities will include site preparation, aggregate extraction, gravel crushing and washing, asphalt crushing, and reclamation. Topsoil will be salvaged and stored separately from other materials for use in reclamation. Reclamation will be progressive where compatible with operations. No species listed on schedule 1 of the Species at Risk Act have been identified within the project study area and the project overlaps with 0.17 of graminoid marsh wetland. The Bow river is 700m from the pit boundary and there are no waterbodies or watercourses within the proposed footprint.&nbsp;

Indigenous Services Canada will be required to issue a permit for the project under the&nbsp;Indian Act.&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
La soci&eacute;t&eacute; Nakoda Oil and Gas Inc. propose d&#39;&eacute;tendre ses activit&eacute;s dans la carri&egrave;re de granulats existante de Goodstoney. Il est pr&eacute;vu que cette carri&egrave;re passe d&#39;une superficie autoris&eacute;e de 10 hectares, avec un volume d&#39;extraction de 200 000 m&egrave;tres cubes, &agrave; une superficie totale de 39,9 hectares et un volume d&#39;extraction r&eacute;cup&eacute;rable estim&eacute; &agrave; 3 345 104 m&egrave;tres cubes, r&eacute;partis sur cinq phases de d&eacute;veloppement. Le projet est situ&eacute; sur les r&eacute;serves Stoney 142, 143 et 144, au sud de l&#39;autoroute 1A, pr&egrave;s de la communaut&eacute; de M&icirc;n&icirc; Thn&icirc;.&nbsp;

Les activit&eacute;s du projet comprendront la pr&eacute;paration du site, l&#39;extraction d&#39;agr&eacute;gats, le concassage et le lavage du gravier, le concassage de l&#39;asphalte et la remise en &eacute;tat. La terre v&eacute;g&eacute;tale sera r&eacute;cup&eacute;r&eacute;e et stock&eacute;e s&eacute;par&eacute;ment des autres mat&eacute;riaux en vue de son utilisation pour la remise en &eacute;tat. La remise en &eacute;tat se fera progressivement, dans la mesure o&ugrave; cela est compatible avec les op&eacute;rations. Aucune esp&egrave;ce inscrite &agrave; l&#39;annexe 1 de la Loi sur les esp&egrave;ces en p&eacute;ril n&#39;a &eacute;t&eacute; identifi&eacute;e dans la zone d&#39;&eacute;tude du projet, et celui-ci empi&egrave;te sur 0,17 hectare de zone humide &agrave; tapis gramino&iuml;de. La rivi&egrave;re Bow se trouve &agrave; 700 m de la limite de la carri&egrave;re et il n&#39;y a pas de plans d&#39;eau ni de cours d&#39;eau dans l&#39;empreinte propos&eacute;e.&nbsp;

Services aux Autochtones Canada devra d&eacute;livrer un permis pour le projet en vertu de la Loi sur les Indiens.&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
Crown Mountain Resources Ltd. is proposing to construct and operate an open-pit metallurgical coal mine in the Elk Valley, approximately 12&nbsp;kilometres from the District of Sparwood in southeastern British Columbia. As proposed, the production capacity of the project would be 3.7&nbsp;million tonnes per year, over a mine-life of about 16&nbsp;years.

&nbsp;

Please note that the proponent for this project was previously NWP Coal Canada Ltd.

properties.description_fr:
Crown Mountain Resources Ltd. propose de construire et d&#39;exploiter une mine de charbon m&eacute;tallurgique &agrave; ciel ouvert dans la vall&eacute;e de la rivi&egrave;re Elk, &agrave; environ 12 kilom&egrave;tres du district de Sparwood, dans le sud-est de la Colombie-Britannique. Le projet, comme propos&eacute;, aurait une capacit&eacute; de production de 3,7 millions de tonnes par ann&eacute;e pendant la dur&eacute;e de vie de la mine, soit environ 16 ans.

&nbsp;

Veuillez noter que le promoteur de ce projet &eacute;tait pr&eacute;c&eacute;demment NWP Coal Canada Ltd.

properties.description_en:
Westcoast Energy GP Inc. (Westcoast) on behalf of Westcoast Energy Limited Partnership, is proposing to replace up to 165 metres each of nominal pipe size (NPS) 30 and NPS 36 pipe at an increased depth of cover through the Deadman River crossing using trenched construction techniques (Project). Bank armoring will be installed within the right-of-way to protect the banks from erosion. The existing NPS 36 pipe will be replaced, with the existing section removed. Westcoast is proposing two potential options for the decommissioned segment of the NPS 30 pipeline at the river crossing and will determine which option Westcoast proceeds with during Project execution. The two possible options being investigated are either to fully remove the existing NPS 30 pipe, or if during construction, removal is deemed not feasible due to Fisheries and Oceans Canada&#39;s applicable least risk timing window, safety, or constructable feasibility, the pipeline will be decommissioned in place at the river crossing.

&nbsp;

The Project footprint is located on federal lands, Skeetchestn Indian Reserve #0, approximately 41 kilometres northwest of Kamloops, British Columbia. Westcoast plans to complete construction from 1 January 2027 to 1 October 2028. &nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Westcoast Energy GP Inc. (&laquo; Westcoast &raquo;), au nom de Westcoast Energy Limited Partnership, propose de remplacer jusqu&#39;&agrave; 165 m&egrave;tres de conduite d&#39;un diam&egrave;tre de 762 mm (NPS 30) et de 914 mm (NPS 36) au point de franchissement de la rivi&egrave;re Deadman, o&ugrave; la hauteur de recouvrement est plus importante, au moyen de techniques de construction avec tranch&eacute;e (&laquo; projet &raquo;). Un enrochement sera install&eacute; dans l&#39;emprise pour prot&eacute;ger les berges contre l&#39;&eacute;rosion. La section de conduite NPS 36 existante sera remplac&eacute;e et enlev&eacute;e. Westcoast propose deux options pour le tron&ccedil;on d&eacute;saffect&eacute; de conduite NPS 30 au franchissement de la rivi&egrave;re et d&eacute;terminera laquelle elle adoptera pendant l&#39;ex&eacute;cution du projet. Les deux options envisag&eacute;es sont soit d&#39;enlever compl&egrave;tement la conduite NPS 30 existante, soit de la d&eacute;saffecter sur place au franchissement de la rivi&egrave;re si, pendant la construction, l&#39;enl&egrave;vement est jug&eacute; impossible compte tenu de la p&eacute;riode de moindre risque applicable de P&ecirc;ches et Oc&eacute;ans Canada, de questions de s&eacute;curit&eacute; ou de la faisabilit&eacute; de construction.

&nbsp;

L&#39;empreinte du projet est situ&eacute;e sur le territoire domanial, dans la r&eacute;serve indienne Skeetchestn no 0, &agrave; environ 41 kilom&egrave;tres au nord-ouest de Kamloops, en Colombie-Britannique. La construction devrait avoir lieu du 1er janvier 2027 au 1er octobre 2028.

properties.description_en:
Invest Ottawa (IO), in partnership with the National Capital Commission (NCC), is undertaking the demolition and redevelopment of&nbsp;Building 441&nbsp;at&nbsp;1740 Woodroffe Avenue, with a target operational readiness date of&nbsp;March 31, 2027.

&nbsp;&nbsp;

The proposed project would take place on leased NCC lands and is subject to a federal land use, design, and real estate&nbsp;transaction (FLUDTA) approval under the National Capital Act.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The existing Building 441 will be demolished and be replaced&nbsp;by&nbsp;a&nbsp;new facility&nbsp;within the same footprint to&nbsp;provide modern, flexible infrastructure to support applied research, technology development, testing, and validation activities in collaboration with government, industry, academic, and research partners.&nbsp;The new building will be used as a machine and workshop with associated support spacesand will&nbsp;complement&nbsp;other&nbsp;existing facilities at Area X.O&nbsp;as a secure&nbsp;innovation campus designed to support advanced experimentation and real-world testing across a range of emerging technology domains. The&nbsp;new&nbsp;building&nbsp;will&nbsp;support current and future partners&nbsp;and&nbsp;will&nbsp;enable multiple organizations to&nbsp;operate&nbsp;concurrently within a shared, purpose-built environment.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

A&nbsp;detailed hazardous materials survey will be completed for&nbsp;the existing building.&nbsp;Hazardous construction materials will be removed and disposed of&nbsp;in accordance with&nbsp;provincial and federal requirements prior to building demolition.

&nbsp;

The work will rely on standard construction equipment&nbsp;with&nbsp;demolition&nbsp;expected to begin in mid- to late 2026 with&nbsp;construction completed by March 31, 2027. Best management practices will be applied for noise, dust, sediment control, and site security. No tree removals are&nbsp;anticipated.

&nbsp;&nbsp;

Through this project, Area X.O will continue to strengthen its role as a collaborative research and testing hub, supporting innovation partnerships and enabling the development, validation, and advancement of next-generation technologies.&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Investir Ottawa (IO), en partenariat avec la Commission de la capitale nationale (CCN), entreprend la d&eacute;molition et le r&eacute;am&eacute;nagement du b&acirc;timent 441 situ&eacute; au 1740 avenue Woodroffe, avec pour objectif une mise en service le 31 mars 2027.

&nbsp;&nbsp;

Le projet propos&eacute; serait r&eacute;alis&eacute; sur des terrains lou&eacute;s de la CCN et est soumis &agrave; l&#39;approbation f&eacute;d&eacute;rale de l&#39;utilisation du sol, du design et des transactions immobili&egrave;res (AFUSDTI).

&nbsp;

Le b&acirc;timent 441 existant sera d&eacute;moli et remplac&eacute; par une nouvelle installation occupant la m&ecirc;me superficie afin de fournir une infrastructure moderne et flexible pour soutenir les activit&eacute;s de recherche appliqu&eacute;e, de d&eacute;veloppement technologique, d&#39;essais et de validation en collaboration avec des partenaires gouvernementaux, industriels, universitaires et de recherche. Le nouveau b&acirc;timent servira d&#39;atelier et de salle des machines, avec des espaces de soutien associ&eacute;s, et viendra compl&eacute;ter les autres installations existantes de la Zone X.O en tant que campus d&#39;innovation s&eacute;curis&eacute; con&ccedil;u pour soutenir l&#39;exp&eacute;rimentation de pointe et les essais en conditions r&eacute;elles dans un large &eacute;ventail de domaines technologiques &eacute;mergents. Le nouveau b&acirc;timent soutiendra les partenaires actuels et futurs et permettra &agrave; plusieurs organisations d&#39;op&eacute;rer simultan&eacute;ment au sein d&#39;un environnement partag&eacute; et sp&eacute;cialement con&ccedil;u &agrave; cet effet.

&nbsp;

Une &eacute;tude d&eacute;taill&eacute;e des mat&eacute;riaux de construction dangereux sera r&eacute;alis&eacute;e pour le b&acirc;timent existant. Les mat&eacute;riaux de construction dangereux seront retir&eacute;s et &eacute;limin&eacute;s conform&eacute;ment aux exigences provinciales et f&eacute;d&eacute;rales avant la d&eacute;molition du b&acirc;timent.

&nbsp;

Les travaux s&#39;appuieront sur du mat&eacute;riel de chantier standard; la d&eacute;molition devrait d&eacute;buter entre le milieu et la fin de l&#39;ann&eacute;e 2026, et la construction s&#39;achever le 31 mars 2027. Les meilleures pratiques de gestion seront mises en &oelig;uvre en mati&egrave;re de bruit, de poussi&egrave;re, de contr&ocirc;le des s&eacute;diments et de s&eacute;curit&eacute; du chantier. Aucun abattage d&#39;arbres n&#39;est pr&eacute;vu.

&nbsp;

Gr&acirc;ce &agrave; ce projet, Zone X.O continuera &agrave; renforcer son r&ocirc;le de p&ocirc;le collaboratif de recherche et d&#39;essais, en soutenant les partenariats d&#39;innovation et en favorisant le d&eacute;veloppement, la validation et l&#39;avancement des technologies de nouvelle g&eacute;n&eacute;ration.

properties.description_en:
The project consists of increasing the capacity of the wastewater treatment plant through the addition of an aerated lagoon with an approximate volume of 3,700 m&sup3;, to be developed on the west side of the existing treatment plant.

The main works planned as part of the project include:


	clearing, stump removal, removal of waste materials, and excavation and backfilling work required for site preparation;
	construction of the lagoon dikes;
	waterproofing of the lagoon;
	installation of piping and backfilling;
	grading of access roads and installation of a security fence.

properties.description_fr:
Le projet consiste &agrave; augmenter la capacit&eacute; de la station de traitement des eaux us&eacute;es par l&#39;ajout d&#39;un &eacute;tang a&eacute;r&eacute; d&#39;un volume approximatif de 3 700 m&sup3;, am&eacute;nag&eacute; sur la face ouest de la station de traitement existante.

Les principaux travaux pr&eacute;vus dans le cadre du projet comprennent :


	le d&eacute;boisement, l&#39;essouchement, l&#39;enl&egrave;vement des mat&eacute;riaux de rebut ainsi que les travaux de d&eacute;blai et de remblai n&eacute;cessaires &agrave; la pr&eacute;paration du site;
	la construction des digues de l&#39;&eacute;tang;
	l&#39;&eacute;tanch&eacute;isation de l&#39;&eacute;tang;
	la pose des conduites et le remblayage;
	le nivellement des chemins d&#39;acc&egrave;s et l&#39;installation d&#39;une cl&ocirc;ture de s&eacute;curit&eacute;.

properties.description_en:
The National Capital Commission (NCC) proposes to demolish two deteriorated agricultural structures located at 3160 Ramsayville Road in Ottawa, Ontario, within the Greenbelt. The site is a historic farmstead visible from Ramsayville Road, Russell Road and Highway 417 and contains several assets, including a farmhouse and barn that will remain. The proposed works involve the demolition of a concrete panel silo and a timber-frame shed/garage.

&nbsp;

The project is proposed on federal lands owned and managed by the NCC and is subject to approval under the National Capital Act.

&nbsp;

Structural inspections completed in November 2025 confirmed that both structures are in an advanced state of deterioration and are no longer viable for safe use or repair. The silo exhibits extensive cracking, material degradation, and failed roof components, while the shed has experienced partial structural collapse and severe deterioration.

&nbsp;

The purpose of the project is to eliminate immediate and long-term health and safety risks, remove non-operational and unsafe structures, reduce liability and maintenance requirements, and support the long-term stewardship and future agricultural use of the property.

&nbsp;

The proposed work includes controlled demolition and complete removal of the silo and shed, including all above- and below-grade components, in accordance with applicable provincial regulations and NCC requirements. Demolition activities will be carried out using standard methods and equipment and sequenced to prevent damage to adjacent structures, including the farmhouse and barn. Vegetation immediately adjacent to the shed may be selectively removed where required to facilitate demolition, including one small tree and localized invasive shrubs. Where required, disturbed areas will be backfilled using clean material (including material generated on site) and graded to ensure safe and stable site conditions.

&nbsp;

The demolition is anticipated to occur in fall 2026, outside the active nesting period for migratory birds.

properties.description_fr:
La Commission de la capitale nationale (CCN) propose de d&eacute;molir deux structures agricoles d&eacute;labr&eacute;es situ&eacute;es au 3160, chemin Ramsayville, &agrave; Ottawa (Ontario), dans la Ceinture de verdure. Le site est une ferme historique visible depuis le chemin Ramsayville, le chemin Russell et l&#39;autoroute 417 et comprend plusieurs &eacute;l&eacute;ments, dont une maison de ferme et une grange qui seront conserv&eacute;es. Les travaux propos&eacute;s consistent en la d&eacute;molition d&#39;un silo en panneaux de b&eacute;ton et d&#39;un garage &agrave; ossature de bois.

&nbsp;

Le projet est propos&eacute; sur des terres f&eacute;d&eacute;rales d&eacute;tenues et g&eacute;r&eacute;es par la CCN et est soumis &agrave; l&#39;approbation en vertu de la Loi sur la capitale nationale.

&nbsp;

Des inspections structurelles r&eacute;alis&eacute;es en novembre 2025 ont confirm&eacute; que les deux structures sont dans un &eacute;tat de d&eacute;t&eacute;rioration avanc&eacute; et ne peuvent plus &ecirc;tre utilis&eacute;es en toute s&eacute;curit&eacute; ni r&eacute;par&eacute;es. Le silo pr&eacute;sente de nombreuses fissures, une d&eacute;gradation des mat&eacute;riaux et des &eacute;l&eacute;ments de toiture d&eacute;faillants, tandis que le garage a subi un effondrement structurel partiel et une d&eacute;t&eacute;rioration grave.

Le projet a pour objectif d&#39;&eacute;liminer les risques imm&eacute;diats et &agrave; long terme pour la sant&eacute; et la s&eacute;curit&eacute;, de d&eacute;molir les structures hors service et dangereuses, de r&eacute;duire les responsabilit&eacute;s et les besoins d&#39;entretien, et de favoriser la gestion durable et l&#39;utilisation agricole future de la propri&eacute;t&eacute;.

&nbsp;

Les travaux propos&eacute;s comprennent la d&eacute;molition contr&ocirc;l&eacute;e et l&#39;enl&egrave;vement complet du silo et du hangar, y compris tous les &eacute;l&eacute;ments situ&eacute;s au-dessus et en dessous du niveau du sol, conform&eacute;ment &agrave; la r&eacute;glementation provinciale en vigueur et aux exigences de la NCC. Les travaux de d&eacute;molition seront r&eacute;alis&eacute;s &agrave; l&#39;aide de m&eacute;thodes et d&#39;&eacute;quipements standard et organis&eacute;s de mani&egrave;re &agrave; &eacute;viter tout dommage aux structures adjacentes, notamment la maison de ferme et la grange. La v&eacute;g&eacute;tation situ&eacute;e &agrave; proximit&eacute; imm&eacute;diate du hangar pourra &ecirc;tre enlev&eacute;e de mani&egrave;re s&eacute;lective si n&eacute;cessaire pour faciliter la d&eacute;molition, notamment un petit arbre et des arbustes envahissants localis&eacute;s. Au besoin, les zones perturb&eacute;es seront remblay&eacute;es &agrave; l&#39;aide de mat&eacute;riaux propres (y compris des mat&eacute;riaux g&eacute;n&eacute;r&eacute;s sur place) et nivel&eacute;es afin de garantir des conditions de s&eacute;curit&eacute; et de stabilit&eacute; sur le site.

&nbsp;

La d&eacute;molition devrait avoir lieu &agrave; l&#39;automne 2026, en dehors de la p&eacute;riode de nidification active des oiseaux migrateurs.

properties.description_en:
To ensure Ottawa&#39;s south west region has the power to grow, Hydro Ottawa Limited (Hydro Ottawa) will construct a new 27.6 kV municipal transformer station on Greenbank Road, approximately 450 metres south of the Hunt Club Road intersection. The station, to be constructed within the National Capital Region Greenbelt, will serve existing customers and support projected growth in electricity demand for new residential and commercial developments in south Nepean for many years to come. The Station will enhance reliability, reduce the size and frequency of outages, and provide redundancy to the area&#39;s electricity system in the event of future extreme weather events. The Greenbank municipal transformer station is one of many future-planning investment projects led by Hydro Ottawa to support growth and grid resilience, and to make the region&#39;s electricity system as sustainable as possible.

The site is located directly adjacent to the existing Hydro One 230kV transmission corridor. This proximity simplifies the interconnection process and improves overall system reliability.&nbsp; The site is approximately 1.6 hectares (ha) in size and is located immediately west of Greenbank Road, approximately 460 m south of West Hunt Club Road in Ottawa, Ontario.&nbsp; The Site is located in the northeast corner of the CFIA&#39;s Ottawa Laboratory, which encompasses approximately 837 ha between Fallowfield Road to the south and Hunt Club Road to the north. The Site is situated within agricultural fields, with relatively small tree stands to the south and a surface water feature (tributary to Graham Creek) to the west. The zoning of the Site is AG (Agricultural).

The Site is bordered by:


	Agricultural lands and meadows and West Hunt Club Rod to the north
	Greenbank Road and agricultural lands belonging to the National Capital Commission to the east
	Agricultural lands, small tree stands, and a drainage feature on CFIA property to the south
	Agricultural ands, a treed tributary corridor and Cedarview Road to the west.


&nbsp;



Figure 1: Site map showing the existing Hydro One transmission lines and the proposed location of the new station

&nbsp;

The Project is anticipated to be completed between Fall 2026 and Spring 2028 and will consist of the following components:


	The construction of a single-level building with a basement (approximately 17 m &times; 25 m) to house critical electrical equipment, including switchgear, fuses, and protection and control systems;
	The development of an open-air electrical yard (approximately 53 m &times; 61 m) including the installation of two transformers, two high-voltage breakers, two high-voltage disconnect switches, and associated equipment mounted on concrete foundations;
	The installation of two firewalls integrated into the electrical yard design to provide visual screening of the transformers;
	The construction of a 6-metre-wide private access road connecting the site to Greenbank Road;
	Site preparation activities, including excavation, installation of geotechnical piles, establishment of a staging area, installation of a security fence, and construction of a parking area;
	Landscaping works, including tree planting, installation of vegetative buffers, and construction of an earth berm along the site frontage; and
	The installation of approximately 4.8 kilometres of underground electrical infrastructure to support the new Greenbank Station and surrounding areas. Including:
	
		duct bank system beneath the existing multi-use pathway along Greenbank Road to be completed in coordination with the City of Ottawa pathway repairs. 
		Install 8.5Mx12m switchgear unit at North-West corner of Greenbank and Fallowfield rd.&nbsp; 
		The underground electrical infrastructure will extend westward for approximately 1.2 kilometres along the north side of Fallowfield Road, where it will connect to the main CFIA campus.
	
	


Public Services and Procurement Canada (PSPC) will act as the lead federal authority for the Project on federal lands. In addition to PSPC, the Project will be reviewed under the Impact Assessment Act by the Canadian Food Inspection Agency (CFIA), in its role as landowner and authorizing authority, and by the National Capital Commission (NCC), as the federal authority responsible for issuing approvals under the National Capital Act.

properties.description_fr:
Pour veiller &agrave; ce que le secteur sud-ouest d&#39;Ottawa dispose de l&#39;&eacute;nergie n&eacute;cessaire pour soutenir sa croissance, Hydro Ottawa limit&eacute;e (Hydro Ottawa) va construire un nouveau poste de transformation municipal de 27,6&nbsp;kV sur le chemin Greenbank, &agrave; environ 450&nbsp;m&egrave;tres au sud de l&#39;intersection avec le chemin Hunt Club. &Eacute;rig&eacute; dans la ceinture de verdure de la r&eacute;gion de la capitale nationale, le poste Greenbank desservira des clients actuels et soutiendra la hausse pr&eacute;vue de la demande d&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute; attribuable &agrave; de nouveaux d&eacute;veloppements r&eacute;sidentiels et commerciaux &agrave; Nepean-Sud, et ce, pendant de nombreuses ann&eacute;es. Le poste va am&eacute;liorer la fiabilit&eacute;, r&eacute;duire l&#39;&eacute;tendue et la fr&eacute;quence des pannes, et assurer une redondance dans le r&eacute;seau d&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute; du secteur en cas de ph&eacute;nom&egrave;nes m&eacute;t&eacute;orologiques extr&ecirc;mes. Le poste de transformation municipal Greenbank fait partie d&#39;une s&eacute;rie de nombreux projets d&#39;investissement porteurs d&#39;avenir men&eacute;s par Hydro Ottawa pour soutenir la croissance et la r&eacute;silience du r&eacute;seau et le rendre aussi durable que possible.

L&#39;emplacement est adjacent &agrave; l&#39;actuel corridor de transport de 230&nbsp;kV d&#39;Hydro One. Cette proximit&eacute; simplifiera le processus d&#39;interconnexion et am&eacute;liorera la fiabilit&eacute; g&eacute;n&eacute;rale du r&eacute;seau. L&#39;emplacement est d&#39;une superficie approximative de 1,6&nbsp;hectare (ha) et est situ&eacute; imm&eacute;diatement &agrave; l&#39;ouest du chemin Greenbank, environ 460&nbsp;m au sud du chemin Hunt Club Ouest &agrave; Ottawa, en Ontario. L&#39;emplacement est &eacute;galement situ&eacute; &agrave; l&#39;angle nord-est du Laboratoire d&#39;Ottawa de l&#39;ACIA, qui s&#39;&eacute;tend sur environ 837&nbsp;ha entre le chemin Fallowfield au sud et le chemin Hunt Club au nord. L&#39;emplacement se trouve sur des terres agricoles qui comprennent des bosquets d&#39;arbres relativement petits au sud ainsi qu&#39;un &eacute;l&eacute;ment hydrographique de surface (un affluent du ruisseau Graham) &agrave; l&#39;ouest. Le zonage de l&#39;emplacement est AG (agricole).

L&#39;emplacement est bord&eacute; par&nbsp;:


	Des terres agricoles et des prairies ainsi que par le chemin Hunt Club Ouest au nord;
	Le chemin Greenbank et des terres agricoles appartenant &agrave; la Commission de la capitale nationale &agrave; l&#39;est;
	Des terres agricoles, des petits bosquets et un syst&egrave;me de drainage sur le terrain de l&#39;ACIA au sud;
	Des terres agricoles, un corridor affluent bois&eacute; et le chemin Cedarview &agrave; l&#39;ouest.


&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

Legend

Orange -&gt; Couloir de transport actuel

Blue -&gt; Emplacement du PTM propos&eacute;

Sch&eacute;ma 1&nbsp;: Carte indiquant les lignes de transport d&#39;Hydro One actuelles et l&#39;emplacement propos&eacute; pour le nouveau poste de transformation

&nbsp;

Le projet devrait &ecirc;tre r&eacute;alis&eacute; entre l&#39;automne 2026 et le printemps 2028. Il comprendra les &eacute;tapes suivantes&nbsp;:


	La construction d&#39;un b&acirc;timent d&#39;un seul &eacute;tage avec un sous-sol (environ 17&nbsp;m x 25&nbsp;m) permettant d&#39;accueillir de l&#39;appareillage &eacute;lectrique essentiel, y compris des dispositifs de commutation, des fusibles et des syst&egrave;mes de protection et de commande;
	L&#39;am&eacute;nagement d&#39;un enclos &agrave; ciel ouvert pour l&#39;&eacute;quipement &eacute;lectrique (environ 53&nbsp;m x 61&nbsp;m) comprenant l&#39;installation de deux transformateurs, deux disjoncteurs &agrave; haute tension, deux sectionneurs d&#39;alimentation &agrave; haute tension et des dispositifs connexes, le tout mont&eacute; sur des bases en b&eacute;ton;
	L&#39;installation de deux murs coupe-feu int&eacute;gr&eacute;s &agrave; la conception de l&#39;enclos afin de prot&eacute;ger les transformateurs;
	La construction d&#39;une voie d&#39;acc&egrave;s priv&eacute;e &ndash; d&#39;une largeur de 6&nbsp;m&egrave;tres &ndash; reliant l&#39;emplacement au chemin Greenbank;
	Des activit&eacute;s de pr&eacute;paration de l&#39;emplacement, y compris de l&#39;excavation, l&#39;installation de fondations g&eacute;otechniques, l&#39;&eacute;tablissement d&#39;une aire de stockage temporaire, l&#39;installation d&#39;une cl&ocirc;ture de s&eacute;curit&eacute; et l&#39;am&eacute;nagement d&#39;un stationnement;
	Des travaux d&#39;am&eacute;nagement paysager, notamment la plantation d&#39;arbres, l&#39;installation de bandes de v&eacute;g&eacute;taux et l&#39;am&eacute;nagement d&#39;un talus de terre le long de la fa&ccedil;ade de l&#39;emplacement;
	L&#39;installation d&#39;environ 4,8&nbsp;kilom&egrave;tres d&#39;infrastructures &eacute;lectriques souterraines destin&eacute;es &agrave; soutenir le nouveau poste Greenbank et les secteurs environnants. Entre autres&nbsp;:
	
		Un r&eacute;seau de canalisations en dessous de la piste multifonctionnelle situ&eacute;e le long du chemin Greenbank, &agrave; r&eacute;aliser en coordination avec la r&eacute;fection de la piste pr&eacute;vue par la Ville d&#39;Ottawa.
		Une installation de commutation (8,5&nbsp;m x 12&nbsp;m) &agrave; l&#39;angle nord-ouest du chemin Greenbank et du chemin Fallowfield.
		Les infrastructures &eacute;lectriques souterraines s&#39;&eacute;tendront &agrave; l&#39;ouest sur une distance d&#39;environ 1,2&nbsp;kilom&egrave;tre le long du c&ocirc;t&eacute; nord du chemin Fallowfield, o&ugrave; elles seront raccord&eacute;es au campus principal de l&#39;ACIA.
	
	


Services publics et Approvisionnement Canada (SPAC) agira comme l&#39;autorit&eacute; f&eacute;d&eacute;rale principale relativement aux terres f&eacute;d&eacute;rales faisant partie du projet. En plus de SPAC, le projet fera l&#39;objet d&#39;un examen en vertu de la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact par l&#39;Agence canadienne d&#39;inspection des aliments (ACIA), en sa qualit&eacute; de propri&eacute;taire foncier et d&#39;autorit&eacute; comp&eacute;tente, et par la Commission de la capitale nationale (CCN), en sa qualit&eacute; d&#39;autorit&eacute; f&eacute;d&eacute;rale responsable d&#39;&eacute;mettre des approbations en vertu de la Loi sur la capitale nationale.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

