&nbsp;

Une &eacute;tude d&eacute;taill&eacute;e des mati&egrave;res&nbsp;de construction&nbsp;dangereuses sera r&eacute;alis&eacute;e pour le b&acirc;timent existant. Les mat&eacute;riaux de construction dangereux seront retir&eacute;s et &eacute;limin&eacute;s conform&eacute;ment aux exigences provinciales et f&eacute;d&eacute;rales avant la d&eacute;molition du b&acirc;timent.&nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;&nbsp;

Les travaux s&#39;appuieront sur du mat&eacute;riel de chantier&nbsp;standard;&nbsp;la d&eacute;molition devrait d&eacute;buter entre le milieu et la fin de l&#39;ann&eacute;e 2026, et les travaux de construction s&#39;acheveront&nbsp;au plus tard le 31 mars 2027. Les meilleures pratiques de gestion seront appliqu&eacute;es en mati&egrave;re de bruit, de poussi&egrave;re, de contr&ocirc;le des s&eacute;diments et de s&eacute;curit&eacute; du chantier. Aucun abattage d&#39;arbres n&#39;est pr&eacute;vu. &nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;&nbsp;

Gr&acirc;ce &agrave; ce projet, Area X.O continuera de renforcer son r&ocirc;le de p&ocirc;le collaboratif de recherche et d&#39;essais, en soutenant les partenariats d&#39;innovation et en favorisant le d&eacute;veloppement, la validation et l&#39;avancement des technologies de nouvelle g&eacute;n&eacute;ration.&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The National Capital Commission (NCC) is proposing the rehabilitation and replacement of an existing culvert under the Gatineau Promenade in Gatineau Park, located approximately 280 metres south of Chemin du Lac Meech (the Project). The culvert conveys water from a pond on the west side of the roadway to a wetland on the east side and has historically experienced repeated blockages, likely due to sediment accumulation and beaver activity. Following a significant rainfall event in August 2024, water levels rose to the point of threatening the roadway, highlighting the need for infrastructure improvements.

&nbsp;

The Project includes the complete replacement of the existing culvert with a new structure designed to restore hydraulic functionality, improve long-term resilience, and meet environmental requirements, including fish passage. Construction activities will include excavation of the roadway, installation of temporary cofferdams, removal of the existing culvert, installation of a new culvert and maintenance access structures, roadway reconstruction, paving, and site restoration.

&nbsp;

Mitigation measures will be implemented to minimize environmental effects, including scheduling work outside sensitive timing windows, implementing erosion and sediment control measures, managing excavated soils appropriately, and restoring disturbed areas. The design incorporates features to support ecological connectivity and reduce the risk of future blockages.

&nbsp;

The Project is required to protect and maintain the Gatineau Promenade by improving drainage and reducing the risk of flooding, while supporting sustainable infrastructure and environmental objectives. The new structure will also help prevent future sediment buildup by providing improved maintenance access (e.g., a manhole).

&nbsp;

The NCC must determine whether this project is likely to cause significant adverse environmental effects under sections 81&ndash;91 of the Impact Assessment Act (2019) and the National Capital Act (1985). A federal land use and design approval (FLUDA) is required for this work.

&nbsp;

Project implementation is anticipated to occur in 2026, with construction scheduled to avoid sensitive environmental periods and to minimize disruption to park users.

&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
La Commission de la capitale nationale (CCN) propose la remise en &eacute;tat et le remplacement d&#39;un ponceau existant situ&eacute; sous la Promenade de Gatineau, dans le parc de la Gatineau, &agrave; environ 280 m&egrave;tres au sud du chemin du Lac Meech (le projet). Le ponceau achemine l&#39;eau d&#39;un laysitu&eacute; du c&ocirc;t&eacute; ouest de la chauss&eacute;e vers une zone humide du c&ocirc;t&eacute; est et a, par le pass&eacute;, connu des obstructions r&eacute;p&eacute;t&eacute;es, probablement dues &agrave; l&#39;accumulation de s&eacute;diments et &agrave; l&#39;activit&eacute; des castors. &Agrave; la suite d&#39;importantes pr&eacute;cipitations en ao&ucirc;t 2024, le niveau de l&#39;eau a augment&eacute; au point de menacer la chauss&eacute;e, soulignant la n&eacute;cessit&eacute; d&#39;am&eacute;liorer les infrastructures.

&nbsp;

Le projet comprend le remplacement complet du ponceau existant par une nouvelle structure con&ccedil;ue pour r&eacute;tablir la fonctionnalit&eacute; hydraulique, am&eacute;liorer la r&eacute;silience &agrave; long terme et r&eacute;pondre aux exigences environnementales, y compris le passage des poissons. Les travaux de construction comprendront l&#39;excavation de la chauss&eacute;e, l&#39;installation de batardeaux temporaires, l&#39;enl&egrave;vement du ponceau existant, l&#39;installation d&#39;un nouveau ponceau et de structures d&#39;acc&egrave;s pour l&#39;entretien, la reconstruction de la chauss&eacute;e, le rev&ecirc;tement et la remise en &eacute;tat du site.

&nbsp;

Des mesures d&#39;att&eacute;nuation seront mises en &oelig;uvre pour minimiser les effets sur l&#39;environnement, notamment en programmant les travaux en dehors des p&eacute;riodes sensibles, en mettant en place des mesures de contr&ocirc;le de l&#39;&eacute;rosion et des s&eacute;diments, en g&eacute;rant de mani&egrave;re appropri&eacute;e les terres excav&eacute;es et en remettant en &eacute;tat les zones perturb&eacute;es. La conception int&egrave;gre des &eacute;l&eacute;ments visant &agrave; favoriser la connectivit&eacute; &eacute;cologique et &agrave; r&eacute;duire le risque de blocages futurs.

&nbsp;

Le projet est n&eacute;cessaire pour prot&eacute;ger et entretenir la Promenade de Gatineau en am&eacute;liorant le drainage et en r&eacute;duisant le risque d&#39;inondation, tout en soutenant les objectifs en mati&egrave;re d&#39;infrastructures durables et d&#39;environnement. La nouvelle structure contribuera &eacute;galement &agrave; pr&eacute;venir l&#39;accumulation future de s&eacute;diments en facilitant l&#39;acc&egrave;s pour l&#39;entretien (par exemple, gr&acirc;ce &agrave; bouche d&#39;&eacute;gout).

&nbsp;

La CCN doit d&eacute;terminer si ce projet est susceptible d&#39;avoir des effets n&eacute;gatifs importants sur l&#39;environnement en vertu des articles 81 &agrave; 91 de la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact (2019) et de la Loi sur la capitale nationale (1985). Une approbation f&eacute;d&eacute;rale de l&#39;utilisation du sol et du design (AFUSD) est requise pour ces travaux.

&nbsp;

La mise en &oelig;uvre du projet est pr&eacute;vue pour 2026, la construction &eacute;tant programm&eacute;e de mani&egrave;re &agrave; &eacute;viter les p&eacute;riodes sensibles sur le plan environnemental et &agrave; minimiser les perturbations pour les usagers du parc.

properties.description_en:
Wharf 01 at the Contrecoeur Terminal is a steel sheet pile wharf built in 1955 on the south shore of the St. Lawrence River. The original sea level at the wharf was -10.80 m (chart datum or ZDC). Over the years, the seabed in front of the wharf has gradually deepened as a result of the propellers and bow thrusters of ships docking and leaving the wharf, to the point where the seabed level is now -11.0 m to -13.5 m ZDC (according to a 2022 bathymetric survey), threatening the stability and safety of the wharf. The Montreal Port Authority (MPA) is therefore required to carry out an emergency operation to raise the seabed at Pier 01 to its original level of -10.80 m.

&nbsp;

To raise the seabed, a layer of clean rock with a diameter of 25 to 150 mm will be placed in the excavation area in front of the quay sheet pile wall. This layer of riprap will be covered with geotextile bags filled with grout for protection. The riprap will be placed using a long-reach excavator mounted on a barge.&nbsp; The excavator bucket will be equipped with a GPS guidance system to ensure precise placement of the riprap. The bucket will place the rock on the seafloor in a controlled descent to limit sediment resuspension. Geotextile bags will be placed on top of the rock and filled with grout using a 50 m long pump truck operating from the quay.

properties.description_fr:
Le quai 01 du terminal de Contrec&oelig;ur est un quai en palplanche d&#39;acier construit en 1955 sur la rive sud du fleuve Saint-Laurent. &Agrave; l&#39;origine, le niveau du fond marin au droit du quai &eacute;tait de -10,80 m (selon le z&eacute;ro des cartes ou ZDC). Sous l&#39;effet des h&eacute;lices et des propulseurs d&#39;&eacute;trave des navires accostant et quittant le quai, entre autres, le fond marin au droit du quai s&#39;est graduellement creus&eacute; au fil des ans, si bien que le niveau du fond marin atteint maintenant -11,0 m &agrave; -13,5 m par rapport au ZDC (selon un relev&eacute; bathym&eacute;trique datant de 2022), ce qui met &agrave; risque la stabilit&eacute; et la s&eacute;curit&eacute; du quai. L&#39;Administration portuaire de Montr&eacute;al (APM) doit donc effectuer une intervention d&#39;urgence pour rehausser le fond marin au droit du quai 01 &agrave; l&#39;&eacute;l&eacute;vation d&#39;origine de -10,80 m.

&nbsp;

Les travaux de rehaussement du fond marin consisteront &agrave; mettre en place une couche de roches propres d&#39;un diam&egrave;tre allant de 25 &agrave; 150 mm dans la zone de creusement situ&eacute;e devant le mur de palplanche du quai. Cette couche d&#39;enrochement sera recouverte de sacs en g&eacute;otextile remplis de coulis pour la prot&eacute;ger. La mise en place de l&#39;enrochement se fera &agrave; l&#39;aide d&#39;une pelle de longue port&eacute;e install&eacute;e sur une barge.&nbsp; Le godet de la pelle sera muni d&#39;un syst&egrave;me de guidage GPS pour assurer la pr&eacute;cision de la mise en place de l&#39;enrochement. Le godet d&eacute;posera la roche sur le fond marin en descente contr&ocirc;l&eacute;e pour limiter la remise en suspension des s&eacute;diments. Les sacs de g&eacute;otextile seront d&eacute;pos&eacute;s sur les roches et remplis de coulis &agrave; l&#39;aide d&#39;un camion-pompe &agrave; bras long de 50 m op&eacute;rant &agrave; partir du quai.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The Kwikwasut&#39;inuxw Haxwa&#39;mis First Nation (KHFN) aims to construct a new seawall and bioengineered slope to address natural threats to&nbsp;KHFN&#39;s Village of Gwa&#39;yas&#39;dums on Gilford Island. Construction of these assets would protect critical infrastructure and services within the community, and reduce risk of population displacement due to natural hazards. Project activites would occur on the KHFN&#39;s Gwayasdums No. 1 Indian Reserve lands.&nbsp;&nbsp;

The project would involve the following components:


	Site preparation works;
	Construction of new seawall, boardwalk, and bioengineered slope;
	Excavation and installation of supporting infrastructure and associated works in project area; and
	Various restoration, drainage, and accessory works.&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
La Premi&egrave;re Nation Kwikwasut&#39;inuxw Haxwa&#39;mis (PNKH) vise &agrave; construire une nouvelle digue et une pente bio-ing&eacute;nierie pour faire face aux menaces naturelles qui p&egrave;sent sur le village de Gwa&#39;yas&#39;dums de PNKH sur l&#39;&icirc;le Gilford. La construction de ces actifs prot&eacute;gerait les infrastructures et les services essentiels au sein de la communaut&eacute; et r&eacute;duirait le risque de d&eacute;placement de population d&ucirc; aux al&eacute;as naturels. Les activit&eacute;s du projet se d&eacute;rouleraient sur les terres de la r&eacute;serve indienne Gwayasdums n&deg; 1 de la PNKH.

Le projet comprendrait les composantes suivantes:


	Pr&eacute;paration du site;
	Construction d&#39;une nouvelle digue, d&#39;une promenade et d&#39;une pente bio-ing&eacute;nierie;
	Excavation et installation des infrastructures de soutien et travaux associ&eacute;s dans la zone du projet; et
	Divers travaux de restauration, de drainage et d&#39;accessoires.

properties.description_en:
Telus Communications Inc. is proposing the installation of a new guyed radiocommunication antenna tower, 102 meters in height as a new telecommunications facility, located on&nbsp;Skeetchestn Reserve, B.C. The tower will include six (6) initial (8 ft.) antennas that will provide cellular, and data services in the area.&nbsp;

An Impact Assessment Act federal lands review was previously conducted by ISED for this project in 2025. &nbsp;The project page for that review can be found here:&nbsp;https://iaac-aeic.gc.ca/050/evaluations/proj/89577



&nbsp;

&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Telus Communications Inc. propose l&#39;installation d&#39;un nouveau pyl&ocirc;ne d&#39;antennes de radiocommunication hauban&eacute;, d&#39;une hauteur de 102 m&egrave;tres, destin&eacute; &agrave; servir de nouvelle infrastructure de t&eacute;l&eacute;communications, situ&eacute; dans la r&eacute;serve de Skeetchestn, en Colombie-Britannique. Le pyl&ocirc;ne sera &eacute;quip&eacute; dans un premier temps de six (6) antennes (de 2,4 m&egrave;tres) qui fourniront des services de t&eacute;l&eacute;phonie mobile et de transmission de donn&eacute;es dans la r&eacute;gion.&nbsp;

Une &eacute;valuation d&#39;impact sur les terres f&eacute;d&eacute;rales, r&eacute;alis&eacute;e en vertu de la loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact, a d&eacute;j&agrave; &eacute;t&eacute; men&eacute;e par l&#39;ISED pour ce projet en 2025. La page du projet consacr&eacute;e &agrave; cette &eacute;valuation est accessible ici :&nbsp;https://iaac-aeic.gc.ca/050/evaluations/proj/89577&nbsp;



&nbsp;

&nbsp;




&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The National Capital Commission (NCC), Real Estate and Development Branch, is proposing the construction of a wetland feature on NCC-owned federal lands at Field Trip Farm on Moodie Drive in Ottawa.

&nbsp;

The project would be located within a low-lying area of previously cultivated agricultural land in the floodplain of a tributary to Stillwater Creek. The area periodically floods during high water events and has naturally evolved into a clearing within an existing hedgerow, providing suitable conditions for a wetland restoration project.

&nbsp;

The proposed works include the excavation of two wetland cells (5000m2) adjacent to the creek, connected to the main channel by small connection channels to allow backwatering during high flow events. Excavated material would be reused around the wetland perimeter and naturalized (5000m2). Native plantings would be installed along the wetland margins, and habitat features such as root wads and basking logs would be added to enhance fish and wildlife habitat.

&nbsp;

The project is intended to improve flood storage, reduce flow velocities, and enhance ecological function while minimizing environmental impacts. The NCC is working in partnership with Ducks Unlimited Canada, the Rideau Valley Conservation Authority, and the City of Ottawa Rural Clean Water Program.

&nbsp;

Phases of Construction:


	Installation of sediment and erosion control methods
	Excavation of the wetland cells with a variety of depths
	Placement of the root wads and basking logs within the wetland features
	Planting of native vegetation in the wetlands and riparian areas
	Connections made to the tributary of Stillwater Creek


&nbsp;

Construction will be carried out using standard earth-moving equipment such as tracked excavators. Temporary work areas will include equipment access routes, staging areas, and material stockpiling areas located within the project footprint. All temporary disturbances will be restored following construction.

&nbsp;

Coordination with the Department of Fisheries and Oceans (DFO) is required due to the presence of fish habitat within the project area.

&nbsp;

The proposed project would take place on lands owned by the NCC and will be subject to a federal land use and design approval under the National Capital Act. The NCC will make an environmental determination under the Impact Assessment Act.

&nbsp;

Temporary environmental effects may include short-term soil disturbance, localized vegetation removal, and increased turbidity during in water works. Tree removal is expected to be minimal and limited to small shrubs or individual trees within the immediate construction footprint.

&nbsp;

No detours, closures, or disruptions to public facilities or access are anticipated during construction.

&nbsp;

Construction is planned for the fall of 2026 with the possibility of phasing the two wetland cells over two years.

properties.description_fr:
La Commission de la capitale nationale (CCN), Direction g&eacute;n&eacute;rale de l&#39;immobilier et du d&eacute;veloppement, propose la construction d&#39;un milieu humide sur des terrains f&eacute;d&eacute;raux appartenant &agrave; la CCN, situ&eacute;s &agrave; la ferme Field Trip, sur Moodie Drive, &agrave; Ottawa.

&nbsp;

Le projet serait situ&eacute; dans une zone basse, anciennement consacr&eacute;e &agrave; l&#39;agriculture, dans la plaine inondable d&#39;un affluent du ruisseau Stillwater. La zone est p&eacute;riodiquement inond&eacute;e lors des crues et s&#39;est naturellement transform&eacute;e en une clairi&egrave;re au sein d&#39;une haie existante, offrant des conditions propices &agrave; un projet de restauration de milieu humide.

&nbsp;

Les travaux propos&eacute;s comprennent l&#39;excavation de deux cellules de milieu humide (5 000 m&sup2;) adjacentes au ruisseau, reli&eacute;es au chenal principal par de petits canaux de raccordement afin de permettre le refoulement des eaux lors des crues. Les mat&eacute;riaux excav&eacute;s seraient r&eacute;utilis&eacute;s autour du p&eacute;rim&egrave;tre du milieu humide et naturalis&eacute;s (5 000 m&sup2;). Des plantations indig&egrave;nes seraient mises en place le long des marges du milieu humide, et des &eacute;l&eacute;ments d&#39;habitat tels que des mottes de racines et des troncs de repos seraient ajout&eacute;s pour am&eacute;liorer l&#39;habitat des poissons et de la faune.

&nbsp;

Le projet vise &agrave; am&eacute;liorer la capacit&eacute; de r&eacute;tention d&#39;eaux de crues, &agrave; r&eacute;duire les vitesses d&#39;&eacute;coulement et &agrave; renforcer la fonction &eacute;cologique tout en minimisant les impacts environnementaux. La CCN travaille en partenariat avec Canards Illimit&eacute;s Canada, l&#39;Office de protection de la nature de la vall&eacute;e de Rideau et le Programme d&#39;assainissement de l&#39;eau en milieu rural de la Ville d&#39;Ottawa.

&nbsp;

Phases de construction :


	Mise en place de mesures de contr&ocirc;le des s&eacute;diments et de l&#39;&eacute;rosion
	Excavation des cellules du milieu humide &agrave; diff&eacute;rentes profondeurs
	Mise en place des touffes de racines et des troncs de repos au sein des &eacute;l&eacute;ments du milieu humide
	Plantation de v&eacute;g&eacute;tation indig&egrave;ne dans le milieu humide et les zones riveraines
	Raccordements au ruisseau Stillwater


&nbsp;

Les travaux de construction seront r&eacute;alis&eacute;s &agrave; l&#39;aide d&#39;&eacute;quipements de terrassement standard, tels que des pelles m&eacute;canique. Les zones de travail temporaires comprendront des voies d&#39;acc&egrave;s pour les &eacute;quipements, des aires de rassemblement et des zones de stockage des mat&eacute;riaux situ&eacute;es dans l&#39;empreinte du projet. Toutes les perturbations temporaires seront remises en &eacute;tat apr&egrave;s la construction.

&nbsp;

Une coordination avec le minist&egrave;re des P&ecirc;ches et des Oc&eacute;ans (MPO) est n&eacute;cessaire en raison de la pr&eacute;sence d&#39;habitat du poisson dans la zone du projet.

&nbsp;

Le projet propos&eacute; serait r&eacute;alis&eacute; sur des terrains appartenant &agrave; la CCN et sera soumis &agrave; une approbation f&eacute;d&eacute;rale de l&#39;utilisation des terres, de la conception et des transactions immobili&egrave;res (AFUSDTI) en vertu de la Loi sur la capitale nationale. La CCN rendra une d&eacute;cision environnementale en vertu de la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation des impacts.

&nbsp;

Les effets environnementaux temporaires pourraient inclure une perturbation &agrave; court terme du sol, l&#39;enl&egrave;vement localis&eacute; de v&eacute;g&eacute;tation et une augmentation de la turbidit&eacute; pendant les travaux dans l&#39;eau. L&#39;abattage d&#39;arbres devrait &ecirc;tre minime et limit&eacute; &agrave; de petits arbustes ou &agrave; des arbres isol&eacute;s situ&eacute;s dans l&#39;empreinte imm&eacute;diate du chantier.

&nbsp;

Aucun d&eacute;tour, fermeture ou perturbation des installations publiques ou de l&#39;acc&egrave;s n&#39;est pr&eacute;vu pendant la construction.

&nbsp;

La construction est pr&eacute;vue pour l&#39;automne 2026, avec la possibilit&eacute; de r&eacute;aliser les deux cellules de milieu humide en phases sur deux ans.

properties.description_en:
The Department of National Defence (DND) is proposing a project. This Project will be completed at Building FF10 (Normandy Hall, 346 Ontario Street). The project area will include the existing parking lot and adjacent drainage swales.

Project work will include, but is not limited to:


	Removal of existing asphalt;
	Raising and adjusting the grade (elevation) throughout the lot and perimeter to eliminate ponding water, including adjusting a minor surface collection swale, which will direct surface flows through the existing vegetated areas to the water;
	Restore and improve existing rip-rap (aggregate) discharge areas within the existing fenceline;
	Remove and replace concrete curbs, gutters and sidewalks within the lot;
	Install new light standards and replace existing light standards within the asphalt lot;
	Install new asphalt and restore all disturbed areas.


It is expected that all work under the Project will be completed within the fenced property boundary; this work is not expected to include in water works or impacts to the top and/or sides of the adjacent shoreline. The Project is required as the conditions of the existing parking lot are poor; additionally, current elevations are ineffective at managing overland flow, which leads to ponding of water within the parking lot during wet conditions and a risk to existing infrastructure. Improvements will decrease the accumulation of water on the asphalt surface to maximize the number of vehicles that can use the lot for parking. Inadequate existing lighting concerns were raised, and this project also aims to improve the lighting throughout the lot. The goal of this project is to provide a safe, modern, and sustainable parking facility that meets current and future operational needs. Project objectives include improving vehicle and pedestrian safety, enhancing stormwater management, reducing maintenance requirements, and improving energy efficiency with LED lighting to support DND&#39;s long-term sustainability goals. The completed project will deliver a durable and efficient parking lot that enhances user experience, aligns with accessibility and environmental standards, and supports the Department&#39;s energy and modernization initiatives.

&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale (MDN) propose un projet. Ce projet sera r&eacute;alis&eacute; au b&acirc;timent FF10 (b&acirc;timent Normandie, 346, rue Ontario). La zone vis&eacute;e par les travaux comprendra le terrain de stationnement actuel et les foss&eacute;s de drainage adjacents.

Les travaux &agrave; effectuer sont, entre autres, les suivants :


	Enl&egrave;vement de l&#39;asphalte;
	&Eacute;l&eacute;vation de la pente dans l&#39;ensemble du stationnement et de son p&eacute;rim&egrave;tre afin d&#39;&eacute;liminer les accumulations d&#39;eau, ce qui comprend l&#39;am&eacute;nagement d&#39;un petit foss&eacute; dirigeant les &eacute;coulements de surface vers le plan d&#39;eau &agrave; travers la v&eacute;g&eacute;tation existante;
	Remise en &eacute;tat et am&eacute;lioration des zones de d&eacute;versement en enrochement (granulats) existantes situ&eacute;es &agrave; l&#39;int&eacute;rieur du p&eacute;rim&egrave;tre;
	Enl&egrave;vement et remplacement des bordures, des goutti&egrave;res et des trottoirs en b&eacute;ton dans le stationnement;
	Emplacement des lampadaires sur la surface asphalt&eacute;e du stationnement;
	Installation d&#39;asphalte neuf et remise en &eacute;tat de toutes les zones perturb&eacute;es.


Tous les travaux devraient &ecirc;tre ex&eacute;cut&eacute;s &agrave; l&#39;int&eacute;rieur des limites du terrain cl&ocirc;tur&eacute;. Aucun travail dans l&#39;eau n&#39;est pr&eacute;vu et aucune partie du rivage ne devrait &ecirc;tre touch&eacute;e. Ces travaux sont n&eacute;cessaires, &eacute;tant donn&eacute; le mauvais &eacute;tat actuel du terrain de stationnement. En outre, les pentes actuelles ne permettent pas un &eacute;coulement efficace des eaux de surface, ce qui cause des accumulations d&#39;eau dans le stationnement en temps de pluie et repr&eacute;sente un risque pour l&#39;infrastructure existante. Les am&eacute;liorations apport&eacute;es permettront de r&eacute;duire les accumulations d&#39;eau sur la surface asphalt&eacute;e et de maximiser ainsi le nombre de v&eacute;hicules pouvant se stationner. Ce projet vise &eacute;galement &agrave; am&eacute;liorer l&#39;&eacute;clairage dans l&#39;ensemble du stationnement en r&eacute;ponse aux pr&eacute;occupations ayant &eacute;t&eacute; soulev&eacute;es &agrave; ce sujet. Le but de ce projet est d&#39;offrir un terrain de stationnement s&eacute;curitaire, moderne et durable qui r&eacute;pond aux besoins op&eacute;rationnels actuels et futurs. Ce projet vise notamment l&#39;am&eacute;lioration de la s&eacute;curit&eacute; des v&eacute;hicules et des pi&eacute;tons, l&#39;am&eacute;lioration de la gestion des eaux de ruissellement, la r&eacute;duction des besoins en entretien et l&#39;augmentation de l&#39;efficacit&eacute; &eacute;nerg&eacute;tique gr&acirc;ce &agrave; un &eacute;clairage DEL afin d&#39;assurer la r&eacute;alisation des objectifs du MDN en mati&egrave;re de durabilit&eacute;. Aux termes des travaux, on disposera d&#39;un terrain de stationnement durable et efficient qui am&eacute;liorera l&#39;exp&eacute;rience des utilisateurs, sera conforme aux normes en mati&egrave;re d&#39;accessibilit&eacute; et d&#39;environnement et contribuera aux initiatives du Minist&egrave;re en mati&egrave;re d&#39;&eacute;nergie et de modernisation.

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
	
		
			
			&nbsp;

			The Upper Similkameen Indian Band (USIB) is completing the detailed design for the domestic water system (DWS) improvements on Chuchuwayha I.R. No. 2 near Hedley, BC. The purpose of this project is to provide safe and reliable domestic water to the community of Chuchuwayha.

			&nbsp;

			The Project will include the following major infrastructure:

			
				Two (2) water supply wells;
				Pump installation into wells;
				Water treatment plant (WTP);
				Transmission watermain;
				Distribution watermain;
				Pressure Reducing Valves;
				Reservoir; and
				Reservoir access road.
			

			&nbsp;

			The proponent has applied to Environment and Climate Change Canada for a Species at Risk Act permit under section 73(3).

			&nbsp;

			The proponent has applied for funding from Indigenous Services Canada&#39;s Community Infrastructure program for the construction of the proposed project.

properties.description_fr:
	
		
			
			La bande indienne Upper Similkameen (USIB) ach&egrave;ve actuellement la conception d&eacute;taill&eacute;e des am&eacute;liorations &agrave; apporter au r&eacute;seau d&#39;alimentation en eau domestique (DWS) de Chuchuwayha I.R. No. 2 pr&egrave;s de Hedley, en Colombie-Britannique. L&#39;objectif de ce projet est de fournir une eau domestique s&ucirc;re et fiable &agrave; la communaut&eacute; de Chuchuwayha.

			&nbsp;

			Le projet comprendra les principales infrastructures suivantes :

			&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Deux (2) puits d&#39;approvisionnement en eau;

			&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Installation de pompes dans les puits;

			&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Station de traitement de l&#39;eau (WTP);

			&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Conduite principale de transport de l&#39;eau;

			&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Conduite principale de distribution de l&#39;eau;

			&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Vannes de r&eacute;duction de pression;

			&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; R&eacute;servoir; et

			&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Route d&#39;acc&egrave;s au r&eacute;servoir.

			&nbsp;

			Le promoteur a demand&eacute; &agrave; Environnement et Changement climatique Canada un permis en vertu de l&#39;article 73(3) de la Loi sur les esp&egrave;ces en p&eacute;ril.

			&nbsp;

			Le promoteur a demand&eacute; un financement au programme Infrastructure communautaire de Services aux Autochtones Canada pour la construction du projet propos&eacute;.

			&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
Rideau Hall&#39;s original wing was constructed in 1838 and it was converted into the Official Residence of the Governor General of Canada in 1864. Over time, several additions and alterations have been made to both the residence and its 79 acre site to suit the evolving needs of its occupants and better reflect and Rideau Hall&#39;s identity as a national symbol. Rideau Hall is a Classified Federal Heritage building, while the complex and its landscaped grounds are designated as a National Historic Site of Canada.

&nbsp;

In support of the National Capital Commission&#39;s (NCC) mandate to maintain, rehabilitate, and safeguard the national heritage of the Official Residences and properties, the proposed scope will address deferred maintenance and it includes:

&nbsp;


	Renewal of the Administration Wing;
	Abatement of designated substances;
	Improvements to universal accessibility and energy performance;
	Purpose-built office space for staffing requirements; and,
	Rehabilitation and improvements to the building envelope of an 1899 Wing.


&nbsp;

The proposed project would take place on lands owned by the NCC, and will be subject to a federal land use, design, and real estate transaction approval under the National Capital Act. Alterations will respect and improve, where possible, the heritage character of the site. The NCC will make an environmental determination under sections 81-91 of the Impact Assessment Act. Additionally, the proposed project is undergoing review by the Federal Heritage Review Office for recommendations to be incorporated into the project&#39;s design.

&nbsp;

Select tree pruning and removals may be conducted to enable proposed project activities. Construction is anticipated to begin in late summer 2026 for completion at the end of 2029.

properties.description_fr:
L&#39;aile d&#39;origine de Rideau Hall a &eacute;t&eacute; construite en 1838, puis transform&eacute;e en r&eacute;sidence officielle du gouverneur g&eacute;n&eacute;ral du Canada en 1864. Au fil du temps, plusieurs ajouts et modifications ont &eacute;t&eacute; apport&eacute;s tant &agrave; la r&eacute;sidence qu&#39;&agrave; son domaine de 79 acres afin de r&eacute;pondre aux besoins changeants de ses occupants et de mieux refl&eacute;ter l&#39;identit&eacute; de Rideau Hall en tant que symbole national. Rideau Hall est un b&acirc;timent class&eacute; au patrimoine f&eacute;d&eacute;ral, tandis que le complexe et ses terrains paysagers sont d&eacute;sign&eacute;s lieu historique national du Canada.

&nbsp;

Conform&eacute;ment au mandat de la Commission de la capitale nationale (CCN) visant &agrave; entretenir, r&eacute;habiliter et pr&eacute;server le patrimoine national des r&eacute;sidences officielles et des propri&eacute;t&eacute;s, le projet propos&eacute; portera sur les travaux d&#39;entretien diff&eacute;r&eacute;s et comprendra :

&nbsp;


	la r&eacute;novation de l&#39;aile administrative ;
	l&#39;&eacute;limination des substances d&eacute;sign&eacute;es ;
	des am&eacute;liorations en mati&egrave;re d&#39;accessibilit&eacute; universelle et de performance &eacute;nerg&eacute;tique ;
	des espaces de bureaux sp&eacute;cialement am&eacute;nag&eacute;s pour r&eacute;pondre aux besoins en personnel ; et ,
	la r&eacute;habilitation et l&#39;am&eacute;lioration de l&#39;enveloppe du b&acirc;timent d&#39;une aile datant de 1899.


&nbsp;

Le projet propos&eacute; serait r&eacute;alis&eacute; sur des terrains appartenant &agrave; la CCN et sera soumis &agrave; une autorisation f&eacute;d&eacute;rale en mati&egrave;re d&#39;utilisation des sols, de conception et de transaction immobili&egrave;re en vertu de la Loi sur la capitale nationale. Les modifications respecteront et am&eacute;lioreront, dans la mesure du possible, le caract&egrave;re patrimonial du site. La CCN rendra une d&eacute;cision environnementale en vertu des articles 81 &agrave; 91 de la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact. De plus, le projet propos&eacute; fait actuellement l&#39;objet d&#39;un examen par le Bureau f&eacute;d&eacute;ral d&#39;examen du patrimoine afin que des recommandations soient int&eacute;gr&eacute;es &agrave; la conception du projet.

&nbsp;

Des travaux d&#39;&eacute;lagage et d&#39;abattage d&#39;arbres cibl&eacute;s pourraient &ecirc;tre effectu&eacute;s pour permettre la r&eacute;alisation des activit&eacute;s du projet propos&eacute;. Les travaux de construction devraient d&eacute;buter &agrave; la fin de l&#39;&eacute;t&eacute; 2026 et s&#39;achever &agrave; la fin de 2029.

properties.description_en:
Duncan&#39;s First Nation is proposing to construct and operate a Waste Transfer Station to receive and sort the community&#39;s residential waste streams including&nbsp;large items, recyclables, residential renovation waste, tires, household hazardous materials, electronics, whitegoods, propane tanks,&nbsp;and derelict vehicles. The waste will be hauled from the new transfer station by Duncan&#39;s First Nation to third-party operated landfills.&nbsp;The transfer station will have a 30-year service life with provision for future&nbsp;expansion to accommodate community growth.&nbsp;

The Transfer Station is located in a previously disturbed borrow pit requiring clearing of second-growth vegetation. The Project will involve the construction of an elevated platform for disposal of residential waste, a designated household hazardous waste collection site with appropriate environmental protections envisioned as a set of&nbsp;modified &quot;sea-can&quot; shipping containers equipped with secondary containment, holding tanks, collection and storage areas&nbsp;for safe temporary storage of household recyclables, derelict vehicles, and bulky items, and an attendant&#39;s shelter.&nbsp;

Due to previous disturbance it is unlikely Species at Risk will be impacted. A wildlife sweep and biophysical assessment was conducted to support an initial application for review, and to support due-diligence environmental management objectives.

As part of the rehabilitation of the Lady Aberdeen Bridge in Gatineau, the Ministry of Transport and Sustainable Mobility (MTMD) plans to carry out the following activities, some of which will take place on federal land owned by the NCC:


&bull; Resurfacing of the roadway at the bridge approaches;
&bull; Replacement of guardrails at the approaches;
&bull; Construction and removal of a temporary detour route between the lanes of Fournier Boulevard;
&bull; Installation and removal of a temporary bike path.


Construction of the temporary detour road is scheduled for summer 2026, while work to repair the roadway at the bridge approaches, replace the guardrails, and install the temporary bike path will take place from April to November 2027. Final work, including restoration of the detour route and road marking, will be completed in the spring of 2028.

properties.description_fr:
Dans le cadre de la r&eacute;fection du pont Lady-Aberdeen &agrave; Gatineau, le minist&egrave;re des Transports et de la Mobilit&eacute; durable (MTMD) pr&eacute;voit r&eacute;aliser les activit&eacute;s suivantes, situ&eacute;es en partie en terre f&eacute;d&eacute;rale, sur la propri&eacute;t&eacute; de la CCN :


&bull; R&eacute;fection de la chauss&eacute;e aux approches du pont;
&bull; Remplacement des glissi&egrave;res aux approches;
&bull; Construction et d&eacute;mant&egrave;lement d&#39;un chemin de d&eacute;viation temporaire entre les art&egrave;res du boulevard Fournier;
&bull; Am&eacute;nagement et d&eacute;mant&egrave;lement d&#39;une piste cyclable temporaire.


La r&eacute;alisation des travaux du chemin de d&eacute;viation temporaire est pr&eacute;vue &agrave; l&#39;&eacute;t&eacute; 2026, alors que les travaux de r&eacute;fection de la chauss&eacute;e aux approches du pont, de remplacement des glissi&egrave;res et d&#39;am&eacute;nagement de la piste cyclable temporaire auront lieu d&#39;avril &agrave; novembre 2027. Des travaux, dont la remise en &eacute;tat des lieux du chemin de d&eacute;viation et le marquage, se r&eacute;aliseront en parach&egrave;vement au printemps 2028.

properties.description_en:
Proposed Project: North Cargo Hardstands&nbsp;

The North Cargo Hardstands Project forms part of the National Trade Corridors Fund (NTCF) funding agreement between the Greater Toronto Airports Authority (GTAA) and Transport Canada. The primary&nbsp;objective&nbsp;of this initiative is to enhance air cargo capacity at Toronto Pearson International Airport.&nbsp;

The proposed development will be&nbsp;located&nbsp;airside near the east end of Runway 05-23, southwest of the intersection of Airport Road and Derry Road, on previously developed land. The facility will support increased&nbsp;aircraft&nbsp;cargo operations and parking capacity. The project scope includes:&nbsp;


	Construction of approximately 120,000 square metres of pavement for&nbsp;aircraft&nbsp;parking and manoeuvring&nbsp;&nbsp;
	Installation of high-mast lighting systems&nbsp;&nbsp;
	Provision of hydrant&nbsp;fueling&nbsp;infrastructure and&nbsp;aircraft&nbsp;servicing equipment&nbsp;&nbsp;
	Development of a new connection to existing Taxiway Juliet&nbsp;&nbsp;
	Implementation of new drainage infrastructure, including a stormwater retention system and oil/water interceptors to manage both quantity and quality of runoff&nbsp;&nbsp;


Construction activities will involve excavation, clearing and grubbing, utility relocation and removal, site grading, installation of underground services, paving, line marking, lighting installation, and concrete works, along with supporting boarding infrastructure.&nbsp;

Sustainability best practices will be integrated into both the design and construction phases, aligning with the broader Long-Term Investment in Facilities and Terminals (LIFT) Program at Toronto Pearson Airport.&nbsp;

Note: The six cargo&nbsp;aircraft&nbsp;stands included in this project form part of GTAA&#39;s broader LIFT Program, which encompasses a total of 10&nbsp;aircraft&nbsp;stands. The remaining stands will be addressed under a separate project posting&nbsp;(Reference # 90410).&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Projet&nbsp;propos&eacute;&nbsp;:&nbsp;Aires de&nbsp;stationnement&nbsp;de fret&nbsp;nord&nbsp;

Le&nbsp;projet&nbsp;des Aires de&nbsp;stationnement&nbsp;de fret&nbsp;nord&nbsp;fait&nbsp;partie&nbsp;de&nbsp;l&#39;accord&nbsp;de&nbsp;financement&nbsp;du Fonds national pour les corridors&nbsp;commerciaux&nbsp;(NTCF) entre la&nbsp;L&#39;Autorit&eacute;&nbsp;a&eacute;roportuaire du Grand Toronto&nbsp;(GTAA) et Transports Canada.&nbsp;L&#39;objectif&nbsp;principal de&nbsp;cette&nbsp;initiative est de&nbsp;renforcer&nbsp;la&nbsp;capacit&eacute;&nbsp;de fret&nbsp;a&eacute;rien&nbsp;&agrave;&nbsp;l&#39;a&eacute;roport&nbsp;international Pearson de Toronto.&nbsp;

Le&nbsp;d&eacute;veloppement&nbsp;propos&eacute;&nbsp;sera&nbsp;situ&eacute;&nbsp;c&ocirc;t&eacute;&nbsp;piste&nbsp;pr&egrave;s de&nbsp;l&#39;extr&eacute;mit&eacute;&nbsp;est de la&nbsp;piste&nbsp;05-23, au&nbsp;sud-ouest&nbsp;de&nbsp;l&#39;intersection&nbsp;de Airport Road et Derry Road, sur un terrain d&eacute;j&agrave;&nbsp;d&eacute;velopp&eacute;.&nbsp;L&#39;installation&nbsp;soutiendra&nbsp;l&#39;augmentation&nbsp;des&nbsp;op&eacute;rations&nbsp;de fret&nbsp;a&eacute;rien&nbsp;et de la&nbsp;capacit&eacute;&nbsp;de&nbsp;stationnement&nbsp;des avions. Le&nbsp;p&eacute;rim&egrave;tre&nbsp;du&nbsp;projet&nbsp;comprend&nbsp;:&nbsp;&nbsp;


	La construction&nbsp;d&#39;environ&nbsp;120 000&nbsp;m&egrave;tres&nbsp;carr&eacute;s&nbsp;de&nbsp;rev&ecirc;tement&nbsp;pour le&nbsp;stationnement&nbsp;et la&nbsp;man&oelig;uvre&nbsp;des avions&nbsp;&nbsp;
	L&#39;installation&nbsp;de&nbsp;syst&egrave;mes&nbsp;d&#39;&eacute;clairage&nbsp;&agrave;&nbsp;m&acirc;t&nbsp;&eacute;lev&eacute;&nbsp;&nbsp;
	La&nbsp;fourniture&nbsp;d&#39;infrastructures&nbsp;de carburant par hydrant et&nbsp;d&#39;&eacute;quipements&nbsp;de service&nbsp;pour&nbsp;avions&nbsp;&nbsp;
	Le&nbsp;d&eacute;veloppement&nbsp;d&#39;une&nbsp;nouvelle liaison vers&nbsp;l&#39;actuelle&nbsp;voie&nbsp;de circulation Juliet&nbsp;&nbsp;
	La mise&nbsp;en&nbsp;place de&nbsp;nouvelles&nbsp;infrastructures de drainage, y&nbsp;compris&nbsp;un&nbsp;syst&egrave;me&nbsp;de&nbsp;r&eacute;tention&nbsp;des eaux&nbsp;pluviales&nbsp;et des&nbsp;s&eacute;parateurs&nbsp;huile/eau pour&nbsp;g&eacute;rer&nbsp;&agrave; la&nbsp;fois&nbsp;la&nbsp;quantit&eacute;&nbsp;et la&nbsp;qualit&eacute;&nbsp;des&nbsp;&eacute;coulements&nbsp;


Les&nbsp;activit&eacute;s&nbsp;de construction&nbsp;impliqueront&nbsp;l&#39;excavation, le&nbsp;d&eacute;frichage&nbsp;et le raclage, le&nbsp;d&eacute;placement&nbsp;et&nbsp;l&#39;enl&egrave;vement&nbsp;des services publics, le&nbsp;nivellement&nbsp;du site,&nbsp;l&#39;installation&nbsp;de services souterrains, le&nbsp;pavage, le&nbsp;marquage&nbsp;des&nbsp;lignes,&nbsp;l&#39;installation&nbsp;d&#39;&eacute;clairage&nbsp;et les travaux&nbsp;en&nbsp;b&eacute;ton,&nbsp;ainsi&nbsp;que&nbsp;l&#39;infrastructure&nbsp;de support&nbsp;pour&nbsp;le&nbsp;boisage.&nbsp;

Les&nbsp;meilleures&nbsp;pratiques de&nbsp;durabilit&eacute;&nbsp;seront&nbsp;int&eacute;gr&eacute;es&nbsp;&agrave; la&nbsp;fois&nbsp;dans les phases de conception et de construction,&nbsp;en&nbsp;s&#39;alignant&nbsp;sur le programme plus large&nbsp;d&#39;investissement&nbsp;&agrave; long&nbsp;terme&nbsp;dans les installations et les&nbsp;terminaux&nbsp;(LIFT) &agrave;&nbsp;l&#39;a&eacute;roport&nbsp;Toronto Pearson.&nbsp;

Remarque :&nbsp;Les six&nbsp;postes&nbsp;d&#39;avions&nbsp;cargo&nbsp;inclus&nbsp;dans&nbsp;ce&nbsp;projet&nbsp;font&nbsp;partie&nbsp;du programme&nbsp;&eacute;largi&nbsp;LIFT de la GTAA, qui&nbsp;comprend&nbsp;un total de 10&nbsp;postes&nbsp;d&#39;avions. Les&nbsp;postes&nbsp;restants&nbsp;seront&nbsp;trait&eacute;s&nbsp;dans le cadre d&#39;un avis de&nbsp;projet&nbsp;distinct&nbsp;(R&eacute;f&eacute;rence # 90410).

properties.description_en:
The Proposed Project: Laydown and Logistics areas&nbsp;

As part of the Greater Toronto Airports Authority&#39;s (GTAA&#39;s) Toronto Pearson Airport Longterm Investment in Facilities &amp; Terminals (LIFT) Program,&nbsp;logistics&nbsp;and laydown areas will be constructed on Airport Lands, to&nbsp;facilitate&nbsp;construction needs.&nbsp;These sites will be developed on&nbsp;unmaintained&nbsp;vegetated&nbsp;areas&nbsp;located&nbsp;both airside and groundside&nbsp;on&nbsp;airport&nbsp;property.&nbsp;The sites will consist of&nbsp;a combination of any of the following:&nbsp;temporary construction trailers, worker parking lot, material laydown, equipment storage, and associated infrastructure to support Airport construction projects.&nbsp;

The sites will undergo a variety of improvements, depending on&nbsp;the current conditions and&nbsp;the requirements for construction.&nbsp;Activities may include, as&nbsp;required,&nbsp;vegetation removal,&nbsp;minor excavation, clearing and grubbing, utility removals /relocations including the addition of temporary pole-mounted lighting with overhead power, re-grading , placement of aggregate and compact areas where required, construction trailers, security booths, transportation services for workers, paving and line painting of parking and trailer areas, stormwater management, and other associated infrastructure. No new permanent buildings are proposed. Trailers will be prefabricated units delivered to the site.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Several sustainability best practices will be incorporated into the projects design and implementation for the wider Toronto Pearson Airport Longterm Investment in Facilities &amp; Terminals (LIFT) Program.

properties.description_fr:
Le projet propos&eacute; : zones de stockage et de logistique&nbsp;

Dans le cadre du&nbsp;programme&nbsp;d&#39;investissement&nbsp;&agrave; long&nbsp;terme&nbsp;dans les installations et les&nbsp;terminaux&nbsp;(LIFT) de&nbsp;l&#39;Autorit&eacute;&nbsp;des&nbsp;a&eacute;roports&nbsp;du Grand Toronto&nbsp;(GTAA) &agrave;&nbsp;l&#39;a&eacute;roport&nbsp;Toronto Pearson, des zones de logistique et de stockage seront am&eacute;nag&eacute;es sur les terrains de l&#39;a&eacute;roport afin de r&eacute;pondre aux besoins de construction.&nbsp;Ces sites seront d&eacute;velopp&eacute;s sur des zones v&eacute;g&eacute;talis&eacute;es non entretenues situ&eacute;es &agrave; la fois c&ocirc;t&eacute; piste et c&ocirc;t&eacute; terre sur la propri&eacute;t&eacute; de l&#39;a&eacute;roport. Les sites comprendront une combinaison de l&#39;un quelconque des &eacute;l&eacute;ments suivants : des roulottes de&nbsp;chantier temporaires, un parking pour les travailleurs, un d&eacute;p&ocirc;t de mat&eacute;riaux, un stockage de mat&eacute;riel et l&#39;infrastructure associ&eacute;e pour soutenir les projets de construction de l&#39;a&eacute;roport.&nbsp;

Les sites subiront une vari&eacute;t&eacute; d&#39;am&eacute;liorations, en fonction des conditions actuelles et des exigences de construction. Les activit&eacute;s peuvent inclure, selon les besoins, l&#39;enl&egrave;vement de la v&eacute;g&eacute;tation, des excavations mineures, le d&eacute;blaiement et le d&eacute;frichage, l&#39;enl&egrave;vement ou le d&eacute;placement des services publics, y compris l&#39;ajout d&#39;un &eacute;clairage temporaire sur poteaux avec alimentation &eacute;lectrique a&eacute;rienne, le&nbsp;re-nivellement, la pose d&#39;agr&eacute;gats et le compactage des zones si n&eacute;cessaire, l&#39;installation de bureaux mobiles, de kiosques de s&eacute;curit&eacute;, des services de transport pour les travailleurs, le pavage et le marquage des zones de stationnement et des zones de bureaux mobiles, la gestion des eaux pluviales et d&#39;autres infrastructures associ&eacute;es. Aucun nouveau b&acirc;timent permanent n&#39;est pr&eacute;vu. Les bureaux mobiles seront des unit&eacute;s pr&eacute;fabriqu&eacute;es livr&eacute;es sur le site.&nbsp;

Les&nbsp;meilleures&nbsp;pratiques&nbsp;en&nbsp;mati&egrave;re de&nbsp;durabilit&eacute;&nbsp;seront&nbsp;int&eacute;gr&eacute;es&nbsp;&agrave; la&nbsp;fois&nbsp;dans les phases de conception et de construction,&nbsp;en&nbsp;alignement&nbsp;avec le&nbsp;programme&nbsp;plus large&nbsp;d&#39;investissement&nbsp;&agrave; long&nbsp;terme&nbsp;dans les installations et&nbsp;terminaux&nbsp;(LIFT) de&nbsp;l&#39;a&eacute;roport&nbsp;Toronto Pearson.&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
Stoney Nakoda Nation is proposing to construct a lift station to service the community of M&icirc;n&icirc; Thn&icirc;. The lift station will be located adjacent to the Elders Lodge. The proposed project will include the construction of a control building, a lift station, an equalization chamber, an access road, and fencing around the site. The new lift station will be tied into the North M&icirc;n&icirc; Thn&icirc; Water and Wastewater Linear Infrastructure Project. Proposed project activities include excavation, installation of water infrastructure, backfill, regrading, and reseeding of disturbed areas.

&nbsp;

The proposed project is located 60 meters north of the Bow River. The site has been previously disturbed and no species at risk or rare plants were identified in the project area. A pre-construction wildlife and nest sweep will be conducted prior to the commencement of any ground disturbance or vegetation clearing activities.

properties.description_fr:
La Nation Stoney Nakoda propose de construire une station de relevage pour desservir la communaut&eacute; de M&icirc;n&icirc; Thn&icirc;. La station de relevage sera situ&eacute;e &agrave; proximit&eacute; de l&#39;Elders Lodge. Le projet propos&eacute; comprendra la construction d&#39;un b&acirc;timent de contr&ocirc;le, d&#39;une station de relevage, d&#39;un bassin d&#39;&eacute;galisation, d&#39;une route d&#39;acc&egrave;s et d&#39;une cl&ocirc;ture autour du site. La nouvelle station de relevage sera raccord&eacute;e au projet d&#39;infrastructure lin&eacute;aire d&#39;approvisionnement en eau et de traitement des eaux us&eacute;es de North M&icirc;n&icirc; Thn&icirc;. Les activit&eacute;s pr&eacute;vues dans le cadre du projet comprennent l&#39;excavation, l&#39;installation d&#39;infrastructures hydrauliques, le remblayage, le nivellement et le r&eacute;ensemencement des zones perturb&eacute;es.

&nbsp;

Le projet propos&eacute; est situ&eacute; &agrave; 60 m&egrave;tres au nord de la rivi&egrave;re Bow. Le site a d&eacute;j&agrave; &eacute;t&eacute; perturb&eacute; et aucune esp&egrave;ce en p&eacute;ril ni aucune plante rare n&#39;a &eacute;t&eacute; identifi&eacute;e dans la zone du projet. Un balayage de la faune et des nids sera effectu&eacute; avant le d&eacute;but de toute activit&eacute; de perturbation du sol ou de d&eacute;frichage de la v&eacute;g&eacute;tation.

properties.description_en:
As part of its commitment to border infrastructure enhancements, the Canada Border Services Agency (CBSA) is upgrading or replacing select land border ports of entry (POE) to modernize its custodial facilities. Included as part of this initiative, is the Paterson POE. The new building will replace the current facility that is past its lifecycle, and will be rebuilt within the existing site footprint.

This will require the construction of new buildings, infrastructure and the demolition of existing facilities. Work will be planned gradually in order to maintain the site operations at all times throughout. Construction is scheduled to begin summer 2026 and completed summer 2028.

The activities associated with the completion of the project include:


	Conduct environmental surveys and works per Construction Environmental Management Plan(s)
	Removal of select trees;
	Excavation and leveling work 
	Potential management and removal of contaminated soils;
	Construction of roadworks&nbsp; and parking areas
	Construction of new buildings, and other infrastructure;
	Demolition of buildings, and other infrastructure;


&nbsp;

As part of the project planning stage, environmental assessments were completed. An Environmental Effects Evaluation performed by WSP Engineering in 2018 included a review of biophysical, socio-economic, and health effects. In 2025, Keystone Engineering was engaged to update these reviews; consequently, a biological field assessment was completed and a Construction Environmental Management Plan was developed.

Additionally, Atkins R&eacute;alis completed an Archaeological Overview Assessment in 2025 to evaluate the potential for proposed works to impact archaeological resources. The potential for the work area was identified as &quot;little to none,&quot; and a procedure has been established in the event of a discovery.

The CBSA has engaged, and will continue to engage, all potentially impacted Indigenous communities. As part of the construction tender, an Indigenous Participation Plan was required, and a minimum of 5% of the total contract value will be awarded to Indigenous businesses.

properties.description_fr:
Dans le cadre de son engagement &agrave; am&eacute;liorer les infrastructures frontali&egrave;res, l&#39;Agence des services frontaliers du Canada (ASFC) proc&egrave;de &agrave; la r&eacute;novation ou au remplacement de certains postes frontaliers terrestres afin de moderniser ses installations de d&eacute;tention. Le poste frontalier de Paterson fait partie de cette initiative. Le nouveau b&acirc;timent remplacera l&#39;installation actuelle, qui a atteint la fin de son cycle de vie, et sera construit sur l&#39;emplacement actuel.

Cela n&eacute;cessitera la construction de nouveaux b&acirc;timents et d&#39;infrastructures, ainsi que la d&eacute;molition des installations existantes. Les travaux seront planifi&eacute;s de mani&egrave;re progressive afin de maintenir le fonctionnement du site &agrave; tout moment. La construction devrait d&eacute;buter &agrave; l&#39;&eacute;t&eacute; 2026 et s&#39;achever &agrave; l&#39;&eacute;t&eacute; 2028.

Les activit&eacute;s associ&eacute;es &agrave; la r&eacute;alisation du projet comprennent :


	R&eacute;alisation d&#39;&eacute;tudes environnementales et de travaux conform&eacute;ment au(x) plan(s) de gestion environnementale de la construction
	Abattage de certains arbres ;
	Travaux d&#39;excavation et de nivellement
	Gestion et enl&egrave;vement &eacute;ventuels des sols contamin&eacute;s ;
	Construction de voiries et d&#39;aires de stationnement
	Construction de nouveaux b&acirc;timents et d&#39;autres infrastructures ;
	D&eacute;molition de b&acirc;timents et d&#39;autres infrastructures ;


Dans le cadre de la phase de planification du projet, des &eacute;valuations environnementales ont &eacute;t&eacute; r&eacute;alis&eacute;es. Une &eacute;valuation des effets sur l&#39;environnement r&eacute;alis&eacute;e par WSP Engineering en 2018 comprenait un examen des effets biophysiques, socio-&eacute;conomiques et sanitaires. En 2025, Keystone Engineering a &eacute;t&eacute; mandat&eacute;e pour actualiser ces examens ; par cons&eacute;quent, une &eacute;valuation biologique sur le terrain a &eacute;t&eacute; r&eacute;alis&eacute;e et un plan de gestion environnementale de la construction a &eacute;t&eacute; &eacute;labor&eacute;.

De plus, Atkins R&eacute;alis a r&eacute;alis&eacute; une &eacute;valuation arch&eacute;ologique pr&eacute;liminaire en 2025 afin d&#39;&eacute;valuer l&#39;impact potentiel des travaux propos&eacute;s sur les ressources arch&eacute;ologiques. Le risque pour la zone de travaux a &eacute;t&eacute; jug&eacute; &laquo; faible &agrave; nul &raquo;, et une proc&eacute;dure a &eacute;t&eacute; mise en place en cas de d&eacute;couverte.

L&#39;Agence des services frontaliers du Canada (ASFC) a consult&eacute;, et continuera de consulter, toutes les communaut&eacute;s autochtones potentiellement touch&eacute;es. Dans le cadre de l&#39;appel d&#39;offres pour la construction, un plan de participation autochtone &eacute;tait requis, et au moins 5 % de la valeur totale du contrat sera attribu&eacute; &agrave; des entreprises autochtones.

properties.description_en:
As part of its commitment to border infrastructure enhancements, the Canada Border Services Agency (CBSA) is upgrading or replacing select land border ports of entry (POE) to modernize its custodial facilities. Included as part of this initiative, is the Pleasant Camp POE. The new building will replace the current facility that is past its lifecycle, and will be rebuilt within the existing site footprint.

This will require the construction of new buildings, infrastructure and the demolition of existing facilities. Work will be planned gradually in order to maintain the site operations at all times throughout. Construction is scheduled to begin summer 2026 and completed summer 2029.

The activities associated with the completion of the project include:


	Conduct environmental surveys and works per Construction Environmental Management Plan(s)
	Excavation and leveling work 
	Potential management and removal of contaminated soils;
	Construction of roadworks&nbsp; 
	Construction of new buildings, and other infrastructure;
	Demolition of buildings, and other infrastructure;


&nbsp;

As part of the project planning stage, environmental assessments were completed. An Environmental Effects Evaluation performed by WSP Engineering in 2018 included a review of biophysical, socio-economic, and health effects. In 2025, Keystone Engineering was engaged to update these reviews; consequently, a biological field assessment was completed and a Construction Environmental Management Plan was developed.

Additionally, Atkins R&eacute;alis completed an Archaeological Overview Assessment in 2025 to evaluate the potential for proposed works to impact archaeological resources. The potential for the work area was identified as &quot;low&quot; and a procedure has been established in the event of a discovery.

The CBSA has engaged, and will continue to engage, all potentially impacted Indigenous communities.

The Project was designed as a comprehensive upgrade to the community&#39;s water system,&nbsp;including the installation of a new potable water treatment, storage, and distribution facility&nbsp;and looping of the existing watermain network to improve water continuity under maintenance&nbsp;and repair scenarios, improve circulation and chlorine residual consistency, and improve water&nbsp;supply capacity throughout the network. Detailed design, design reporting, tender documents,&nbsp;specifications, and all other PAR-related submission documentation was prepared and&nbsp;submitted to Indigenous Services Canada (ISC) for the complete Project scope in December&nbsp;2025.

&nbsp;

This proposal has revised the existing Project to support the exclusive tendering and construction of the Watermain Loop&nbsp;Extension works as Phase 1 of the Project, while maintaining alignment with the remaining&nbsp;treatment, storage, pumping, and fire water infrastructure to be completed in future phases.

&nbsp;

The revised project scope for this proposal is limited to Phase 1 of the Project and focuses&nbsp;specifically on the Watermain Loop Extension. The intent of Phase 1 is to improve system&nbsp;redundancy and operational reliability by looping the existing dead-end sections of the&nbsp;distribution network around the southern intersection of Carp Lake Road and Sekani Drive to&nbsp;strengthen the existing watermain system in preparation for future treatment, storage, and&nbsp;distribution upgrades.

&nbsp;

The project components include:

- Water main extension to loop system with 250mm diameter SDR18 PVC water distribution around the southern intersection of Carp Lake Road and Sekani Drive.
- Installation of a new frontage road along Carp Lake Road from Sekani Drive (south) to the existing gas station parking.
- Two connections to the existing potable water distribution system.

&nbsp;

The existing bolted steel standpipe reservoir offers insufficient fire flow protection rates, volume, and pressure&nbsp;for both residential and commercial buildings.&nbsp; The existing reservoir has experienced freezing,&nbsp;resulting in structural damage and extended water residence times that have contributed to reduced water&nbsp;quality.&nbsp; The reservoir is approaching the end of a typical service lifespan, and the roof and interior are&nbsp;currently unsafe to access, limiting complete and thorough inspections.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Options are currently being explored as part of the design phase of the replacement/upgrade project.&nbsp; The feasibility study for the project resulted in Option 1 being chosen by the McLeod Lake Indian Band, which coinsists of:

&bull;&nbsp; The continued use of existing water supply wells PW86-1 and PW15-1

&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;Installation of a new treatment/ booster station east of Sekani Drive, adjacent to the intersection of&nbsp;Sekani Drive and Reservoir Road (near existing pumphouse).&nbsp;

&bull;&nbsp; Installation of a new in-ground concrete water storage reservoir adjacent to new treatment/ booster&nbsp;station, sized to meet domestic water demands and residential fire flows prescribed by Fire&nbsp;Underwriters Survey 2020.&nbsp;

&bull;&nbsp; Connection to existing potable water distribution system.&nbsp;

&bull;&nbsp; Installation of a separate new fire system with lake intake, fire pump, and dedicated fire line sized to&nbsp;meet fire flow demands for the commercial and non-residential buildings.&nbsp;

&bull;&nbsp; Installation of the new dedicated fire line to existing and proposed hydrants in the vicinity of existing&nbsp;non-residential community building and the proposed new Wellness Center as well as stubs in each&nbsp;direction for future expansion.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Option 1 proposes a reservoir that will be sized to meet the domestic water demand fire flows&nbsp;for one- and two-family homes. The change from an existing above-ground reservoir to an in-ground concrete&nbsp;storage reservoir will reduce freezing risk and offer preferred operation and maintenance conditions.&nbsp;Option 1 also offers design features that will enhance the effectiveness and performance of the system.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Land area consists of road right-of-ways, cleared land, and cleared land with some recent regrowth of shrubs and saplings.

&nbsp;



&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Le r&eacute;servoir actuel en acier boulonn&eacute; offre un d&eacute;bit, un volume et une pression insuffisants pour la protection contre les incendies des b&acirc;timents r&eacute;sidentiels et commerciaux. &nbsp;Le r&eacute;servoir existant a subi le gel, ce qui a entra&icirc;n&eacute; des dommages structurels et des temps de s&eacute;jour prolong&eacute;s de l&#39;eau qui ont contribu&eacute; &agrave; r&eacute;duire la qualit&eacute; de l&#39;eau. &nbsp;Le r&eacute;servoir approche de la fin de sa dur&eacute;e de vie typique, et le toit et l&#39;int&eacute;rieur ne sont actuellement pas s&ucirc;rs, ce qui limite les inspections compl&egrave;tes et approfondies.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Des options sont actuellement &eacute;tudi&eacute;es dans le cadre de la phase de conception du projet de remplacement/am&eacute;lioration. &nbsp;L&#39;&eacute;tude de faisabilit&eacute; du projet a conduit la bande indienne de McLeod Lake &agrave; choisir l&#39;option 1, qui consiste &agrave;:

&nbsp;

&bull;&nbsp; L&#39;utilisation continue des puits d&#39;approvisionnement en eau existants PW86-1 et PW15-1

&bull;&nbsp; L&#39;installation d&#39;une nouvelle station de traitement/surpression &agrave; l&#39;est de Sekani Drive, &agrave; c&ocirc;t&eacute; de l&#39;intersection de Sekani Drive et de Reservoir Road (pr&egrave;s de la station de pompage existante).&nbsp;

&bull;&nbsp; Installation d&#39;un nouveau r&eacute;servoir souterrain en b&eacute;ton adjacent &agrave; la nouvelle station de traitement/surpression, dimensionn&eacute; pour r&eacute;pondre &agrave; la demande en eau domestique et aux d&eacute;bits d&#39;incendie r&eacute;sidentiels prescrits par l&#39;&eacute;tude Fire Underwriters Survey 2020.&nbsp;

&bull;&nbsp; Raccordement au r&eacute;seau de distribution d&#39;eau potable existant.&nbsp;

&bull;&nbsp; Installation d&#39;un nouveau r&eacute;seau d&#39;incendie s&eacute;par&eacute; avec prise d&#39;eau dans le lac, pompe &agrave; incendie et conduite d&#39;incendie d&eacute;di&eacute;e, dimensionn&eacute; pour r&eacute;pondre aux besoins en d&eacute;bit d&#39;incendie des b&acirc;timents commerciaux et non r&eacute;sidentiels.

&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;L&#39;installation d&#39;une nouvelle conduite d&#39;incendie d&eacute;di&eacute;e aux bouches d&#39;incendie existantes et propos&eacute;es &agrave; proximit&eacute; du b&acirc;timent communautaire non r&eacute;sidentiel existant et du nouveau centre de bien-&ecirc;tre propos&eacute;, ainsi que des embranchements dans chaque direction pour une expansion future.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

L&#39;option 1 propose un r&eacute;servoir qui sera dimensionn&eacute; pour r&eacute;pondre &agrave; la demande en eau domestique et aux d&eacute;bits d&#39;incendie pour les maisons unifamiliales et bifamiliales. Le passage d&#39;un r&eacute;servoir en surface &agrave; un r&eacute;servoir en b&eacute;ton enterr&eacute; r&eacute;duira les risques de gel et offrira des conditions d&#39;exploitation et d&#39;entretien optimales. L&#39;option 1 pr&eacute;sente &eacute;galement des caract&eacute;ristiques de conception qui am&eacute;lioreront l&#39;efficacit&eacute; et les performances du syst&egrave;me.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Le terrain se compose d&#39;emprises routi&egrave;res, de terres d&eacute;frich&eacute;es et de terres d&eacute;frich&eacute;es avec quelques arbustes et jeunes arbres r&eacute;cemment repouss&eacute;s.

&nbsp;



&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The Bay Fortune SCH layout is characterized by wharf infrastructure located on the north and south sides of Fortune River. The facilities on the southern side include a series of rigid wharves oriented to form a well-protected harbour basin. The southern wharves consist of seven (7) separate and conjoined structures including an inner timber pile marginal wharf (SCH Facility Number #410) measuring approximately 61.5 m in length and 3.7 m in width with a timber deck system.&nbsp; The marginal wharf deck transitions to an asphalt travel surface with a concrete launching ramp (#504) located inside the harbour basin perpendicular to the western end of the wharf. The subject wharf is at the end of its service life and is currently load restricted and thus requires complete replacement.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

A proposed new marginal wharf will be constructed along the same alignment and will measure approximately 62.7 m long and 7.65 m wide.&nbsp; The new construction will initially involve the complete demolition and removal of wharf #410 including timber piles, pile caps, stringers, decking, sheathing, wales and ladders.&nbsp; Concurrently, excavation will be carried out for the removal of approximately 1800 cubic meters (m3) of material including asphalt, surficial soils and saturated ballast sediments.&nbsp; The demolition and removals will also include a timber retaining wall located adjacent to the launching ramp (#501).&nbsp; There are also eight (8) private wood-frame buildings located directly behind wharf #410 that will be removed by the owners prior to the start of construction.

&nbsp;

The new wharf design has a timber pile foundation, reinforced concrete pile caps and deck system as well as a timber sheathing fendering system.&nbsp; A tie-back anchoring system will be installed for lateral support as well as a 2 m-high retaining wall on the back side to minimize settlement and loss of backfill materials.&nbsp; The underside of the structure will include a core stone berm sloped and protected with armour stone to provide additional stability and to absorb wave energy.&nbsp; The new wharf will be constructed to an elevation of 3.70 m above chart datum and the area directly behind will be backfilled, compacted and graded to blend into the existing service area with a new asphalt travel surface.&nbsp; A new electrical and lighting system will be installed on the new structure.&nbsp; The construction will also include a new 22 m-long retaining wall at the western end of the wharf adjacent to the launching ramp.&nbsp; This wall will be a king pile structure consisting of steel H-piles with interstitial concrete panels (commonly referred to as a Berlin Wall) to provide a stable interface between the ramp and the existing service area.

&nbsp;

The work is expected to be conducted using large commercial vehicles and equipment for heavy civil construction such as excavators, cranes, front-end loaders, and trucks operating from the upland and existing structures.&nbsp; Upland areas of the SCH will likely be used as a staging area for equipment storage and as a lay-down area for demolition and construction materials (treated timber, steel piles, and concrete panels).

&nbsp;

Construction activities may commence as early as September 2026, however actual project commencement is subject to DFO-SCH operational priorities and funding, as well as the completion of regulatory approval processes.&nbsp; The scope of the environmental effects determination (subject to S.82 of the Impact Assessment Act) will, therefore, be based on the works being completed over a period of 18 months commencing within a period of 5 years following the determination of significance of environmental effects.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The Bay Fortune SCH is a core fishing harbour that was developed to serve the fishing industry in the area.&nbsp; The harbour currently has considerable marine infrastructure and remains well situated and protected to support both the commercial fishing and aquaculture industries.

&nbsp;

The main purpose of this project is to replace and upgrade existing infrastructure so that the harbour can continue to serve the fishing and aquaculture industries. Wharf #410 is an integral component of the overall harbour infrastructure as a service and berthing facility. Given that the existing wharf is well beyond its service life and is load-restricted, the status quo of leaving the deteriorated structure available and in service is not currently a viable option. DFO-SCH considered design alternatives and selected the timber pile structure option as the most technical and economically feasible construction approach.&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
L&#39;am&eacute;nagement du PPB de Bay Fortune est caract&eacute;ris&eacute; par des infrastructures de quai situ&eacute;es sur les rives nord et sud de la rivi&egrave;re Fortune. Les installations du c&ocirc;t&eacute; sud incluent une s&eacute;rie de quais rigides dispos&eacute;s de mani&egrave;re &agrave; former un bassin portuaire bien prot&eacute;g&eacute;. Les quais du c&ocirc;te sud comprennent sept (7) structures distinctes et adjacentes, y compris un quai marginal int&eacute;rieur de pieux de bois (installation PPB #410) mesurant environ 61.5 m de longueur et 3.7 m de largeur, dot&eacute; d&#39;un syst&egrave;me de tablier en bois. Le tablier du quai se prolonge par une surface de circulation asphalt&eacute;e, avec une rampe de mise &agrave; l&#39;eau en b&eacute;ton (installation PPB #504) situ&eacute;e &agrave; l&#39;int&eacute;rieur du bassin portuaire, perpendiculairement &agrave; l&#39;extr&eacute;mit&eacute; ouest du quai marginal. Le quai faisant l&#39;objet de la pr&eacute;sente &eacute;valuation a atteint la fin de sa dur&eacute;e de vie utile et fait actuellement l&#39;objet de restrictions de charge; un remplacement complet est donc requis.

&nbsp;

Un nouveau quai marginal propos&eacute; sera construit selon la m&ecirc;me alignement et mesurera approximativement 62.7 m de longueur et 7.65 m de largeur. La nouvelle construction n&eacute;cessitera d&#39;abord la d&eacute;molition compl&egrave;te et l&#39;enl&egrave;vement du quai #410, y compris les pieux de bois, les semelles de pieu, les longerines, le tablier, les rev&ecirc;tements, les raidisseurs et les &eacute;chelles. Parall&egrave;lement, des travaux d&#39;excavation seront r&eacute;alis&eacute;s afin d&#39;enlever approximativement 1800 m&egrave;tres cubes (m&sup3;) de mat&eacute;riaux, y compris de l&#39;asphalte, des sols de surface et des s&eacute;diments de ballast satur&eacute;s.&nbsp; Les travaux de d&eacute;molition et d&#39;enl&egrave;vement comprendront &eacute;galement un mur de sout&egrave;nement en bois situe &agrave; proximit&eacute; de la rampe de mise &agrave; l&#39;eau (installation PPB #501). De plus, huit (8) b&acirc;timents priv&eacute;s &agrave; ossature de bois, situ&eacute;s directement &agrave; l&#39;arri&egrave;re du quai #410, seront retir&eacute;s par leurs propri&eacute;taires avant le d&eacute;but des travaux de construction.

&nbsp;

La conception nouvelle du quai comprend d&#39;une fondation des pieux de bois, des semelles de pieu en b&eacute;ton renforc&eacute;, et d&#39;un syst&egrave;me de tablier, ainsi qu&#39;un syst&egrave;me de d&eacute;fenses d&#39;embarcation de rev&ecirc;tements de bois. Un syst&egrave;me d&#39;ancrage par tirants sera install&eacute; afin d&#39;assurer la stabilit&eacute; lat&eacute;rale, ainsi qu&#39;un mur de sout&egrave;nement d&#39;une hauteur de 2 m du c&ocirc;t&eacute; arri&egrave;re afin de limiter les tassements et la perte des mat&eacute;riaux de remplissage. La sous-face de la structure comprendra d&#39;une berme en roche &agrave; noyau, am&eacute;nag&eacute;e en pente et prot&eacute;g&eacute;e par des pierres de carapace, afin d&#39;am&eacute;liorer la stabilit&eacute; et d&#39;absorber l&#39;&eacute;nergie des vagues. Le nouveau quai sera construit &agrave; une &eacute;l&eacute;vation de 3.70 m au-dessus du z&eacute;ro des cartes et la zone situ&eacute;e directement &agrave; l&#39;arri&egrave;re sera remplit, compact&eacute;e, et nivel&eacute;e afin de s&#39;int&eacute;grer &agrave; la zone de service existante avec une nouvelle surface de circulation asphalt&eacute;e. Un nouveau syst&egrave;me &eacute;lectrique et d&#39;&eacute;clairage sera &eacute;galement install&eacute; sur la nouvelle structure. Les travaux comprendront en outre la construction d&#39;un nouveau mur de sout&egrave;nement d&#39;une longueur de 22 m &agrave; l&#39;extr&eacute;mit&eacute; ouest du quai, adjacent &agrave; la rampe de mise &agrave; l&#39;eau. Ce mur sera une structure &laquo;&nbsp;king pile&nbsp;&raquo;, compos&eacute; de pieux H en acier avec des panneaux de b&eacute;ton interstitiels (commun&eacute;ment appel&eacute; mur de Berlin), afin d&#39;assurer une interface stable entre la rampe et la zone de service existante.

&nbsp;

Les travaux devraient &ecirc;tre r&eacute;alis&eacute;s &agrave; l&#39;aide de v&eacute;hicules commerciaux lourds et d&#39;&eacute;quipements de construction civile lourde, tels que des excavatrices, des grues, des chargeuses frontales et des camions, op&eacute;rant depuis les zones en amont et les structures existantes. Les zones en amont du PPB seront vraisemblablement utilis&eacute;es comme aires de mise en place pour l&#39;entreposage de l&#39;&eacute;quipement ainsi que comme zones de d&eacute;p&ocirc;t pour les mat&eacute;riaux de d&eacute;molition et de construction (bois trait&eacute;, les pieux d&#39;acier et les panneaux de b&eacute;ton).

&nbsp;

Les travaux de construction pourraient d&eacute;buter d&egrave;s septembre 2026; toutefois, le d&eacute;marrage r&eacute;el du projet d&eacute;pend des priorit&eacute;s op&eacute;rationnelles et du financement de MPO-PPB, ainsi que de l&#39;approbation r&eacute;glementaire. L&#39;&eacute;valuation des effets environnementaux (sujet &agrave; l&#39;article 82 de la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact) tiendra donc compte de la r&eacute;alisation des travaux sur une p&eacute;riode de 18 mois d&eacute;butant dans les 5 ans suivant la d&eacute;termination de la port&eacute;e des effets environnementaux.

&nbsp;

Le PPB de Bay Fortune est un port de p&ecirc;che principal qui a &eacute;t&eacute; am&eacute;nag&eacute; pour desservir l&#39;industrie de la p&ecirc;che dans la r&eacute;gion. Le havre dispose actuellement d&#39;importantes infrastructures maritimes et demeure bien situ&eacute; et prot&eacute;g&eacute; pour soutenir les industries de la p&ecirc;che commerciale et de l&#39;aquaculture.

&nbsp;

L&apos;objectif principal de ce projet est de remplacer et mettre &agrave; jour l&apos;infrastructure existante lorsque le port peut continuer &agrave; servir les industries de la p&ecirc;che et d&apos;aquaculture. Le quai #410 constitue un &eacute;l&eacute;ment essentiel de l&apos;ensemble de l&apos;infrastructure portuaire &agrave; titre d&apos;installation d&apos;accostage et de services. &Eacute;tant donn&eacute; que le quai existant a largement d&eacute;pass&eacute; sa dur&eacute;e de vie utile et qu&apos;il est soumis &agrave; des restrictions de charge, le maintien de statu quo, soit laisser la structure d&eacute;t&eacute;rior&eacute;e en place et en service, ne constitue pas une option viable &agrave; l&apos;heure actuelle. MPO-PPB a examin&eacute; diff&eacute;rentes options de conception et a retenu la solution de structure &agrave; pieux de bois comme l&apos;approche de construction la plus r&eacute;alisable sur les plans technique et &eacute;conomique.

properties.description_en:
The City of Ottawa&#39;s Intersection Control Measures Program has identified the need to modify the existing offset intersections of Conroy Road and Davidson Road due to poor traffic operations and road safety concerns. Following completion of a Schedule C Municipal Class Environmental Assessment it was determined that realignment of the east leg of Davidson Road, approximately 325 metres, is preferred to construct a single point intersection with a roundabout as the recommended traffic control device.

&nbsp;

The National Capital Commission (NCC) owns the land surrounding both Conroy Road and Davidson Road rights of way. Additional property required to construct the roundabout, as well as the Davidson Road realignment, will require lands from the NCC. The project requires a Federal Land Use, Design and Transaction Approval under the National Capital Act and an Environmental Effects Evaluation under Section 82 of the Impact Assessment Act. Environment and Climate Change Canada&#39;s (ECCC) involvement is related to its responsibilities under the Species at Risk Act (SARA), as the project has the potential to interact with species at risk (SAR) individuals and/or residences on federal lands. Tree removal and vegetation clearing required for the Davidson Road realignment and roundabout construction may affect wetlands and interact with potential bat roosting habitat and Blanding&#39;s Turtle individuals. In accordance with SARA, ECCC advised that a permit may be required where project activities could result in the incidental harm to individuals or the damage or destruction of a species at risk residence.

&nbsp;

Minor widening of the west leg of Davidson Road and both legs of Conroy Road will be required approaching the proposed roundabout. Modifications to existing roadside ditches and replacement of driveway culverts will be included with construction of the roundabout and the Davidson Road realignment, as required. A multi-use pathway will be included surrounding the proposed roundabout, with pedestrian crossovers on each leg of the intersection. Area street lighting will be upgraded to meet current lighting standards. A portion of an existing overhead hydro and telecom system located in the vicinity of the existing east leg Davidson Road right of way will be relocated into the realigned Davidson Road right of way. Approximately 380 trees will be removed as part of the project. Naturalization of the old Davidson Road right of way through reforestation planting is planned to address the NCC&#39;s tree compensation requirements. Four trees will be planted for every tree that was removed. Realignment of roadside ditches to follow the roadways is planned to maintain stormwater runoff in the area consistent with existing conditions.

&nbsp;

A portion of the roundabout and the realigned Davidson Road will be constructed on land that is currently part of the Pine Grove Forest. This area was used for agricultural purposes until around the late 1960&#39;s with previous farm residences located in the immediate vicinity. The area underwent naturalized coniferous plantings and now contains mixed woodland, coniferous swamp, and coniferous forest.

&nbsp;

Construction is expected to commence in 2026/2027 pending approvals, including budget and overall construction coordination. A Public Information Session will be held by the City of Ottawa in advance of construction to outline staging, detours, and any road closures required.

&nbsp;

For more information, please visit ottawa.ca/ConroyDavidson.

properties.description_fr:
Le personnel du Programme des mesures de contr&ocirc;le aux intersections de la Ville d&#39;Ottawa a d&eacute;termin&eacute; qu&#39;il y avait lieu de modifier les intersections d&eacute;cal&eacute;es entre les chemins Conroy et Davidson en raison de probl&egrave;mes de circulation et de s&eacute;curit&eacute; routi&egrave;re qu&#39;elles engendrent. &Agrave; l&#39;issue d&#39;une &eacute;tude d&#39;&eacute;valuation environnementale municipale de port&eacute;e g&eacute;n&eacute;rale men&eacute;e en vertu de l&#39;Annexe &laquo;&nbsp;C&nbsp;&raquo;, le personnel a conclu que la modification du trac&eacute; de l&#39;embranchement est du chemin Davidson, sur une distance d&#39;environ 325&nbsp;m&egrave;tres, &eacute;tait la solution &agrave; privil&eacute;gier pour ramener ces intersections &agrave; un seul point et am&eacute;nager un carrefour giratoire comme dispositif de r&eacute;gulation de la circulation recommand&eacute;.

&nbsp;

La Commission de la capitale nationale (CCN) est propri&eacute;taire des terrains entourant les emprises du chemin Conroy et du chemin Davidson. Les terrains suppl&eacute;mentaires n&eacute;cessaires &agrave; l&#39;am&eacute;nagement du carrefour giratoire ainsi qu&#39;&agrave; la modification du trac&eacute; du chemin Davidson devront &ecirc;tre acquis aupr&egrave;s de la CCN. Le projet doit obtenir une approbation f&eacute;d&eacute;rale de l&#39;utilisation du sol, du design et des transactions immobili&egrave;res en vertu de la Loi sur la capitale nationale ainsi qu&#39;une &eacute;valuation des effets environnementaux en vertu de l&#39;article&nbsp;82 de la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation des impacts. La participation d&#39;Environnement et Changement climatique Canada (ECCC) est li&eacute;e aux responsabilit&eacute;s qui lui sont d&eacute;volues en vertu de la Loi sur les esp&egrave;ces en p&eacute;ril (LEP), car le projet pourrait avoir des r&eacute;percussions sur des individus d&#39;esp&egrave;ces en p&eacute;ril ou des habitats de ceux-ci situ&eacute;s sur des terres f&eacute;d&eacute;rales. L&#39;abattage d&#39;arbres et le d&eacute;broussaillage n&eacute;cessaires &agrave; la modification du trac&eacute; du chemin Davidson et &agrave; l&#39;am&eacute;nagement du carrefour giratoire pourraient avoir des r&eacute;percussions sur les milieux humides et sur des habitats potentiels de chauves-souris ainsi que de tortues serpentines. Conform&eacute;ment &agrave; la LEP, ECCC a indiqu&eacute; qu&#39;un permis pourrait &ecirc;tre requis si le projet pouvait causer un pr&eacute;judice accessoire &agrave; des individus ou, encore, endommager ou d&eacute;truire l&#39;habitat d&#39;esp&egrave;ces en p&eacute;ril.

&nbsp;

Un l&eacute;ger &eacute;largissement de l&#39;embranchement ouest du chemin Davidson et des deux embranchements du chemin Conroy sera n&eacute;cessaire &agrave; l&#39;approche du carrefour giratoire propos&eacute;. Des modifications des foss&eacute;s en bordure de rue et le remplacement des ponceaux d&#39;entr&eacute;e de cour seront inclus dans les travaux d&#39;am&eacute;nagement du carrefour giratoire et de modification du trac&eacute; du chemin Davidson, selon les besoins. Un sentier polyvalent sera am&eacute;nag&eacute; autour du carrefour giratoire propos&eacute; ainsi que des passages pour pi&eacute;tons &agrave; chaque embranchement de l&#39;intersection. L&#39;&eacute;clairage de rue sera modernis&eacute; afin qu&#39;il soit conforme aux normes d&#39;&eacute;clairage en vigueur. Une partie du r&eacute;seau a&eacute;rien d&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute; et de t&eacute;l&eacute;communications situ&eacute; &agrave; proximit&eacute; de l&#39;emprise actuelle de l&#39;embranchement est du chemin Davidson sera d&eacute;plac&eacute;e vers l&#39;emprise du nouveau trac&eacute; du chemin Davidson. Environ 380&nbsp;arbres seront abattus dans le cadre du projet. La naturalisation de l&#39;ancienne emprise du chemin Davidson par la plantation de nouveaux arbres est pr&eacute;vue pour r&eacute;pondre aux exigences de compensation en mati&egrave;re d&#39;arbres de la Commission de la capitale nationale (CCN). Quatre arbres seront plant&eacute;s pour chaque arbre abattu. Les foss&eacute;s en bordure de rue seront d&eacute;plac&eacute;s afin qu&#39;ils suivent le nouveau trac&eacute; de la rue, ce qui permettra de maintenir l&#39;&eacute;coulement des eaux pluviales dans le secteur comme c&#39;est le cas pr&eacute;sentement.

&nbsp;

Une partie du carrefour giratoire et du nouveau trac&eacute; du chemin Davidson sera construite sur un terrain qui fait actuellement partie de la pin&egrave;de. Cette zone &eacute;tait utilis&eacute;e &agrave; des fins agricoles jusqu&#39;&agrave; la fin des ann&eacute;es&nbsp;1960 environ. Des r&eacute;sidences agricoles se trouvaient autrefois &agrave; proximit&eacute; imm&eacute;diate. La zone a fait l&#39;objet de plantations de conif&egrave;res et abrite aujourd&#39;hui une for&ecirc;t mixte, un mar&eacute;cage de conif&egrave;res et une for&ecirc;t de conif&egrave;res.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Les travaux devraient d&eacute;buter en 2026 ou en 2027, sous r&eacute;serve de l&#39;obtention des autorisations n&eacute;cessaires, notamment en mati&egrave;re de budget et de coordination g&eacute;n&eacute;rale du chantier. Une s&eacute;ance d&#39;information publique, qui aura lieu avant le d&eacute;but des travaux, permettra la Ville d&#39;Ottawa de pr&eacute;senter le d&eacute;roulement des travaux, les d&eacute;tours qui seront mis en place et les fermetures de rues pr&eacute;vues.

&nbsp;

Pour en savoir plus, veuillez consulter ottawa.ca/DavidsonConroy.

properties.description_en:
Crystal Creek Homes is proposing to construct Black Birch Heights - a residential development located at Taza Park on Tsuut&#39;ina Nation reserve lands. The approximately 11632 square metre development consists of two six storey buildings containing in total 345 units atop a single level parkade.&nbsp;

The lot for the proposed project is located on an already cleared and serviced and will therefore tie into existing water, storm, and sanitary services, use Tsuut&#39;ina Nation public roadways and tie into electrical infrastructure grid.

Indigenous Services Canada is required to issue subleases under&nbsp;Section 53(1) of the Indian Act. The Project is not in the vicinity of any known species at risk or waterbodies.

properties.description_fr:
Crystal Creek Homes propose de construire Black Birch Heights, un complexe r&eacute;sidentiel situ&eacute; &agrave; Taza Park, sur les terres de la r&eacute;serve de la Nation Tsuut&#39;ina. Ce projet d&#39;une superficie d&#39;environ 11 632 m&egrave;tres carr&eacute;s comprend deux (2) immeubles de six &eacute;tages abritant au total 345 logements, construits au-dessus d&#39;un parking &agrave; un seul niveau.&nbsp;

Le terrain destin&eacute; au projet propos&eacute; est d&eacute;j&agrave; d&eacute;frich&eacute; et viabilis&eacute; ; il sera donc raccord&eacute; aux r&eacute;seaux existants d&#39;eau, d&#39;eaux pluviales et d&#39;assainissement, empruntera les voies publiques de la nation Tsuut&#39;ina et sera raccord&eacute; au r&eacute;seau &eacute;lectrique.

Services aux Autochtones Canada est tenu de conclure des contrats de sous-location en vertu du paragraphe 53(1) de la Loi sur les Indiens. Le projet ne se situe &agrave; proximit&eacute; d&apos;aucune esp&egrave;ce en p&eacute;ril ni d&apos;aucun plan d&apos;eau connus.

properties.description_en:
The purpose of the Kainai Interconnect Project is to install a new connection onto the NGTL System to supply natural gas service to a customer. The Project would consist of the installation of a new nominal pipe size (NPS) 1.5-inch hot tap to the existing NGTL GP NPS 6 Bailey&#39;s Bottom Lateral and approximately 10.5 meters of NPS 1.5-inch pipe to supply gas to the customer. The maximum operating pressure would be 9,020 kilopascals. The target in-service date for the facility is May 2026.

&nbsp;

The Project would be located on an existing NGTL GP pipeline right-of-way (ROW). This pipeline ROW is governed by a registered ROW agreement issued by His Majesty the King in Right of Canada and administered by Indian Oil and Gas Canada and is located on Blood Tribe &ndash; Kainai Nation, Reserve (Blood 148) lands located in SW 28-007-22 W4M, approximately 16 kilometres southwest of Lethbridge, Alberta.

properties.description_fr:
L&#39;objectif du projet d&#39;interconnexion Kainai est d&#39;installer un nouveau raccordement au r&eacute;seau de NGTL pour approvisionner un client en gaz naturel. Le projet comprendrait le raccordement par piquage sur conduite en charge d&#39;une nouvelle conduite d&#39;un diam&egrave;tre nominal de 48,26&nbsp;mm (NPS 1.5) &agrave; la canalisation lat&eacute;rale Bailey&#39;s&nbsp;Bottom de 168,28 mm (NPS 6) existante de NGTL GP, ainsi que l&#39;ajout d&#39;environ 10,5&nbsp;m d&#39;une conduite de 48,26&nbsp;mm (NPS 1.5) pour approvisionner le client en gaz. La pression maximale d&#39;exploitation serait de 9&nbsp;020&nbsp;kilopascals. La mise en service devrait avoir lieu en mai&nbsp;2026.

&nbsp;

Le projet sera r&eacute;alis&eacute; &agrave; l&#39;int&eacute;rieur de l&#39;emprise pipelini&egrave;re existante de NGTL GP. Celle-ci est assujettie &agrave; une entente d&#39;emprise enregistr&eacute;e, d&eacute;livr&eacute;e par Sa Majest&eacute; le Roi du Chef du Canada et administr&eacute;e par P&eacute;trole et gaz des Indiens du Canada, et est situ&eacute;e sur des terres de r&eacute;serve (Blood 148) de la Tribu des Blood &ndash; Nation Kainai &agrave; la coordonn&eacute;e SW 28007-22 W4M, &agrave; environ 16&nbsp;km au sud-ouest de Lethbridge, en Alberta.

properties.description_en:
The Department of National Defence (DND) is proposing a project. This project is being completed to replace three (3) existing grass athletic fields with two (2) artificial turf fields at the Royal Military College  CFB Kingston. Work under this project will include, but is not limited to:


	Removal of existing grass and topsoil and excavation to prepare for the installation of the turf;
	Installation of a new turf field; and
	Once work is complete, all disturbed areas will be reinstated.


The existing light standards will remain in place and are not included in the scope of the project. Work is expected to start Fall 2026 and end in the Fall of 2027.

&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale (MDN) propose un projet. Ce projet vise &agrave; remplacer trois (3) terrains de sport en gazon naturel par deux (2) terrains en gazon synth&eacute;tique au  Coll&egrave;ge militaire royal &agrave; la BFC Kingston. Les travaux r&eacute;alis&eacute;s dans le cadre de ce projet comprendront notamment ce qui suit :


	Le retrait du gazon naturel et de la terre et l&#39;excavation en vue de l&#39;installation du gazon synth&eacute;tique;
	L&#39;installation du gazon synth&eacute;tique sur les terrains;
	La remise en &eacute;tat des zones endommag&eacute;es lorsque les travaux seront termin&eacute;s.


Les lampadaires actuels resteront en place et ne sont pas inclus dans la port&eacute;e du projet. Les travaux devraient commencer &agrave; l&#39;automne 2026 et se terminer &agrave; l&#39;automne 2027.

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The subdivision project is being undertaken to address housing shortages for Sts&apos;ailes community members.

&nbsp;

The first phase of the proposed subdivision will include 75 single family lots, a lot for an Elders&apos; Village (multi-family lot), the Telmexwawtexw Healing Center (Telmexw), and the Child and Family Services (CFS) Administration Building. Funding for many of these houses and community facilities has already been approved by BC Housing.

&nbsp;

The timely delivery of water, wastewater, and subdivision infrastructure is critical to the success of two major BC Housing&ndash;funded developments already approved and being designed in Sts&apos;ailes:


	44-unit Healing Centre housing project supporting the Telmexw Awtexw Healing Centre, and
	49-unit community rental housing project serving Sts&apos;ailes&apos; restored jurisdiction of Child and Family Services, families returning home and Elders wishing to age in place.


&nbsp;

Both projects are scheduled for occupancy by January 2028 and are fully dependent on the completion of the supporting infrastructure.&nbsp; The infrastructure is also essential to the operations of the Snowoyelh Department, which administers Child and Family Services (CFS) under Sts&apos;ailes&apos; restored jurisdiction.

&nbsp;

The supporting infrastructure includes potable water and sanitary sewer systems, stormwater management infrastructure, electrical and third-party utilities, and a 20m road Right-of-Way (ROW) with paved single lane roads, pedestrian pathways and multi-use trails.&nbsp; The project is being completed in conjunction with two other projects: the Sts&apos;ailes Water System Upgrades project and the Sts&apos;ailes Wastewater System Upgrades project. &nbsp;These projects are progressing together so that the new buildings can connect to the community wastewater system, and to ensure the existing water system has the capacity to support the demands of the proposed subdivision. &nbsp;The details of the Water and Wastewater projects can be found within their respective Registry postings.



&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Ce projet de lotissement vise &agrave; rem&eacute;dier &agrave; la p&eacute;nurie de logements pour les membres de la communaut&eacute; de Sts&apos;ailes.

&nbsp;

La premi&egrave;re phase du lotissement propos&eacute; comprendra 75 terrains destin&eacute;s &agrave; des maisons individuelles, un terrain pour un village des a&icirc;n&eacute;s (terrain multifamilial), le centre de soins Telmexwawtexw (Telmexw) et le b&acirc;timent administratif des Services &agrave; l&apos;enfance et &agrave; la famille (CFS). Le financement d&apos;une grande partie de ces logements et de ces &eacute;quipements collectifs a d&eacute;j&agrave; &eacute;t&eacute; approuv&eacute; par BC Housing.

&nbsp;

La mise en place en temps opportun des infrastructures d&apos;approvisionnement en eau, de gestion des eaux us&eacute;es et de lotissement est essentielle &agrave; la r&eacute;ussite de deux grands projets immobiliers financ&eacute;s par BC Housing, d&eacute;j&agrave; approuv&eacute;s et en cours de conception &agrave; Sts&apos;ailes :


	un projet de 44 logements pour le centre de gu&eacute;rison Telmexw Awtexw, et
	un projet de 49 logements locatifs communautaires destin&eacute;s &agrave; la juridiction r&eacute;tablie de Sts&apos;ailes en mati&egrave;re de services &agrave; l&apos;enfance et &agrave; la famille, aux familles qui rentrent chez elles et aux a&icirc;n&eacute;s souhaitant vieillir chez eux.


&nbsp;

La mise en service des deux projets est pr&eacute;vue pour janvier 2028 et d&eacute;pend enti&egrave;rement de l&apos;ach&egrave;vement des infrastructures de soutien. Ces infrastructures sont &eacute;galement essentielles au fonctionnement du d&eacute;partement de Snowoyelh, qui g&egrave;re les services &agrave; l&apos;enfance et &agrave; la famille (CFS) dans le cadre de la comp&eacute;tence r&eacute;tablie de Sts&apos;ailes.

&nbsp;

Les infrastructures de soutien comprennent des r&eacute;seaux d&#39;eau potable et d&#39;&eacute;gouts sanitaires, des infrastructures de gestion des eaux pluviales, des r&eacute;seaux &eacute;lectriques et des services publics tiers, ainsi qu&#39;une emprise routi&egrave;re de 20 m&egrave;tres comprenant des routes &agrave; voie unique rev&ecirc;tues, des all&eacute;es pi&eacute;tonnes et des sentiers polyvalents.&nbsp; Le projet est r&eacute;alis&eacute; en parall&egrave;le avec deux autres projets : le projet de modernisation du r&eacute;seau d&#39;eau de Sts&apos;ailes et le projet de modernisation du r&eacute;seau d&#39;assainissement de Sts&apos;ailes. Ces projets avancent de concert afin que les nouveaux b&acirc;timents puissent &ecirc;tre raccord&eacute;s au r&eacute;seau d&#39;assainissement communautaire et pour garantir que le r&eacute;seau d&#39;eau existant ait la capacit&eacute; de r&eacute;pondre aux besoins du lotissement propos&eacute;. Les d&eacute;tails des projets relatifs &agrave; l&#39;eau et aux eaux us&eacute;es sont disponibles dans leurs publications respectives au Registre.

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The Water System Upgrades project is being undertaken to address existing deficiencies in the water system and to meet the increased demands resulting from the proposed subdivision development. &nbsp;The first phase of the proposed subdivision will include 75 single family lots, a lot for an Elders&apos; Village (multi-family lot), the Telmexwawtexw Healing Center (Telmexw), and the Child and Family Services (CFS) Administration Building. &nbsp;The full future subdivision buildout will include an additional 189 single family lots, resulting in a total of 264 single family lots in the subdivision buildout.

&nbsp;

The timely delivery of water, wastewater, and subdivision infrastructure is critical to the success of two major BC Housing&ndash;funded developments already approved and being designed in Sts&apos;ailes:


	44-unit Healing Centre housing project supporting the Telmexw Awtexw Healing Centre, and
	49-unit community rental housing project serving Sts&apos;ailes&apos; restored jurisdiction of Child and Family Services, families returning home and Elders wishing to age in place.


&nbsp;

Both projects are scheduled for occupancy by January 2028 and are fully dependent on the completion of the supporting infrastructure.&nbsp; The infrastructure is also essential to the operations of the Snowoyelh Department, which administers Child and Family Services (CFS) under Sts&apos;ailes&apos; restored jurisdiction.

&nbsp;

The existing water supply, treatment, storage, and distribution system were assessed during the Feasibility Study to determine the required upgrades to support this proposed development, resulting in the following recommendations:


	Wells and Well Pumps: Install new well pumps to meet the Phase 1 Subdivision and Current Community maximum day demand. The development of a Well Protection Plan is recommended for the existing wells. The plan should include regular annual monitoring for hydrocarbon and turbidity parameters.
	Treatment Building: Construct an upgraded treatment facility equipped with a new chlorine disinfection system. Piping should be sized for the full Subdivision Buildout demands. Plan for future installation of cartridge filters if required.
	Reservoir Storage: Upgrade water reservoir storage to meet the water demands of the full Subdivision Buildout, requiring a minimum working volume of 1218 m3.
	Distribution System: Loop existing watermains to meet fire flow capacity of 60 L/s for residential buildings and 80 L/s for community buildings.


&nbsp;



&nbsp;

In&nbsp;order to ensure user safety by preventing service disruptions related to the condition of the suspension cables on the Pierre-Laporte Bridge and to extend the structure&#39;s useful life, the Ministry of Transport and Sustainable Mobility (MTMD) plans to replace the suspension cables, which will involve removing all 160 suspension cables attached to the anchor blocks of the main cables and replacing them.

The following work will be carried out above the channel:


	Installation of temporary work platforms at the bottom of each suspension cable;
	Installation of temporary supports or upgrading of existing supports for each suspension cable;
	Installation of temporary walkways along the suspension cables;
	Removal of existing suspension cables;
	Replacement of the anchor console at the base of the suspension cables;
	Removal and replacement of certain collars (at selected locations);
	Painting of collars left in place;
	Installation of new hangers;
	Removal of temporary hangers and work platforms at the bottom of the hangers;
	Touch-up painting of areas left without protective coating following the work;
	Replacement of handrails on the suspension cables;
	Installation of air ducts on the suspension cables of axes 14, 14&#39;, 56, and 56&#39;;
	Coating of the suspension cable;
	Dismantling of walkways along the cable.


Related work is also planned, such as:


	Installation of a dehumidification system for the suspension cables;
	Internal inspection of the suspension cables;
	Installation of a dehumidification system for the central chambers;
	Removal of temporary diagonals in the truss beams.


The work is scheduled to be carried out between August 2026 and December 2029 for the replacement of the suspension cables. The installation of the dehumidification systems will be completed in the fall of 2030.

properties.description_fr:
Dans le but d&#39;assurer la s&eacute;curit&eacute; des usagers en &eacute;vitant les ruptures de services en lien avec l&#39;&eacute;tat des suspentes du pont Pierre-Laporte, et de prolonger la dur&eacute;e de vie utile de l&#39;ouvrage, le minist&egrave;re des Transports et de la Mobilit&eacute; durable&nbsp;(MTMD) pr&eacute;voit r&eacute;aliser des travaux de remplacement des suspentes impliquant l&#39;enl&egrave;vement de tous les c&acirc;bles de suspente (160) s&#39;appuyant sur les collets des c&acirc;bles porteurs et leur remplacement.

Les activit&eacute;s suivantes se d&eacute;rouleront au-dessus du chenal :


	Installation de plateformes de travail temporaires au bas de chaque suspente;
	Installation de supports temporaires ou mise &agrave; niveau du support existant pour chacune de suspentes;
	Installation de passerelles temporaires le long des c&acirc;bles porteurs;
	Enl&egrave;vement de la suspente existante;
	Remplacement de la console d&#39;ancrage &agrave; la base des suspentes;
	Enl&egrave;vement et remise en place de certains collets (aux endroits s&eacute;lectionn&eacute;s);
	Peinturage des collets maintenus en place;
	Installation des nouvelles suspentes;
	Enl&egrave;vement de suspentes temporaires et de plateformes de travail au bas des suspentes;
	Peinturage par retouche des zones laiss&eacute;es sans rev&ecirc;tement de protection &agrave; la suite des travaux;
	Remplacement des mains courantes sur les c&acirc;bles porteurs;
	Installation des conduits d&#39;air aux suspentes des axes 14, 14&#39;, 56 et 56&#39;;
	Enrobage du c&acirc;ble porteur;
	D&eacute;mant&egrave;lement des passerelles le long du c&acirc;ble.


Des travaux connexes sont &eacute;galement pr&eacute;vus, tels que :


	L&#39;installation d&#39;un syst&egrave;me de d&eacute;shumidification des c&acirc;bles porteurs;
	L&#39;inspection interne des c&acirc;bles porteurs;
	L&#39;installation d&#39;un syst&egrave;me de d&eacute;shumidification des chambres centrales;
	L&#39;enl&egrave;vement des diagonales temporaires dans les poutres triangul&eacute;es.


La r&eacute;alisation des travaux est pr&eacute;vue entre ao&ucirc;t 2026 et d&eacute;cembre 2029 pour le remplacement des suspentes. Les travaux d&#39;installation des syst&egrave;mes de d&eacute;shumidification seront compl&eacute;t&eacute;s &agrave; l&#39;automne 2030.

P&ecirc;ches et Oc&eacute;ans Canada&nbsp;&ndash; La Direction des ports pour petits bateaux propose de reconstruire le brise-lames situ&eacute; &agrave; l&#39;entr&eacute;e du port pour petits bateaux de Cape&nbsp;John, dans le comt&eacute; de Pictou, en Nouvelle-&Eacute;cosse. Le brise-lames est une structure en enrochement constitu&eacute;e de couches de roches de noyau, de pierres de filtration et de pierres de protection, le tout dispos&eacute; en forme de L.&nbsp; La partie centrale de la structure mesure environ 140&nbsp;m de long, tandis que la section ext&eacute;rieure en forme de L a une longueur d&#39;environ 70&nbsp;m. Le projet propos&eacute; consiste &agrave; reconstruire les 75&nbsp;premiers m&egrave;tres de l&#39;&eacute;pi, qui s&#39;&eacute;tendent &agrave; partir du rivage et qui ont &eacute;t&eacute; les plus expos&eacute;s et les plus touch&eacute;s par les d&eacute;g&acirc;ts caus&eacute;s par la temp&ecirc;te.

&nbsp;

La reconstruction sera effectu&eacute;e &agrave; l&#39;aide d&#39;&eacute;quipement terrestre, comme des chargeuses, des excavatrices et des camions qui acc&eacute;deront au brise-lames depuis la zone de service situ&eacute;e &agrave; l&#39;arri&egrave;re de la structure. La zone de service sera &eacute;galement utilis&eacute;e comme site de transition pour le stockage de l&#39;&eacute;quipement et le d&eacute;p&ocirc;t des mat&eacute;riaux. Les quatre &agrave; six&nbsp;tonnes de pierres de protection qui sont en place actuellement seront enlev&eacute;es, r&eacute;cup&eacute;r&eacute;es et remises en place dans le cadre du nouvel ouvrage. Une autre couche de pierres de protection de quatre &agrave; six&nbsp;tonnes sera transport&eacute;e et plac&eacute;e sur la face c&ocirc;t&eacute; mer. Dans l&#39;ensemble, le brise-lames sera &eacute;largi d&#39;environ 1,8&nbsp;m et &eacute;lev&eacute; &agrave; une hauteur de 6,3&nbsp;m au-dessus du z&eacute;ro des cartes pour &ecirc;tre adapt&eacute; &agrave; la hausse pr&eacute;vue du niveau de la mer et emp&ecirc;cher tout d&eacute;bordement en cas de temp&ecirc;te. Il en r&eacute;sultera une augmentation d&#39;environ 133&nbsp;m2 de l&#39;empreinte au sol sous le niveau de la mar&eacute;e haute normale.

&nbsp;

Les travaux de construction devraient commencer &agrave; l&#39;hiver&nbsp;2026 et &ecirc;tre achev&eacute;s d&#39;ici la fin du mois de mars&nbsp;2027. Le lancement du projet d&eacute;pendra toutefois des priorit&eacute;s op&eacute;rationnelles de la Direction des ports pour petits bateaux de P&ecirc;ches et Oc&eacute;ans Canada et du financement que le programme est en mesure d&#39;obtenir, de m&ecirc;me que des processus d&#39;approbation r&eacute;glementaire. C&#39;est pourquoi les travaux pourraient &ecirc;tre retard&eacute;s. La port&eacute;e de l&#39;&eacute;tude d&#39;impact (soumise &agrave; la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact) reposera donc sur l&#39;ach&egrave;vement des travaux sur une p&eacute;riode de douze&nbsp;(12)&nbsp;mois commen&ccedil;ant dans les cinq&nbsp;(5)&nbsp;ann&eacute;es suivant la conclusion de l&#39;&eacute;tude.

&nbsp;

Le port pour petits bateaux de Cape&nbsp;John est actuellement un port de p&ecirc;che essentiel qui a &eacute;t&eacute; am&eacute;nag&eacute; pour servir l&#39;industrie de la p&ecirc;che dans la r&eacute;gion. Le port dispose actuellement de nombreuses infrastructures maritimes et demeure bien situ&eacute; et prot&eacute;g&eacute; pour soutenir les activit&eacute;s de p&ecirc;che locales. L&#39;objectif principal du projet propos&eacute; est de r&eacute;parer les infrastructures actuelles afin de maintenir la viabilit&eacute; du port pour la p&ecirc;che commerciale et d&#39;autres secteurs d&#39;activit&eacute; commerciale et r&eacute;cr&eacute;ative.

properties.description_en:
The Department of National Defence (DND) is proposing a project. As part of Canada&#39;s North American Aerospace Defense Command (NORAD) modernization plan, DND is investing in a new Northern Approaches Surveillance System (NASS) to significantly expand NORAD and the Canadian Armed Forces&#39; (CAF) situational awareness of objects approaching and entering Canadian airspace from the North. NASS will include the Arctic Over-the-Horizon Radar (A-OTHR) system that will provide early warning radar coverage and threat tracking.

The A-OTHR capability will be located in Southern Ontario and will extend NORAD and the CAF&#39;s situational awareness into the Canadian North and the North Atlantic.

Development at the site will focus on installation of receiving antennas. Land preparation will include flattening of land and removal of any obstructions that would impede the radar&#39;s signal. The receiving site will be installed on that portion of the property previously used for agriculture; there is no intent for development to occur within the boundary of the Minesing Wetlands

While specific infrastructure needs are being finalized, the A-OTHR system will require supporting infrastructure at each site:


	Fully equipped operational building;
	Physical security features;
	Maintenance and storage facility;
	Access road and parking; and
	Utilities (power, water, wastewater, stormwater, communications).


Additional information is available on the  Department of National Defence website.

properties.description_fr:
Le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale (MDN) propose un projet. Dans le cadre du plan canadien pour la modernisation du Commandement de la d&eacute;fense a&eacute;rospatiale de l&#39;Am&eacute;rique du Nord (NORAD), le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale investit dans un nouveau syst&egrave;me de surveillance des voies d&#39;approche du Nord (SSVAN) qui permettra au NORAD, et aux Forces arm&eacute;es canadiennes (FAC) d&#39;avoir une meilleure connaissance de la situation des objets qui s&#39;approchent de l&#39;espace a&eacute;rien canadien ou qui y p&eacute;n&egrave;trent &agrave; partir du Nord. Le SSVAN comprendra le syst&egrave;me de radar transhorizon qui fournira une couverture radar d&#39;alerte avanc&eacute;e et un suivi des menaces.

La capacit&eacute; de radar transhorizon sera situ&eacute;e dans le sud de l&#39;Ontario et permettra au NORAD et aux FAC d&#39;avoir une meilleure connaissance de la situation dans le Nord canadien et l&#39;Atlantique Nord.

Les travaux sur le site porteront principalement sur l&#39;installation d&#39;antennes de r&eacute;ception. La pr&eacute;paration du terrain comprendra le nivellement du sol et l&#39;enl&egrave;vement de tout obstacle susceptible de perturber le signal du radar. Le site de r&eacute;ception sera install&eacute; sur la partie de la propri&eacute;t&eacute; qui &eacute;tait auparavant utilis&eacute;e &agrave; des fins agricoles; il n&#39;est pas pr&eacute;vu que le d&eacute;veloppement se fasse &agrave; l&#39;int&eacute;rieur des limites des terres humides de Minesing.

Alors que les besoins en mati&egrave;re d&#39;infrastructure sont pr&eacute;cis&eacute;s, le syst&egrave;me A-OTHR n&eacute;cessitera une infrastructure de soutien sur chacun des sites:


	b&acirc;timent op&eacute;rationnel enti&egrave;rement &eacute;quip&eacute;;
	dispositifs de s&eacute;curit&eacute; physiques;
	installation d&#39;entretien et d&#39;entreposage;
	chemin d&#39;acc&egrave;s et stationnement; et
	services publics (&eacute;lectricit&eacute;, eau, eaux us&eacute;es, eaux pluviales, communications).


Des informations compl&eacute;mentaires sont disponibles sur  le site Web du minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale.

properties.description_en:
The physical activities for the project include the construction, installation, modification, maintenance, expansion, replacement, removal, and operation of the gas distribution system including mains, services, equipment, facilities and infrastructure required to provide natural gas distribution service to the existing residents and commercial buildings within Lubicon Lake Band Settlement.

The physical works within Lubicon Lake Band Settlement Lands include the installation of underground mains and services within the new residential subdivision identified in 1105220 DWG IFA R2. The gas mains will be installed by a combination of trenchless horizontal direction drilling, plowing and trenching with electrical and internet utilities. Additional tree clearing may be required in certain areas which will be identified during time of construction.

Note that this submission is for ATCO Gas only and not on behalf of any other utilities doing work within the same area.&nbsp;

The National Capital Commission (NCC) is acquiring an 8.9-hectare parcel of land located adjacent to Gatineau Park at 241 Boulevard de la Cit&eacute;-des-Jeunes in Gatineau (the &quot;Asticou Centre&quot;). The NCC proposes to undertake the demolition of nine (9) existing institutional buildings located on this parcel of land for the purpose of eventually re-naturalizing the site.

&nbsp;

This project supports several NCC policies and long-term land management objectives, particularly those related to the stewardship of federal lands, the protection and restoration of natural environments. This project advances NCC&#39;s broader goals for sustainable land use, landscape restoration, and the responsible planning of federal real property in the National Capital Region.

&nbsp;

The proposed project would take place on National Capital Commission (NCC) lands and approval under the Federal Land Use, Design and Transaction Approval (FLUDTA) process is required for the demolition of the existing buildings.

&nbsp;

The scope of work will include but may not be limited to the following: &nbsp;


	abatement of hazardous construction substances;
	removing the buildings;
	removing subsurface structures;
	backfilling the building footprints.


&nbsp;

The buildings that are scheduled for removal are Blocks&nbsp;100, 200, 300, 400, 600, 700, 800, 900, and 1000. These buildings are single storey structures with one (1) basement level. Block 500 and associated existing parking lots will be retained.

&nbsp;

All buildings have undergone detailed hazardous materials surveys. Hazardous construction materials will be removed and disposed of in accordance with provincial and federal requirements prior to building demolition. Subsurface structures, including foundations, basement slabs, underground utilities, and other buried infrastructure will also be removed. Soil quality has been assessed and determined to be non-hazardous.

&nbsp;

Heritage mitigation obligations associated with the project included detailed photographic documentation and a virtual tour of the buildings, and these were accepted by the Federal Heritage Buildings Review Office (FHBRO).

&nbsp;

The 8.9-hectare parcel of the Asticou Centre being acquired by the NCC is located immediately east of Gatineau Park&#39;s wooded lands. The overall Asticou Centre site contains or is adjacent to several ecological features, including a permanent fish-bearing water course, intermittent watercourses and associated wetlands. These hydrological features are outside the planned demolition work area, but measures will be implemented to prevent possible impacts from erosion and sediment.

&nbsp;

There are species of conservation interest in the general area such as wood thrush, bats, snapping and painted turtles. Measures to exclude these species from the demolition work area and buildings will be implemented prior to nesting seasons. An inspection by a qualified biologist will be completed after the installation of the exclusion measures but prior to the start of the work. Work will be required to stop in zones where species are identified pending instructions and recommendations from a qualified biologist.

&nbsp;

The work will rely on standard construction equipment, including excavators, loaders, haul trucks, and compaction equipment. The demolition is expected to begin in mid- to late 2026 with completion in Spring 2028. Best management practices will be applied for noise, dust, sediment control, and site security. No tree removals are anticipated, and a 90&nbsp;percent waste diversion target will be pursued through material recycling and recovery.

&nbsp;

Once cleared and long-term restoration is completed, the site will contribute to improved ecological connectivity with Gatineau Park. The parking lot (P-8) used by the public to access Gatineau Park is expected to remain accessible throughout this work.

properties.description_fr:
La Commission de la Capitale Nationale (CCN) fait l&#39;acquisition d&#39;une parcelle de terrain de 8,9 hectares situ&eacute;e &agrave; proximit&eacute; du parc de la Gatineau, au 241, boulevard de la Cit&eacute;-des-Jeunes, &agrave; Gatineau (le &laquo; Centre Asticou &raquo;). La CCN propose de proc&eacute;der &agrave; la d&eacute;molition de neuf (9) b&acirc;timents institutionnels existants situ&eacute;s sur ce terrain en vue de la naturalisation future du site.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Ce projet s&#39;inscrit dans le cadre de plusieurs politiques et objectifs &agrave; long terme de la CCN en mati&egrave;re de gestion des terres, notamment ceux li&eacute;s &agrave; la gestion des terres f&eacute;d&eacute;rales, &agrave; la protection et &agrave; la restauration des milieux naturels. Il contribue &agrave; la r&eacute;alisation des objectifs g&eacute;n&eacute;raux de la CCN en mati&egrave;re d&#39;utilisation durable des terres, de la restauration des paysages et de la planification responsable des biens immobiliers f&eacute;d&eacute;raux dans la r&eacute;gion de la capitale nationale.

&nbsp;

Le projet propos&eacute; serait r&eacute;alis&eacute; sur des terrains de la Commission de la capitale nationale (CCN) et l&#39;approbation dans le cadre du processus d&#39;approbation f&eacute;d&eacute;rale de l&#39;utilisation du sol, du design et des transactions immobili&egrave;res (AFUSDTI) est requise pour la d&eacute;molition des b&acirc;timents existants.

&nbsp;

L&#39;&eacute;tendue des travaux comprendra, sans s&#39;y limiter, les &eacute;l&eacute;ments suivants :&nbsp;&nbsp;


	l&#39;&eacute;limination des substances de construction dangereuses;
	la d&eacute;molition des b&acirc;timents;
	la d&eacute;molition des structures souterraines;
	remblayage des empreintes des b&acirc;timents.


&nbsp;

Les b&acirc;timents dont la d&eacute;molition est pr&eacute;vue sont les blocs 100, 200, 300, 400, 600, 700, 800, 900 et 1000. Il s&#39;agit de structures d&#39;un &eacute;tage avec un (1) niveau de sous-sol. Le bloc 500 et parkings existants seront conserv&eacute;s.

&nbsp;

Tous les b&acirc;timents ont fait l&#39;objet d&#39;&eacute;tudes approfondies visant &agrave; recenser les mat&eacute;riaux de construction dangereux. Les mat&eacute;riaux de construction dangereux seront retir&eacute;s et &eacute;limin&eacute;s conform&eacute;ment aux exigences provinciales et f&eacute;d&eacute;rales avant la d&eacute;molition des b&acirc;timents. Les structures souterraines, notamment les fondations, les dalles de sous-sol, les r&eacute;seaux souterrains et autres infrastructures enfouies, seront &eacute;galement retir&eacute;es. La qualit&eacute; du sol a &eacute;t&eacute; &eacute;valu&eacute;e et jug&eacute;e non dangereuse.

&nbsp;

Les obligations en mati&egrave;re de protection du patrimoine associ&eacute;es au projet comprenaient une documentation photographique d&eacute;taill&eacute;e et une visite virtuelle des b&acirc;timents, lesquelles ont &eacute;t&eacute; accept&eacute;es par le Bureau d&#39;examen des &eacute;difices f&eacute;d&eacute;raux du patrimoine (BE&Eacute;FP).

&nbsp;

La parcelle de 8,9 hectares du Centre Asticou est situ&eacute;e imm&eacute;diatement &agrave; l&#39;est des terres bois&eacute;es du parc de la Gatineau. L&#39;ensemble du site du Centre Asticou contient ou est adjacent &agrave; plusieurs &eacute;l&eacute;ments &eacute;cologiques, notamment un cours d&#39;eau a r&eacute;gime permanent, des cours d&#39;eau intermittents et des zones humides. Ces &eacute;l&eacute;ments hydrologiques se trouvent en dehors de la zone pr&eacute;vue pour les travaux de d&eacute;molition, mais des mesures seront mises en &oelig;uvre pour pr&eacute;venir les impacts potentiels li&eacute;s &agrave; l&#39;&eacute;rosion et aux s&eacute;diments.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

La r&eacute;gion abrite des esp&egrave;ces pr&eacute;sentant un int&eacute;r&ecirc;t pour la conservation, telles que la grive des bois, les chauves-souris, ainsi que la tortue serpentine et la tortue peinte. Des mesures visant &agrave; &eacute;loigner ces esp&egrave;ces de la zone des travaux de d&eacute;molition et des b&acirc;timents seront mises en place avant le d&eacute;but des saisons de nidification. Une inspection men&eacute;e par un biologiste qualifi&eacute; sera effectu&eacute;e apr&egrave;s l&#39;installation des mesures d&#39;&eacute;loignement, mais avant le d&eacute;but des travaux. Les travaux devront &ecirc;tre interrompus dans les zones o&ugrave; des esp&egrave;ces auront &eacute;t&eacute; identifi&eacute;es, dans l&#39;attente des instructions et des recommandations d&#39;un biologiste qualifi&eacute;.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Les travaux feront appel &agrave; de l&#39;&eacute;quipement de construction standard, notamment des pelles m&eacute;caniques, des chargeuses, des camions de transport et de compactage. La d&eacute;molition devrait d&eacute;buter entre le milieu et la fin de l&#39;ann&eacute;e 2026 et s&#39;achever au printemps 2028. Les meilleures pratiques de gestion seront appliqu&eacute;es en mati&egrave;re de bruit, de poussi&egrave;re, de contr&ocirc;le des s&eacute;diments et de s&eacute;curit&eacute; du site. Aucun abattage d&#39;arbres n&#39;est pr&eacute;vu, et un objectif de d&eacute;tournement des d&eacute;chets de 90 % sera vis&eacute; gr&acirc;ce au recyclage et &agrave; la valorisation des mat&eacute;riaux.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Une fois le site d&eacute;blay&eacute; et la restauration &agrave; long terme achev&eacute;e, celui-ci contribuera &agrave; am&eacute;liorer la connectivit&eacute; &eacute;cologique avec le parc de la Gatineau. Le parking (P-8) utilis&eacute; par le public pour acc&eacute;der au parc de la Gatineau devrait rester accessible pendant toute la dur&eacute;e des travaux.&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The site located at 4420 West Hunt Club is a Greenbelt heritage farmstead within the National Capital Commission&#39;s (NCC) agricultural real estate portfolio. Today, the property is leased by Indigenous Experiences, a long-term tenant with the mission of sharing land, stories, and food from an Indigenous perspective. The site has become a thriving Indigenous cultural agritourism destination in the National Capital Region. 

&nbsp;

The 164-acre property currently has 4 main buildings on site: 1) the Riding Arena, 2) the Mamawii Lodge, 3) the Heritage Barn, and 4) the Farmhouse. All of these buildings are currently used by the tenant as part of their programming and operations. The Mamawii Lodge is a 442 m2 wood framed building with medal cladding that was built in the 1970s and was retrofit as a Banquet Hall in 2001. Today, the lodge is used for the Farm&#39;s programming and as an office building.

&nbsp;

The proposed project involves constructing a single-storey 499 m2 addition to the Mamawii Lodge building. This expansion will function as the property&#39;s main meeting area for visitors and will offer cultural exhibits, a larger marketplace and store, space for workshops and arts and crafts, office space for staff, and improved washrooms facilities. 

&nbsp;

The project also includes electrical upgrades that would supply the Lodge expansion and permit the construction of electric vehicle (EV) charging stations in the existing parking lot. The existing overhead single phase hydro service will be replaced with a new overhead 3 phase distribution. Additionally, a pad-mounted transformer will be installed next to the parking lot and underground distribution will supply the Lodge expansion and EV chargers. Lastly, a fire hydrant will be installed along with 4 below-ground holding tanks for fire suppression as well as one wastewater holding tank.

&nbsp;

Construction is planned to begin in May 2026 and will be completed by December 2026. No impacts to the Farm&#39;s programming or site closures are expected as a result of the construction. Additionally, no tree removals are anticipated as part of this project, but any tree removals will be compensated on-site following an approved compensation ratio.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

This project is proposed on lands owned by the NCC and is subject to a federal land use, design and transaction approval under the National Capital Act. The NCC must determine whether the proposed project is likely to cause significant adverse environmental effects in compliance with section 81-91 of the Impact Assessment Act.

properties.description_fr:
Le site situ&eacute; au 4420 West Hunt Club est une ferme patrimoniale de la Ceinture de verdure faisant partie du portefeuille immobilier agricole de la Commission de la capitale nationale (CCN). Aujourd&#39;hui, la propri&eacute;t&eacute; est lou&eacute;e par Indigenous Experiences, un locataire &agrave; long terme dont la mission est de partager la terre, les histoires et la nourriture d&#39;un point de vue autochtone. Le site est devenu une destination d&#39;agrotourisme culturel autochtone florissante dans la r&eacute;gion de la capitale nationale. 

&nbsp;

La propri&eacute;t&eacute; de 164 acres compte actuellement 4 b&acirc;timents principaux sur le site : 1) le man&egrave;ge, 2) le pavillon Mamawii, 3) la grange patrimoniale et 4) la maison. Tous ces b&acirc;timents sont actuellement utilis&eacute;s par le locataire dans le cadre de ses programmes et de ses activit&eacute;s. Le pavillon Mamawii est un b&acirc;timent &agrave; charpente en bois de 442 m2 avec un rev&ecirc;tement en t&ocirc;le, construit dans les ann&eacute;es 1970 et r&eacute;am&eacute;nag&eacute; en salle de banquet en 2001. Aujourd&#39;hui, le pavillon est utilis&eacute; pour la programmation de la ferme et sert de b&acirc;timent administratif.

&nbsp;

Le projet propos&eacute; consiste &agrave; construire une extension de 499 m2 sur un seul &eacute;tage du pavillon Mamawii. Cette extension servira de principal espace de rencontre de la propri&eacute;t&eacute; pour les visiteurs et proposera des expositions culturelles, un march&eacute; et une boutique plus spacieux, des espaces pour des ateliers et des activit&eacute;s artistiques et artisanales, des bureaux pour le personnel, ainsi que des sanitaires am&eacute;lior&eacute;s. 

&nbsp;

Le projet comprend &eacute;galement des travaux de modernisation &eacute;lectrique destin&eacute;s &agrave; alimenter l&#39;extension du pavillon Mamawii et &agrave; permettre la construction de bornes de recharge pour v&eacute;hicules &eacute;lectriques (VE) dans le stationnement existant. Le r&eacute;seau &eacute;lectrique a&eacute;rien monophas&eacute; existant sera remplac&eacute; par un nouveau r&eacute;seau de distribution a&eacute;rien triphas&eacute;. De plus, un transformateur sur socle sera install&eacute; &agrave; c&ocirc;t&eacute; du stationnement et un r&eacute;seau de distribution souterrain alimentera l&#39;extension du pavillon Mamawii et les bornes de recharge pour VE. Enfin, une borne d&#39;incendie sera install&eacute;e, ainsi que quatre r&eacute;servoirs souterrains destin&eacute;s &agrave; alimenter la borne et un r&eacute;servoir de stockage des eaux us&eacute;es.

&nbsp;

Le d&eacute;but des travaux est pr&eacute;vu en mai 2026 et leur ach&egrave;vement en d&eacute;cembre 2026. Aucun impact sur la programmation de la Ferme ni de fermeture du site ne sont attendus en raison des travaux. De plus, aucun abattage d&#39;arbres n&#39;est pr&eacute;vu dans le cadre de ce projet, mais tout abattage sera compens&eacute; sur place selon un ratio de compensation approuv&eacute;.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Ce projet est propos&eacute; sur des terrains appartenant &agrave; la CCN et est assujetti &agrave; une approbation f&eacute;d&eacute;rale de l&#39;utilisation du sol, du design et des transactions immobili&egrave;res en vertu de la Loi sur la capitale nationale. La CCN doit d&eacute;terminer si le projet propos&eacute; est susceptible d&#39;entra&icirc;ner des effets n&eacute;gatifs importants sur l&#39;environnement, conform&eacute;ment aux articles 81 &agrave; 91 de la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation des impacts.

Pont Honor&eacute;-Mercier, am&eacute;nagement espace vert.

Projet&nbsp;: HMP0015

Le pont Honor&eacute;-Mercier (le &laquo; pont &raquo; a &eacute;t&eacute; construit entre 1932 et 1934, sous la responsabilit&eacute; de la Corporation du Pont de lac Saint-Louis. La responsabilit&eacute; du pont est transf&eacute;r&eacute;e au gouvernement du Qu&eacute;bec en 1942. Par ailleurs, en 1932, le gouvernement du Canada prend l&#39;engagement de prioriser les travailleurs autochtones qualifi&eacute;s pour l&#39;entretien et la r&eacute;novation du pont.

Entre 1958 et 1959, dans le cadre de la construction de la Voie maritime, l&#39;Administration de la Voie maritime du Saint-Laurent (AVMSL) a rehauss&eacute; et prolong&eacute; la partie Sud du pont afin de permettre le passage des navires et une section du pont est &eacute;largie &agrave; quatre voies. Ainsi, un partage de responsabilit&eacute;s est convenu entre les gouvernements provincial et f&eacute;d&eacute;ral. Depuis 1998, les sections 1 &agrave; 4 sont sous la juridiction de Les Ponts Jacques Cartier et Champlain Incorpor&eacute;e (PJCCI). 

Le gouvernement du Canada travaille &agrave; faire avancer la r&eacute;conciliation et &agrave; renouveler la relation avec les Autochtones, une relation fond&eacute;e sur la reconnaissance, le respect, la coop&eacute;ration et le partenariat. Ainsi, le pr&eacute;sent projet, d&eacute;velopp&eacute; en partenariat avec le Conseil Mohawk de Kahnaw&agrave;:ke (MCK), vise notamment&nbsp;:


	Renouveler les relations avec la communaut&eacute; de Kahnaw&agrave;:ke par le biais de la valorisation de la culture et l&#39;histoire Mohawk;
	Revitaliser le terrain vacant &agrave; l&#39;approche sud-est du pont en cr&eacute;ant un espace de rassemblement et une porte d&#39;entr&eacute;e de la ville de Kahnaw&agrave;:ke.


Plus sp&eacute;cifiquement, les travaux comprennent principalement, sans toutefois s&#39;y limiter&nbsp;:


	Am&eacute;nager un parcours lin&eacute;aire &agrave; l&#39;approche sud-est du pont, sur le terrain situ&eacute; entre Old Malone Road et la bretelle de la route 132 ouest vers la route 138 ouest;
	Reforester ou reboiser le terrain vacant;
	Am&eacute;nager des espaces de rassemblement et de rencontres;
	Am&eacute;nager des sentiers et acc&egrave;s pi&eacute;tonnier;
	Am&eacute;nager des zones de stationnement permanent et occasionnel;
	Mettre en valeur la culture et l&#39;histoire Mohawk par l&#39;int&eacute;gration d&#39;&eacute;l&eacute;ments d&#39;&oelig;uvres d&#39;art dans l&#39;am&eacute;nagement;
	Installer un nouvel &eacute;clairage pour la s&eacute;curit&eacute; et la mise en valeur de l&#39;am&eacute;nagement;
	G&eacute;rer les eaux de pluies par la bior&eacute;tention.


Durant les travaux qui seront effectu&eacute;s &agrave; compter du printemps 2026 et qui prendront fin en 2027, la circulation sera maintenue sur Old Malone Road, la route 132 et sur la bretelle de la route 132 ouest vers la route 138 ouest. Des fermetures partielles et ponctuelles seront toutefois n&eacute;cessaires pour certains travaux critiques tels que la construction des stationnements, des acc&egrave;s et des plantations en bordure de Old Malone Road.

properties.description_en:
Projects that were undergoing a comprehensive study at the time the provisions of the Canadian Environmental Assessment Act, 2012 came into force will continue to follow the requirements of the former Act. Under the former Act, the Canadian Environmental Assessment Agency is responsible for conducting the comprehensive study of this project.

KSM Mining Inc. proposes to develop a gold, copper, silver, and molybdenum mine in the Kerr, Sulphurets and Mitchell Creek watersheds. The project is located approximately 65 km northwest of Stewart, BC. The Project is expected to have an average ore extraction rate of approximately 130&nbsp;000 tonnes per day over an anticipated 52-year mine life. Ore would be mined by a combination of open pit and underground mining methods from four mineral deposits: the Mitchell, Sulphurets, Kerr, and Iron Cap deposits. Waste rock storage dumps, an ore grinding circuit, water storage facility, water treatment plant, selenium treatment plant, several small hydroelectric projects, diversion tunnels, access roads, camp facilities, explosives factory and magazine, and supporting infrastructure would also be located at the Mine Site. A pair of 23 kilometer long tunnels would allow the transportation of crushed ore to a concentrator plant and tailings management facility located in the Treaty and Teigen Creek drainages of the Bell-Irving River. Electricity would be provided to the project via tunnel and transmission line which would connect to the Northwest Transmission Line. Two separate access roads, the Treaty Creek access road and the Coulter Creek access road, would provide access for the trucking of supplies to the mine and ore concentrate to Highway 37.

&nbsp;

Please note that the proponent was formerly known as the Seabridge Gold Inc.&nbsp;

The Department of National Defence (DND) is proposing a project. The 2026 Pavement Program Repair/Recap is being completed to repair and recapitalize several paved surfaces throughout Canadian Forces Base (CFB) Kingston. This work will generally include, but is not limited to: partial and full removal and replacement of pavement and associated sidewalks, curbs, gutters, catch basins, drainage improvements, sewer cleaning, as well as granular shoulders and riprap spillways at the following locations:


	Lundy&#39;s Lane and select adjoining roads;
	Atlantic Avenue and Blue Bell Lane;
	Princess Royal Avenue and associated parking lots;
	Select unnamed roadways and lots between Princess Mary and Canal Du Nord;
	The eastern portion of Satellite Avenue; and
	The parking lots at MH36 (east of Moro Street).


Some vegetation removal may be required to facilitate this work, and limited quantities of excess soils are expected to be generated during excavation activities. Once work is completed, all disturbed areas will be reinstated. Work is expected to start Summer 2026 and end in the Fall of 2027.

properties.description_fr:
Le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale (MDN) propose un projet. Le programme de r&eacute;paration et de r&eacute;fection des chauss&eacute;es 2026 est en cours de r&eacute;alisation afin de r&eacute;parer et de remettre en &eacute;tat plusieurs surfaces rev&ecirc;tues dans l&#39;ensemble de la base des Forces canadiennes (BFC) Kingston. Ces travaux comprendront notamment : l&#39;enl&egrave;vement partiel ou total et le remplacement des chauss&eacute;es ainsi que des trottoirs, des bordures, des caniveaux et des puisards associ&eacute;s; l&#39;am&eacute;lioration du drainage; le nettoyage des &eacute;gouts; ainsi que la mise en place d&#39;accotements granulaires et de d&eacute;versoirs en enrochement aux emplacements suivants :


	All&eacute;e Lundy et certaines routes adjacentes;
	Avenue Atlantic et all&eacute;e Blue Bell;
	Avenue Princess Royal et les stationnements associ&eacute;s;
	Certaines routes et certains terrains sans nom entre Princess Mary et Canal Du Nord;
	La partie est de l&#39;avenue Satellite;
	Les stationnements du MH36 (&agrave; l&#39;est de la rue Moro).


Il pourrait &ecirc;tre n&eacute;cessaire de proc&eacute;der &agrave; quelques travaux de d&eacute;broussaillage pour faciliter ces travaux, et les travaux d&#39;excavation devraient g&eacute;n&eacute;rer une quantit&eacute; limit&eacute;e de d&eacute;blais. Une fois les travaux termin&eacute;s, toutes les zones perturb&eacute;es seront remises en &eacute;tat. Les travaux devraient commencer &agrave; l&#39;&eacute;t&eacute; 2026 et s&#39;achever &agrave; l&#39;automne 2027.

properties.description_en:
Woodland Cree Nation is proposing to construct a Waste Transfer Station.&nbsp;The transfer station will receive the community&#39;s household waste including&nbsp;large items, recyclables, residential renovation waste, tires, household hazardous wastes, electronics, whitegoods, propane tanks,&nbsp;and derelict vehicles. The waste will be hauled from the new transfer station by Woodland Cree to landfills operated by Peace River&nbsp;Waste Management Company.&nbsp;The transfer station will have a 30-year service life with provision for future&nbsp;expansion to accommodate future growth.&nbsp;

The Transfer Station is located in a previously disturbed area and no vegetation clearing is required to initiate the Project. The Project will involve the construction of an elevated platform for disposal of residential waste, a designated household hazardous waste collection site with appropriate environmental protections, envisioned as a set of&nbsp;modified &quot;sea-can&quot; shipping containers equipped with secondary containment, holding tanks, and collection and storage areas&nbsp;for safe temporary storage of household hazardous waste, and a recyclables collection and sorting area.&nbsp;

Typical waste generation is expected for completion of this project and will not include hazardous waste. All waste produced will&nbsp;be disposed of at an appropriate off-site waste disposal facility.&nbsp;Fill materials will be imported for construction. The source for the fill material is unknown at this time. Technical specifications indicating the soil type, clean soil source, and&nbsp;testing will be obtained prior to use. Testing will primarily be geotechnical, but chemistry testing may be included to ensure&nbsp;there is no contamination.&nbsp;

Due to previous disturbance it is unlikely Species at Risk will be impacted. A wildlife sweep will be completed by qualified professionals prior to construction.&nbsp;

The Black Creek Sanitary Trunk Sewer (Phase 1) project, located in Toronto, Ontario, is a major infrastructure initiative designed to expand wastewater servicing capacity in the Black Creek sewershed. Phase 1 includes the construction of the Keele Relief Trunk Sewer (12.9 km), Jane Relief Sewer (3.9 km), five flow diversion structures, real-time monitoring and control systems, and a Combined Sewer Overflow (CSO) Storage Tunnel (0.5 km). These upgrades will form a &quot;twinned&quot; trunk sewer system with the existing Black Creek Sanitary Trunk Sewer, improving conveyance and reducing overflow events. Planning is underway, with construction scheduled from December 2026 to September 2031. The project will enable an estimated 60,500 additional housing units and support population growth of 130,400 residents and 65,700 jobs, particularly in the Downsview area. Outcomes include enhanced wastewater capacity, reduced flooding and CSO events, and support for long-term housing and employment growth beyond 2051. This initiative is critical to Toronto&#39;s urban intensification strategy and aligns with the city&#39;s Official Plan and Housing Action Plan.

A small component of the project (measuring 912.58 m) is occuring on federal land in Downsview Park.&nbsp;


	The section of the project occurring on Downsview Park is located on the north western section of Downsview Park.
	The project area is situated within a highly modified urban environment and included a permanent engineered surface waterbody (lake).
	The project area appears to have been previously disturbed.
	The location consists of landscaped vegetation and roughly 7 m from a stormwater pond within Downsview Park.&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Le projet d&#39;&eacute;gout sanitaire principal de Black Creek (phase 1), situ&eacute; &agrave; Toronto, en Ontario, est un projet d&#39;infrastructure majeur visant &agrave; augmenter la capacit&eacute; de traitement des eaux us&eacute;es dans le bassin versant de Black Creek. La phase 1 comprend la construction du collecteur principal de d&eacute;rivation Keele (12,9 km), du collecteur secondaire de d&eacute;rivation Jane (3,9 km), de cinq structures de d&eacute;rivation de d&eacute;bit, de syst&egrave;mes de surveillance et de contr&ocirc;le en temps r&eacute;el et d&#39;un tunnel de stockage des d&eacute;bordements d&#39;&eacute;gouts unitaires (0,5 km). Ces am&eacute;liorations permettront de cr&eacute;er un r&eacute;seau d&#39;&eacute;gouts collecteurs &laquo; jumel&eacute; &raquo; avec l&#39;&eacute;gout collecteur sanitaire existant de Black Creek, ce qui am&eacute;liorera le transport des eaux us&eacute;es et r&eacute;duira les d&eacute;bordements. La planification est en cours, la construction &eacute;tant pr&eacute;vue de d&eacute;cembre 2026 &agrave; septembre 2031. Le projet permettra la construction d&#39;environ 60 500 unit&eacute;s de logement suppl&eacute;mentaires et soutiendra la croissance d&eacute;mographique de 130 400 habitants et la cr&eacute;ation de 65 700 emplois, en particulier dans la r&eacute;gion de Downsview. Les r&eacute;sultats attendus comprennent une capacit&eacute; accrue du traitement des eaux us&eacute;es, une r&eacute;duction des inondations et des d&eacute;bordements d&#39;&eacute;gouts unitaires, ainsi qu&#39;un soutien &agrave; la croissance &agrave; long terme du logement et de l&#39;emploi au-del&agrave; de 2051. Cette initiative est essentielle &agrave; la strat&eacute;gie d&#39;intensification urbaine de Toronto et s&#39;inscrit dans le cadre du plan officiel et du plan d&#39;action pour le logement de la ville.&nbsp;

Une partie du projet (d&#39;une longueur de 912,58 m) se d&eacute;roule sur un terrain f&eacute;d&eacute;ral situ&eacute; dans le parc Downsview.&nbsp;


	La partie du projet qui se d&eacute;roule dans le parc Downsview est situ&eacute;e dans la partie nord-ouest du parc.
	La zone du projet est situ&eacute;e dans un environnement urbain fortement modifi&eacute; et comprend un plan d&#39;eau artificiel permanent (un lac).
	La zone du projet semblait avoir d&eacute;j&agrave; &eacute;t&eacute; perturb&eacute;e.
	Le site comprend une v&eacute;g&eacute;tation paysag&egrave;re et se trouve &agrave; environ 7 m d&#39;un bassin d&#39;eaux pluviales dans le parc Downsview.&nbsp;

Le projet de parc solaire &agrave; l&#39;&eacute;chelle industrielle de la bande d&#39;Upper Nicola et de l&#39;Okanagan Nation Alliance devrait &ecirc;tre un projet solaire photovolta&iuml;que (PV) de 24 MWdc/15 MWac connect&eacute; au r&eacute;seau de BC Hydro. Il sera situ&eacute; sur le c&ocirc;t&eacute; ouest du lot 99 de la r&eacute;serve de la bande sup&eacute;rieure de Nicola IR#1, couvrant 38,83 hectares (95,95 acres) de terres actuellement non am&eacute;nag&eacute;es, l&eacute;g&egrave;rement ondul&eacute;es et pr&eacute;sentant une v&eacute;g&eacute;tation basse compos&eacute;e principalement d&#39;arbustes et de gramin&eacute;es basses. L&#39;adresse du site sera le 6905 Double Gate Drive, Douglas, BC.

La dur&eacute;e de vie du projet est estim&eacute;e &agrave; 40 ans. Le site, une fois achev&eacute; et mis en service, comprendra 37 296 modules, soit environ 20 000 panneaux photovolta&iuml;ques mont&eacute;s au sol, ainsi que 111 onduleurs &agrave; cha&icirc;nes, six transformateurs &eacute;lectriques de 3 MVA, une route d&#39;acc&egrave;s en gravier d&#39;environ 4,82 km (3 miles) de 6 m (19,7 pieds) de large, une cl&ocirc;ture de 2,13 m&egrave;tres (7 pieds) de haut avec des fils barbel&eacute;s, des portes verrouillables permettant l&#39;acc&egrave;s sur le site. Une courte ligne de distribution de 1,546 km et une petite sous-station seront utilis&eacute;es pour l&#39;interconnexion

&nbsp;

Depuis 1917, le pont de Qu&eacute;bec relie L&eacute;vis et la ville de Qu&eacute;bec. Il permet la travers&eacute;e du fleuve St-Laurent pour de multiples modes de transport&nbsp;: le transport actif (pi&eacute;tons et cyclistes), le transport automobile et le transport ferroviaire. Depuis novembre 2024, la soci&eacute;t&eacute; d&#39;&eacute;tat f&eacute;d&eacute;rale, Les Ponts Jacques Cartier et Champlain Incorpor&eacute;e (PJCCI) est propri&eacute;taire superficiaire de la structure du pont de Qu&eacute;bec alors que le Canadien National (CN) est propri&eacute;taire superficiaire du tablier ferroviaire, et le minist&egrave;re des Transports et de la Mobilit&eacute; durable du Qu&eacute;bec (MTMD) est responsable du tablier routier incluant le trottoir.

Le Contrat 62778 a pour objectif la r&eacute;alisation de travaux de nettoyage, de pr&eacute;paration, de renforcement et de peinturage d&#39;&eacute;l&eacute;ments d&#39;acier sur le c&ocirc;t&eacute; sud du pont de Qu&eacute;bec. Plus sp&eacute;cifiquement, les travaux comprennent principalement, sans s&#39;y limiter :


	Le renforcement d&#39;&eacute;l&eacute;ments d&#39;acier ainsi que le nettoyage et la peinture de certains contreventements sous le tablier de la trav&eacute;e 3 cantilever ouest et du portique d&#39;entr&eacute;e;
	La r&eacute;paration d&#39;un gousset de la trav&eacute;e 2 ancr&eacute;e ouest ;
	L&#39;enl&egrave;vement du syst&egrave;me&nbsp;de mise en lumi&egrave;re du portique d&#39;entr&eacute;e de la trav&eacute;e 2 ancr&eacute;e ouest;
	Les travaux d&eacute;buteront en 2026 et seront compl&eacute;t&eacute;s au 1er d&eacute;cembre 2026.


&nbsp;

Ces travaux n&eacute;cessiteront diverses fermetures &agrave; la circulation afin de permettre leur r&eacute;alisation. Les entraves &agrave; la circulation pourront inclure des fermetures compl&egrave;tes ou partielles, de jour ou de nuit, de fins de semaine ou de longue dur&eacute;e. Des chemins de d&eacute;tour seront pr&eacute;vus pour les fermetures compl&egrave;tes, le cas &eacute;ch&eacute;ant, en collaboration avec le MTMD.

Le projet pr&eacute;voit un ensemble de mesures de protection de l&#39;environnement pour ce type de travaux, notamment en lien avec la pr&eacute;sence potentielle de faucons p&egrave;lerins et de leurs nids &agrave; proximit&eacute; des zones de travail ainsi que la gestion des m&eacute;thodes de construction afin de contr&ocirc;ler les probl&eacute;matiques de contamination.bon endroit pour &eacute;voqu&eacute; cet &eacute;l&eacute;ment

Le projet propos&eacute; consiste &agrave; am&eacute;liorer le port pour petits bateaux de Grand &Eacute;tang en rempla&ccedil;ant un quai et un quai flottant par un nouvel &eacute;pi de quai et un quai longitudinal. Le projet pr&eacute;voit &eacute;galement le dragage d&#39;une partie du bassin du port et la construction de nouveaux dispositifs de protection des berges.

&nbsp;

Le quai existant est un ouvrage en pieux de bois qui sera enti&egrave;rement d&eacute;moli. La structure a d&eacute;pass&eacute; la fin de sa dur&eacute;e de vie utile et s&#39;est d&eacute;t&eacute;rior&eacute;e au point o&ugrave; elle est d&eacute;sormais soumise &agrave; des restrictions de charge et finira par &ecirc;tre barricad&eacute;e. Le projet vise &eacute;galement l&#39;enl&egrave;vement d&#39;un quai flottant adjacent et d&#39;un petit b&acirc;timent &agrave; ossature de bois situ&eacute; &agrave; c&ocirc;t&eacute; du nouveau quai.

&nbsp;

La nouvelle structure comprendra un nouvel &eacute;pi de quai et un nouveau quai longitudinal. Les travaux seront r&eacute;alis&eacute;s selon le m&ecirc;me trac&eacute; que le quai existant, mais seront d&eacute;cal&eacute;s d&#39;environ 25 m&egrave;tres vers le nord afin d&#39;agrandir le bassin et de permettre la navigation de bateaux de p&ecirc;che conventionnels de plus grande taille. Le nouveau quai longitudinal sera construit perpendiculairement au nouvel &eacute;pi de quai et aura une longueur approximative de 43 m. Les deux quais seront de construction similaire, avec des fondations sur pieux en tuyau d&#39;acier, des semelles sur pieux et tabliers en b&eacute;ton, ainsi que des syst&egrave;mes de d&eacute;fenses compos&eacute;s de pieux de bois et de rev&ecirc;tement. Les nouveaux quais seront construits &agrave; une altitude de 3,65 m au-dessus du z&eacute;ro des cartes et le quai longitudinal s&#39;abaissera progressivement pour rejoindre le niveau de la voie d&#39;acc&egrave;s publique adjacente.

&nbsp;

Des travaux de dragage seront n&eacute;cessaires dans plusieurs secteurs du port afin d&#39;&eacute;largir le bassin et d&#39;&eacute;liminer certaines zones peu profondes de mani&egrave;re &agrave; garantir une navigation et une man&oelig;uvrabilit&eacute; plus s&eacute;curitaires dans le port. Le volume de dragage est estim&eacute; &agrave; 3 500 m&egrave;tres cubes mesure en place (MCMP) et la profondeur de dragage pr&eacute;vue est de 2,3 m sous le z&eacute;ro des cartes. Tous les d&eacute;blais de dragage seront charg&eacute;s et transport&eacute;s hors site pour &ecirc;tre &eacute;limin&eacute;s &agrave; terre sur un site approuv&eacute; de gestion de mati&egrave;res dragu&eacute;es.

&nbsp;

Le projet comprendra &eacute;galement la construction d&#39;ouvrages de protection du rivage au bout du quai longitudinal, qui seront reli&eacute;s au rev&ecirc;tement de protection des berges d&eacute;j&agrave; en place sur la propri&eacute;t&eacute; de l&#39;administration portuaire. Un nouveau rev&ecirc;tement rocheux de 25 m de long avec des pentes lat&eacute;rales (horizontales/verticales) de 2:1 sera construit &agrave; l&#39;aide d&#39;un m&eacute;lange de pierres filtrantes et de pierres de protection r&eacute;cup&eacute;r&eacute;es et import&eacute;es.

&nbsp;

Les travaux seront effectu&eacute;s &agrave; l&#39;aide d&#39;&eacute;quipement lourd comme des excavatrices, des grues, des chargeuses frontales et des camions travaillant &agrave; partir des structures existantes ou de plateformes de travail temporaires. Si des mat&eacute;riaux doivent &ecirc;tre stock&eacute;s temporairement, la zone de stockage sera situ&eacute;e dans le port pour petits bateaux et g&eacute;r&eacute;e par l&#39;administration portuaire afin d&#39;&eacute;viter toute perturbation des activit&eacute;s de p&ecirc;che.

&nbsp;

Les travaux de construction devraient commencer &agrave; l&#39;automne 2025 et s&#39;achever &agrave; la fin du mois de mars 2027. Cependant, le lancement du projet d&eacute;pend des priorit&eacute;s op&eacute;rationnelles et du financement obtenu par la Direction des ports pour petits bateaux de P&ecirc;ches et Oc&eacute;ans Canada, ainsi que de l&#39;ach&egrave;vement des processus d&#39;approbation r&eacute;glementaire. Les travaux pourraient donc &ecirc;tre retard&eacute;s. La port&eacute;e de l&#39;&eacute;tude d&#39;impact (soumise &agrave; la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact) reposera donc sur l&#39;ach&egrave;vement des travaux sur une p&eacute;riode de douze (12) mois commen&ccedil;ant dans les cinq (5) ann&eacute;es suivant la conclusion de l&#39;&eacute;tude.

&nbsp;

Le port pour petits bateaux de Grand &Eacute;tang est actuellement un port de p&ecirc;che essentiel qui a &eacute;t&eacute; am&eacute;nag&eacute; pour servir l&#39;industrie de la p&ecirc;che dans la r&eacute;gion. Le port dispose actuellement de nombreuses infrastructures maritimes et demeure bien situ&eacute; et prot&eacute;g&eacute; pour soutenir la p&ecirc;che locale et les activit&eacute;s des navires de passage. L&#39;objectif principal du projet propos&eacute; est de remplacer les infrastructures actuelles afin de maintenir la viabilit&eacute; du port pour la p&ecirc;che commerciale et les autres secteurs d&#39;activit&eacute; commerciale et r&eacute;cr&eacute;ative.

properties.description_en:
In Lebanon, the target communities in the informal settlements rely on construction of temporary latrines and the desludging of latrine pits. Oxfam will construct temporary latrines to ensure safe access for women and girls to safe sanitation facilities and, as a result, prevent gender-based violence (GBV). The emergency latrines will be made of zinc sheet, and porcelain Arabic seats, and connected to holding tanks. The location of the latrines will be selected in coordination with the community and landowner. Latrines will be constructed at a suitable distance of no less than 30 metres from any water source to ensure no contamination occurs. The holding tank will be desludged regularly in coordination with the local authority. Oxfam in Lebanon will rehabilitate water infrastructure to ensure a reliable water supply for the community. The rehabilitation may include repairing water pumps, electrical components, and solar water pumping systems. The selection of water supply systems for rehabilitation will be conducted in coordination with the water establishment. In all locations, Oxfam will rehabilitate water supply systems which provide water to both Lebanese and Syrians. Oxfam, in coordination with the landlord and municipality in Bekaa in the informal settlement, will construct 80 latrines made of zinc sheet (size 1.2m width, 1.2m length, 1.2m height). Arabic toilet seats of porcelain will be installed in it and connected to an underground plastic holding tank (1m3). Desludging of the holding tank will be conducted regularly in coordination with the local authority and dumped in wastewater treatment unit managed by the local authority. Oxfam in Lebanon follows the sector standards in the implementation of the activity, and monitor it at site level, during transfer, and at dump site level. 

In coordination with the water establishment, Oxfam in Lebanon, in Bekaa and in the south will rehabilitate four water supply system infrastructures. This will include, but not limited to, repairing or replacing water pumps, repairing electrical components, repairing solar water pumping system by changing solar panel or other items. No changes will be made to the existing infrastructure, only repair will be conducted to ensure that the system is functional. Oxfam in Lebanon, in Bekaa and in the south, will rehabilitate 3 existing water points for people to collect drinkable water, in coordination with the municipality and community. The water points will have four water taps with a trench below with gravel (soak pit) 1m2 to collect wastewater. The repairs will include installation of 1 m3 plastic tank, water taps, and water treatment system, and repair of drainage system. As per its standard procedure, Oxfam in Lebanon will obtain the landowners&#39; written approval before commencing any latrine construction activities. To ensure the effective execution of its project activities, Oxfam is engaged in collaborative efforts with the municipalities, water establishments and communities in the target regions, where it provides humanitarian assistance. The selection and approval of the water infrastructure for rehabilitation and upgrading will be conducted in coordination with the water establishments.

The climate in Lebanon is typically sunny, dry and with relatively short rainy season. The areas are prone to both drought and floods, and rain patterns tend to be erratic. The annual precipitation is between 700 and 1,000 mm. Therefore, water scarcity remains a pressing issue, and this situation is expected to worsen, affecting agriculture, food security, and public health alike. According to the K&ouml;ppen-Geiger Climate Classification, Lebanon falls primarily under the Hot-Summer Mediterranean Climate (Csa). However, due to its diverse topography, the country has multiple climate zones. In Baalback Bekaa region, the K&ouml;ppen-Geiger Climate Classification, is BSh &ndash; Hot Semi-Arid Climate &ndash; with hot summers, cooler winters and low precipitation. In Nabateih (South), the climate is classifed as Csa Hot-Summer Mediterranean Climate, hot dry summer and mild, wet winter and higher precipitation compared to Baalback Bekaa region. Extreme weather events are expected to have severe impact on Lebanon&#39;s food sovereignty, while energy poverty continues to limit access to reliable and affordable energy. A few bouts of rain during the last several winter seasons were enough to cause flooding and property damage because of ill- maintained infrastructure, while fires have led to the burning of many green forests and refugee settlements due to poor safety and care measures. Displacement and migration from agricultural regions to urban centers are expected to increase, placing additional strain on infrastructure, governance, and resources. Lebanon&#39;s already fragile infrastructure, weakened by inadequate investments and poor governance, is scarcely equipped to cope with the escalating frequency and intensity of extreme weather events.

In Syria, the project will address urgent humanitarian needs in Aleppo (As-Safira) and Rural Damascus (Maliha, Kafr Batna) by implementing multi-sectoral interventions focused on WASH (Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene), Protection, and Gender-Based Violence (GBV) risk reduction. These interventions will ensure that communities affected by conflict and displacement have access to essential services, safe infrastructure, and sustainable solutions that enhance their resilience. Oxfam will rehabilitate water supply infrastructure, including boreholes, pumping stations, and main pipelines. This will involve repairing or replacing damaged pumps, electrical components, and filtration systems, ensuring a safe and consistent water supply. Solar-powered pumping systems will be installed to mitigate energy shortages. The project will also rehabilitate existing sewage systems and support desludging services to prevent contamination and health risks. New latrines and septic tanks will be installed where necessary, particularly in schools, health centres, and communal areas. Communities will also receive hygiene kits, including menstrual hygiene management (MHM) items, soap, and water purification tablets, while awareness campaigns will be conducted to promote safe hygiene practices. To ensure smooth implementation, Oxfam will coordinate with the relevant Syrian authorities, including municipal offices, Local Water Establishments (LWEs), and line ministries. Specific actions required include obtaining permits for infrastructure rehabilitation and water network repairs, facilitating technical collaboration with water and sanitation departments for system assessments and maintenance, and engaging local community leaders and governance structures to promote ownership and long-term sustainability of interventions. Oxfam will work closely with local community committees, women&#39;s groups, and youth networks to ensure that interventions are tailored to community needs. Training sessions will be provided to Water Management Committees (WMCs) to oversee water distribution and maintenance of rehabilitated infrastructure. In addition, women-led initiatives will be supported to enhance participation in decision-making processes related to WASH and protection services.

Syria has a predominantly Mediterranean climate, characterised by hot, dry summers and cool, wet winters, with significant sub-regional variations. The coastal areas experience higher humidity and precipitation, while inland and desert regions have arid to semi-arid conditions with extreme temperature fluctuations between day and night. The country&#39;s annual average rainfall varies from 800&ndash;1,000 mm in the western coastal areas to less than 200 mm in the eastern desert regions. The targeted areas are characterized by semi-arid climatic conditions, with water scarcity exacerbated by prolonged conflict and damage to existing infrastructure. The degradation of sanitation networks has led to frequent sewage overflows, contamination of groundwater sources, and increased risks of waterborne diseases such as cholera, leishmaniasis, and diarrhoea. In addition, the energy crisis and fuel shortages impact water pumping operations, making renewable solutions like solar power crucial. As-Safira (Aleppo Governorate) is classified as semi-arid, with limited rainfall and high evaporation rates. Drought conditions and groundwater depletion have reduced access to potable water, while high summer temperatures (often exceeding 40&deg;C) increase the demand for cooling and water resources. Maliha and Kafr Batna (Rural Damascus Governorate) experience a continental Mediterranean climate, with hot, dry summers and cold winters. The winter season brings occasional snowfall and frost, which can disrupt water infrastructure and increase energy needs. Meanwhile, prolonged dry periods in summer lead to water shortages and poor air quality due to dust storms. The ongoing climate crisis has intensified environmental degradation in Syria, compounding the effects of conflict and economic instability. The key challenges include water scarcity and desertification, rising temperatures and heat waves, extreme weather events, and increased risk of disease outbreaks. Additionally, limited access to renewable energy solutions makes communities reliant on fuel-based generators, further exacerbating air pollution. Implementing solar-powered water pumps under this project will mitigate dependency on diesel-powered systems. To address these climate-related risks, the project will rehabilitate climate-resilient water and sanitation infrastructure, ensuring efficient water distribution and sustainable wastewater management, introduce solar energy solutions for water pumping stations, reducing reliance on fossil fuels and ensuring uninterrupted water access, enhance community awareness and capacity-building on climate adaptation strategies, including water conservation and sustainable hygiene practices, and strengthen early warning systems and disaster preparedness to mitigate risks from climate-induced hazards such as floods and droughts. By integrating climate adaptation into project design, the intervention aims to enhance community resilience, ensuring that the most vulnerable populations in As-Safira, Maliha, and Kafr Batna can withstand and recover from the increasing impacts of climate change.

In Yemen, the project will target affected internally displaced persons (IDPs) integrated in host communities as well as the hosting communities in Al-Qubaytah (Lahj) and Maqbanah (Taiz), addressing ongoing severe water scarcity, inadequate sanitation facilities, and heightened public health risks, including the spread of cholera. The project will also mitigate heightened gender-based violence (GBV) risk faced by women and girls due to inadequate sanitation facilities. The project will improve Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) services through capacity building of Water Management Committees; will support community WASH management plans; will work on construction and rehabilitation of water and sanitation infrastructure, as well as hygiene promotion. Oxfam in Yemen, in coordination with local authorities and community representatives, will construct a total of 140 household latrines (40 in Lahj and 100 in Taiz) for the most vulnerable households ensuring accessibility for people with disabilities and gender-segregated facilities where necessary. Additionally, 110 latrines, (80 in Lahj and 30 in Taiz) will be rehabilitated. This will include pit repairs and improved drainage systems. All latrines will have brick superstructures, fitted with Arabic-style porcelain toilet seats and lined substructures to prevent groundwater contamination. Furthermore, Oxfam will rehabilitate 6 water supply schemes (5 in Lahj and 1 in Taiz), including the repair and extension of pipelines and the installation of three community tap schemes to improve water distribution. Oxfam will implement quick fixes on three water supply schemes in Lahj, ensuring that each undergoes a yield assessment to determine sustainable groundwater extraction. In addition, two community water harvesting tanks will be constructed in Lahj, and 140 household water storage tanks (40 in Lahj and 100 in Taiz) will be distributed to vulnerable households to improve water access and storage capacity. Finally, solar-powered water pumping systems will be rehabilitated or newly installed where possible, to ensure sustainable energy use for water supply. In order to address solid waste management, two community-led solid waste collection points will be established in targeted areas, improving waste disposal and public health conditions. These initiatives will be implemented in coordination with local authorities and community-led initiatives to ensure sustainability. Additionally, drainage and flood prevention structures will be reinforced in high-risk areas to mitigate environmental contamination and protect water sources. The selection and approval of the water infrastructure for rehabilitation and upgrading will be conducted in coordination with the GARWASP - General Authority for Rural Water Supply Projects - the government body responsible for overseeing rural water supply initiatives, infrastructure development, and water resource management in rural areas. Oxfam will obtain the landowners&#39; written approval before commencing any water and sanitation facility construction activities. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Yemen has an arid to semi-arid climate, with extreme variations in temperature and rainfall across different regions. The project areas of Al-Qubaytah (in Lahj) and Maqbanah (in Taiz) experience hot summers and mild winters, with annual precipitation ranging between 200 and 500 mm. According to the K&ouml;ppen-Geiger Climate Classification, the project areas fall under the hot semi-arid and arid desert climate zones. Lahj, particularly in Al-Qubaytah, has a dry, mountainous landscape, while Taiz, including Maqbanah, features rugged terrain with wadis and seasonal watercourses that are prone to flash floods during heavy rainfall events. Rainfall is erratic, primarily occurring during two short rainy seasons, and is often insufficient to replenish groundwater resources. Water scarcity remains a critical issue, exacerbated by high evaporation rates, prolonged droughts, and unsustainable water extraction. These challenges directly impact agriculture, food security, and public health, increasing reliance on alternative water sources, including unsanitary open wells and unsustainable water trucking. The region faces a persistent water deficit, with many communities relying on deep boreholes or surface water, which is often contaminated due to inadequate sanitation infrastructure. Extreme weather events, such as droughts, sandstorms, and seasonal flash floods, pose significant risks to infrastructure, livelihoods, and public health. Poorly maintained drainage systems and unregulated solid waste disposal contribute to environmental degradation, leading to the contamination of drinking water sources.

&nbsp;

This project includes the construction of a small office and combined warehouse space on a greenfield site adjacent to the Snootli Creek Hatchery main office building. Approximately 12 Cottonwood trees will be cleared for the footprint of the building. The office and warehouse space will be approximately 220 m2 and will include a small kitchen and washroom, some office space, and conditioned warehouse space with a large roll-top door. The foundation will be slab on-grade with strip footings. The structure will be pre-fabricated steel with a metal roof, clad in durable hardy board. For services, the building will be connected to a new BC Hydro meter, as well as the Hatchery back-up power plant, and a small septic field will also be developed adjacent to the building. Construction equipment will include a small excavator, crane, and ready-mix concrete truck. Construction period will be from April 2023 &ndash; October 2023. 

&nbsp;

No in-water works are anticipated for this project.

properties.description_fr:
Ce projet comprend la construction d&#39;un petit bureau et d&#39;un entrep&ocirc;t connexe sur un site vierge adjacent au b&acirc;timent principal de l&#39;&eacute;closerie du ruisseau Snootli. Il faudra abattre environ 12&nbsp;peupliers pour l&#39;empreinte du b&acirc;timent. L&#39;espace du bureau et de l&#39;entrep&ocirc;t aura une superficie d&#39;environ 220&nbsp;m2 et comprendra une petite cuisine et des toilettes, un espace de bureau et un espace d&#39;entreposage climatis&eacute; avec une grande porte roulante. La fondation sera constitu&eacute;e d&#39;une dalle au sol et de semelles filantes. La structure sera en acier pr&eacute;fabriqu&eacute; avec un toit en m&eacute;tal, recouvert d&#39;un panneau dur durable. Pour les services, le b&acirc;timent sera reli&eacute; &agrave; un nouveau compteur de BC Hydro, ainsi qu&#39;&agrave; la centrale &eacute;lectrique de secours de l&#39;&eacute;closerie, et un petit champ d&#39;&eacute;puration sera &eacute;galement am&eacute;nag&eacute; pr&egrave;s du b&acirc;timent. L&#39;&eacute;quipement de construction comprendra une petite excavatrice, une grue, et un camion-b&eacute;tonni&egrave;re. La p&eacute;riode de construction s&#39;&eacute;tendra d&#39;avril 2023 &agrave; octobre 2023. 

&nbsp;

Aucun travail dans l&#39;eau n&#39;est pr&eacute;vu pour ce projet.

properties.description_en:
The proposed project involves the replacement of the existing floating wharves including selected steel anchor piles at the Meteghan Small Craft Harbour in Digby County, NS.&nbsp; The floating wharf facilities are in three (3) pier configurations oriented perpendicular to the main service area.&nbsp; Each pier consists of four (4) treated timber floating wharf units connected to five (5) steel anchor piles.&nbsp; The fairway clearances between the three (3) sets of piers are 41 m and 52 m.&nbsp; Each pier is connected to concrete abutments at the seaward edge of the service area by 17.5 m-long aluminum gangways.&nbsp; All floating wharves are at the end of their service lives and anchor piles on the east and west float piers are severely deteriorated and also require replacement.&nbsp; The pipe piles on the middle float pier were replaced in 2018 and will remain to be re-used on the new float units.&nbsp; The proposed project involves the complete removal of all floating wharves and the cut-off or removal of all anchor piles on the east and west floating wharf piers.

&nbsp;

New 407 mm diameter pipe piles will be driven into the substrate to elevations of approximately 10.5 m below chart datum and extend up to 8.5 m above chart datum.&nbsp; The floating wharf piers will be replaced with similar treated timber floating wharf units 3 m wide and ranging in length from 16.7 m to 18.5 m.&nbsp; The units will be connected with guide bars to the pipe piles at both ends of each pier and interstitially between each unit and joined together with new chains, brackets and slider plates.&nbsp; The total length of the east and west floating wharf piers will be 78.5 m, while the middle floating wharf pier will measure 71 m in length.&nbsp; Each new pier will be reconnected to the shoreline at the edge of the service area by the existing aluminum gangways that will be salvaged for reuse.

&nbsp;

The proposed project will require large vehicles and equipment including floating plant barge equipment for the pile driving and core drilling operations. &nbsp;All land-based vehicles and heavy equipment such as excavators, cranes, pile driving and core drilling equipment and trucks will access the site via existing public roads that provide direct access to Meteghan harbour.&nbsp; The floating plant equipment may consist of sectional barges trucked to the site, unloaded by cranes and assembled in the water or a larger barge towed to the site by tug boat.

&nbsp;

Construction activities are anticipated to commence in spring 2026 and be completed by the end of March 2027.&nbsp; Project commencement is, however, subject to DFO-SCH operational priorities and funding, as well as the completion of regulatory approval processes, therefore work may be delayed.&nbsp; The scope of the impact assessment (subject to the Impact Assessment Act) will, therefore, be based on the works being completed over a period of 6 months commencing within a period of 5 years following finalization of the assessment.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The Meteghan Small Craft Harbour is the largest core fishing harbour in the area that was developed to serve the fishing community year-round.&nbsp; The main purpose of the proposed project is to replace dilapidated infrastructure to support the continued viability of the harbour for the commercial fishery and the local economy.

properties.description_fr:
Le projet propos&eacute; consiste &agrave; remplacer les quais flottants existants, y compris certains pieux d&#39;ancrage en acier, au port pour petits bateaux de Meteghan, dans le comt&eacute; de Digby (N.-&Eacute;.). Les installations de quais flottants sont configur&eacute;es en trois (3) jet&eacute;es orient&eacute;es perpendiculairement &agrave; la zone de service principale. Chaque jet&eacute;e est constitu&eacute;e de quatre (4) unit&eacute;s de quais flottants en bois trait&eacute;, reli&eacute;es &agrave; cinq (5) pieux d&#39;ancrage en acier. Les d&eacute;gagements dans les chenaux entre les trois (3) ensembles de jet&eacute;es sont de 41 m et 52 m. Chaque jet&eacute;e est raccord&eacute;e &agrave; des cul&eacute;es en b&eacute;ton situ&eacute;es au bord ext&eacute;rieur de la zone de service au moyen de passerelles en aluminium de 17,5 m de longueur. Tous les quais flottants ont atteint la fin de leur vie utile, et les pieux d&#39;ancrage des jet&eacute;es est et ouest sont gravement d&eacute;t&eacute;rior&eacute;s et doivent &eacute;galement &ecirc;tre remplac&eacute;s. Les pieux tubulaires de la jet&eacute;e centrale ont &eacute;t&eacute; remplac&eacute;s en 2018 et seront r&eacute;utilis&eacute;s avec les nouvelles unit&eacute;s flottantes. Le projet propos&eacute; pr&eacute;voit le retrait complet de tous les quais flottants et la coupe ou l&#39;enl&egrave;vement de tous les pieux d&#39;ancrage des jet&eacute;es flottantes est et ouest.

&nbsp;

De nouveaux pieux tubulaires de 407 mm de diam&egrave;tre seront enfonc&eacute;s dans le substrat jusqu&#39;&agrave; des altitudes d&#39;environ 10,5 m sous le z&eacute;ro des cartes et s&#39;&eacute;l&egrave;veront jusqu&#39;&agrave; 8,5 m au-dessus du z&eacute;ro des cartes. Les jet&eacute;es de quais flottants seront remplac&eacute;es par des unit&eacute;s similaires en bois trait&eacute;, d&#39;une largeur de 3 m, et d&#39;une longueur variant de 16,7 m &agrave; 18,5 m. Les unit&eacute;s seront reli&eacute;es aux pieux tubulaires &agrave; l&#39;aide de barres de guidage aux deux extr&eacute;mit&eacute;s de chaque jet&eacute;e ainsi qu&#39;entre chaque unit&eacute;, et assembl&eacute;es &agrave; l&#39;aide de nouvelles cha&icirc;nes, de nouveaux supports et de plaques coulissantes. La longueur totale des jet&eacute;es flottantes est et ouest sera de 78,5 m, tandis que la jet&eacute;e flottante centrale aura une longueur de 71 m. Chaque nouvelle jet&eacute;e sera raccord&eacute;e au rivage, &agrave; la limite de la zone de service, au moyen des passerelles en aluminium existantes qui seront r&eacute;cup&eacute;r&eacute;es aux fins de r&eacute;utilisation.

&nbsp;

Le projet propos&eacute; n&eacute;cessitera l&#39;utilisation de gros v&eacute;hicules et d&#39;&eacute;quipements, y compris des barges d&#39;&eacute;quipement flottant pour les op&eacute;rations d&#39;enfoncement des pieux et de carottage. Tous les v&eacute;hicules terrestres et l&#39;&eacute;quipement lourd, tels que les excavatrices, les grues, l&#39;&eacute;quipement d&#39;enfoncement des pieux, l&#39;&eacute;quipement de carottage et les camions, auront acc&egrave;s au site par les routes publiques existantes qui m&egrave;nent directement au port de Meteghan. L&#39;&eacute;quipement flottant pourrait comprendre des barges modulaires transport&eacute;es au site par camion, d&eacute;charg&eacute;es par des grues et assembl&eacute;es dans l&#39;eau, ou une barge plus grande remorqu&eacute;e jusqu&#39;au site par un remorqueur.

&nbsp;

Les activit&eacute;s de construction devraient commencer au printemps 2026 et se terminer d&#39;ici la fin mars 2027. Toutefois, le d&eacute;but des travaux d&eacute;pendra des priorit&eacute;s op&eacute;rationnelles et du financement de MPO-PB, ainsi que de l&#39;obtention des approbations r&eacute;glementaires; les travaux pourraient donc &ecirc;tre retard&eacute;s. La port&eacute;e de l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact (en vertu de la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact) sera donc fond&eacute;e sur l&#39;hypoth&egrave;se que les travaux seront r&eacute;alis&eacute;s sur une p&eacute;riode de 6 mois d&eacute;butant dans les 5 ann&eacute;es suivant la finalisation de l&#39;&eacute;valuation.

&nbsp;

Le port pour petits bateaux de Meteghan est le plus grand port de p&ecirc;che central de la r&eacute;gion, am&eacute;nag&eacute; pour servir la communaut&eacute; de p&ecirc;cheurs toute l&#39;ann&eacute;e. L&#39;objectif principal du projet propos&eacute; est de remplacer des infrastructures d&eacute;labr&eacute;es afin de soutenir la viabilit&eacute; continue du port pour la p&ecirc;che commerciale et l&#39;&eacute;conomie locale.

properties.description_en:
Associated conducted a feasibility investigation in 2020, which identified four&nbsp;concept plans to shift from the use of septic&nbsp;tanks&nbsp;to&nbsp;a centralized&nbsp;CWWS.&nbsp;The&nbsp;recommended CWWS concept is a&nbsp;piped collection system&nbsp;(i.e., sanitary lines, lift station, and forced main)&nbsp;and aerated lagoon system with surface&nbsp;discharge&nbsp;(i.e., treatment system). The lagoon system will be&nbsp;located at the&nbsp;previous&nbsp;gravel pit&nbsp;area&nbsp;in the southwest of&nbsp;the community and the&nbsp;proposed outflow&nbsp;will be pumped north&nbsp;into&nbsp;Babine Lake

The proposed infrastructure&nbsp;includes&nbsp;the following:&nbsp;

&bull;&nbsp;A&nbsp;wastewater treatment facility (WWTF), including an aeration building and lagoons. This will be&nbsp;constructed&nbsp;in the&nbsp;previous&nbsp;gravel pit&nbsp;location&nbsp;in areas that are predominantly pre-disturbed, situated at least 30 m away&nbsp;from the highwater mark of Fulton River.&nbsp;It&nbsp;will&nbsp;also&nbsp;be situated at least 30 m from the community gas station,&nbsp;and 100 m from residential&nbsp;homes.&nbsp;The WWTF will require&nbsp;a&nbsp;clearing and grubbing area of approximately&nbsp;22,931&nbsp;m2&nbsp;(Figure 1-1).&nbsp;The immediate footprint of the WWTF, including an access road, will be&nbsp;approximately&nbsp;4,895&nbsp;m2, encompassed&nbsp;by approximately 550&nbsp;m of perimeter fencing.

&nbsp;&bull;&nbsp;A lift station near the intersection of Lazelle Road and Babine Crescent, with&nbsp;an approximate&nbsp;footprint of&nbsp;553&nbsp;m2.&nbsp;

&nbsp;&bull;&nbsp;A&nbsp;force&nbsp;main&nbsp;extending approximately&nbsp;898&nbsp;m from the&nbsp;lift station to the WWTF.&nbsp;The&nbsp;force&nbsp;main&nbsp;will be&nbsp;installed within the existing right-of-way of Main&nbsp;Street and Eagle Road. The&nbsp;force&nbsp;main will&nbsp;encroach into the&nbsp;riparian area of Fulton River (i.e., within 15 m of the highwater mark)&nbsp;; however, no riparian vegetation will be&nbsp;removed&nbsp;as the alignment is along an existing dirt road&nbsp;.&nbsp;

&bull;&nbsp;A sanitary sewer&nbsp;collection main&nbsp;to service residential houses along Lazelle Road, Leon Hill Avenue, Main&nbsp;Street, and Babine Crescent. The sanitary sewer line will be approximately&nbsp;1,342&nbsp;m long and will&nbsp;be&nbsp;constructed entirely within&nbsp;pre-disturbed areas.&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
En 2020, Associated a men&eacute; une &eacute;tude de faisabilit&eacute; qui a permis d&#39;identifier quatre options pour passer de l&#39;utilisation de fosses septiques &agrave; un syst&egrave;me centralis&eacute; de traitement des eaux us&eacute;es (CWWS). Le concept de CWWS recommand&eacute; comprend un r&eacute;seau de collecte par canalisations (&agrave; savoir des conduites d&#39;assainissement, une station de relevage et une conduite de refoulement) ainsi qu&#39;un syst&egrave;me de lagunes a&eacute;r&eacute;es avec rejet en surface (c&#39;est-&agrave;-dire un syst&egrave;me de traitement). Le syst&egrave;me de lagunes sera situ&eacute; sur l&#39;ancien site de la gravi&egrave;re, au sud-ouest de la communaut&eacute;, et l&#39;effluent propos&eacute; sera pomp&eacute; vers le nord, dans le lac Babine

L&#39;infrastructure propos&eacute;e comprend les &eacute;l&eacute;ments suivants :&nbsp;

&bull; Une station d&#39;&eacute;puration des eaux us&eacute;es (WWTF), comprenant un b&acirc;timent d&#39;a&eacute;ration et des lagunes. Elle sera construite sur l&#39;ancien site de la gravi&egrave;re, dans des zones d&eacute;j&agrave; perturb&eacute;es, &agrave; au moins 30 m de la laisse de haute mer de la rivi&egrave;re Fulton. Elle sera &eacute;galement situ&eacute;e &agrave; au moins 30 m de la station-service de la communaut&eacute; et &agrave; 100 m des habitations. La STEP n&eacute;cessitera une zone de d&eacute;boisement et de d&eacute;frichage d&#39;environ 22 931 m&sup2; (figure 1-1). L&#39;empreinte imm&eacute;diate de la STEP, y compris une route d&#39;acc&egrave;s, sera d&#39;environ 4 895 m&sup2;, entour&eacute;e d&#39;une cl&ocirc;ture p&eacute;riph&eacute;rique d&#39;environ 550 m.

&nbsp;&bull; Une station de relevage situ&eacute;e pr&egrave;s de l&#39;intersection de Lazelle Road et de Babine Crescent, d&#39;une superficie d&#39;environ 553 m&sup2;.&nbsp;

&bull; Une conduite de refoulement s&#39;&eacute;tendant sur environ 898 m, de la station de relevage jusqu&#39;&agrave; la station d&#39;&eacute;puration. La conduite de refoulement sera install&eacute;e dans l&#39;emprise existante de Main Street et d&#39;Eagle Road. Elle empi&eacute;tera sur la zone riveraine de la rivi&egrave;re Fulton (c&#39;est-&agrave;-dire &agrave; moins de 15 m de la laisse de haute mer) ; toutefois, aucune v&eacute;g&eacute;tation riveraine ne sera supprim&eacute;e, car le trac&eacute; suit un chemin de terre existant.&nbsp;

&bull; Une conduite collectrice d&#39;&eacute;gouts sanitaires desservant les habitations situ&eacute;es le long de Lazelle Road, Leon Hill Avenue, Main Street et Babine Crescent. La conduite d&#39;&eacute;gouts sanitaires aura une longueur d&#39;environ 1 342 m et sera enti&egrave;rement construite dans des zones d&eacute;j&agrave; perturb&eacute;es.&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
Bearspaw First Nation is proposing the construction of a new water treatment plant (WTP) to supply water to the residents of Eden Valley 216 and to replace the existing temporary water treatment system. The original WTP was completely destroyed by a fire in 2022 at such time the temporary WTP was installed. The Project will be located at Eden Valley 216 approximately ~130m south of Highway 541, just immediately south of the Highwood River, in LSD-01-15-017-04 W5M &amp; LSD-16-10-017-04 W4M. The overall footprint of the project is 4,330 square metres.

&nbsp;

Activities of the Project includes, demolition and removal of the burned WTP foundation to accommodate construction of the new WTP; expanded residual settling pond; construction of new residual settling pond; relocation and construction of a new stormwater drainage channel east of the WTP; installation of perimeter fence around the entire reconstructed WTP facility; installation of a new vault with pumps at the existing raw water storage reservoir.

&nbsp;

No tree clearing is anticipated for this project, the new outer perimeter fence shall only encompass previously disturbed land. Installation of the new vault and pumps for the raw water storage facility will largely occur within previously disturbed (compacted and graveled) ground. The nearest waterbody relative to the proposed WTP is the Highwood River (ID2065). However, the WTP is &gt;30m away from the bed and shore of the Highwood River and the scope of the project will not include any in-stream works (e.g. intake/outfall maintenance).

properties.description_fr:
La Premi&egrave;re nation de Bearspaw propose la construction d&#39;une nouvelle station de traitement d&#39;eau (STEP) pour approvisionner en eau les r&eacute;sidents d&#39;Eden Valley 216 et remplacer le syst&egrave;me temporaire de traitement d&#39;eau existant. L&#39;usine de traitement de l&#39;eau d&#39;origine a &eacute;t&eacute; compl&egrave;tement d&eacute;truite par un incendie en 2022, date &agrave; laquelle l&#39;usine de traitement de l&#39;eau temporaire a &eacute;t&eacute; install&eacute;e. Le projet sera situ&eacute; &agrave; Eden Valley 216, &agrave; environ 130 m au sud de l&#39;autoroute 541, imm&eacute;diatement au sud de la rivi&egrave;re Highwood, dans les zones LSD-01-15-017-04 W5M et LSD-16-10-017-04 W4M. L&#39;empreinte globale du projet est de 4 330 m&egrave;tres carr&eacute;s.

&nbsp;

Les activit&eacute;s du projet comprennent la d&eacute;molition et l&#39;enl&egrave;vement des fondations br&ucirc;l&eacute;es de la station d&#39;&eacute;puration pour permettre la construction de la nouvelle station d&#39;&eacute;puration ; l&#39;agrandissement du bassin de d&eacute;cantation des r&eacute;sidus ; la construction d&#39;un nouveau bassin de d&eacute;cantation des r&eacute;sidus ; le d&eacute;placement et la construction d&#39;un nouveau canal de drainage des eaux pluviales &agrave; l&#39;est de la station d&#39;&eacute;puration ; l&#39;installation d&#39;une cl&ocirc;ture p&eacute;riph&eacute;rique autour de l&#39;ensemble de la station d&#39;&eacute;puration reconstruite ; l&#39;installation d&#39;une nouvelle vo&ucirc;te avec des pompes au r&eacute;servoir de stockage de l&#39;eau brute existant.

&nbsp;

Aucun d&eacute;frichement n&#39;est pr&eacute;vu dans le cadre de ce projet, la nouvelle cl&ocirc;ture ext&eacute;rieure n&#39;englobera que les terrains d&eacute;j&agrave; perturb&eacute;s. L&#39;installation de la nouvelle vo&ucirc;te et des pompes pour le r&eacute;servoir d&#39;eau brute se fera en grande partie sur des terrains d&eacute;j&agrave; perturb&eacute;s (compact&eacute;s et gravillonn&eacute;s). Le plan d&#39;eau le plus proche de la station d&#39;&eacute;puration propos&eacute;e est la rivi&egrave;re Highwood (ID2065). Cependant, la station d&#39;&eacute;puration se trouve &agrave; plus de 30 m du lit et de la rive de la rivi&egrave;re Highwood et le projet ne comprendra pas de travaux dans le cours d&#39;eau (par exemple, l&#39;entretien des prises d&#39;eau et des d&eacute;versoirs).

properties.description_en:
The Department of National Defence (DND) is proposing a project. The proposed Project consists of the replacement of the Main Entrance Bridge at 14 Wing Canadian Forces Base (CFB) Greenwood. The existing structure will be removed and replaced with a new bridge designed to meet current operational, safety, and infrastructure requirements while maintaining access to the base. The Project will be completed in several phases, including:


	Site Mobilization, including establishment of access, staging areas, and environmental protection measures;
	Demolition of the existing bridge deck and associated in-stream structures, with temporary retention of abutments where required for site isolation;
	Foundation work, including construction of new footings to support the replacement bridge;
	Trenching and utility installation, including directional drilling as required;
	Bridge installation, involving placement of precast bridge components; and
	Roadworks, including installation of guardrails, signage, and surface restoration.

properties.description_fr:
Le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale (MDN) propose un projet. Le projet propos&eacute; consiste &agrave; remplacer le pont de l&#39;entr&eacute;e principale de la 14e Escadre de la base des Forces canadienne (BFC) Greenwood. La structure existante sera d&eacute;molie et remplac&eacute;e par un nouveau pont con&ccedil;u pour r&eacute;pondre aux exigences actuelles en mati&egrave;re op&eacute;rationnel, de s&eacute;curit&eacute; et d&#39;infrastructure, tout en pr&eacute;servant l&#39;acc&egrave;s &agrave; la base. Le projet sera r&eacute;alis&eacute; en plusieurs phases, notamment:


	Mise en place du chantier, y compris l&#39;am&eacute;nagement des voies d&#39;acc&egrave;s, des zones de stockage et des mesures de protection de l&#39;environnement ;
	D&eacute;molition du tablier du pont existant et des ouvrages associ&eacute;s situ&eacute;s dans le cours d&#39;eau, avec conservation temporaire des cul&eacute;es lorsque cela est n&eacute;cessaire pour l&#39;isolation du chantier;
	Travaux de fondation, y compris la construction de nouvelles bases/semelles pour soutenir le pont de remplacement;
	Creusement de tranch&eacute;es et installation des r&eacute;seaux, y compris le forage directionnel si n&eacute;cessaire;
	Installation du pont, impliquant la mise en place d&#39;&eacute;l&eacute;ments pr&eacute;fabriqu&eacute;s; et
	Travaux routiers, y compris l&#39;installation de barri&egrave;res de s&eacute;curit&eacute;, de la signalisation et la remise en &eacute;tat de la chauss&eacute;e.

properties.description_en:
Built between 1964 and 1965, the Estacade was designed to control ice flow on the St. Lawrence&nbsp;River and reduce the risk of flooding and erosion on &Icirc;le Notre-Dame and &Icirc;le Sainte-H&eacute;l&egrave;ne. This&nbsp;structure spans 2040 metres between &Icirc;le des S&oelig;urs and the St. Lawrence Seaway dike. It is 18&nbsp;metres wide. A dedicated bicycle and pedestrian path was added to the structure in 2015. The&nbsp;
Estacade is mainly used by emergency vehicles. Maintenance work performed on the structure over the years has included replacing restraint&nbsp;systems, repairing foundation unit footings, reinforcing the deck with transverse post-tensioning,&nbsp;
and repairing concrete in the beams.&nbsp;Major work is required to uphold the structure&#39;s service life over the long term.&nbsp;
This work will include:
&bull; Repairs to 8 foundation unit footings
&bull; Concrete repairs and crack injections in the shafts of 18 foundation units
&bull; Replacement of bearings
&bull; Repairs to about ten pedestal blocks
&bull; Repairs to the concrete in beams
&bull; Installation of joint gaskets
&bull; Various other repairs
This work is scheduled to start in summer 2025 and finish in 2028. The project will include&nbsp;operational, aesthetic, architectural, historical and ecosystem aspects. For the work on the&nbsp;foundation units, barges may be used, and cofferdams may be temporarily installed. This work will&nbsp;be performed as per the requirements of the applicable regulatory authorities. The dedicated&nbsp;
bicycle path will remain open to pedestrians and cyclists throughout most of the work and users are&nbsp;invited to subscribe to our X account @mobiliteactive to stay informed. Vehicles will have&nbsp;unhindered access to the structure at all times. Access for boating may also be maintained during&nbsp;the work.

properties.description_fr:
L&#39;Estacade, construite entre 1964 et 1965, servait &agrave; contr&ocirc;ler le mouvement des glaces sur le fleuve&nbsp;Saint-Laurent et &agrave; limiter les risques d&#39;inondation et d&#39;&eacute;rosion des &icirc;les Notre-Dame et Sainte-H&eacute;l&egrave;ne. Elle mesure 2 040 m&egrave;tres de long entre l&#39;&icirc;le des S&oelig;urs et la digue de la Voie maritime du&nbsp;Saint-Laurent. Sa largeur est de 18 m&egrave;tres. En 2015, une piste cyclable et pi&eacute;tonni&egrave;re a &eacute;t&eacute;&nbsp;
construite en site propre. L&#39;Estacade sert principalement pour les v&eacute;hicules d&#39;urgence. Au fil du temps, des travaux visant &agrave; assurer l&#39;entretien de la structure ont eu lieu, notamment le&nbsp;replacement des dispositifs de retenue, la r&eacute;paration de semelles des unit&eacute;s de fondation, le&nbsp;renforcement du tablier avec l&#39;ajout de posttension transversale ainsi que la r&eacute;paration du b&eacute;ton&nbsp;
des poutres.&nbsp;Des travaux importants doivent &ecirc;tre r&eacute;alis&eacute;s pour assurer la durabilit&eacute; de l&#39;ouvrage.&nbsp;
Ces travaux comprennent notamment :
&bull; la r&eacute;paration de 8 semelles des unit&eacute;s de fondation;
&bull; la r&eacute;paration de b&eacute;ton et l&#39;injection de fissures du f&ucirc;t de 18 unit&eacute;s de fondation;
&bull; le remplacement des appareils d&#39;appui;
&bull; la r&eacute;paration d&#39;une dizaine de blocs d&#39;assise;
&bull; la r&eacute;paration de poutres;
&bull; l&#39;installation de garnitures de joint en silicone;
&bull; d&#39;autres r&eacute;parations diverses.
Les travaux sont pr&eacute;vus d&eacute;buter &agrave; l&#39;&eacute;t&eacute; 2025 et terminer en 2028. Le projet prendra en consid&eacute;ration&nbsp;les aspects op&eacute;rationnels, esth&eacute;tiques, architecturaux, historiques et &eacute;cosyst&eacute;miques. Pour&nbsp;permettre l&#39;ex&eacute;cution des travaux sur les unit&eacute;s de fondation, des barges pourraient &ecirc;tre utilis&eacute;es et&nbsp;des batardeaux pourraient &ecirc;tre install&eacute;s de fa&ccedil;on temporaire. Ces travaux seront ex&eacute;cut&eacute;s&nbsp;
conform&eacute;ment aux exigences des autorit&eacute;s r&eacute;glementaires comp&eacute;tentes. La piste cyclable en site&nbsp;propre demeurera ouverte aux pi&eacute;tons et aux cyclistes pendant la majeure partie des travaux. Les&nbsp;usagers sont invit&eacute;s &agrave; s&#39;abonner &agrave; notre compte X @mobiliteactive pour rester inform&eacute;. Un acc&egrave;s&nbsp;sans entrave est pr&eacute;vu en tout temps pour le passage des v&eacute;hicules d&#39;urgence. La navigation pourra&nbsp;&eacute;galement &ecirc;tre maintenue durant les travaux.

properties.description_en:
Public Notice

&nbsp;

Sea Island Conservation Area Dike Upgrade Project &ndash; Public Comments Invited

&nbsp;

July 18, 2025&nbsp;&ndash; The authorities must determine whether the proposed project is likely to cause significant adverse environmental effects. To help inform this determination, the authorities invite comments from the public respecting the determination. Written comments must be submitted by August 18, 2025.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Fish and Fish Habitat Protection Program Fisheries and Oceans Canada
200 - 401 Burrard Street
Vancouver, British Columbia V6C 3S4
Email:&nbsp;DFO.PACFPP.PPPPAC.MPO@dfo-mpo.gc.ca

&nbsp;

The Proposed Project

Vancouver Airport Authority is proposing to upgrade the dike system at the Sea Island Conservation Area in Richmond, B.C. The proposed project will raise the existing dike by approximately 1m to improve flood protection for the Vancouver International Airport and related infrastructure on Sea Island.

&nbsp;

The project consists of upgrading a 2.5 km long section of dike on the northern portion of Sea Island between McDonald Road and Ferguson Road. Most of the land in the project footprint is within the Sea Island Conservation Area which is administered by Environment and Climate Change Canada via the Canadian Wildlife Service. Small portions of land within or adjacent to the project footprint are owned or administered by the Musqueam First Nation (Sea Island IR No. 3), the Vancouver Fraser Port Authority and Canadian Forest Products. Project funding has been provided by Transport Canada. Activities required for the project include clearing vegetation, placement of dike fill material, relocation of an existing drainage ditch and site restoration.

properties.description_fr:
Avis public

&nbsp;

Projet d&#39;am&eacute;lioration du syst&egrave;me de digues &ndash; Sea Island Conservation Area &ndash; P&eacute;riode de consultation publique

&nbsp;

18 Julliet 2025&nbsp;&ndash; Les administrations doivent d&eacute;terminer si la proposition de projet est susceptible d&#39;entra&icirc;ner des effets environnementaux n&eacute;gatifs importants. Pour permettre de d&eacute;terminer ce qu&#39;il en est, les administrations invitent le public &agrave; leur faire part de ses commentaires. Les commentaires &eacute;crits doivent &ecirc;tre envoy&eacute;s au plus tard le 18 Ao&ucirc;t 2025.

&nbsp;

Fish and Fish Habitat Protection Program Fisheries and Oceans Canada
Pi&egrave;ce 200 - 401 rue Burrard
Vancouver (Colombie-Britannique) V6C 3S4
Courriel :&nbsp;DFO.PACFPP.PPPPAC.MPO@dfo-mpo.gc.ca

&nbsp;

Le projet propos&eacute;

L&#39;Administration de l&#39;a&eacute;roport de Vancouver propose d&#39;am&eacute;liorer le r&eacute;seau de digues situ&eacute; dans la Sea Island Conservation Area, &agrave; Richmond, en Colombie-Britannique. Le projet propose d&#39;&eacute;lever d&#39;environ un m&egrave;tre la digue existante dans le but d&#39;accro&icirc;tre la protection contre les inondations de l&#39;a&eacute;roport international de Vancouver et de l&#39;infrastructure connexe sur Sea Island.

&nbsp;

Le projet concerne une section de digue de 2,5 kilom&egrave;tres situ&eacute;e dans le nord de Sea Island, entre le McDonald Road et le Ferguson Road. La majeure partie des terres vis&eacute;e par le projet se trouvent dans la Sea Island Conservation Area, qui est g&eacute;r&eacute;e par Environnement et Changement climatique Canada, par l&#39;entremise du Service canadien de la faune. De petites portions des terres situ&eacute;es &agrave; l&#39;int&eacute;rieur ou &agrave; proximit&eacute; du p&eacute;rim&egrave;tre du projet appartiennent &agrave; la Premi&egrave;re Nation Musqueam (r&eacute;serve indienne de Sea Island no3), &agrave; l&#39;Administration portuaire Vancouver Fraser et &agrave; Canadian Forest Products ou sont g&eacute;r&eacute;es par celles-ci. Transports Canada a accord&eacute; le financement du projet. Les activit&eacute;s du projet comprennent les suivantes : d&eacute;frichement, installation de mat&eacute;riaux de remblai pour la digue, d&eacute;placement d&#39;un foss&eacute; de drainage et remise en &eacute;tat du site.

properties.description_en:
k?ik?????m (Kwikwetlem First Nation) are proposing to restore the hydraulic connection between the Reeve Slough and the Coquitlam River by constructing new inlet and outlet channels and excavating a low gradient pilot channel through Reeve Slough to reestablish downstream flows. The Project will involve dredging and regrading the&nbsp;Reeve Slough, construction of a new inlet and outlet channel, installation of aquatic and riparian habitat features, and replacement of a non-functioning culvert.&nbsp;The Project will be designed and constructed with an in-kind partnership with Fisheries and Oceans Canada (DFO).

&nbsp;

The proponent has applied to Environment and Climate Change Canada for a Species at Risk Act permit under section 73(3).

properties.description_fr:
La Premi&egrave;re Nation de Kwikwetlem (k?ik?????m) propose de r&eacute;tablir la connexion hydraulique entre le bras mort de Reeve et la rivi&egrave;re Coquitlam en construisant de nouveaux canaux d&#39;entr&eacute;e et de sortie et en creusant un canal pilote &agrave; faible pente dans le bras mort de Reeve afin de r&eacute;tablir le d&eacute;bit en aval. Le projet comprendra le dragage et le reprofilage du bras mort de Reeve, la construction d&#39;un nouveau canal d&#39;entr&eacute;e et de sortie, l&#39;am&eacute;nagement d&#39;habitats aquatiques et riverains et le remplacement d&#39;un ponceau d&eacute;fectueux. Le projet sera con&ccedil;u et r&eacute;alis&eacute; en partenariat avec P&ecirc;ches et Oc&eacute;ans Canada (MPO).

&nbsp;

Le promoteur a d&eacute;pos&eacute; une demande de permis en vertu de la Loi sur les esp&egrave;ces en p&eacute;ril, conform&eacute;ment au paragraphe 73(3), aupr&egrave;s d&#39;Environnement et Changement climatique Canada.

properties.description_en:
The National Capital Commission (NCC) is proposing electrical infrastructure upgrades at Jacques Cartier Park North (JCPN) located in Gatineau, Quebec, to support future largescale public events, such as, Winterlude and Canada Day (the Project). These improvements align with NCC priorities to enhance year-round animation and public programming along the Ottawa River shoreline as well as infrastructure planning guidelines from the NCC&#39;s National Capital Core Area Plan (2025). Initial Project consultation began in June 2021, with power needs based on Winterlude&#39;s high consumption. Since 2021, additional consultations regarding the Project have been conducted by the NCC Design and Construction team in collaboration with Heritage Canada, the City of Gatineau, and the NCC Gatineau Park Team. These sessions addressed subjects including programming options, potential events or uses, as well as power requirements.

&nbsp;

The Project scope includes the installation of a new Hydro-Qu&eacute;bec service connection and a main distribution cabinet. It also includes adding new power pedestals and event connection points at key locations throughout JCPN, considering future event needs and the existing park landscape. HydroQu&eacute;bec will complete all work on its distribution network, including relocating an existing service line and will be limited to previously disturbed areas. An NCC awarded contractor will install the JCPN electrical infrastructure and electrical line connections within JCPN. Project footprints nearby existing trees will be kept at a minimum and hydrovac excavation will be used over open trench methods within tree root zones to minimize impacts.

&nbsp;

These electrical upgrades are required to meet modern power demands for major events and reduce reliance on temporary generators. Once completed, the new system will provide reliable, expanded electrical capacity to support current and future programming needs within JCPN.

&nbsp;

The NCC must determine whether this project is likely to cause significant adverse environmental effects under sections 81-91 of the Impact Assessment Act (2019) and the National Capital Act (1985). A federal land use and design approval (FLUDA) is required for this work.

&nbsp;

Project implementation is targeted to commence in Spring of 2026 and be completed by December 2026, following final design coordination with Hydro-Qu&eacute;bec and procurement of qualified contractors.

properties.description_fr:
La Commission de la capitale nationale (CCN) propose de moderniser l&#39;infrastructure &eacute;lectrique du parc Jacques-Cartier Nord (PJCN), situ&eacute; &agrave; Gatineau, au Qu&eacute;bec, afin de permettre la tenue d&#39;&eacute;v&eacute;nements publics d&#39;envergure, tels que le Bal de Neige et la f&ecirc;te du Canada (le projet). Ces am&eacute;liorations s&#39;inscrivent dans les priorit&eacute;s de la CCN visant &agrave; rehausser l&#39;animation et la programmation publique tout au long de l&#39;ann&eacute;e le long des rives de la rivi&egrave;re des Outaouais, ainsi que dans les lignes directrices de planification des infrastructures du Plan du c&oelig;ur de la capitale nationale de la CCN (2025). Les premi&egrave;res consultations sur le projet ont d&eacute;but&eacute; en juin 2021, les besoins en &eacute;lectricit&eacute; &eacute;tant bas&eacute;s sur la consommation &eacute;lev&eacute;e du Bal de Neige. Depuis 2021, des consultations suppl&eacute;mentaires concernant le projet ont &eacute;t&eacute; men&eacute;es par l&#39;&eacute;quipe de conception et de construction de la CCN, en collaboration avec Patrimoine Canada, la Ville de Gatineau et l&#39;&eacute;quipe du parc de la Gatineau de la CCN. Ces s&eacute;ances ont port&eacute; sur des sujets tels que les options de programmation, les &eacute;v&eacute;nements ou utilisations potentiels, ainsi que les besoins en &eacute;lectricit&eacute;.

&nbsp;

La port&eacute;e du projet comprend l&#39;installation d&#39;un nouveau raccordement au r&eacute;seau d&#39;Hydro-Qu&eacute;bec et d&#39;une armoire de distribution principale. Elle comprend &eacute;galement l&#39;ajout de nouveaux socles &eacute;lectriques et de points de raccordement pour les &eacute;v&eacute;nements &agrave; des endroits cl&eacute;s du PJCN, en tenant compte des besoins futurs en mati&egrave;re d&#39;&eacute;v&eacute;nements et du paysage actuel du parc. Hydro-Qu&eacute;bec r&eacute;alisera tous les travaux sur son r&eacute;seau de distribution, y compris le d&eacute;placement d&#39;une ligne de service existante, et se limitera aux zones d&eacute;j&agrave; perturb&eacute;es. Un entrepreneur retenu par la CCN installera l&#39;infrastructure &eacute;lectrique du PJCN et les raccordements &eacute;lectriques &agrave; l&#39;int&eacute;rieur du PJCN. L&#39;empreinte du projet &agrave; proximit&eacute; des arbres existants sera r&eacute;duite au minimum et l&#39;excavation par hydro-aspiration sera utilis&eacute;e plut&ocirc;t que les m&eacute;thodes de tranch&eacute;e ouverte dans les zones racinaires des arbres afin de minimiser les impacts.

&nbsp;

Ces mises &agrave; niveau &eacute;lectriques sont n&eacute;cessaires pour r&eacute;pondre aux besoins &eacute;nerg&eacute;tiques modernes des grands &eacute;v&eacute;nements et r&eacute;duire la d&eacute;pendance aux g&eacute;n&eacute;rateurs temporaires. Une fois achev&eacute;, le nouveau syst&egrave;me fournira une capacit&eacute; &eacute;lectrique fiable et &eacute;tendue pour r&eacute;pondre aux besoins actuels et futurs du PJCN en mati&egrave;re de programmation.

&nbsp;

La CCN doit d&eacute;terminer si ce projet est susceptible d&#39;avoir des effets n&eacute;gatifs importants sur l&#39;environnement en vertu des articles 81 &agrave; 91 de la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact (2019) et de la Loi sur la capitale nationale (1985). Une approbation f&eacute;d&eacute;rale de l&#39;utilisation du sol et du design (AFUSD) est requise pour ces travaux.

&nbsp;

La mise en &oelig;uvre du projet devrait d&eacute;buter au printemps 2026 et s&#39;achever en d&eacute;cembre 2026, apr&egrave;s la coordination finale de la conception avec Hydro-Qu&eacute;bec et la s&eacute;lection d&#39;entrepreneurs qualifi&eacute;s.

properties.description_en:
Xaxli&#39;p Development LP has partnered with Salish Elements to form the Xaxli&#39;p Salish&nbsp;Limited Partnership (XSLP) with plans to build a 51% Xaxli&#39;p-owned green energy&nbsp;utility to produce liquified hydrogen fuel.

&nbsp;

This will require a Lease of Lot 9-2-1 on Fountain IR1B to XSLP for the purpose of a green hydrogen production facility.

&nbsp;

Xaxli&#39;pmec will vote on Monday, January&nbsp;26, 2026, to determine if Lot 9-2-1 Fountain&nbsp;IR 1B will be designated for lease to the&nbsp;Xaxli&#39;p Salish LP for 99 years. The land&nbsp;vote follows a formal process set out by&nbsp;Indigenous Services Canada (ISC).

&nbsp;

Hydrogen will be created through the electrolysis method, which involves running an electric current through&nbsp;water to separate the hydrogen and oxygen molecules.&nbsp; If the electricity used in the electrolysis&nbsp;process comes from a renewable source (such as hydro, wind, and solar), this kind of hydrogen&nbsp;can be called green hydrogen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Energy can then be produced using a fuel cell: a device that generates electricity from&nbsp;the energy released by turning hydrogen fuel and oxygen (from the air) into water. Fuel cells&nbsp;can be small enough to power a vehicle, including cars, trucks, and ships, or large enough to&nbsp;provide power to a whole community.

&nbsp;

Construction will include the hydrogen facility, parking, and all associated infrastructure such as water and wastewater connections, hydro, and telecommunications.&nbsp; It is not yet determined where the water will be sourced for the electrolysis (water servicing vs. other source such as a watercourse), and where the treated discharge water will outlet (to ground vs. to the river).&nbsp; These details will develop as the project proceeds through the environmental review process.

&nbsp;

Construction is anticipated to take an&nbsp;estimated two years to complete the&nbsp;hydrogen production facility.

&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Xaxli&#39;p Development LP s&#39;est associ&eacute; &agrave; Salish Elements pour former la soci&eacute;t&eacute; en commandite Xaxli&#39;p Salish Limited Partnership (XSLP) dans le but de construire une centrale d&#39;&eacute;nergie verte d&eacute;tenue &agrave; 51 % par Xaxli&#39;p pour produire de l&#39;hydrog&egrave;ne liqu&eacute;fi&eacute;.

&nbsp;

Cela n&eacute;cessitera la location du lot 9-2-1 sur Fountain IR1B &agrave; XSLP afin d&#39;y installer une usine de production d&#39;hydrog&egrave;ne vert.

&nbsp;

Xaxli&#39;pmec votera le lundi 26 janvier 2026 afin de d&eacute;terminer si le lot 9-2-1 Fountain IR 1B sera lou&eacute; &agrave; Xaxli&#39;p Salish LP pour une dur&eacute;e de 99 ans. Le vote foncier suit un processus officiel &eacute;tabli par Services aux Autochtones Canada (SAC).

&nbsp;

L&#39;hydrog&egrave;ne sera produit par &eacute;lectrolyse, un proc&eacute;d&eacute; qui consiste &agrave; faire passer un courant &eacute;lectrique dans l&#39;eau afin de s&eacute;parer les mol&eacute;cules d&#39;hydrog&egrave;ne et d&#39;oxyg&egrave;ne. Si l&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute; utilis&eacute;e dans le processus d&#39;&eacute;lectrolyse provient d&#39;une source renouvelable (telle que l&#39;hydro&eacute;lectricit&eacute;, l&#39;&eacute;nergie &eacute;olienne et l&#39;&eacute;nergie solaire), ce type d&#39;hydrog&egrave;ne peut &ecirc;tre qualifi&eacute; d&#39;hydrog&egrave;ne vert.

&nbsp;

L&#39;&eacute;nergie peut ensuite &ecirc;tre produite &agrave; l&#39;aide d&#39;une pile &agrave; combustible : un dispositif qui g&eacute;n&egrave;re de l&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute; &agrave; partir de l&#39;&eacute;nergie lib&eacute;r&eacute;e par la transformation de l&#39;hydrog&egrave;ne et de l&#39;oxyg&egrave;ne (provenant de l&#39;air) en eau. Les piles &agrave; combustible peuvent &ecirc;tre suffisamment petites pour alimenter un v&eacute;hicule, notamment une voiture, un camion ou un navire, ou suffisamment grandes pour alimenter toute une communaut&eacute;.

&nbsp;

La construction comprendra l&#39;installation d&#39;hydrog&egrave;ne, un parking et toutes les infrastructures associ&eacute;es telles que les raccordements &agrave; l&#39;eau et aux eaux us&eacute;es, l&#39;hydro&eacute;lectricit&eacute; et les t&eacute;l&eacute;communications. &nbsp;Il n&#39;a pas encore &eacute;t&eacute; d&eacute;termin&eacute; d&#39;o&ugrave; proviendra l&#39;eau utilis&eacute;e pour l&#39;&eacute;lectrolyse (approvisionnement en eau ou autre source telle qu&#39;un cours d&#39;eau) et o&ugrave; les eaux us&eacute;es trait&eacute;es seront rejet&eacute;es (dans le sol ou dans la rivi&egrave;re). &nbsp;Ces d&eacute;tails seront pr&eacute;cis&eacute;s au fur et &agrave; mesure que le projet avancera dans le processus d&#39;&eacute;valuation environnementale.

&nbsp;

La construction de l&#39;installation de production d&#39;hydrog&egrave;ne devrait prendre environ deux ans.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
Marathon Gold Corporation is proposing the construction, operation, decommissioning, and reclamation of an open-pit gold mine and on-site mill located at Valentine Lake, approximately 55 kilometres southwest of Millertown in Newfoundland and Labrador. As proposed, the Valentine Gold Project would include three open pits, disposal piles, crushing and stockpiling areas, site infrastructure, a tailings management facility, and mine site haul and access roads. Production capacity is estimated at 10,960 tonnes per day of high- and low-grade ore, over a planned operation of about 14 years.

&nbsp;

Please note that the proponent was formerly known as Calibre Mining Corp.

properties.description_fr:
Marathon Gold Corporation propose la construction, l&#39;exploitation, la d&eacute;saffectation et la remise en &eacute;tat d&#39;une mine d&#39;or &agrave; ciel ouvert et d&apos;une usine de traitement sur place, situ&eacute;es au lac Valentine, &agrave; environ 55 kilom&egrave;tres au sud-ouest de Millertown, &agrave; Terre-Neuve-et-Labrador. Tel qu&#39;il est propos&eacute;, le projet aurif&egrave;re de Valentine comprendra trois mines &agrave; ciel ouvert, des haldes &agrave; st&eacute;riles, des aires de concassage et d&#39;entreposage, l&#39;infrastructure du site, une installation de gestion des r&eacute;sidus ainsi que des routes de transport et d&#39;acc&egrave;s au site minier. La capacit&eacute; de production est estim&eacute;e &agrave; 10 960 tonnes de minerai &agrave; haute et faible teneur par jour, sur une p&eacute;riode d&apos;exploitation pr&eacute;vue d&apos;environ 14 ans.

&nbsp;

Veuillez noter que le promoteur &eacute;tait pr&eacute;c&eacute;demment intitul&eacute; Calibre Mining Corp.

properties.description_en:
The proposed project will include the construction of a lined, mine water retention pond to aid in ongoing mine water management.&nbsp; The proposed pond will be constructed off of Camerons Lane in New Victoria, Cape Breton Regional Municipality, in Nova Scotia.&nbsp; The project will consist of clearing and grubbing of an area of small trees and scrub brush that will measure approximately 4,800 sqm in size.&nbsp; The contractor will excavate the cleared area saving the top 0.5m of material as overburden and excavate an additional 2m-2.5m in depth and using this material to construct the earthen berms of the retention pond, complete with 2:1 side slopes on the water side and 3:1 side slope on the outer side. The footprint of the completed pond will measure approximately 1,500sqm and will have a capacity of approximately 2,000 meters cubed of water.&nbsp; The project will also consist of the construction of a small, slab on grade, electrical control building measuring approximately 3.1m by 3.7m in size, the installation of 250 meters of 3&quot; (7.6cm) diameter PVC pipe from existing well to the proposed pond, as well as the extension of existing electrical supply lines on site to the proposed new building.&nbsp; 

&nbsp;

Water will be held in the retention pond and monitored.&nbsp; Water will be monitored for metals, acidity, and general chemistry. Toxicity testing would also be completed on the water.&nbsp; If water sample results meet background conditions, the mine water would be discharged through a 500mm discharge pipe out of the wall of the pond (with a boot welded to the liner) and then into a rock lined drain to a large on-site wetland. &nbsp;The flow is estimated to be approximately 50USgpm to a maximum of 100USgpm.

properties.description_fr:
Le projet propos&eacute; comprendra la construction d&#39;un bassin de r&eacute;tention des eaux de mine avec rev&ecirc;tement afin de faciliter la gestion continue des eaux de mine. Le bassin propos&eacute; sera construit pr&egrave;s de Camerons Lane, &agrave; New Victoria, dans la municipalit&eacute; r&eacute;gionale du Cap-Breton, en Nouvelle-&Eacute;cosse. Le projet comprendra le d&eacute;frichage et l&#39;essouchement d&#39;une zone d&#39;environ 4&nbsp;800 m&sup2;, peupl&eacute;e de petits arbres et de broussailles. L&#39;entrepreneur excavera la zone d&eacute;gag&eacute;e en conservant les 0,5 m sup&eacute;rieurs de mat&eacute;riaux comme morts-terrains et en creusant une profondeur suppl&eacute;mentaire de 2 &agrave; 2,5 m. Ces mat&eacute;riaux serviront &agrave; construire les talus du bassin de r&eacute;tention, avec des pentes lat&eacute;rales de 2:1 c&ocirc;t&eacute; eau et de 3:1 c&ocirc;t&eacute; ext&eacute;rieur. L&#39;emprise au sol du bassin une fois termin&eacute; mesurera environ 1&nbsp;500 m&sup2; et aura une capacit&eacute; d&#39;environ 2&nbsp;000 m&sup3; d&#39;eau. Le projet comprendra &eacute;galement la construction d&#39;un petit b&acirc;timent de contr&ocirc;le &eacute;lectrique sur dalle mesurant environ 3,1 m sur 3,7 m, l&#39;installation de 250 m&egrave;tres de tuyaux en PVC de 3 po (7,6 cm) de diam&egrave;tre du puits existant jusqu&#39;&agrave; l&#39;&eacute;tang propos&eacute;, ainsi que l&#39;extension des lignes d&#39;alimentation &eacute;lectrique existantes sur place jusqu&#39;au nouveau b&acirc;timent propos&eacute;.

&nbsp;

L&#39;eau sera retenue dans le bassin de r&eacute;tention et surveill&eacute;e. La teneur en m&eacute;taux, l&#39;acidit&eacute; et les caract&eacute;ristiques chimiques g&eacute;n&eacute;rales seront contr&ocirc;l&eacute;es. Des analyses de toxicit&eacute; seront &eacute;galement effectu&eacute;es. Si les r&eacute;sultats des &eacute;chantillons d&#39;eau sont conformes aux conditions ambiantes, l&#39;eau de la mine sera rejet&eacute;e par une conduite de 500 mm hors de la paroi du bassin (avec un manchon soud&eacute; &agrave; la membrane), puis dans un drain enrochement jusqu&#39;&agrave; une grande zone humide sur le site. Le d&eacute;bit est estim&eacute; &agrave; environ 50 gallons US/min et un maximum de 100 gallons US/min.

properties.description_en:
The National Capital Commission (NCC) is undertaking a re-naturalization initiative west of Boulevard St. Joseph in Gatineau, Quebec to improve ecological integrity and address pathway infrastructure challenges. As part of this effort, a short 20-meter segment of the Leamy Creek multi-use pathway is proposed for removal and re-naturalization. In addition, to support safety, a small &le;1 m2 section of manicured grass will be converted to asphalt pathway to allow for safe navigation of the pathway intersection for cyclists (the Project). 

&nbsp;

The scope of the Project will include cutting and removing asphalt and the granular base of the existing pathway as well as the removal of a corrugated steel pipe culvert and associated culvert infrastructure (i.e., granular base and inlet and outlet armour wall) at the south extent of the 20-meter segment of pathway to be removed. Following the culvert removal, the area will be graded to match upstream and downstream conditions. Topsoil will replace the existing granular for the pathway segment and the disturbed culvert area and a natural wet meadow seed mix will be applied to match surrounding natural environment existing conditions. The removal of the culvert will not affect hydrology, since the intermittent watercourse morphology and downstream flow will be maintained.

&nbsp;

With the exception to the minor addition of asphalt to ensure cyclist safety and the culvert works, all activities will be confined to the existing footprint of the asphalt multi-use pathway. Due to the Project&#39;s location within the Phil&eacute;mon-Leamy Corridor Critical Habitat area of the Western Chorus Frog (Pseudacris triseriata) (Great Lakes / St. Lawrence - Canadian Shield population) and the potential for individuals to be incidentally present within vicinity of the Project area, a Species at Risk Act, 2002 (SARA) permit may be required. The Project is expected to benefit the Western Chorus Frog by facilitating the creation of a net addition of new terrestrial habitat.

&nbsp;

The Project works are planned to be of short duration and will be scheduled when Western Chorus Frog is expected to occupy breeding ponds and not the potential terrestrial habitat areas for feeding or movement adjacent to the Project footprint. Therefore, implementation will be targeted&nbsp;for either&nbsp;(April 01 &ndash; June 01) when WCF will not be within the potential terrestrial habitat areas or when individuals are expected to occupy hibernation habitat (October 01 &ndash; March 01) thereby reducing potential disturbances or species interactions.

&nbsp;

The NCC and Environment and Climate Change Canada must&nbsp;determine&nbsp;whether this project is likely to cause significant adverse environmental effects under&nbsp;sections 81-91 of the&nbsp;Impact Assessment Act&nbsp;(2019)&nbsp;and the&nbsp;National Capital Act&nbsp;(1985).

properties.description_fr:
La Commission de la capitale nationale (CCN) entreprend une initiative de renaturalisation &agrave; l&#39;ouest du boulevard Saint-Joseph &agrave; Gatineau, au Qu&eacute;bec, afin d&#39;am&eacute;liorer l&#39;int&eacute;grit&eacute; &eacute;cologique et de relever les d&eacute;fis li&eacute;s &agrave; l&#39;infrastructure des sentiers. Dans le cadre de cette initiative, il est propos&eacute; de supprimer et de renaturaliser un court tron&ccedil;on de 20 m&egrave;tres de la piste polyvalente du ruisseau Leamy. De plus, pour des raisons de s&eacute;curit&eacute;, une petite section de gazon entretenu de &le;1 m2 sera convertie en piste asphalt&eacute;e afin de permettre aux cyclistes de circuler en toute s&eacute;curit&eacute; &agrave; l&#39;intersection de la piste (le projet).

&nbsp;

Le projet comprendra la d&eacute;coupe et l&#39;enl&egrave;vement de l&#39;asphalte et de la base granulaire de la piste existante, ainsi que l&#39;enl&egrave;vement d&#39;un ponceau en acier ondul&eacute; et de l&#39;infrastructure associ&eacute;e (c&#39;est-&agrave;-dire la base granulaire et les parois de protection &agrave; l&#39;entr&eacute;e et &agrave; la sortie) &agrave; l&#39;extr&eacute;mit&eacute; sud du tron&ccedil;on de 20 m&egrave;tres de la piste &agrave; enlever. Apr&egrave;s l&#39;enl&egrave;vement du ponceau, la zone sera nivel&eacute;e pour correspondre aux conditions en amont et en aval. La terre v&eacute;g&eacute;tale remplacera le granulat existant pour le segment de piste et la zone perturb&eacute;e du ponceau, et un m&eacute;lange de semences de prairie humide naturelle sera appliqu&eacute; afin de correspondre aux conditions existantes de l&#39;environnement naturel environnant. L&#39;enl&egrave;vement du ponceau n&#39;aura aucune incidence sur l&#39;hydrologie, puisque la morphologie intermittente du cours d&#39;eau et le d&eacute;bit en aval seront maintenus.

&nbsp;

&Agrave; l&#39;exception de l&#39;ajout mineur d&#39;asphalte pour assurer la s&eacute;curit&eacute; des cyclistes et des travaux sur le ponceau, toutes les activit&eacute;s seront confin&eacute;es &agrave; l&#39;empreinte existante de la piste polyvalente asphalt&eacute;e. En raison de l&#39;emplacement du projet dans la zone d&#39;habitat essentiel du corridor Phil&eacute;mon-Leamy de la rainette faux-grillon de l&#39;Ouest (Pseudacris triseriata) (population des Grands Lacs / Saint-Laurent et du Bouclier canadien) et de la possibilit&eacute; que des individus soient accidentellement pr&eacute;sents &agrave; proximit&eacute; de la zone du projet, un permis en vertu de la Loi sur les esp&egrave;ces en p&eacute;ril de 2002 (LEP) pourrait &ecirc;tre n&eacute;cessaire. Le projet devrait profiter &agrave; la rainette faux-grillon de l&#39;Ouest en facilitant la cr&eacute;ation d&#39;un ajout net de nouveaux habitats terrestres.

&nbsp;

Les travaux du projet devraient &ecirc;tre de courte dur&eacute;e et seront programm&eacute;s lorsque la rainette faux-grillon de l&#39;Ouest devrait occuper les &eacute;tangs de reproduction et non les zones d&#39;habitat terrestre potentielles pour se nourrir ou se d&eacute;placer &agrave; proximit&eacute; de l&#39;empreinte du projet. Par cons&eacute;quent, la mise en &oelig;uvre se fera soit entre le 1er avril et le 1er juin, lorsque la rainette faux-grillon de l&#39;Ouest ne se trouvera pas dans les zones d&#39;habitat terrestre potentiel, soit entre le 1er octobre et le 1er mars, lorsque les individus devraient occuper leur habitat d&#39;hibernation, r&eacute;duisant ainsi les perturbations potentielles ou les interactions entre les esp&egrave;ces.

&nbsp;

La CCN et Environnement et Changement climatique Canada doivent d&eacute;terminer si ce projet est susceptible d&#39;avoir des effets n&eacute;gatifs importants sur l&#39;environnement en vertu des articles 81 &agrave; 91 de la&nbsp;Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact&nbsp;(2019) et de la&nbsp;Loi sur la capitale nationale&nbsp;(1985).

properties.description_en:
The Mink River Small Craft Harbour (SCH)&#39;s configuration is characterized by rigid and floating wharf infrastructure that extends from the upland to the north and south of the property to form an enclosed basin. The southern wharf is a combination of an outer pier and inner marginal structure with multiple construction types that were all built over 50 years ago.&nbsp; As such, all of this wharf infrastructure is at the end of its service life and requires complete replacement.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The southern wharf consists of four (4) conjoined structures including an outer timber pile section (SCH Facility Number (#) 401) measuring approximately 16.2 m in length and 11.5 m in width with a timber deck system.&nbsp; The inner structures (#402, #404, and #406) consist of a timber pile and embedded sheathing wall construction around a remnant timber cribwork, core stone infill and an asphalt and gravel travel surface.&nbsp; The most inner section of wharf transitions to the gravel service area (#920) with a concrete launching ramp (#501) located inside the harbour basin directly adjacent to the wharf approach.

&nbsp;

The proposed new wharf will be approximately 99 m long and comprised of an outer pier section measuring 80 m in length and 13.7 m in width as well as an inner marginal section 19 m long.&nbsp; The reconstruction will initially involve the complete demolition of wharf #401 and partial removals of the inner wharf components with the bottom of the remnant timber cribwork remaining in place.&nbsp; The perimeter of the demolished structures will be encapsulated by a new king pile wall structure (i.e., steel H piles and concrete panels commonly referred to as a Berlin Wall).&nbsp; It will be constructed along the same alignment as the existing wharf structures, but offset by approximately 1.0 m to facilitate the new construction.&nbsp; The H piles will be driven in place with the sides of the new 80 m-long outer pier section braced across near the top with steel tie rods.&nbsp; The end of the pier wall as well as the inner 19 m-long marginal wharf section will be tied back to concrete anchor blocks for lateral stability.&nbsp; Pre-cast concrete panels will be lowered in place between the piles, the new structure will be backfilled with core stone with a new gravel surface gravel layer placed on top.&nbsp; A layer of rip rap will be placed all along the outside perimeter of the new walls for scour protection.&nbsp; The reconstructed wharf will be raised approximately 1.9 m and constructed to an elevation of 3.75 m above chart datum for adaptation to projected sea-level rise and prevent overtopping in storm conditions.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The construction will also include a new 30 m-long freestanding retaining wall along the inside of the wharf approach, adjacent to the launching ramp.&nbsp; This wall will consist of steel H-piles driven to bedrock, with treated timber lagging installed between the upper 2 m of the pile webs, providing a stable transition to the existing service area.

&nbsp;

The work is expected to be conducted using large commercial vehicles and equipment for heavy civil construction such as excavators, cranes, front-end loaders, and trucks operating from the upland and existing structures.&nbsp; Upland areas of the SCH will likely be used as a staging area for equipment storage and as a lay-down area for demolition and construction materials (treated timber, steel piles, and concrete panels).

&nbsp;

Construction activities may commence as early as September 2026, however actual project commencement is subject to DFO-SCH operational priorities and funding, as well as the completion of regulatory approval processes.&nbsp; The scope of the environmental effects determination (subject to S.82 of the Impact Assessment Act) will, therefore, be based on the works being completed over a period of 18 months commencing within a period of 5 years following the determination of significance of environmental effects.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The Mink River SCH is a core fishing harbour that was developed to serve the fishing industry in the area.&nbsp; The harbour currently has considerable marine infrastructure and remains well situated and protected to support both the commercial fishing and aquaculture industries.&nbsp; Given its sheltered location, there is minimal ice cover in the winter and with the proximity to mussel leases, the harbour operates year-round.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The main purpose of this project is to carry out reconstruction of the existing infrastructure so that the harbour can continue to serve the fishing and aquaculture industries.&nbsp; The southern wharf is an integral component of the overall harbour infrastructure as a service and berthing facility as well as providing harbour protection and access for land-based dredging equipment.&nbsp; Given that the existing infrastructure is well beyond its service life, the status quo of leaving the deteriorated wharf structures available and in use is not currently a viable option.&nbsp; DFO-SCH considered design alternatives and selected the king pile structure option as the most technical and economically feasible construction approach.

properties.description_fr:
La configuration du port pour petits bateaux (PPB) de Mink River est caract&eacute;ris&eacute;e par des infrastructures de quai fixes et flottantes qui s&#39;&eacute;tendent depuis les terrains en amont, au nord et au sud de la propri&eacute;t&eacute;, afin de former un bassin ferm&eacute;. Le quai sud constitue une combinaison d&#39;un quai ext&eacute;rieur et d&#39;une structure marginale int&eacute;rieure, comprenant plusieurs types de construction qui ont tous &eacute;t&eacute; r&eacute;alis&eacute;s il y a plus de 50 ans. Par cons&eacute;quent, l&#39;ensemble de cette infrastructure de quai a atteint la fin de sa dur&eacute;e de vie utile et n&eacute;cessite un remplacement complet.

&nbsp;

Le quai sud est compos&eacute; de quatre (4) structures jointes, dont une section ext&eacute;rieure sur pieux de bois (installation du PPB num&eacute;ro (no.) 401) mesurant environ 16,2 m de longueur et 11,5 m de largeur, avec un tablier en bois. Les structures int&eacute;rieures (no. 402, no. 404 et no. 406) sont constitu&eacute;es d&#39;une construction sur pieux de bois et d&#39;un mur de palplanches int&eacute;gr&eacute;es autour d&#39;un vestige de caisson en bois, avec un remplissage de pierre de noyau et une surface de roulement en asphalte et en gravier. La section la plus int&eacute;rieure du quai fait la transition vers l&#39;aire de service en gravier (no. 920), avec une rampe de mise &agrave; l&#39;eau en b&eacute;ton (no. 501) situ&eacute;e &agrave; l&#39;int&eacute;rieur du bassin du havre, directement adjacente &agrave; l&#39;approche du quai.

&nbsp;

Le nouveau quai propos&eacute; aura une longueur approximative de 99 m et sera compos&eacute; d&#39;une section de quai ext&eacute;rieur de 80 m de longueur et de 13,7 m de largeur, ainsi que d&#39;une section marginale int&eacute;rieure de 19 m de longueur. La reconstruction comprendra d&#39;abord la d&eacute;molition compl&egrave;te du quai no. 401 et l&#39;enl&egrave;vement partiel des composantes int&eacute;rieures du quai, le fond du caisson en bois existant demeurant en place. Le p&eacute;rim&egrave;tre des structures d&eacute;molies sera encapsul&eacute; par une nouvelle structure de mur &agrave; pieux principaux (c.-&agrave;-d. des pieux en H d&#39;acier et des panneaux de b&eacute;ton, commun&eacute;ment appel&eacute;s mur de type &laquo; Berlin &raquo;). Cette structure sera construite selon le m&ecirc;me alignement que les quais existants, mais avec un d&eacute;calage d&#39;environ 1,0 m afin de faciliter les nouveaux travaux. Les pieux en H seront battus en place, et les c&ocirc;t&eacute;s de la nouvelle section de quai ext&eacute;rieur de 80 m de longueur seront contrevent&eacute;s pr&egrave;s du sommet &agrave; l&#39;aide de tirants d&#39;acier. L&#39;extr&eacute;mit&eacute; du mur du quai, de m&ecirc;me que la section marginale int&eacute;rieure de 19 m de longueur, seront ancr&eacute;es &agrave; des blocs d&#39;ancrage en b&eacute;ton afin d&#39;assurer la stabilit&eacute; lat&eacute;rale. Des panneaux de b&eacute;ton pr&eacute;fabriqu&eacute;s seront mis en place entre les pieux, la nouvelle structure sera remblay&eacute;e avec de la pierre de noyau, puis une nouvelle couche de surface en gravier sera ajout&eacute;e. Une couche d&#39;enrochement sera mise en place sur tout le p&eacute;rim&egrave;tre ext&eacute;rieur des nouveaux murs afin d&#39;assurer la protection contre l&#39;affouillement. Le quai reconstruit sera rehauss&eacute; d&#39;environ 1,9 m et construit &agrave; une &eacute;l&eacute;vation de 3,75 m au-dessus du z&eacute;ro des cartes marines, afin de s&#39;adapter &agrave; l&#39;&eacute;l&eacute;vation projet&eacute;e du niveau de la mer et de pr&eacute;venir le surversement lors de conditions de temp&ecirc;te.

&nbsp;

Les travaux comprendront &eacute;galement la construction d&#39;un nouveau mur de sout&egrave;nement autoportant d&#39;environ 30 m de longueur le long de l&#39;int&eacute;rieur de l&#39;approche du quai, adjacent &agrave; la rampe de mise &agrave; l&#39;eau. Ce mur sera compos&eacute; de pieux en H d&#39;acier enfonc&eacute;s jusqu&#39;au substratum rocheux, avec des madriers en bois trait&eacute; install&eacute;s entre les &acirc;mes des pieux sur les 2 m sup&eacute;rieurs, assurant une transition stable vers l&#39;aire de service existante.

&nbsp;

Les travaux devraient &ecirc;tre r&eacute;alis&eacute;s &agrave; l&#39;aide de v&eacute;hicules commerciaux lourds et d&#39;&eacute;quipements de construction civile lourde, tels que des excavatrices, des grues, des chargeuses frontales et des camions, op&eacute;rant depuis les zones en amont et les structures existantes. Les zones en amont du PPB seront vraisemblablement utilis&eacute;es &nbsp;comme aires de mise en place pour l&#39;entreposage de l&#39;&eacute;quipement ainsi que comme zones de d&eacute;p&ocirc;t pour les mat&eacute;riaux de d&eacute;molition et de construction (bois trait&eacute;, les pieux d&#39;acier et les panneaux de b&eacute;ton).

&nbsp;

Les travaux de construction pourraient d&eacute;buter d&egrave;s septembre 2026; toutefois, le d&eacute;marrage r&eacute;el du projet d&eacute;pend des priorit&eacute;s op&eacute;rationnelles et du financement de MPO-PPB, ainsi que de l&#39;approbation r&eacute;glementaire. L&#39;&eacute;valuation des effets environnementaux (sujet &agrave; l&#39;article 82 de la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact) tiendra donc compte de la r&eacute;alisation des travaux sur une p&eacute;riode de 18 mois d&eacute;butant dans les 5 ans suivant la d&eacute;termination de la port&eacute;e des effets environnementaux.

&nbsp;

Le PPB de Mink River est un port de p&ecirc;che principal qui a &eacute;t&eacute; am&eacute;nag&eacute; pour desservir l&#39;industrie de la p&ecirc;che dans la r&eacute;gion. Le havre dispose actuellement d&#39;importantes infrastructures maritimes et demeure bien situ&eacute; et prot&eacute;g&eacute; pour soutenir les industries de la p&ecirc;che commerciale et de l&#39;aquaculture. En raison de son emplacement abrit&eacute;, la couverture de glace y est minimale en hiver et, compte tenu de la proximit&eacute; des concessions mytilicoles, le havre est exploit&eacute; toute l&#39;ann&eacute;e.

&nbsp;

L&#39;objectif principal de ce projet est de proc&eacute;der &agrave; la reconstruction des infrastructures existantes afin que le havre puisse continuer &agrave; desservir les industries de la p&ecirc;che et de l&#39;aquaculture. Le quai sud constitue un &eacute;l&eacute;ment essentiel de l&#39;infrastructure globale du havre, tant comme installation de service et d&#39;accostage que pour assurer la protection du havre et l&#39;acc&egrave;s aux &eacute;quipements de dragage terrestres. &Eacute;tant donn&eacute; que l&#39;infrastructure existante a largement d&eacute;pass&eacute; sa dur&eacute;e de vie utile, le maintien du statu quo, soit laisser les structures de quai d&eacute;t&eacute;rior&eacute;es disponibles et en service, ne constitue pas une option viable &agrave; l&#39;heure actuelle. P&ecirc;ches et Oc&eacute;ans Canada &ndash; Ports pour petits bateaux (MPO-PPB) a examin&eacute; diff&eacute;rentes options de conception et a retenu la solution de structure &agrave; pieux principaux comme l&#39;approche de construction la plus r&eacute;alisable sur les plans technique et &eacute;conomique.

properties.description_en:
Tsuut&#39;ina Nation is proposing to construct a deep sanitary sewer line along Bullhead road. The proposed sewer line will service existing community buildings including the community hall, the fire station, Sarcee townsite and the museum as well as the future medical center.&nbsp; The sewer line will run from the site of the proposed medical center along Bullhead road to the museum. The sewer line will be approximately 5.5 km long with a 20 meter wide right of way. There will be a total of 33 manholes and one lift station on route.&nbsp;

Site preparation will include the removal of shrubs and trees from the ditch next to the road. All trees will be retained on reserve for community use. The project will also require the removal of some fencing, the stripping of topsoil, trenching, and excavation. Directional drilling will be used to cross existing roads and to tie into services along the route. The sewer line will cut through a portion of undeveloped land northwest of the Museum where a 5m wide gravel road will be developed beside the pipeline to allow for servicing of three manholes proposed in that area.

Indigenous Services Canada is providing funding under the Capital Facilities and Maintenance Program (CFMP). The project is not located near any waterbodies and is not expected to impact any species at risk. Tree and shrub removal will be completed outside of bird nesting and rearing timeframes. Disturbed areas will be re-seeded with native species upon completion of the work.

properties.description_fr:
La nation Tsuut&#39;ina propose de construire une canalisation d&#39;&eacute;gout sanitaire profonde le long de Bullhead Road. La canalisation d&#39;&eacute;gout propos&eacute;e desservira les b&acirc;timents communautaires existants, notamment la salle communautaire, la caserne de pompiers, le village de Sarcee et le mus&eacute;e, ainsi que le futur centre m&eacute;dical.&nbsp; La canalisation d&#39;&eacute;gout s&#39;&eacute;tendra du site du centre m&eacute;dical propos&eacute; le long de Bullhead Road jusqu&#39;au mus&eacute;e. Elle aura une longueur d&#39;environ 5,5 km et une emprise de 20 m&egrave;tres de large. Il y aura au total 33 regards d&#39;&eacute;gout et une station de relevage sur le trac&eacute;.&nbsp;

La pr&eacute;paration du site comprendra l&#39;enl&egrave;vement des arbustes et des arbres du foss&eacute; situ&eacute; &agrave; c&ocirc;t&eacute; de la route. Tous les arbres seront conserv&eacute;s dans la r&eacute;serve pour &ecirc;tre utilis&eacute;s par la communaut&eacute;. Le projet n&eacute;cessitera &eacute;galement l&#39;enl&egrave;vement de certaines cl&ocirc;tures, le d&eacute;capage de la couche arable, le creusement de tranch&eacute;es et des travaux d&#39;excavation. Un forage directionnel sera utilis&eacute; pour traverser les routes existantes et raccorder les services le long du trac&eacute;. La canalisation d&#39;&eacute;gout traversera une partie du terrain non am&eacute;nag&eacute; au nord-ouest du mus&eacute;e, o&ugrave; une route en gravier de 5 m de large sera am&eacute;nag&eacute;e &agrave; c&ocirc;t&eacute; de la canalisation afin de permettre l&#39;entretien des trois regards propos&eacute;s dans cette zone.

Services aux Autochtones Canada fournit un financement dans le cadre du Programme des immobilisations et de l&#39;entretien (PIE). Le projet n&#39;est situ&eacute; &agrave; proximit&eacute; d&#39;aucun plan d&#39;eau et ne devrait avoir aucune incidence sur les esp&egrave;ces en p&eacute;ril. L&#39;enl&egrave;vement des arbres et des arbustes sera effectu&eacute; en dehors des p&eacute;riodes de nidification et d&#39;&eacute;levage des oiseaux. Les zones perturb&eacute;es seront r&eacute;ensemenc&eacute;es avec des esp&egrave;ces indig&egrave;nes &agrave; la fin des travaux.

properties.description_en:
The Chaudi&egrave;re Crossing, the oldest crossing in the National Capital Region, remains a critical link between Ottawa, Ontario, and Gatineau, Quebec. It is a complex infrastructure asset consisting of 8 structures. Recent inspections and studies show that the southern structures of the Chaudi&egrave;re Crossing need repair and replacement work to keep the crossing safe for users.

The southern structures of the Chaudi&egrave;re Crossing will be renewed by Public Services and Procurement Canada (PSPC). This overarching renewal project includes replacing the Bronson Channel Bridge, rehabilitating the Ottawa Hydro Electric Power Commission Channel Bridge (Power Channel Bridge) substructures and replacing the Power Channel Bridge superstructure, and rehabilitating the Buchanan Channel Culvert. To facilitate this work, the existing utility infrastructure owned by Hydro Ottawa, Bell and Enbridge, which are currently supported on the southern structures, must be temporarily removed from the structures and relocated to a suitable alternative location.

This specific component of the southern structures of the Chaudi&egrave;re Crossing project involves constructing a temporary shared alternate path for Hydro Ottawa, Bell, and Enbridge. A utility truss bridge, founded on bedrock at both ends of the structure on federal land owned and managed by the National Capital Commission (NCC), will be built to span the Bronson Channel on the east side of the existing Bronson Channel Bridge. From the southern project limits at Booth St to the utility truss bridge, a common trench will house underground conduits and a gas line for rerouting the utilities. The utilities will then cross the Bronson Channel, supported on the utility truss. The common trench will continue on the north side of the truss bridge to cross Middle St. Beyond Middle St, the utilities will be surface-mounted, with a bond breaker placed over the existing building foundation before installation. To cross the Power Channel, steel conduits and a gas line will be surface-mounted on the intake channel walls and across the GS#4 generating station intake deck. Finally, all three utilities will reconnect to their original alignment at the northern project limit on Booth St. Coordination with PSPC to manage potential lane closures needed to remove the existing utility infrastructure will be required. The temporarily relocated infrastructure (including the utility truss) will be decommissioned once the renewal of the southern structures of the Chaudi&egrave;re Crossing project is completed by PSPC, and the utilities have been relocated to their permanent position on the southern structures.

The temporary utility infrastructure relocation on NCC lands is anticipated to commence in the summer/fall of 2025 and be completed prior to the winter of 2026.

The NCC lands where the infrastructure will be temporarily relocated include a segment on the southern shore of the Bronson Channel immediately east of Booth St and north of a multiuse pathway, and Victoria Island, a 5.6-hectare island located in the Ottawa River recognized as a place of special significance for the Algonquin Peoples. Victoria Island has a long history of mixed industrial, commercial and residential land uses dating back to the late 1800s. Soil, groundwater and sediment at the site are contaminated from these former land use activities. The NCC is currently remediating the site. The island will remain closed until the remediation is completed in 2028. Coordination will be required with the NCC as landowner and manager of the site remediation and other projects in the area.

The overarching renewal of the southern structures of the Chaudi&egrave;re Crossing project includes the reinstallation of the Hydro Ottawa, Bell and Enbridge infrastructure onto the rehabilitated and replaced structures on a long-term basis.

As the project proponent, owner and provider of funding and authorizations enabling the overarching infrastructure renewal, PSPC will be the lead authority responsible for coordinating the section 82 determination required under the Impact Assessment Act (IAA). As the provider of federal land and an approval under the National Capital Act to enable the temporary relocation of the infrastructure owned by Hydro Ottawa, Bell and Enbridge, the NCC also has a trigger to make a section 82 determination for this project component.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The Lac La Ronge Indian Band (LLRIB) is proposing to upgrade and expand it&#39;s current lagoon system. The existing two-cell facultative / exfiltration lagoon, located on provincial Crown land approximately 0.85 km southwest of Lac La Ronge and 0.4 km east of Demchenko Lake, provides wastewater treatment for the LLRIB reserves 156 and 156B and surrounding rural areas that utilize septic hauling. The lagoon is directly connected to the gravity sewer systems, pumping stations and force mains to provide wastewater service for Air Ronge and the LLRIB reserves 156 and 156B. Construction of the lagoon and upgrades occurred in 1996 and 1997. Based on the UMA 1998 record drawings, the existing lagoon primary cell with a soil bentonite liner has an area of 8.76 ha and a secondary cell that acts as an exfiltration cell with a portion of the treated effluent discharging bi-annually from the northeast corner of the facility into a muskeg wetland the length of which is approximately 900 m and located south of Lac La Ronge. The secondary cell with an effective volume of 222,000 m^3 having a reduced storage volume and is&nbsp; functioning as an exfiltration cell and lacks an engineered liner. The cells are divided by an earthen dyke. The primary cell has a liquid depth of 1.5 m, the secondary cell has a liquid depth of 2.1 m, both having a freeboard of 1.0 m. Upgrades to the existing lagoon system are necessary to provide adequate treatment and storage capacity for current and future needs up to the year 2046.

&nbsp;

Of the three options considered an aerated lagoon with nitrification using submerged attached growth reactor (SAGR) cells for a 10-year operational life cycle and continuous discharge is proposed.&nbsp; The proposed system consists of a lagoon wastewater building (blower building) with a coarse step-screening system, mechanical room, electrical room and blower room, connection to a new three-phase power line (undertaken by SaskPower), two partially mixed lagoon cells which are aerated with a positive displacement blower and oxygen diffusers which hang from floating laterals in the lagoon cell. The purpose of these cells is to provide oxygen and contact time for natural bacteria to convert contaminants (BOD5, ammonia, and TSS) to carbon dioxide, water, and inert ash and nitrates. Each of the two aeration cells are anticipated to be 16.245 hectares (ha) in size, occupying the existing primary and about half of the existing secondary cell. Each of the two SAGR cells will be 0.216 ha in size. The project will also include upgrades for sewage pumping system (SPS) #2 to manage septage receiving where the flow will pass through the coarse screen at the Lagoon Wastewater Building thereby eliminating a truck dump chute at the aerated cells.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
La bande indienne de Lac La Ronge (LLRIB) propose de moderniser et d&#39;agrandir son syst&egrave;me actuel de lagunes. Le lagon facultatif / d&#39;exfiltration &agrave; deux cellules existant, situ&eacute; sur les terres provinciales de la Couronne &agrave; environ 0,85 km au sud-ouest de Lac La Ronge et 0,4 km &agrave; l&#39;est du lac Demchenko, fournit le traitement des eaux us&eacute;es pour les r&eacute;serves LLRIB 156 et 156B ainsi que les zones rurales environnantes qui utilisent le transport de fosses septiques. Le lagon est directement reli&eacute; aux syst&egrave;mes d&#39;&eacute;gouts gravitaires, aux stations de pompage et aux conduites principales pour fournir le service d&#39;eaux us&eacute;es &agrave; Air Ronge et aux r&eacute;serves LLRIB 156 et 156B. La construction du lagon et les am&eacute;liorations ont eu lieu en 1996 et 1997. Selon les plans d&#39;enregistrement de l&#39;UMA de 1998, la cellule primaire existante du lagon avec un rev&ecirc;tement de bentonite du sol a une superficie de 8,76 ha et une cellule secondaire qui agit comme une cellule d&#39;exfiltration avec une portion de l&#39;effluent trait&eacute; se d&eacute;versant deux fois par an du coin nord-est de l&#39;installation dans une zone humide &agrave; mouches d&#39;environ 900 m de long, situ&eacute;e au sud du lac La Ronge. La cellule secondaire, avec un volume effectif de 222 000 m^3, a un volume de stockage r&eacute;duit et fonctionne comme une cellule d&#39;exfiltration et ne poss&egrave;de pas de rev&ecirc;tement modifi&eacute;. Les cellules sont divis&eacute;es par une digue de terre. La cellule primaire a une profondeur liquide de 1,5 m, la cellule secondaire une profondeur liquide de 2,1 m, toutes deux ayant un franc-bord de 1,0 m. Des am&eacute;liorations du syst&egrave;me lagunaire existant sont n&eacute;cessaires afin d&#39;assurer une capacit&eacute; ad&eacute;quate de traitement et de stockage pour les besoins actuels et futurs jusqu&#39;en 2046.

&nbsp;

Parmi les trois options envisag&eacute;es, un lagon a&eacute;r&eacute; avec nitrification utilisant des cellules de r&eacute;acteur de croissance submerg&eacute; attach&eacute; (SAGR) pour un cycle de vie op&eacute;rationnel de 10 ans et un d&eacute;bit continu est propos&eacute;.&nbsp; Le syst&egrave;me propos&eacute; comprend un b&acirc;timent d&#39;&eacute;gouts de lagune (b&acirc;timent de soufflage) avec un syst&egrave;me de filtrage &agrave; escaliers grossiers, une salle m&eacute;canique, une salle &eacute;lectrique et une salle de soufflage, une connexion &agrave; une nouvelle ligne &eacute;lectrique triphas&eacute;e (r&eacute;alis&eacute;e par SaskPower), deux cellules de lagon partiellement mixtes a&eacute;r&eacute;es avec un souffleur &agrave; d&eacute;placement positif et des diffuseurs d&#39;oxyg&egrave;ne suspendus &agrave; des lat&eacute;raux flottants dans la cellule lagunaire. Le but de ces cellules est de fournir de l&#39;oxyg&egrave;ne et du temps de contact aux bact&eacute;ries naturelles pour convertir les contaminants (BOD5, ammoniac et TSS) en dioxyde de carbone, eau, cendres et nitrates inertes. Chacune des deux cellules d&#39;a&eacute;ration devrait mesurer 16,245 hectares (ha), occupant la cellule primaire existante et environ la moiti&eacute; de la cellule secondaire existante. Chacune des deux cellules SAGR mesurera 0,216 ha de taille. Le projet comprendra &eacute;galement des am&eacute;liorations du syst&egrave;me de pompage des eaux us&eacute;es (SPS) #2 afin de g&eacute;rer la r&eacute;ception des s&eacute;verains l&agrave; o&ugrave; le d&eacute;bit passera &agrave; travers la grille grossi&egrave;re du b&acirc;timent des eaux us&eacute;es du Lagoon, &eacute;liminant ainsi une trappe de d&eacute;versement pour camions aux cellules a&eacute;r&eacute;es.

properties.description_en:
Piikani Resource Development Ltd. (PRDL) is proposing to develop the Piikani Wind Project on Piikani Nation reserve lands. The proposed project will have a capacity of 150 megawatts and will involve the construction of approximately 22-27 wind turbines and associated infrastructure. Associated infrastructure includes underground collector lines, access roads, a project collector substation, an operations and maintenance&nbsp; building, a temporary construction laydown area, and temporary crane paths.

&nbsp;

The Project area includes all or parts of 16 sections of land and is located on native grasslands currently used for grazing. There are several wetlands and intermittent watercourses in the project area but no navigable waters. Wildlife surveys indicate the presence of several listed Species at Risk including the little brown bat, the northern long-eared bat, Sprague&#39;s pipit, ferruginous hawk, long-billed curlew, and Baird&#39;s sparrow. No vegetation species listed under the Species at Risk Act were observed in the project area during the surveys.

&nbsp;

Indigenous Services Canada will be issuing an Indian Act land instrument for this project and is therefore required by Section 82 of the Impact Assessment Act to make a determination on the project&#39;s environmental effects. Prairies Economic Development Canada has provided funding for the feasibility stages of the project and is therefore not currently required to issue a determination but may become required to at a later stage.&nbsp;Power generated from the project will tie into the Alberta Interconnected Electrical System.

properties.description_fr:
Piikani Resource Development Ltd. (PRDL), propose de d&eacute;velopper le projet &eacute;olien Piikani sur les terres de la r&eacute;serve de la nation Piikani. Le projet propos&eacute; aura une capacit&eacute; de 150 m&eacute;gawatts et comprendra la construction d&#39;environ 22 &agrave; 27 &eacute;oliennes et des infrastructures associ&eacute;es. Les infrastructures connexes comprennent des lignes collectrices souterraines, des routes d&#39;acc&egrave;s, une sous-station collectrice, un b&acirc;timent d&#39;exploitation et d&#39;entretien, une aire de stockage temporaire pour la construction et des chemins de grue temporaires.

&nbsp;

La zone du projet comprend la totalit&eacute; ou une partie de 16 sections de terrain et est situ&eacute;e sur des prairies indig&egrave;nes actuellement utilis&eacute;es pour le p&acirc;turage. La zone du projet compte plusieurs zones humides et cours d&#39;eau intermittents, mais aucune voie navigable. Les &eacute;tudes sur la faune indiquent la pr&eacute;sence de plusieurs esp&egrave;ces en p&eacute;ril inscrites, notamment la petite chauve-souris brune, la chauve-souris &agrave; longues oreilles du Nord, le pipit de Sprague, la buse rouilleuse, le courlis &agrave; long bec et le bruant de Baird. Aucune esp&egrave;ce v&eacute;g&eacute;tale inscrite en vertu de la Loi sur les esp&egrave;ces en p&eacute;ril n&#39;a &eacute;t&eacute; observ&eacute;e dans la zone du projet lors des &eacute;tudes.

&nbsp;

Services aux Autochtones Canada &eacute;mettra un instrument foncier en vertu de la Loi sur les Indiens pour ce projet et est donc tenu, en vertu de l&#39;article 82 de la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact, de prendre une d&eacute;cision concernant les effets environnementaux du projet. D&eacute;veloppement &eacute;conomique des Prairies Canada a fourni un financement pour les &eacute;tapes de faisabilit&eacute; du projet et n&#39;est donc pas tenu pour l&#39;instant de prendre une d&eacute;cision, mais pourrait &ecirc;tre tenu de le faire &agrave; un stade ult&eacute;rieur. L&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute; produite dans le cadre du projet sera inject&eacute;e dans le r&eacute;seau &eacute;lectrique interconnect&eacute; de l&#39;Alberta.&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
In 2018, the federal government of Canada created Laboratories Canada (LabsCanada), a long-term strategy to modernize federal laboratories.&nbsp;This initiative&nbsp;seeks&nbsp;to&nbsp;position Canada as a global leader in science and innovation, through the creation of a national network of modern laboratories. The&nbsp;TerraCanada&nbsp;Hub will promote collaboration between complementary federal science departments and academia to&nbsp;advance&nbsp;the sustainable development of land and resources,&nbsp;including critical minerals, to strengthen Canada&#39;s resilience, sovereignty and green economy through collaborative research and&nbsp;innovation.&nbsp;

The project is&nbsp;located&nbsp;at the National Research Council (NRC) Montreal Road Campus in Ottawa, Ontario, at the southwest corner of Montreal Road and Blair Road. The area is characterized by a mix of residential neighborhoods, institutional campuses, and commercial corridors. The region&nbsp;benefits&nbsp;from access to public transit, active transportation networks, and proximity to healthcare and educational institutions. The project promises transformative benefits for Canadians by fostering innovation, environmental stewardship, and economic resilience.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

The full vision of the TC NCA project will be delivered in components. Funding has been secured for Component 1 that includes a stand-alone facility with parking lots, loading areas, driveways,&nbsp;roadways&nbsp;and pedestrian pathways. The&nbsp;area of the building is expected to be&nbsp;33,564&nbsp;m2&nbsp;and PSPC will be the custodian of the building.&nbsp;

The construction of Component 1 will be carried out&nbsp;in&nbsp;a series of distinct phases.&nbsp;Phase 1 of the TC NCA project consisted of enabling and early works to prepare the site,&nbsp;including excavation and site services for storm, sanitary, and water infrastructure; site clearing and tree protection; channel realignment; roadway adjustments; installation of temporary construction facilities; and early utility and geothermal field loop installation. These activities&nbsp;establish&nbsp;the necessary groundwork for future project phases. The&nbsp;initial&nbsp;enabling work is set to start in Spring 2026.&nbsp;&nbsp;

PHASE&nbsp;2:&nbsp;MAIN PROJECT BUILDING.&nbsp;

The&nbsp;TC NCA&nbsp;facility design for the&nbsp;TerraCanada&nbsp;Hub has been developed in alignment with the NRC Campus Master Plan to create a distinctive presence that enhances the local neighbourhood and&nbsp;establishes&nbsp;a new science hub within the main NRC Montreal Road Campus.&nbsp;The design balances flexible, adaptable, and scalable laboratory spaces and meets key scientific&nbsp;objectives, programming goals, operational models, and whole-building sustainability ambitions consistent with&nbsp;LabsCanada&#39;s&nbsp;Repeatable Laboratory Design Framework.&nbsp;

This second phase of the TC NCA project will consist of all construction activities&nbsp;required&nbsp;to complete the facility. Phase 2 of the project will include the following activities:&nbsp;


	
	Construction of structural steel and mass timber building, including mechanical&nbsp;and&nbsp;elecrical&nbsp;systems and fit-up.&nbsp;
	



	
	Grading&nbsp;and landscape including irrigation (if&nbsp;required)&nbsp;
	



	
	Internal Roadways,&nbsp;sidewalks&nbsp;and active modes connections&nbsp;&nbsp;
	



	
	Parking lots and loading areas&nbsp;&nbsp;
	



	
	Site lighting&nbsp;&nbsp;
	



	
	Fences and gates&nbsp;&nbsp;
	



	
	Retaining Wall&nbsp;
	



	
	Pick-up/drop-off shelter&nbsp;
	


PSPC will oversee Phase 2 and&nbsp;subsequent&nbsp;phases of the TC NCA overarching project on federal land as lead authority, with reviews, permits, and approval from federal agencies as required.&nbsp;&nbsp;In addition to PSPC, Phase 2 and subsequent phases of the TC NCA overarching project will also be reviewed under the&nbsp;Impact Assessment Act&nbsp;by the NRC as the current landowner and provider of authorizations in such capacity, and by the National Capital Commission (NCC)&nbsp;as provider of Federal Approvals under the&nbsp;National Capital Act&nbsp;to enable the undertaking.

properties.description_fr:
En 2018, le gouvernement du Canada a lanc&eacute; Laboratoires Canada, une strat&eacute;gie &agrave; long terme visant &agrave; moderniser les laboratoires f&eacute;d&eacute;raux. Cette initiative vise &agrave; positionner le Canada comme un chef de file mondial en mati&egrave;re de science et d&#39;innovation, gr&acirc;ce &agrave; la cr&eacute;ation d&#39;un r&eacute;seau national de laboratoires modernes.&nbsp;Le p&ocirc;le&nbsp;TerraCanada&nbsp;(TC) favorisera la collaboration entre les minist&egrave;res f&eacute;d&eacute;raux vocation scientifiques compl&eacute;mentaires et le milieu universitaire&nbsp;en vue de faire progresser le d&eacute;veloppement durable&nbsp;des terres et des ressources naturelles, y compris les&nbsp;min&eacute;raux critiques, afin de&nbsp;renforcer la r&eacute;silience, la souverainet&eacute; et l&#39;&eacute;conomie verte du Canada gr&acirc;ce &agrave; la recherche et &agrave; l&#39;innovation collaboratives.&nbsp;

Le projet est situ&eacute; sur le campus du Conseil national de recherches (CNRC) le long du chemin Montr&eacute;al, &agrave; Ottawa, Ontario, &agrave; l&#39;angle sud-ouest d l&#39;intersection de la route Montr&eacute;al et du chemin Blair. Le secteur environnant se caract&eacute;rise par un m&eacute;lange de quartiers r&eacute;sidentiels, de campus institutionnels et de corridors commerciaux. Il b&eacute;n&eacute;ficie d&#39;un bon acc&egrave;s au transport en commun, de r&eacute;seaux de transport actif et de la proximit&eacute; des &eacute;tablissements de sant&eacute; et d&#39;enseignement. Le projet offrira des retomb&eacute;es durables et transformatrices pour les Canadiens en favorisant l&#39;innovation, la g&eacute;rance de l&#39;environnement et la r&eacute;silience &eacute;conomique.&nbsp;

La vision compl&egrave;te du p&ocirc;le TC RCN sera r&eacute;alis&eacute;e en plusieurs &eacute;tapes. Le financement a &eacute;t&eacute; obtenu pour la Composante 1, qui comprend un b&acirc;timent autonome dot&eacute;es d&#39;aires de stationnement, des zones de chargement, des voies d&#39;acc&egrave;s, des routes et des sentiers&nbsp;pi&eacute;tonniers. Ce b&acirc;timent, d&#39;une superficie pr&eacute;vue de&nbsp;33,564&nbsp;m2&nbsp;sera, &agrave; terme, sous la responsabilit&eacute; de SPAC.&nbsp;

La construction de la Composante 1 se r&eacute;alisera en plusieurs phases distinctes. La Phase 1 consistera &agrave;&nbsp;entamer&nbsp;les travaux de pr&eacute;paration du site, y compris&nbsp;l&#39;excavation&nbsp;et&nbsp;les services&nbsp;pour l&#39;infrastructure d&#39;eau&nbsp;pluviale,&nbsp;sanitaires et potable; d&eacute;frichement du chantier de protection des arbres; r&eacute;alignement&nbsp;de&nbsp;foss&eacute;,&nbsp;am&eacute;nagement&nbsp;de chauss&eacute;e,&nbsp;montage d&#39;installations&nbsp;de construction temporaires;&nbsp;installation pr&eacute;coce&nbsp;des infrastructures&nbsp;pour la boucle du champ g&eacute;othermique.&nbsp;Ces activit&eacute;s&nbsp;jettent les bases n&eacute;cessaires aux phases futures du projet.&nbsp;Les premiers travaux pr&eacute;paratoires devraient&nbsp;commencer au printemps 2026.&nbsp;

PHASE 2 :&nbsp;B&Acirc;TIMENT PRINCIPAL DU PROJET.&nbsp;

La conception actuelle des installations du&nbsp;p&ocirc;le TC RCN&nbsp;a &eacute;t&eacute; &eacute;labor&eacute;e en harmonie avec le plan directeur du campus du CNRC afin de cr&eacute;er une pr&eacute;sence distinctive qui rehausse le quartier local et &eacute;tablit un nouveau centre scientifique dans le campus principal du CNRC sur le chemin Montr&eacute;al. La conception &eacute;quilibre les espaces de laboratoire flexibles, adaptables et &eacute;volutifs et r&eacute;pond aux principaux objectifs scientifiques, aux objectifs de programmation, aux mod&egrave;les op&eacute;rationnels et aux ambitions de durabilit&eacute; de l&#39;ensemble du b&acirc;timent, conform&eacute;ment au Cadre de&nbsp;Conception&nbsp;Reproductible&nbsp;de Laboratoires de Laboratoires Canada.&nbsp;

La conception des installations du&nbsp;TC&nbsp;RCN&nbsp;tient compte du co&ucirc;t du cycle de vie et de l&#39;endurance du b&acirc;timent ainsi que des&nbsp;investissements en capital&nbsp;initiaux. Ces mesures de durabilit&eacute; visent &agrave; s&#39;aligner sur les objectifs LEED, WELL et&nbsp;de&nbsp;Laboratoires Canada pour&nbsp;ces&nbsp;installations. Cette deuxi&egrave;me phase du projet de TC&nbsp;RCN&nbsp;comprendra toutes les activit&eacute;s de construction n&eacute;cessaires &agrave; l&#39;ach&egrave;vement de l&#39;installation. La phase 2 du projet comprendra les activit&eacute;s suivantes :&nbsp;


	
	Construction de&nbsp;b&acirc;timent&nbsp;en&nbsp;acier&nbsp;et bois massif, y&nbsp;compris&nbsp;les&nbsp;syst&egrave;mes&nbsp;m&eacute;caniques&nbsp;et&nbsp;&eacute;lectriques&nbsp;et&nbsp;l&#39;am&eacute;nagement&nbsp;int&eacute;rieur.&nbsp;
	



	
	Nivellement et&nbsp;am&eacute;naement&nbsp;paysager, y compris l&#39;irrigation (si n&eacute;cessaire)&nbsp;
	



	
	Routes internes, trottoirs et liaisons&nbsp;de&nbsp;modes actives&nbsp;
	



	
	Stationnement et zone chargement&nbsp;
	



	
	&Eacute;clairage du site&nbsp;
	



	
	Cl&ocirc;tures et barri&egrave;res&nbsp;
	



	
	Mur de sout&egrave;nement&nbsp;
	



	
	Abri d&#39;embarquement et de d&eacute;barquement&nbsp;
	


SPAC supervisera la phase 2 et les phases subs&eacute;quentes du projet global de TC&nbsp;RCN&nbsp;sur les terres f&eacute;d&eacute;rales en tant qu&#39;autorit&eacute; responsable, avec des&nbsp;revues, des permis et l&#39;approbation d&#39;organismes f&eacute;d&eacute;raux, au besoin. En plus de SPAC, la phase 2 et les phases subs&eacute;quentes du projet global de TC&nbsp;RCN&nbsp;seront &eacute;galement examin&eacute;es en vertu de la&nbsp;Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact&nbsp;par le CNRC en tant que propri&eacute;taire actuel du terrain et fournisseur des autorisations &agrave; ce titre, et par la Commission de la&nbsp;Capitale&nbsp;Nationale (CCN) en tant que fournisseur des approbations f&eacute;d&eacute;rales en vertu de la&nbsp;Loi sur la capitale nationale&nbsp;pour permettre le projet. &nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The proposed project is part of the National Trade Corridors Fund (NTCF) financing agreement reached between Montreal Port Authority (MPA) and Transport Canada (TC).&nbsp;The MPA plans to install three (3) variable message signs within the port territory, between sections 53 and 71 (Mercier-Hochelaga-Maisonneuve borough).

In general, the planned works can be summarized as follows:


	Excavation and installation of foundations and electrical conducts;
	Installation of supporting structures;
	Mounting of variable message signs;
	Electrical and telecommunication connections.


The works are scheduled to begin in early 2026.

properties.description_fr:
Le projet propos&eacute; s&#39;inscrit dans le cadre de l&#39;entente de financement avec le Fonds national des corridors commerciaux (FNCC) conclue entre l&#39;Administration portuaire de Montr&eacute;al (APM) et Transports Canada (TC). L&#39;APM pr&eacute;voit l&#39;installation de trois (3) panneaux &agrave; messages variables &agrave; l&#39;int&eacute;rieur du territoire portuaire, entre les sections 53 et 71 (arrondissement Mercier-Hochelaga-Maisonneuve).

De fa&ccedil;on g&eacute;n&eacute;rale, les travaux planifi&eacute;s se r&eacute;sument comme suit&nbsp;:


	Excavation et installation de massifs de fondation et de massifs &eacute;lectriques;
	Installation de structures de support;
	Montage de panneaux &agrave; message variables sur les supports;
	Travaux de raccordement &eacute;lectrique et de t&eacute;l&eacute;communication.


Les travaux sont pr&eacute;vus au d&eacute;but de l&#39;ann&eacute;e 2026.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

Le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale (MDN) a propos&eacute; un projet. Le b&acirc;timent 325 est une station de pompage et une usine de purification d&#39;eau utilis&eacute;e pour la suppression des incendies et l&#39;approvisionnement en eau domestique sur le polygone de tir a&eacute;rien de Cold Lake (PTACL). Ce b&acirc;timent est en mauvais &eacute;tat et n&eacute;cessite des r&eacute;novations. Il est propos&eacute; de construire un nouveau b&acirc;timent pr&eacute;fabriqu&eacute; &agrave; proximit&eacute; de la station actuelle afin de remplacer l&#39;infrastructure vieillissante.

Les travaux requis comprennent :


	le d&eacute;broussaillage et l&#39;enl&egrave;vement de la v&eacute;g&eacute;tation environnante ;
	l&#39;excavation pour la dalle du nouveau b&acirc;timent ;
	la construction du b&acirc;timent pr&eacute;fabriqu&eacute; (avec la nouvelle construction de l&#39;entr&eacute;e d&#39;eau dans le lac Primrose);
	l&#39;ajout d&#39;une station de remplissage pour camions ;
	la construction d&#39;une nouvelle route en gravier ;
	le nivellement et l&#39;am&eacute;nagement paysager de la zone environnante ;
	le raccordement &agrave; la conduite d&#39;eau existante ;
	et, selon l&#39;&eacute;valuation de l&#39;&eacute;tat actuel, le remplacement (ou la nouvelle construction) de l&#39;entr&eacute;e d&#39;eau dans le lac Primrose.

properties.description_en:
The Department of National Defence (DND) is proposing a project. At building MC44, there are currently two 23,000 litres fuel tanks (one for diesel and one for regular unleaded gasoline). The tanks, pumps and dispensers were installed in 1999 and are past their end-of-life dates. The pumping system controls are no longer supported by the supplier, and the condition of the existing oil / water separator will also be assessed. The refueling station is to undergo upgrades and replacement of existing equipment which may include, but is not limited to the following:


	Replacement/upgrade of existing fuel tanks and dispensers;
	New canopy/roof/lighting;
	New permanent standby generator;
	Paving of the station area;
	New outdoor wash rack / bay.


The project work is anticipated to begin in the fall of 2026 and is expected to be completed by the fall of 2027. Earthworks are expected to occur for the replacement of the canopy, tanks, new wash rack / bay, paved areas and related infrastructure. Prior to the commencement of work activities, sediment and erosion controls will be applied where appropriate to prevent sediment release from the Site and adjacent areas, including a drainage ditch that exists at the south end of the Project Site. Soil will be assessed for contamination and managed appropriately. The existing stormwater sewer network that services the Project Area is equipped with an OWS that intercepts surface water from the refueling station and mitigates the release of Petroleum, POL as well as sediments to the southern ditch.

&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale (MDN) propose un projet. Au b&acirc;timent MC44, il y a actuellement deux r&eacute;servoirs de carburant de 23 000 litres (un pour le diesel et un pour l&#39;essence sans plomb). Les r&eacute;servoirs, pompes et distributeurs ont &eacute;t&eacute; install&eacute;s en 1999 et ont d&eacute;pass&eacute; leur date de fin de vie. Les commandes du syst&egrave;me de pompage ne sont plus prises en charge par le fournisseur. De plus, l&#39;&eacute;tat du s&eacute;parateur eau-huile actuel doit &eacute;galement &ecirc;tre &eacute;valu&eacute;. L&#39;escale d&#39;avitaillement doit &ecirc;tre am&eacute;lior&eacute;e et les &eacute;quipements existants doivent &ecirc;tre remplac&eacute;s, ce qui peut inclure, sans s&#39;y limiter, les &eacute;l&eacute;ments suivants:


	remplacement/modernisation des r&eacute;servoirs de carburant et distributeurs existants;
	remplacement de l&#39;abri, du toit et de l&#39;&eacute;clairage;
	installation d&#39;une nouvelle g&eacute;n&eacute;ratrice de r&eacute;serve permanente;
	pavage de la zone d&#39;escale;
	construction de nouveaux postes et d&#39;une nouvelle aire de lavage ext&eacute;rieur.


Les travaux du projet devraient commencer &agrave; l&#39;automne 2026 et &ecirc;tre achev&eacute;s d&#39;ici l&#39;automne 2027. Des travaux de terrassement devraient &ecirc;tre r&eacute;alis&eacute;s pour remplacer l&#39;abri et les r&eacute;servoirs et installer les postes et l&#39;aire de lavage, le rev&ecirc;tement du sol et les infrastructures connexes. Avant le d&eacute;but des travaux, des contr&ocirc;les des s&eacute;diments et de l&#39;&eacute;rosion seront r&eacute;alis&eacute;s lorsque cela est appropri&eacute; afin d&#39;emp&ecirc;cher le rejet de s&eacute;diments depuis le site et les zones adjacentes, y compris un foss&eacute; de drainage situ&eacute; &agrave; l&#39;extr&eacute;mit&eacute; sud du site du projet. Le sol sera &eacute;valu&eacute; pour la contamination et g&eacute;r&eacute; de mani&egrave;re appropri&eacute;e. Le r&eacute;seau d&#39;&eacute;gouts pluviaux existant qui dessert la zone de projet est &eacute;quip&eacute; d&#39;un s&eacute;parateur eau-huile qui intercepte les eaux de surface de l&#39;escale d&#39;avitaillement et att&eacute;nue les rejets de p&eacute;trole, d&#39;huiles et de lubrifiants ainsi que de s&eacute;diments vers le foss&eacute; sud.

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
Sunrock Industries Canada ULC. is proposing to construct a new ready-mix plant at 1050 Farewell Street in Oshawa, Ontario.&nbsp;

The ready-mix concrete plant footprint will be about 375m2 and consist of 2 silos that will store cement and cement supplements, a conveyor to load the aggregates into the bins, internal aggregate and sand loading bins, weigh hoppers, a dust collector, water tanks, and a loading point for transferring the materials to the ready-mix truck.&nbsp;The ready-mix concrete plant would produce about 500 cubic metres of concrete per day. Return concrete will be removed from the site on an ongoing basis and recycled off-site. There will be no crushing of recycled concrete conducted on-site. Water collection and treatment facilities and utility services would be installed to support the plant operations. Stormwater will be discharged into the municipal storm sewer system.

The plant will typically operate Monday to Friday between 06:00 and 19:00. However, the plant may occasionally operate up to 24 hours per day and on weekends.

properties.description_fr:
Sunrock Industries Canada ULC. propose de construire une nouvelle centrale &agrave; b&eacute;ton pr&ecirc;t &agrave; l&#39;emploi au 1050, rue Farewell, &agrave; Oshawa, en Ontario.&nbsp;

La centrale &agrave; b&eacute;ton pr&ecirc;t &agrave; l&#39;emploi occupera une superficie d&#39;environ 375&nbsp;m&sup2; et comprendra deux silos destin&eacute;s au stockage du ciment et des additifs, un convoyeur pour charger les granulats dans les bacs, des bacs internes de chargement des granulats et du sable, des tr&eacute;mies de pesage, un d&eacute;poussi&eacute;reur, des r&eacute;servoirs d&#39;eau et un point de chargement pour le transfert des mat&eacute;riaux vers les camions malaxeurs de b&eacute;ton pr&ecirc;t &agrave; l&#39;emploi.&nbsp;La centrale &agrave; b&eacute;ton pr&ecirc;t &agrave; l&#39;emploi produira environ 500&nbsp;m&egrave;tres cubes de b&eacute;ton par jour. Les restes de b&eacute;ton seront retir&eacute;s du site de mani&egrave;re continue et recycl&eacute;s hors site. Il n&#39;y aura pas de concassage du b&eacute;ton recycl&eacute; sur le site. Des installations de collecte et de traitement de l&#39;eau, ainsi que des installations de services publics, seront mises en place pour soutenir le fonctionnement de la centrale. Les eaux de ruissellement seront rejet&eacute;es dans le r&eacute;seau municipal d&#39;&eacute;gouts pluvial.

La centrale fonctionnera g&eacute;n&eacute;ralement du lundi au vendredi, de 6&nbsp;h &agrave; 19&nbsp;h. Toutefois, la centrale pourra occasionnellement fonctionner jusqu&#39;&agrave; 24&nbsp;heures par jour et en fin de semaine

Le projet propos&eacute;

Westbow Construction Group (Westbow) propose de d&eacute;velopper la partie sud des terres de la Premi&egrave;re Nation de Kwaw-kwaw-Apilt, &agrave; Chilliwack, en Colombie-Britannique, pour en faire une communaut&eacute; r&eacute;sidentielle. La proposition comprend la construction de maisons en rang&eacute;e, d&#39;appartements, de routes, d&#39;une &eacute;cole et d&#39;infrastructures connexes. Le projet comprend &eacute;galement le remblayage de certaines parties de Waterlily Slough, le d&eacute;frichage de l&#39;habitat riverain, la construction d&#39;un chemin d&#39;agr&eacute;ment en gravier, l&#39;installation d&#39;exutoires d&#39;eaux pluviales et l&#39;installation d&#39;un pont &agrave; ponceau en arc au-dessus du canal de d&eacute;rivation de Waterlily Slough.

&nbsp;

Au total, environ 2&nbsp;600&nbsp;m2 d&#39;habitat en cours d&#39;eau et 12&nbsp;000&nbsp;m2 d&#39;habitat riverain seront touch&eacute;s. La proposition pr&eacute;voit des mesures de compensation pour l&#39;habitat afin de contrebalancer ces effets. La compensation propos&eacute;e porte sur l&#39;am&eacute;lioration des zones aquatiques et riveraines sur le site. Un dispositif de contre-courant mouill&eacute; du ruisseau Chilliwack sera construit dans les zones humides du canal de d&eacute;rivation de Waterlily Slough. De plus, la partie inf&eacute;rieure de Waterlily Slough sera am&eacute;lior&eacute;e gr&acirc;ce &agrave; la construction de plusieurs mouilles et &agrave; l&#39;&eacute;limination des barri&egrave;res &agrave; poissons et des d&eacute;bris anthropiques.

Le projet propos&eacute;

Le projet comprendra la construction d&#39;un b&acirc;timent d&#39;un &eacute;tage (1 170 m&sup2;) et d&#39;un b&acirc;timent de trois &eacute;tages (603 m&sup2; au premier &eacute;tage), d&#39;une aire de jeux ext&eacute;rieure et d&#39;un parking, pour une superficie totale au sol de plus de 1 770 m&sup2; et une superficie totale du projet d&#39;environ 0,9 ha.

Les activit&eacute;s comprennent la construction d&#39;une nouvelle route, de raccordements lat&eacute;raux (eau et eaux us&eacute;es/&eacute;gouts), la pr&eacute;paration du site (d&eacute;frichage, d&eacute;racinement et nivellement), le pavage et la construction de b&acirc;timents.

properties.description_en:
The City of North Bay is proposing to replace 11 H-Piles that currently secure five strings of floats at the North Bay Waterfront Marina located on the eastern shores of Lake Nipissing. &nbsp;The existing piles have become damaged and are not functioning as intended.

The old H-piles will be cut off below the lake bottom and removed. New H piles will be positioned in a similar orientation as the existing piles and installed by driving the pile into bedrock using pile-driving equipment. All work will occur in the nearshore environment with depths of 2 metres or less. &nbsp;

The project will utilize heavy equipment, including, but not limited to, a crane and/or excavator. Temporary works may include a laydown area in the parking lot of the marina and rock platforms on the gabion wall to support heavy equipment used for the removal and replacement of the piles. Environmental protection measures may include the use of cofferdams to isolate the piles, tree protections, and sediment and erosion control measures.

The Proposed Project

The project will include the installation of water, sanitary, and storm infrastructure as well as a full road infrastructure complete with base, sub-base, asphalt, and curb for the future development of 30 lots. The approximate project footprint is 8 hectares. Project activities include site preparation (clearing and grubbing of the site), levelling, installation of piping, and road construction.

March 6, 2026 &ndash; Please note the project scope was updated to include an additional 4 lots (34 lots in total across 9.2ha). &nbsp;This area was already captured within the baseline environmental data, and the expanded scope does not alter the overall environmental effects assessment. As there are no new or increased impacts identified, the environmental determination was made based on the updated scope.&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Le projet propos&eacute;

Le projet comprendra l&#39;installation d&#39;infrastructures hydrauliques, sanitaires et pluviales, ainsi que d&#39;une infrastructure routi&egrave;re compl&egrave;te avec fondation, sous-fondation, asphalte et bordures pour le d&eacute;veloppement futur de 30 lots. La superficie approximative du projet est de 8 hectares. Les activit&eacute;s du projet comprennent la pr&eacute;paration du site (d&eacute;frichage et d&eacute;racinement), le nivellement, l&#39;installation de canalisations et la construction de routes.

6 mars 2026 &ndash; Veuillez noter que la port&eacute;e du projet a &eacute;t&eacute; mise &agrave; jour afin d&#39;inclure 4 lots suppl&eacute;mentaires (34 lots au total sur 9,2 ha). &nbsp;Cette zone &eacute;tait d&eacute;j&agrave; prise en compte dans les donn&eacute;es environnementales de r&eacute;f&eacute;rence, et l&#39;&eacute;largissement de la port&eacute;e ne modifie en rien l&#39;&eacute;valuation globale des effets sur l&#39;environnement. Aucun impact nouveau ou accru n&#39;ayant &eacute;t&eacute; identifi&eacute;, la d&eacute;cision environnementale a &eacute;t&eacute; prise sur la base de la port&eacute;e mise &agrave; jour.&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The Department of National Defence (DND) is proposing a project. As part of Canada&#39;s North American Aerospace Defense Command (NORAD) modernization plan, DND is investing in a new Northern Approaches Surveillance System (NASS) to significantly expand NORAD and the Canadian Armed Forces&#39; (CAF) situational awareness of objects approaching and entering Canadian airspace from the North. NASS will include the Arctic Over-the-Horizon Radar (A-OTHR) system that will provide early warning radar coverage and threat tracking.

The A-OTHR capability will be located in Southern Ontario and will extend NORAD and the CAF&#39;s situational awareness into the Canadian North and the North Atlantic.

Development at the site will focus on installation of transmitting antennas. Land preparation will include flattening of the land and removal of any obstructions that would impede the radar&#39;s signal, including potential clearing of forested areas or filling of wetlands.

While specific infrastructure needs are being finalized, the A-OTHR system will require supporting infrastructure at each site:


	Fully equipped operational building;
	Physical security features;
	Maintenance and storage facility;
	Access road and parking; and
	Utilities (power, water, wastewater, stormwater, communications).


Additional information is available on the  Department of National Defence website.

properties.description_fr:
Le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale (MDN) propose un projet. Dans le cadre du plan canadien pour la modernisation du Commandement de la d&eacute;fense a&eacute;rospatiale de l&#39;Am&eacute;rique du Nord (NORAD), le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale investit dans un nouveau syst&egrave;me de surveillance des voies d&#39;approche du Nord (SSVAN) qui permettra au NORAD, et aux Forces arm&eacute;es canadiennes (FAC) d&#39;avoir une meilleure connaissance de la situation des objets qui s&#39;approchent de l&#39;espace a&eacute;rien canadien ou qui y p&eacute;n&egrave;trent &agrave; partir du Nord. Le SSVAN comprendra le syst&egrave;me de radar transhorizon qui fournira une couverture radar d&#39;alerte avanc&eacute;e et un suivi des menaces.

La capacit&eacute; de radar transhorizon sera situ&eacute;e dans le sud de l&#39;Ontario et permettra au NORAD et aux FAC d&#39;avoir une meilleure connaissance de la situation dans le Nord canadien et l&#39;Atlantique Nord.

L&#39;am&eacute;nagement du site consistera principalement en l&#39;installation d&#39;antennes &eacute;mettrices. La pr&eacute;paration du site comprendra l&#39;aplanissement du terrain et l&#39;&eacute;limination de tout ce qui pourrait faire obstacle aux signaux radar, ce qui comprend le d&eacute;frichage &eacute;ventuel de zones bois&eacute;es ou le remplissage &eacute;ventuel de zones humides.

Bien que les besoins pr&eacute;cis en mati&egrave;re d&#39;infrastructure ne soient pas encore confirm&eacute;s, le syst&egrave;me de radar transhorizon n&eacute;cessitera une infrastructure de soutien sur chaque site :


	b&acirc;timent op&eacute;rationnel enti&egrave;rement &eacute;quip&eacute;;
	dispositifs de s&eacute;curit&eacute; physiques;
	installation d&#39;entretien et d&#39;entreposage;
	chemin d&#39;acc&egrave;s et stationnement; et
	services publics (&eacute;lectricit&eacute;, eau, eaux us&eacute;es, eaux pluviales, communications).


Des informations compl&eacute;mentaires sont disponibles sur  le site Web du minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale.

properties.description_en:
The Canadian Coast Guard is planning to dismantle the remaining infrastructure at its telecommunications site located at Heath Point on Anticosti Island.

The scope of work includes :


	Removal of diesel and helicopter fuel storage systems that have been permanently decommissioned;
	Removal of sections of the guyed tower that was taken down in 2025;
	Removal and disposal of three (3) generators;
	Demolition of the three (3) shelters on site, including&nbsp; walkways and stairs;
	Demolition of the overhead cable bridge that connected the electronic equipment shelter to the guyed tower;
	Removal of a satellite antenna;
	Removal of the Environment and Climate Change Canada weather installations;


The debris will be slung and sorted into containers on a Canadian Coast Guard vessel positioned approximately 1 km off the site.

properties.description_fr:
La Garde c&ocirc;ti&egrave;re canadienne planifie le d&eacute;mant&egrave;lement des infrastructures restantes &agrave; son ancien site de t&eacute;l&eacute;communications situ&eacute; &agrave; Pointe Heath sur l&#39;&Icirc;le d&#39;Anticosti.

La port&eacute;e des travaux comprend :&nbsp;


	Le retrait des syst&egrave;mes de stockage de di&eacute;sel et de carburant pour h&eacute;licopt&egrave;res qui ont &eacute;t&eacute; mis hors service de mani&egrave;re permanente, au pr&eacute;alable;
	Le retrait des sections du pyl&ocirc;ne hauban&eacute; qui a &eacute;t&eacute; mis au sol en 2025;
	Le retrait et disposition des groupes &eacute;lectrog&egrave;nes;
	La d&eacute;molition des trois (3) abris pr&eacute;sents sur le site, incluant les passerelles et escaliers;
	La d&eacute;molition du pont de c&acirc;bles a&eacute;rien qui reliait l&apos;abri des &eacute;quipements &eacute;lectroniques au pyl&ocirc;ne hauban&eacute;;
	Le retrait d&apos;une antenne satellite;
	Le retrait des anciennes installations m&eacute;t&eacute;orologique d&apos;Environnement et Changement climatique Canada.


Les d&eacute;bris seront &eacute;lingu&eacute;s et tri&eacute;s vers des conteneurs dispos&eacute;s sur un navire de la Garde c&ocirc;ti&egrave;re canadienne positionn&eacute; &agrave; environ 1 km au large du site.


Les travaux sont planifi&eacute;s &agrave; l&apos;&eacute;t&eacute; 2026, soit dans les mois de mai et juillet.

properties.description_en:
To support growth at DP World Fraser Surrey and Fraser Grain Terminal, additional rail arrival, departure, and storage trackage is proposed in the Port Authority Rail Yard (PARY), which is adjacent the terminal, to the east. This project proposes to extend the existing PARY rail siding tracks towards the north, taking the total yard trackage from 23,600 feet, to 42,540. This work includes the following components.


	Partially demolishing and realigning the existing B026 trackwork, west of the previous Republic Rabanco facility;
	Reconfiguring PARY Track 93: Removing one (1) turnout and realignment of trackage;
	Reconfiguring and extending six existing PARY tracks &ndash; Tracks 94 to 99; and
	Constructing new utility protection for Metro Vancouver&#39;s sanitary line: partially demolishing the existing un-piled utility protection slab under Tracks 93, and adding two (2) cap beams, founded on a total of approximately 42 helical piles, which will support a mix of pre-cast concrete panels and cast-in-place slabs over the sanitary line.

Pearson International Fuel Facilities Corporation (PIFFC) is the owner of a fuel storage facility at the YYZ Pearson International Airport, located on Elmbank Road, Mississauga ON that supplies jet fuel to the airport.

&nbsp;

As part of the proposed project, PIFFC will install jet fuel transfer lines to connect an existing third-party pipeline to the existing PIFFC facility. The proposed project consists of a new metering station to connect to the third-party pipeline, the installation of dual jet fuel transfer lines (20&quot; diameter and 12&quot; diameter, respectively) of approximately 1.8 km in length, and associated equipment. The new jet fuel transfer lines will be constructed to the latest version of CSA Z662 and will include below ground piping with connections to an aboveground metering station and will be installed with active leak detection monitoring.

properties.description_fr:
Pearson International Fuel Facilities Corporation (PIFFC) est le propri&eacute;taire des infrastructures d&#39;un parc de r&eacute;servoirs de carburant situ&eacute; sur la rue Elmbank &agrave; YYZ a&eacute;roport Pearson de Toronto, qui fournit du carburant d&#39;aviation &agrave; l&#39;a&eacute;roport.

&nbsp;

Dans le cadre du projet propos&eacute;, PIFFC installera des nouvelles lignes de transfert de carburant d&#39;aviation pour relier le pipeline actuel de tierce partie &agrave; l&#39;installation PIFFC actuel. Le projet propos&eacute; comprend une nouvelle station de comptage et l&#39;installation d&#39;un double ligne de transfert de carburant d&#39;aviation (deux lignes de transfert en parall&egrave;les, 20 pouces et 12 pouces en diam&egrave;tre, respectivement) d&#39;environ 1,8 km de longueur, ainsi que les &eacute;quipements associ&eacute;s. Les nouvelles lignes de transfert seront construites conform&eacute;ment &agrave; la derni&egrave;re version de la norme CSA Z662 et incluront de la tuyauterie souterraine reli&eacute;e &agrave; une station de comptage hors-sol, et seront &eacute;quip&eacute;es d&#39;un syst&egrave;me de d&eacute;tection de fuites actif.&nbsp;

Le projet propos&eacute;

Le projet comprendra la construction d&#39;un immeuble de bureaux de 1 920 m&sup2; et d&#39;un parking d&#39;environ 1 880 m&sup2; pouvant accueillir 77 v&eacute;hicules. La superficie totale approximative du projet est de 1,06 hectare. Les activit&eacute;s du projet comprennent la pr&eacute;paration du site (d&eacute;frichage et d&eacute;racinement), le nivellement, la construction, le raccordement aux r&eacute;seaux communautaires d&#39;eau et d&#39;&eacute;gouts, l&#39;am&eacute;nagement paysager, le pavage et la construction de routes.

Le projet est propos&eacute; sur un terrain en cours d&#39;ajout &agrave; la r&eacute;serve ; par cons&eacute;quent, une &eacute;valuation environnementale en vertu de l&#39;article 82 est en cours conform&eacute;ment &agrave; la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact.

properties.description_en:
As part of its infrastructure modernization plan, the Port of Quebec intends to rebuild wharves 104, 105, and 106. Built nearly 100 years ago, these wharves have undergone several repairs over time. Despite these interventions, the wharves have reached the end of their useful life, as evidenced by expert assessments and numerous monitoring reports. This deterioration forces the Port to restrict the weight of equipment and goods that can be transported through them, which significantly complicates operations and weakens the supply chain that depends on these facilities.

After analyzing various options, no repair solution could guarantee the extension of the quays&#39; lifespan, their long-term stabilization, and the restoration of operational capabilities. The Port must therefore rebuild the quays using sheet pile cells positioned in front of the existing structures, a robust solution adapted to current needs. The proposed alignment will eliminate the operational and technical constraints related to the current geometry and will significantly improve the safety of maneuvers and, consequently, operational flexibility. This reconstruction allows for the implementation of certain adaptive measures related to the effects of climate change, including adjusting the height of the quays to account for a potential rise in the river&#39;s water level.

This new configuration will also offer the opportunity to integrate enhanced infrastructure intelligence, notably through the addition of measurement systems and sensors to feed predictive models. These will support proactive asset management, optimize intervention planning, and improve the overall resilience of the port system. Furthermore, the reconstruction will fully prepare for the energy transition by integrating infrastructure ready to accommodate shore power systems.

This reconstruction project also aims to achieve Envision Silver certification, an international standard in sustainable development. The project will be carried out using a progressive design-build (PDB) approach, which allows for increased collaboration, better risk management, and systematic consideration of environmental and community issues throughout the various project phases.

Planned works

&nbsp;

This new quay structure (sheet pile cells) will be built in front of the existing structures, forming a continuous line from quay 103 to quay 107. It will incorporate the necessary facilities for modern quays that meet the needs of industry.&nbsp;

The reconstruction will have the effect :


	to move the quays slightly forward towards the river;
	to ensure their stability and security for several decades;
	restore operational capacity in line with industry needs.


Given the progress of the wharf in the aquatic environment, the riverbed will also be slightly dredged to standardize to the currently available water depth and thus allow for the safe berthing of ships.

The work will be carried out over approximately 27 months.

&nbsp;

Please note that an environmental impact assessment will be conducted to evaluate the project&#39;s impacts in accordance with the Impact Assessment and Mitigation Process (IAMP). All valuable environmental components that could be affected by the project will be considered, including but not limited to:


	Noise environment;
	Light pollution;
	Air quality;
	Water quality;
	Fish and their habitat.


&nbsp;

A monitoring and follow-up program will be proposed and must be consistent with the anticipated impacts.

properties.description_fr:
Dans le cadre du plan de modernisation des infrastructures, le Port de Qu&eacute;bec souhaite reconstruire les quais 104, 105 et 106.&nbsp;Construits il y a pr&egrave;s de 100 ans, ces quais ont subi plusieurs r&eacute;parations au fil du temps.&nbsp;Malgr&eacute; ces interventions, les quais ont atteint la fin de leur vie utile, comme en t&eacute;moignent les expertises et les nombreux suivis effectu&eacute;s. Cette d&eacute;gradation oblige le Port &agrave; restreindre le poids des &eacute;quipements et des marchandises pouvant y transiter, ce qui complique consid&eacute;rablement les op&eacute;rations et fragilise la cha&icirc;ne d&#39;approvisionnement qui d&eacute;pend de ces infrastructures.

Apr&egrave;s avoir analys&eacute; diff&eacute;rentes options, aucune solution de r&eacute;paration ne permettait d&#39;assurer la prolongation de leur dur&eacute;e de vie, leur stabilisation de fa&ccedil;on durable et de r&eacute;tablir les capacit&eacute;s op&eacute;rationnelles. Le Port doit donc&nbsp;reconstruire les quais &agrave; l&#39;aide de cellules de palplanches positionn&eacute;s devant les structures existantes, une solution robuste et adapt&eacute;e aux besoins actuels.&nbsp;L&#39;alignement propos&eacute; &eacute;liminera les contraintes op&eacute;rationnelles et techniques li&eacute; &agrave; la g&eacute;om&eacute;trie actuelle et am&eacute;liorera significativement la s&eacute;curit&eacute; des man&oelig;uvres et par le fais m&ecirc;me sa flexibilit&eacute; op&eacute;rationnelle. Cette reconstruction permet de mettre en place certaines mesures adaptatives reli&eacute;es aux effets des changements climatiques, notamment la hauteur des quais pour tenir compte d&#39;une hausse potentielle du niveau d&#39;eau du fleuve.

Cette nouvelle configuration offrira &eacute;galement l&#39;occasion d&#39;int&eacute;grer une intelligence accrue des infrastructures, notamment par l&#39;ajout de syst&egrave;mes de mesure et de capteurs permettant d&#39;alimenter des mod&egrave;les pr&eacute;dictifs. Ceux-ci soutiendront une gestion proactive des actifs, optimiseront la planification des interventions et am&eacute;lioreront la r&eacute;silience globale du syst&egrave;me portuaire. De plus, la reconstruction permettra de pr&eacute;parer pleinement la transition &eacute;nerg&eacute;tique, en int&eacute;grant des infrastructure pr&ecirc;te &agrave; accueillir les syst&egrave;mes d&#39;&eacute;lectrification &agrave; quai.

Ce projet de reconstruction vise &eacute;galement l&#39;obtention de la certification Envision Argent, une norme internationale en d&eacute;veloppement durable. Le projet sera r&eacute;alis&eacute; en mode CCP (conception-construction progressif), ce qui permet une collaboration accrue, une&nbsp;meilleure gestion des risques et une consid&eacute;ration syst&eacute;matique des enjeux environnementaux et de cohabitation tout au long des diff&eacute;rentes phases de projet.

Travaux pr&eacute;vus

Cette nouvelle structure de quai (cellules de palplanches) sera construite devant les structures actuelles, pour former une ligne continue du quai 103 au quai 107. Ils int&eacute;greront les installations n&eacute;cessaires &agrave; des quais modernes et r&eacute;pondant aux besoins de l&#39;industrie.

La reconstruction aura pour effet :


	d&#39;avancer l&eacute;g&egrave;rement les quais vers le fleuve;
	d&#39;assurer leur stabilit&eacute; et leur s&eacute;curit&eacute; pour plusieurs d&eacute;cennies;
	r&eacute;tablir une capacit&eacute; op&eacute;rationnelle en ad&eacute;quation avec les besoins l&#39;industrie.


&Eacute;tant donn&eacute; l&#39;avancement du quai dans le milieu aquatique, le fond du fleuve sera aussi l&eacute;g&egrave;rement dragu&eacute; pour s&#39;uniformiser &agrave; la profondeur d&#39;eau actuellement disponible et ainsi permettre l&#39;accostage s&eacute;curitaire des navires.

Les travaux s&#39;&eacute;chelonneront sur environ 27 mois.

&Agrave; noter qu&#39;une&nbsp;&eacute;tude des effets environnementaux sera r&eacute;alis&eacute;e pour &eacute;valuer les impacts du projet&nbsp;conform&eacute;ment au Processus d&#39;&eacute;valuation et d&#39;att&eacute;nuation des impacts (PEAI). Toutes les composantes environnementales valoris&eacute;es pouvant &ecirc;tre affect&eacute;es par le projet seront consid&eacute;r&eacute;es, notamment et sans s&#39;y limiter :


	Environnement sonore;
	Pollution lumineuse;
	Qualit&eacute; de l&#39;air;
	Qualit&eacute; de l&#39;eau;
	Le poisson et son habitat.


Un programme de surveillance et de suivi sera propos&eacute; et devra &ecirc;tre cons&eacute;quent des impacts anticip&eacute;s.

properties.description_en:
Eskay Creek Mining Limited is proposing the construction, operation and closure of an open-pit gold and silver mine located approximately 85&nbsp;kilometres northwest of Stewart, British Columbia. As proposed, the Eskay Creek Revitalization Project would produce up to 3.6&nbsp;million tonnes of ore per year (approximately 10,000&nbsp;tonnes per day) over 13&nbsp;years of operations. The 18-year mine life would include a two-year construction phase, 13-year operation phase, and three-year reclamation and closure phase. The project is located on the same site as the underground Eskay Creek mine, which is no longer operating, and the proponent will make use of some of its existing facilities and infrastructure.

&nbsp;

Please note that the proponent of this project was previously Skeena Resources Limited.

properties.description_fr:
Eskay Creek Mining Limited&nbsp;propose la construction, l&#39;exploitation et la fermeture d&#39;une mine d&#39;or et d&#39;argent &agrave; ciel ouvert, situ&eacute;e &agrave; environ 85&nbsp;kilom&egrave;tres au nord-ouest de Stewart, en Colombie-Britannique. Tel que propos&eacute;, le projet de revitalisation d&#39;Eskay Creek produirait jusqu&#39;&agrave; 3,6&nbsp;millions de tonnes de minerai par an (environ 10,000 tonnes par jour) sur une p&eacute;riode d&#39;exploitation de 13&nbsp;ans. La dur&eacute;e de vie totale de la mine serait-de 18 ans, incluant une phase de construction de deux ans, une phase d&#39;exploitation de 13&nbsp;ans et une phase de remise en &eacute;tat et de fermeture de trois ans. Le projet est situ&eacute; sur le m&ecirc;me site que la mine souterraine d&#39;Eskay Creek, qui n&#39;est plus en activit&eacute;, et le promoteur r&eacute;utilisera certaines de ses installations et infrastructures existantes.

&nbsp;

Veuillez noter que le promoteur de ce projet &eacute;tait pr&eacute;c&eacute;demment Skeena Resources Limited.

properties.description_en:
Gitga&#39;at First Nation is planning to construct a road which rings the Hartley Bay community, linking the community barge ramp to the newly constructed Upper Lake Road and Malsey Bay road. The construction of a ring road will improve access around Hartley Bay, movement of materials, function as a fire break, and an emergency egress route.

&nbsp;

The proposed ring road is 1148.8m long, with an approximate 20m wide limit of cut (right-of-way). The proposed ring road would parallel an existing road right-of-way and fire break for the majority of its length. The road will require 11 culverts, where the road alignment crosses drainages and non-fish bearing stream channels as well as a 21.336m all steel portable clear spanning bridge constructed over the fish bearing Gabion River.

&nbsp;

The proponent has applied to Environment and Climate Change Canada for a Species at Risk Act permit under section 73(3).

properties.description_fr:
La Premi&egrave;re Nation Gitga&#39;at pr&eacute;voit de construire une route qui encercle la communaut&eacute; de Hartley Bay, reliant la rampe de barge de la communaut&eacute; &agrave; la nouvelle route Upper Lake et &agrave; la route Malsey Bay. La construction de cette route circulaire am&eacute;liorera l&#39;acc&egrave;s autour de Hartley Bay, facilitera le transport de mat&eacute;riaux, servira de coupe-feu et constituera une route d&#39;&eacute;vacuation d&#39;urgence.

&nbsp;

La route circulaire propos&eacute;e mesure 1148,8 m&egrave;tres de long, avec une largeur approximative de 20 m&egrave;tres pour la coupe (droit de passage). La route circulaire propos&eacute;e longera un droit de passage existant et une coupe-feu sur la majeure partie de sa longueur. La construction de la route n&eacute;cessitera l&#39;installation de 11 ponceaux, l&agrave; o&ugrave; l&#39;alignement de la route traverse des canalisations de drainage et des ruisseaux non-poissonneux, ainsi qu&#39;un pont portatif en acier de 21,336 m&egrave;tres de port&eacute;e libre, qui sera construit au-dessus de la rivi&egrave;re Gabion, un cours d&#39;eau poissonneux.

&nbsp;

Le promoteur a demand&eacute; &agrave; Environnement et Changement climatique Canada un permis en vertu de l&#39;article 73(3) de la Loi sur les esp&egrave;ces en p&eacute;ril.

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The British Columbia (BC) Ministry of Transportation and Infrastructure is proposing the replacement of the Sackum Overhead Bridge structure (the Project) located on Trans-Canada Highway No.1, between Spences Bridge, BC and Lytton, BC. The Sackum Overhead Bridge, which spans Sackum Creek and the Canadian Pacific Kansas City Railway, was built in the 1950s and is reaching the end of its service life, therefore the bridge requires replacement to maintain Trans-Canada Highway No. 1 transportation connectivity. Part of the Project will intersect Sackum Indian Reserve (IR) No. 3 and Gulada IR No. 3A. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

The Project will entail construction of a new bridge and approaches in a new alignment, road enhancement work to improve access to an adjacent cemetery, removal of a passing lane north of the bridge and decommissioning of a pullout south of the bridge, and demolition of the old bridge structure. Project activities that are expected to occur on IR lands include vegetation and tree clearing, regrading for construction access, demolition of the existing bridge structure, installation of temporary hydro poles, and reclamation. The project activities on IR land are subject to a s.82 determination under the Impact Assessment Act.

&nbsp;

The proponent has applied to Environment and Climate Change Canada for a Species at Risk Act permit under section 73(3).

properties.description_fr:
Le Minist&egrave;re des transports et de l&#39;infrastructure de la Colombie-Britannique (C.-B.) propose de remplacer la structure du passage sup&eacute;rieur de Sackum (le projet) situ&eacute; sur la route Transcanadienne no 1, entre Spences Bridge (C.-B.) et Lytton (C.-B.). Le passage sup&eacute;rieur de Sackum, qui enjambe le ruisseau Sackum et le chemin de fer Canadien Pacifique Kansas City, a &eacute;t&eacute; construit dans les ann&eacute;es 1950 et arrive &agrave; la fin de sa dur&eacute;e de vie. Le passage doit donc &ecirc;tre remplac&eacute; pour maintenir la connectivit&eacute; des transports sur la route Transcanadienne no 1. Une partie du projet croisera la r&eacute;serve indienne (RI) n&deg; 3 de Sackum et la RI n&deg; 3A de Gulada.&nbsp;

Le projet comprendra la construction d&#39;un nouveau passage et de ses trav&eacute;es d&#39;approche dans un nouvel alignement, des travaux d&#39;am&eacute;lioration de la route pour faciliter l&#39;acc&egrave;s &agrave; un cimeti&egrave;re adjacent, l&#39;enl&egrave;vement d&#39;une voie de d&eacute;passement au nord du passage et la mise hors service d&#39;une voie d&#39;arr&ecirc;t au sud du passage, ainsi que la d&eacute;molition de l&#39;ancienne structure du passage. Les activit&eacute;s du projet qui devraient se d&eacute;rouler sur les terres de RI comprennent le d&eacute;frichement de la v&eacute;g&eacute;tation et des arbres, le nivellement pour l&#39;acc&egrave;s &agrave; la construction, la d&eacute;molition de la structure existante du passage, l&#39;installation de poteaux &eacute;lectriques temporaires et la remise en &eacute;tat. Les activit&eacute;s du projet sur les terres de RI sont soumises &agrave; une d&eacute;termination en vertu de l&#39;article 82 de la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact.

Le promoteur a demand&eacute; &agrave; Environnement et Changement climatique Canada un permis en vertu de l&#39;article 73(3) de la Loi sur les esp&egrave;ces en p&eacute;ril.

properties.description_en:
Westbow Construction Group is proposing an expansion of the Cedarbrook Housing Development on the Skway Indian Reserve No. 5 (Shxwh&aacute;:y&nbsp;Village) in Chilliwack, BC. The development will consist of a six-story apartment block that will provide approximately 84 apartment units. The project footprint is approximately 3, 530 m2 and is situated in an area dominated by young deciduous trees with minimal coarse woody debris or leaf litter. The project is intended to supply housing for families in the Chilliwack area.

&nbsp;

The proponent has applied to Environment and Climate Change Canada for a Species at Risk Act permit under section 73(3).

The Canadian Pacific Railway (CPR) overhead bridge on the Kichi Zibi Mikan (formerly Sir John A. Macdonald Parkway) was originally built in 1966 for the Canadian Pacific Railway. It crosses over the Trillium multi-use pathway and the old railway, which now connects to Chief William Commanda Bridge between Ottawa and Gatineau. The bridge is made of a three-span reinforced concrete structure with a variable depth deck, perched abutments and double-legged inclined piers. A minor repair was done to the bridge in 2006. The bridge is approximately 41.5 m long and 24.1 m wide.

The planned rehabilitation aims to repair severe deterioration of concrete on the deck, the abutment wall and abutment slope protection; replace waterproofing and asphalt; and replace expansion joints, the sidewalk and the railing to meet code requirement for crash-tested barriers. 

The scope of work will include but may not be limited to the following:


	Reduce traffic to one lane in each direction using a temporary detour. Phase 1 will focus on the eastbound lanes, followed by Phase 2 on the westbound lanes.&nbsp;
	Install temporary traffic signage and road markings for each phase.&nbsp;
	Temporarily relocate concrete traffic barriers during construction phases.
	Excavate flagstone paved embankments to expose footings at both abutments.&nbsp;
	Perform partial-depth concrete removals and repairs on abutments and piers.&nbsp;
	Install temporary supports under the bridge deck, then remove and replace bearings and seats.&nbsp;
	Repair damaged concrete in deck ends and soffit.&nbsp;
	Backfill and reinstate flagstone paving.&nbsp;
	Remove the existing railings and cantilevered overhang from deck and approach slabs.&nbsp;
	Rebuild the deck overhang and install new railing curb and approach slabs.&nbsp;
	Install new crash-tested railings.&nbsp;
	Remove the existing asphalt and waterproofing and repair deteriorated concrete.&nbsp;
	Remove the deck joints and convert to semi-integral ends.&nbsp;
	Apply waterproofing and pavement.&nbsp;
	Install new road markings and clean up the site.&nbsp;


&nbsp;

The NCC will review the project under the Impact Assessment Act. During construction, there will be temporary impacts to the roadway and pathway under the bridge. However, to mediate those impacts:


	One lane of traffic will remain open in each direction on Kichi Zibi Mikan.
	The multi-use pathway under the bridge will stay accessible.
	The public will receive clear communication and updates about traffic changes.


Close coordination to minimize traffic disruption will occur with Public Services and Procurement Canada, the City of Ottawa, OC Transpo, the Ville de Gatineau and STO, and align with nearby capital projects such as the Energy Services Acquisition Program (ESAP), the O-Train, and other interprovincial crossings projects.&nbsp; 

The project is scheduled to take place from April 2026 to April 2027.

The National Capital Commission (NCC) launched the Fall Rhapsody shuttle service in 2015, offering transportation between the Capital&#39;s core and Gatineau Park on weekends in October. It has proven to be a very popular option, with a peak ridership in 2019 estimated at 15,000 people over four weekends. As this transit program is currently evolving into a permanent service expanding into the spring, summer and winter months, there is a need for appropriate infrastructure to replace the current temporary solutions.

Seven shuttle stop locations were selected within the Gatineau Park parkway network, including:


	Camp Fortune;
	Champlain Lookout;
	King Mountain Trail;
	Lauriault Trail&ndash;Mulvihill picnic area;
	Mackenzie King Estate;
	Pink Lake Lookout; and
	the South Entrance.


&nbsp;

The proposed bus shelter design at these locations will include outdoor waiting areas, platforms for onboarding and offboarding, shelters, seating, signage and landscaping. Certain stops will also include universally accessible washrooms. The shelters will sit adjacent to and work alongside existing Gatineau Park infrastructure, programs and services. Construction is planned to begin in summer 2025.

A characterization of the natural environment in the work and access zones was carried out. It described the terrestrial and aquatic environments that will be affected by the construction of shuttle shelter program infrastructure. Mitigation measures such as erosion, sediment control and tree protection will be implemented by the contractor to protect terrestrial and aquatic wildlife and their habitats.&nbsp;

The project was proposed by the NCC on land under its stewardship (Gatineau Park). It is subject to federal land use, design and transaction approval (FLUDA) under the National Capital Act. Coordination with the Department of Fisheries and Oceans (DFO) is required, as DFO must issue a letter of notification under the Fisheries Act for planned work in fish habitat.

The proposed project will affect Gatineau Park users at the seven locations. The NCC will inform the public and stakeholders of any anticipated traffic delays or planned detours.

properties.description_fr:
En 2015, la Commission de la capitale nationale (CCN) lan&ccedil;ait un service de navette dans le cadre du Coloris automnal, afin d&#39;assurer le transport entre les centres-villes de Gatineau et d&#39;Ottawa et le parc de la Gatineau en octobre. Ce service s&#39;est av&eacute;r&eacute; tr&egrave;s populaire, atteignant un pic d&#39;affluence estimatif de 15&nbsp;000&nbsp;utilisations en 2019 (sur quatre weekends).

Ce service de transport collectif, actuellement offert au printemps, en &eacute;t&eacute; et en hiver, est en voie de devenir permanent. Il requiert donc l&#39;am&eacute;nagement d&#39;une infrastructure plus appropri&eacute;e pour remplacer les solutions temporaires adopt&eacute;es jusqu&#39;&agrave; maintenant aux arr&ecirc;ts.

Dans le r&eacute;seau de promenades du parc de la Gatineau, les sept emplacements suivants ont &eacute;t&eacute; choisis pour y am&eacute;nager des abribus&nbsp;:


	Camp Fortune;
	le belv&eacute;d&egrave;re Champlain;
	le sentier du Mont-King;
	l&#39;aire de piquenique Mulvihill du sentier Lauriault;
	le domaine Mackenzie-King;
	le lac Pink;
	l&#39;entr&eacute;e sud.


&nbsp;

Ces abribus comporteront les &eacute;l&eacute;ments conceptuels suivants&nbsp;: une aire d&#39;attente, une plateforme pour monter et descendre de la navette, un abri, du mobilier pour s&#39;asseoir, de l&#39;affichage et des &eacute;l&eacute;ments d&#39;am&eacute;nagement paysager. Certains arr&ecirc;ts comprendront des toilettes universellement accessibles. Les arr&ecirc;ts seront adjacents &agrave; des &eacute;l&eacute;ments d&#39;infrastructure, programmes ou services pr&eacute;existants et fonctionneront en parall&egrave;le. Le d&eacute;but des travaux est pr&eacute;vu pour l&#39;&eacute;t&eacute; 2025.

La caract&eacute;risation du milieu naturel dans les zones de construction et d&#39;acc&egrave;s a &eacute;t&eacute; r&eacute;alis&eacute;e. Cette caract&eacute;risation d&eacute;crit les milieux terrestres et aquatiques affect&eacute;s par la construction de l&#39;infrastructure n&eacute;cessaire pour am&eacute;nager les arr&ecirc;ts. Pour prot&eacute;ger la faune terrestre et aquatique et leurs habitats, la soci&eacute;t&eacute;&nbsp;entrepreneure mettra en &oelig;uvre&nbsp;des mesures d&#39;att&eacute;nuation telles que des contr&ocirc;les, pour les s&eacute;diments et contre l&#39;&eacute;rosion, ainsi que des mesures de protection des&nbsp;arbres.

La CCN se propose d&#39;entreprendre ce projet sur un terrain dont elle assure l&#39;intendance, c&#39;est-&agrave;-dire le parc de la Gatineau. Le projet est assujetti &agrave; l&#39;obtention d&#39;une approbation f&eacute;d&eacute;rale de l&#39;utilisation du sol, du design et des transactions immobili&egrave;res, comme le prescrit la Loi sur la capitale nationale.

La coordination avec le minist&egrave;re des P&ecirc;ches et des Oc&eacute;ans est n&eacute;cessaire, car en vertu de la Loi sur les p&ecirc;ches, ce minist&egrave;re doit &eacute;mettre une lettre de notification pour tout travail pr&eacute;vu dans l&#39;habitat du poisson.

Aux sept endroits indiqu&eacute;s, le projet aura une incidence sur les personnes qui circulent dans le parc de la Gatineau. La CCN avisera les parties prenantes et le public en g&eacute;n&eacute;ral de tout retard pr&eacute;vu sur les routes et de tout d&eacute;tour.

properties.description_en:
Kitsumkalum First Nation proposes upgrades to the domestic water system (DWS) at I.R. No. 1 located west of the City of Terrace, BC. The work includes developing two new groundwater supply wells (Well 4-23 and Well 5-23), installing raw-water piping to a new water treatment plant (WTP), and constructing a new WTP with chemical pre-treatment, clarification, filtration, and UV/chlorine disinfection. A new cast-in-place concrete water storage reservoir will be built south of the existing reservoirs, along with a transmission main connecting the WTP to the reservoir and distribution piping tying into the existing system.

&nbsp;

The Project also includes grading and improving access roads to support construction and long-term operations. Four water-main creek crossings are required: two culvert replacements at Unnamed Creeks 1 and 2, an open-cut trench crossing of Eneeksaguilaguaw Creek between the old and new reservoir sites, and a culvert installation with open-cut trenching at Stream A near Cemetery Road.

&nbsp;

The Project involves ground disturbance, watercourse crossings, and construction of new water infrastructure, all within the existing community water system footprint.

properties.description_fr:
La Premi&egrave;re Nation Kitsumkalum propose des am&eacute;liorations au r&eacute;seau d&#39;alimentation en eau domestique (DWS) de la r&eacute;serve indienne n&deg; 1 situ&eacute;e &agrave; l&#39;ouest de la ville de Terrace, en Colombie-Britannique. Les travaux comprennent la construction de deux nouveaux puits d&#39;approvisionnement en eau souterraine (puits 4-23 et puits 5-23), l&#39;installation de canalisations d&#39;eau brute vers une nouvelle usine de traitement de l&#39;eau (WTP) et la construction d&#39;une nouvelle WTP avec pr&eacute;traitement chimique, clarification, filtration et d&eacute;sinfection par UV/chlore. Un nouveau r&eacute;servoir de stockage d&#39;eau en b&eacute;ton coul&eacute; sur place sera construit au sud des r&eacute;servoirs existants, ainsi qu&#39;une conduite principale de transport reliant l&#39;usine de traitement d&#39;eau au r&eacute;servoir et des canalisations de distribution raccord&eacute;es au r&eacute;seau existant.

&nbsp;

Le projet comprend &eacute;galement le nivellement et l&#39;am&eacute;lioration des routes d&#39;acc&egrave;s afin de faciliter la construction et l&#39;exploitation &agrave; long terme. Quatre passages de conduites principales au-dessus de ruisseaux sont n&eacute;cessaires : le remplacement de deux ponceaux au niveau des ruisseaux sans nom 1 et 2, un passage &agrave; ciel ouvert au-dessus du ruisseau Eneeksaguilaguaw entre l&#39;ancien et le nouveau site du r&eacute;servoir, et l&#39;installation d&#39;un ponceau avec tranch&eacute;e &agrave; ciel ouvert au niveau du ruisseau A pr&egrave;s de Cemetery Road.

&nbsp;

Le projet implique des travaux de terrassement, des passages au-dessus de cours d&#39;eau et la construction de nouvelles infrastructures hydrauliques, le tout dans l&#39;empreinte du r&eacute;seau d&#39;approvisionnement en eau communautaire existant.

Le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale (MDN) a propos&eacute; un projet. Le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale propose de construire un champ de neutralisation des explosifs et munitions (NEM) &agrave; la 12e Escadre Shearwater, &agrave; Shearwater, en Nouvelle-&Eacute;cosse. Actuellement, la Force op&eacute;rationnelle interarm&eacute;es ne dispose pas d&#39;un champ de NEM dans la r&eacute;gion d&#39;Halifax pour &eacute;liminer les munitions dont l&#39;&eacute;limination est confi&eacute;e &agrave; l&#39;Unit&eacute; de plong&eacute;e de la flotte de l&#39;Atlantique de la Marine royale canadienne. Les munitions r&eacute;elles et les munitions au phosphore blanc sont actuellement transport&eacute;es sur des voies publiques jusqu&#39;&agrave; la Base de soutien de la 5e Division du Canada Gagetown &agrave; Oromocto, au Nouveau-Brunswick, pour y &ecirc;tre &eacute;limin&eacute;es en toute s&eacute;curit&eacute;. Cette pratique n&#39;est pas exemplaire et met beaucoup de pression sur le personnel limit&eacute; de l&#39;Unit&eacute;. Le champ de NEM propos&eacute; permettra de rem&eacute;dier &agrave; ce probl&egrave;me de s&eacute;curit&eacute; pour l&#39;Unit&eacute;.

Le champ de NEM comprendra plusieurs zones, notamment :


	une zone cl&ocirc;tur&eacute;e dot&eacute;e d&#39;une sabli&egrave;re entour&eacute;e d&#39;une berme pour l&#39;&eacute;limination des munitions au phosphore blanc;
	une zone cl&ocirc;tur&eacute;e recouverte de terre ou de gravier fin et entour&eacute;e d&#39;une berme pour l&#39;&eacute;limination de toutes les autres munitions non explos&eacute;es (UXO) classiques;
	un ensemble de pr&eacute;paration op&eacute;rationnelle (abri de d&eacute;molition) constitu&eacute; d&#39;un conteneur d&#39;exp&eacute;dition intermodal entour&eacute; d&#39;ouvrages de protection.

properties.description_en:
The Proposed Project 

&nbsp;

Weenusk First Nation is proposing the construction of 4 detached houses and a trailer home around the community.&nbsp;Each lot is 929 square metres and&nbsp;three lots require the demolition of existing residential units due to structural damages from fire or abandonment. Other construction activities will include: excavation of topsoil, backfilling and compacting new sand and gravel, grubbing, grading and levelling, foundation laying, ditching for culvert installation around the lots, and installation of electrical and plumbing. Debris will be disposed at the local community landfill.&nbsp;Any hazardous waste generated will be sent out via air or ground transportation in accordance with applicable federal regulations. Aggregate will be sourced from a nearby gravel pit. The new homes will replace homes that burnt down and mitigate overcrowded housing. Construction is estimated to start in June 2026 to October 2027.&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Projet propos&eacute;

&nbsp;

La Premi&egrave;re Nation de Weenusk propose la construction de quatre maisons individuelles et d&#39;une maison mobile dans les environs de la communaut&eacute;. Chaque lot mesure 929 m&egrave;tres carr&eacute;s et trois d&#39;entre eux n&eacute;cessitent la d&eacute;molition des habitations existantes, endommag&eacute;es par un incendie ou abandonn&eacute;es. Les travaux de construction comprendront : l&#39;excavation de la terre v&eacute;g&eacute;tale, le remblayage et le compactage de sable et de gravier, le dessouchage, le nivellement, la pose des fondations, le creusement de foss&eacute;s pour l&#39;installation de ponceaux autour des lots, ainsi que l&#39;installation des r&eacute;seaux d&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute; et de plomberie. Les d&eacute;bris seront enlev&eacute;s &agrave; la d&eacute;charge communautaire. Les d&eacute;chets dangereux produits seront transport&eacute;s par voie a&eacute;rienne ou terrestre conform&eacute;ment &agrave; la r&eacute;glementation f&eacute;d&eacute;rale en vigueur. Les agr&eacute;gats proviendront d&#39;une gravi&egrave;re situ&eacute;e &agrave; proximit&eacute;. Ces nouvelles habitations remplaceront les maisons d&eacute;truites par les flammes et contribueront &agrave; r&eacute;duire la surpopulation du logement. Les travaux devraient d&eacute;buter entre juin 2026 et octobre 2027.

properties.description_en:
The Small Craft Harbours Branch of Fisheries and Oceans Canada proposes to undertake the development of a dredge material management site intended to be used for long-term storage of sediment derived from maintenance dredging activities conducted at Sonora Small Craft Harbour in Guysborough County, Nova Scotia. Approximately 4,500 m3 of sediment is dredged from the harbour on a four (4) year cycle to ensure safe navigability and berthage of vessels. The recently acquired property (PID #35238096) is intended to be used for long-term storage of sediment dredged from the Sonora SCH.

&nbsp;

Options for reuse of this dredge material will be explored such that a portion of the material may be stored on site temporarily, however, it is anticipated that the majority of the material will be managed on site over the long-term.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Site works will involve the construction of an access road within the proposed property that will facilitate the transportation of dredge material from the harbour to the selected location within the proposed property that will be designed to store the material. Vegetation in the area will be cleared and soil at the management site will be reworked to create ditches and install silt fencing to manage surface water runoff from the site. As dredged material is intended to be end-dumped at the property and left to dewater, limited excavations are anticipated to be required to prepare the site.

&nbsp;

The material will be managed within the central portion of the property, which will provide a treed buffer around the containment area that will minimize the view from adjacent properties as well as from Sonora Road.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Construction activities are anticipated to commence in February 2026 and be completed by the end of March 2026.&nbsp; Project commencement is, however, subject to DFO-SCH operational priorities and funding, as well as the completion of regulatory approval processes, therefore work may be delayed.&nbsp; The scope of the impact assessment (subject to the Impact Assessment Act) will, therefore, be based on the works being completed over a period of 4 months commencing within a period of 5 years following finalization of the assessment.

properties.description_fr:
La Direction des ports pour petits bateaux de P&ecirc;ches et Oc&eacute;ans Canada propose d&#39;entreprendre l&#39;am&eacute;nagement d&#39;un site de gestion des mat&eacute;riaux de dragage destin&eacute; &agrave; l&#39;entreposage &agrave; long terme des s&eacute;diments issus des activit&eacute;s de dragage d&#39;entretien men&eacute;es au port pour petits bateaux de Sonora, dans le comt&eacute; de Guysborough, en Nouvelle-&Eacute;cosse. Environ 4 500 m3 de s&eacute;diments sont dragu&eacute;s dans le port tous les quatre ans afin d&#39;assurer la navigation et l&#39;amarrage s&eacute;curitaires des navires. Le site r&eacute;cemment achet&eacute; (IDP no 35238096) est destin&eacute; au stockage &agrave; long terme des s&eacute;diments dragu&eacute;s dans le port de Sonora.

&nbsp;

Des options seront explor&eacute;es pour la r&eacute;utilisation de ces d&eacute;blais de dragage afin qu&#39;une partie des mat&eacute;riaux puisse &ecirc;tre stock&eacute;e temporairement sur le site, mais la majorit&eacute; des mat&eacute;riaux devrait &ecirc;tre g&eacute;r&eacute;e sur le site &agrave; long terme.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Les travaux effectu&eacute;s sur place comprendront la construction d&#39;une voie d&#39;acc&egrave;s sur le site propos&eacute;, ce qui facilitera le transport des mat&eacute;riaux de dragage depuis le port jusqu&#39;&agrave; l&#39;emplacement choisi sur le site propos&eacute;, qui sera am&eacute;nag&eacute; pour le stockage des mat&eacute;riaux. La zone sera d&eacute;broussaill&eacute;e et le sol du site de gestion des mat&eacute;riaux sera retravaill&eacute; pour cr&eacute;er des foss&eacute;s et installer des cl&ocirc;tures anti-&eacute;rosion afin de contr&ocirc;ler le ruissellement de l&#39;eau provenant du site. &Eacute;tant donn&eacute; que l&#39;on pr&eacute;voit de d&eacute;verser les d&eacute;blais de dragage sur le site et de les laisser s&#39;&eacute;goutter, on s&#39;attend &agrave; ce que des excavations limit&eacute;es soient n&eacute;cessaires pour pr&eacute;parer le site.

&nbsp;

Les mat&eacute;riaux seront g&eacute;r&eacute;s dans la partie centrale du site, qui offrira une zone tampon bois&eacute;e autour de la zone de confinement, ce qui limitera la visibilit&eacute; depuis les propri&eacute;t&eacute;s avoisinantes et la route de Sonora.

&nbsp;

Les travaux de construction devraient commencer en f&eacute;vrier 2026 et &ecirc;tre achev&eacute;s d&#39;ici la fin du mois de mars 2026. Le lancement du projet d&eacute;pendra toutefois des priorit&eacute;s op&eacute;rationnelles de la Direction des ports pour petits bateaux de P&ecirc;ches et Oc&eacute;ans Canada (PPB du MPO) et du financement que le programme est en mesure d&#39;obtenir, de m&ecirc;me que des processus d&#39;approbation r&eacute;glementaire. Les travaux pourraient donc &ecirc;tre retard&eacute;s. La port&eacute;e de l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact (assujettie &agrave; la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact) reposera donc sur l&#39;ach&egrave;vement des travaux sur une p&eacute;riode de 4 mois commen&ccedil;ant dans les cinq (5) ann&eacute;es suivant la conclusion de l&#39;&eacute;valuation.

properties.description_en:
Black Lake First Nation is proposing the construction of a new 3 bay firehall which will house all firefighting equipment needs of the community. The project consists on the construction of new 455 sq.m. building, and landscaping of the surrounding site (approximately 1.5 ha of site development).&nbsp; The fire hall will be situated along the access road at the northern entrance to the community. While the general location along the access road has been confirmed, the Nation has not yet determined whether the facility will be constructed on the east or west side of the road.

&nbsp;

The proposed project sites considered are largely bordered by lands in a natural state. Site development will include clearing and grubbing, topsoil stripping, and excavation to footing depths. The building will be serviced by water, sewer, power, and communication lines. Water and sewer servicing alignment will be tied into the existing mains located within the adjacent roadway. Power and communication lines and routing will be installed by the respective utility companies. All anticipated waste generated from construction activities will be responsibly handled and disposed of to a designated facility for such materials.

properties.description_fr:
La Premi&egrave;re Nation de Black Lake propose la construction d&#39;une nouvelle caserne de pompiers de 3 baies qui couvrira tous les besoins en &eacute;quipement de lutte contre les incendies de la communaut&eacute;. Le projet consiste en la construction d&#39;un nouveau terrain de 455 m&sup2;. la construction et l&#39;am&eacute;nagement paysager du site environnant (environ 1,5 ha de d&eacute;veloppement du site).&nbsp; La caserne de pompiers sera situ&eacute;e le long de la route d&#39;acc&egrave;s &agrave; l&#39;entr&eacute;e nord de la communaut&eacute;. Bien que l&#39;emplacement g&eacute;n&eacute;ral le long de la route d&#39;acc&egrave;s ait &eacute;t&eacute; confirm&eacute;, la Nation n&#39;a pas encore d&eacute;termin&eacute; si l&#39;installation sera construite du c&ocirc;t&eacute; est ou ouest de la route.

&nbsp;

Les sites propos&eacute;s sont en grande partie bord&eacute;s de terres &agrave; l&#39;&eacute;tat naturel. Le d&eacute;veloppement du site comprendra le d&eacute;frichage et le d&eacute;broussage, le d&eacute;capage de la couche arable et l&#39;excavation jusqu&#39;aux fondations. Le b&acirc;timent sera desservi par des lignes d&#39;eau, d&#39;&eacute;gouts, d&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute; et de communication. L&#39;alignement des services d&#39;eau et d&#39;&eacute;gouts sera reli&eacute; aux conduites principales existantes situ&eacute;es &agrave; l&#39;int&eacute;rieur de la chauss&eacute;e adjacente. Les lignes d&#39;alimentation et de communication ainsi que le routage seront install&eacute;s par les compagnies d&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute; respectives. Tous les d&eacute;chets anticip&eacute;s g&eacute;n&eacute;r&eacute;s lors des activit&eacute;s de construction seront trait&eacute;s de mani&egrave;re responsable et &eacute;limin&eacute;s dans une installation d&eacute;sign&eacute;e pour ces mat&eacute;riaux.

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The existing fuel oil system serving 350 King Edward Avenue&#39;s life safety emergency genset and two (2) client gensets have been identified during their annual inspections that they are not in conformance with the current fuel oil code for fuel oil burning equipment CAN/CSA B139-15 - Installation code for oil-burning equipment. The fuel system is identified and registered under ECCC# 00003613.

The objective of this project is to correct deficiencies within the fuel-oil system to satisfy codes for oil-burning equipment. The generators will also be inspected to determine the existing condition for generators.

The comment period has now ended.&nbsp;

Correction of deficiencies detected in the technical report of a specialist consultant. These deficiencies are compared to the code CSA B139, CCME 2003 and to the SOR 2008-197 regulations and concern the oil tank system registered with Environment Canada under the number EC-00035826 which has a total capacity greater than 5000L. The consultant will ensure that the corrections are made so that the system becomes compliant with the codes CSA B139-2009 and CSA B139-2019, CSA-C282-09, CCME 2003, construction code and safety code and SOR regulations 2008-197.
Examples of corrective measures to be taken: repairing fittings, modifying the piping, installing an oil-tight coating, replacing hoses, modifying piping supports, replacing the pump starting system.

The comment period has now ended.&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
&nbsp;

Correction des d&eacute;ficiences d&eacute;tect&eacute;es dans le rapport technique d&#39;un consultant sp&eacute;cialis&eacute;. Ces d&eacute;ficiences sont par rapport au code CSA B139, CCME 2003 et &agrave; la r&egrave;glementation SOR 2008-197 et concernent le syst&egrave;me de r&eacute;servoirs p&eacute;troliers enregistr&eacute; aupr&egrave;s d&#39;Environnement Canada sous le num&eacute;ro EC-00035826 etqui totalise une capacit&eacute; sup&eacute;rieure &agrave; 5000L. Le consultant va s&#39;assurer que les corrections sont apport&eacute;es afin que le syst&egrave;me devienne conforme aux codes CSA B139-2009 et CSA B139-2019, CSA-C282-09, CCME 2003, code de construction et code de s&eacute;curit&eacute; et &agrave; la r&egrave;glementation SOR 2008-197.

Exemples de correctifs &agrave; apporter&nbsp;: r&eacute;parer des raccords, modifier la tuyauterie, installer un rev&ecirc;tement &eacute;tanche aux hydrocarbures, remplacer des flexibles, modifier des supports de tuyauterie, remplacer le syst&egrave;me de d&eacute;marrage des pompes.

La p&eacute;riode des commentaires est maintenant termin&eacute;e.

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
Remove and replace asphalt in the South-East parking lot. Ensure adequate cross-fall for drainage, adjust catch basins as necessary. Investigate and reuse subgrade if possible. Coordinate the placement of conduit to accommodate any future need for car charging stations. Provide a layout and signage following CSA B-651 for accessibility.
&nbsp;

The comment period has now ended.&nbsp;

The Place du Portage III (PDP3) renewal project consists in the replacement of base building components that have now reached the end of their useful life, and in the modernization of the space to meet Government of Canada Workplace Fit-Up Standards. The project will include accessibility upgrades to the main entrances, modifications to some of the public and retail spaces, replacement of the building envelope, upgrades to the Information Technology (IT) / Audio-Visual (AV) systems, new mechanical and electrical systems, as well as reinforcement of the building&#39;s structure such as to meet the most recent seismic code requirements. 

The renewal of the complex will increase the performance of the building by reducing the environmental footprint and the building&#39;s energy consumption. Additionally, it will provide improved accessibility for users, will result in a densification of the building, and will extend the life expectancy of the complex. Landscaping and exterior concrete work will be necessary in order to support these renovations, and offer opportunities to improve the outdoor areas around the building in terms of accessibility and greening. 

The comment period has now ended.&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Le projet de renouvellement de la Place du Portage III (PDP3) consiste au remplacement des &eacute;l&eacute;ments du b&acirc;timent de base qui ont maintenant atteint la fin de leur vie utile ainsi qu&#39;&agrave; la modernisation de l&#39;espace pour r&eacute;pondre aux normes d&#39;am&eacute;nagement en Milieu de travail du Gouvernement du Canada. Le projet comprendra des mises &agrave; niveau d&#39;accessibilit&eacute; aux entr&eacute;es principales, des modifications &agrave; certains espaces publics et commerciaux, le remplacement de l&#39;enveloppe du b&acirc;timent, des mises &agrave; niveau des syst&egrave;mes de technologie de l&#39;information (TI) / audiovisuel (AV), de nouveaux syst&egrave;mes m&eacute;caniques et &eacute;lectriques, ainsi que le renforcement de la structure du b&acirc;timent afin de r&eacute;pondre aux exigences les plus r&eacute;centes du code parasismique.

Le renouvellement du complexe augmentera les performances du b&acirc;timent en r&eacute;duisant l&#39;empreinte environnementale et la consommation &eacute;nerg&eacute;tique du b&acirc;timent. De plus, il offrira une meilleure accessibilit&eacute; aux utilisateurs, entra&icirc;nera une densification du b&acirc;timent et prolongera la dur&eacute;e de vie du complexe. Des am&eacute;nagements paysagers et des travaux sur le b&eacute;ton ext&eacute;rieur seront n&eacute;cessaires afin de soutenir ces r&eacute;novations et offrir des opportunit&eacute;s d&#39;am&eacute;liorer l&#39;ext&eacute;rieur du b&acirc;timent en termes d&#39;accessibilit&eacute; et d&#39;espaces vert.&nbsp;

La p&eacute;riode des commentaires est maintenant termin&eacute;e.

properties.description_en:
The project is to change the existing fuel boiler to a natural gas one, install a new gas line to the building and excavate and remove the underground fuel tank (22,765 L). The land is owned by Transport Canada and is leased by DND according to an MOU between the two departments. 

Building 351 has historically been heated using an oil-fired boiler system which utilized furnace oil, stored in an UST several metres east of the building, as a fuel source. Following a recent review of heating options, it was decided to convert the building to a natural gas system and to remove the boiler and furnace oil UST. It is understood that the UST was installed in 1993, has a capacity of 22,750 L, and is constructed of double-walled fibreglass. The tank is registered with ECCC as EC00009221. 

The comment period has now ended.&nbsp;

Project intent is to remove the redundant pad-mounted transformer and switchgear outside the DND Data Centre. The project area is expected to be about 70m2, and is outside of the building envelope. The building itself has a footprint over 1000m2.
In summary the contractor will:
&bull; Perform locates around work area;
&bull; Lift 15kV transformer from pad and remove from site;
&bull; Remove protective bollards and pad;
&bull; Saw cut section of asphalt and excavate to depth required to remove concrete duct bank and conduit
&bull; Reinstate disturbed areas.
&nbsp;

The comment period has now ended.&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Le projet vise &agrave; retirer le transformateur et l&#39;appareillage redondants mont&eacute;s sur socle &agrave; l&#39;ext&eacute;rieur du centre de donn&eacute;es du MDN. La zone du projet devrait &ecirc;tre d&#39;environ 70 m2 et se trouve &agrave; l&#39;ext&eacute;rieur de l&#39;enveloppe du b&acirc;timent. Le b&acirc;timent lui-m&ecirc;me a une superficie de plus de 1000 m2.
En r&eacute;sum&eacute;, le contractant:
&bull; Effectuer des localisations autour de la zone de travail;
&bull; Soulevez le transformateur de 15 kV du socle et retirez-le du site;
&bull; Enlever les bornes de protection et le tampon;
&bull; Scier une section d&#39;asphalte et creuser &agrave; la profondeur requise pour enlever la banque de conduits et le conduit en b&eacute;ton
&bull; R&eacute;tablir les zones perturb&eacute;es.

La p&eacute;riode des commentaires est maintenant termin&eacute;e.

properties.description_en:
Repair of existing underground tunnel located in vicinity of National Defence Medical Centre Dental Wing and Central Heating Plant. Project scope is excavation and exposure of the tunnel structure, and resealing of the tunnel&#39;s expansion joints. Specific project activities will include excavating to expose the exterior walls of the existing concrete tunnel, repairing the joints, followed by returning the soil back into place with dressing.

It is expected that this project will be completed in Spring 2021. 

The comment period has now ended.&nbsp;

Disconnect the septic tank from the dam keeper residence and PSPC office. Remove the septic tank and leaching bed. Install new septic system composed of new septic tank and wastewater treatment systems or raised leaching bed. The configuration of the system will be decided with the aid of a specialist given restrictions of the location. Restore connection of the office to the septic system.

The comment period has now ended.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The project involves the design, supply, and install a permanent (i.e. ice-resistant) waterway barrier at Latchford Dam. The new waterway barrier will remain in place year-round and must be able to withstand environmental conditions in all four seasons including ice and debris loads. The current waterway barrier is seasonal and not designed to withstand ice forces. The new barrier will also meet Transport Canada requirements. 

The waterway barrier floats are expected to be log-shaped yellow floats tied together with shackles and weldless links or chains to form a continuous barrier with a short gap between individual floats. 

The chain of floats are expected to be anchored at the river banks by mechanical or epoxy anchors drilled into rock, or by anchors bars cast within precast concrete blocks, or by some other means.&nbsp; An in-water anchor is also expected to be necessary, as the existing waterway barrier contains one.&nbsp; 

&nbsp;

The comment period has now ended.&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Le projet comprend la conception, la fourniture et l&#39;installation d&#39;une barri&egrave;re de voie navigable permanente (r&eacute;sistante &agrave; la glace) au barrage Latchford. La nouvelle barri&egrave;re de voie navigable restera en place toute l&#39;ann&eacute;e et doit pouvoir r&eacute;sister aux conditions environnementales au cours des quatre saisons, y compris les charges de glace et de d&eacute;bris. La barri&egrave;re de la voie navigable actuelle est saisonni&egrave;re et n&#39;est pas con&ccedil;ue pour r&eacute;sister aux forces des glaces. La nouvelle barri&egrave;re r&eacute;pondra &eacute;galement aux exigences de Transports Canada.

On s&#39;attend &agrave; ce que les flotteurs de barri&egrave;re de voie navigable soient des flotteurs jaunes en forme de rondin attach&eacute;s ensemble avec des manilles et des maillons ou des cha&icirc;nes sans soudure pour former une barri&egrave;re continue avec un court espace entre les flotteurs individuels.

On s&#39;attend &agrave; ce que la cha&icirc;ne de flotteurs soit ancr&eacute;e sur les berges de la rivi&egrave;re par des ancres m&eacute;caniques ou &eacute;poxy perc&eacute;es dans la roche, ou par des barres d&#39;ancrage coul&eacute;es dans des blocs de b&eacute;ton pr&eacute;fabriqu&eacute;s, ou par d&#39;autres moyens. Un ancrage dans l&#39;eau devrait &eacute;galement &ecirc;tre n&eacute;cessaire, car la barri&egrave;re de voie navigable existante en contient un.

&nbsp;

La p&eacute;riode des commentaires est maintenant termin&eacute;e.&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The project is the removal of 5 underground storage tanks and their associated piping. Tanks will be excavated and removed using an excavator. Once removed, they will be vented and rendered unusable. Tanks will be excavated, vented and removed using an excavator. The tank will be put on a flatbed for offsite disposal. The fill immediately surrounding the tank will be disposed of but no soil remediation past the tank nest will be completed at part of this project. The tanks were pumped in December 2019. If liquids are observed inside the tank at the time of removal, they will be pumped again and the liquid will be disposed of as per the regulation.
&nbsp;

The comment period has now ended.&nbsp;

The Sir John Carling (SJC) Main building and East Annex were demolished in 2014.&nbsp; The SJC West Annex was left intact.&nbsp; The building has been vacant since 2009 and it has recently been determined that it must undergo full demolition.&nbsp; The West Annex is on the future site of The Ottawa Hospital and it has been determined that it cannot be used in the development of the new hospital. 

The project will consist of full deconstruction with no rebuild, and include decommissioning, removal of all demolition debris off site and reinstatement of the site.&nbsp; A temporary access road from Prince of Wales Drive to the&nbsp;site will be constructed as part of the deconstruction project. 

The building contains asbestos, mould, and phenol-containing water. Prior to, and throughout the demolition activities, the West Annex must undergo a full dewatering plan.&nbsp;

The comment period has now ended.&nbsp;

The first phase of the project was a new prefabricated cyclist bridge between the Hull Trestle and Hull Causeway structures at the north end of the Chaudi&egrave;re Crossing in Ottawa to accommodate southbound cyclists with construction beginning in summer 2020. 

The second phase consists of the widening of the existing Hull Causeway structure to carry two vehicular lanes and one northbound cycle lane and widening the existing sidewalk between the Hull Causeway and the Union Bridge. The anticipated duration of the construction is 28 weeks, commencing in winter 2022.

The comment period has now ended.&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
La premi&egrave;re phase du projet &eacute;tait une nouvelle structure cycliste pr&eacute;fabriqu&eacute;e entre les structures Hull Trestle et la chauss&eacute;e de Hull &agrave; l&#39;extr&eacute;mit&eacute; nord de la Traverse des Chaudi&egrave;res &agrave; Ottawa pour accueillir les cyclistes en direction sud avec des travaux d&eacute;butant en &eacute;t&eacute; 2020.

La deuxi&egrave;me phase consiste &agrave; &eacute;largir la structure existante de la chauss&eacute;e de Hull pour transporter deux voies pour v&eacute;hicules et une voie cyclable en direction nord et &agrave; &eacute;largir le trottoir existant entre la chauss&eacute;e de Hull et le pont Union. La dur&eacute;e pr&eacute;vue de la construction est de 28 semaines, &agrave; compter de l&#39;hiver 2022.

La periode des commentaires est maintenant termin&eacute;e.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The project will result in the retrofit of SLTB C-Wing to establish new accommodation for the Government Operations Center (GOC). The project scope will also include adding a new lobby outside of the existing building, replacing existing exterior glazing and raising the roof of the top floor to create a higher interior space within the building.

Digging is likely in order to have the lobby sit on concrete piles or foundation wall. Existing landscape will be reinstated after completion of construction. Trees may be removed if within the new lobby footprint.&nbsp;

The comment period has now ended.&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Le projet entra&icirc;nera la modernisation du SLTB C-Wing afin d&#39;&eacute;tablir de nouveaux locaux pour le Centre des op&eacute;rations du gouvernement (COG). La port&eacute;e du projet comprendra &eacute;galement l&#39;ajout d&#39;un nouveau entr&eacute;e&nbsp;&agrave; l&#39;ext&eacute;rieur du b&acirc;timent existant, le remplacement du vitrage ext&eacute;rieur existant et l&#39;&eacute;l&eacute;vation du toit du dernier &eacute;tage pour cr&eacute;er un espace int&eacute;rieur plus &eacute;lev&eacute; dans le b&acirc;timent.

L&#39;excavation est probable&nbsp;afin que l&#39;entr&eacute;e&nbsp;soit assis sur des pieux en b&eacute;ton ou un mur de fondation. Le paysage existant sera r&eacute;tabli une fois la construction termin&eacute;e. Les arbres peuvent &ecirc;tre supprim&eacute;s s&#39;ils se trouvent dans la nouvelle empreinte de&nbsp;l&#39;entr&eacute;e.

La periode des commentaires est maintenant termin&eacute;e.&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The current conditions at the Finance Annex building require PPE to access the majority of the building due the potential risk for an occupational exposure from settled dust that has been identified to contain contaminant levels above acceptable concentrations. The contents of the building and the base building need to be cleaned following appropriate procedures. The current tenant NRCan needs to have their items moved from the Finance Annex building to their new storage location and the building needs to be cleaned and returned to PSPC. The removal of the material will require the installation of shoring and opening the walls.
&nbsp;

The comment period has now ended.&nbsp;

The Ridley Island Energy Export Facility Limited Partnership is proposing the Ridley Island Energy Export Facility Project (REEF or the Project). REEF was formerly known as the Vopak Pacific Canada Project, which received determinations in accordance with the requirements of Section 67 of the Canadian Environmental Assessment Act, 2012 and Section 82 of the Impact Assessment Act (IAA) from the Prince Rupert Port Authority, Transport Canada, and Environment and Climate Change Canada. 

&nbsp;

These determinations found that the Vopak Pacific Canada Project is not likely to cause significant adverse environmental effects. Please see Canadian Impact Assessment Registry Reference Number 81744 for more information on the Vopak Pacific Canada Project assessment. 

&nbsp;

REEF requires removal of 11.7 ha of additional terrestrial habitat that was not previously proposed in the Vopak Pacific Canada Project assessment. Environment and Climate Change Canada must make a determination as to whether the removal of 11.7 ha of terrestrial habitat for REEF is likely to cause significant adverse environmental effects under IAA s.82.

properties.description_fr:
La soci&eacute;t&eacute; en commandite de l&#39;Installation d&#39;exportation d&#39;&eacute;nergie de l&#39;&icirc;le Ridley propose le projet d&#39;installation d&#39;exportation d&#39;&eacute;nergie de l&#39;&icirc;le Ridley (REEF ou le projet). Le REEF &eacute;tait auparavant connu sous le nom de projet de Vopak Pacific Canada, qui a fait l&#39;objet de d&eacute;cisions, conform&eacute;ment aux exigences de l&#39;article 67 de la Loi canadienne sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation environnementale (2012) et de l&#39;article 82 de la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact (LEI), par l&#39;Administration portuaire de Prince Rupert, Transports Canada et Environnement et Changement climatique Canada. 

&nbsp;

Ces d&eacute;cisions concluaient que le projet de Vopak Pacific Canada n&#39;&eacute;tait pas susceptible d&#39;entra&icirc;ner des effets environnementaux n&eacute;gatifs importants. Veuillez consulter le num&eacute;ro de r&eacute;f&eacute;rence 81744 du Registre canadien d&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact pour obtenir de plus amples renseignements sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation du projet de Vopak Pacific Canada. 

&nbsp;

Le REEF exige l&#39;enl&egrave;vement de 11,7 ha d&#39;habitat terrestre suppl&eacute;mentaire, ce qui n&#39;avait pas &eacute;t&eacute; propos&eacute; auparavant dans l&#39;&eacute;valuation du projet de Vopak Pacific Canada. Environnement et Changement climatique Canada doit d&eacute;terminer si l&#39;enl&egrave;vement de 11,7 ha d&#39;habitat terrestre pour le REEF est susceptible d&#39;entra&icirc;ner des effets environnementaux n&eacute;gatifs importants en vertu de l&#39;article 82 de la LEI.

properties.description_en:
The City of Ottawa is proposing a major rehabilitation of the Carling Avenue Bridge. The bridge is located within urban Ottawa, just south of the existing Lincoln Fields Bus Rapid Transit Station and future Light Rail Transit (LRT) Station, crossing over the Kichi Zibi Mikan Parkway (the Parkway) and the Southwest (SW) Transitway; the bridge and existing right-of-way (ROW) are owned and managed by the City of Ottawa.

The proposed bridge rehabilitation&mdash;occurring entirely outside NCC lands&mdash;generally includes bridge deck repairs and modifications to approach roadways, repairs to concrete surfaces, structural steel recoating, modifications to bridge lighting and utility relocations.

Temporary staging areas are needed for the bridge rehabilitation. These staging areas will be on National Capital Commission (NCC) land, on the north and south sides of the west end of the bridge. &nbsp;This part of the project is subject to a federal land use, design, and real estate transaction approval under&nbsp;the National Capital Act, and a determination under the Impact Assessment Act.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;



The two staging areas will be placed in existing green spaces inside the ramp loops and will cover about 3,300 square metres in total. These staging areas will be used for the contractor&#39;s site trailers, storage of material and equipment, the field office for contract administration, and parking for construction staff.

Before use, the staging areas will be prepared by temporarily covering existing grass surfaces with geotextile material and a layer of aggregates. No excavation is planned. No tree removal is expected, and the existing trees on the edges of the staging areas will be protected. Construction access points will be needed from the multi-use pathways on both sides of the Parkway, and measures will be put in place to safely manage pedestrians and cyclists. Work under the bridge will require scaffolding and protection enclosures,&nbsp; and traffic controls will be used for any work above and near the Parkway. All temporary work will be removed, and any disturbed areas will be reinstated once construction is finished.

The project is currently in the design phase, which is expected to finish in fall of 2026. Construction is planned to begin in winter of 2026 (depending on the completion of the Stage 2 Light Rail Transit project) and finish by summer 2029.

Serpent River First Nation has proposed a remediation project for the metals, Sulphate, low pH, petroleum&nbsp;hydrocarbons (PHC), and polycyclic&nbsp;aromatic hydrocarbons (PAH) impacts at the Former Cutler Acid Site. The project involves excavation of all areas with impacted soil, excluding areas impacted only with low pH which will be remediated with hydrated lime, will be taken to a MECP licensed landfill or selected treatment facility.&nbsp;The Site currently contains approximately 82,200 m3&nbsp;of&nbsp;contaminated soil requiring excavation and off-Site disposal.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Physical activities will include tree clearing and grubbing, culvert and ditch installations, excavation of impacted soil, and removal of terrestrial debris (fill, concrete house foundation, and construction and&nbsp;demolition materials such as concrete, bricks, wood, metal machinery parts, metal piping, reinforcing bars, and&nbsp;wire). After excavation is completed, the site will be backfilled and restored to a natural state in accordance with Serpent River First Nation&#39;s native grass and plant species. Any gravel roadways that were present will prior to excavation will be reinstated.&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
La Premi&egrave;re Nation de Serpent River a propos&eacute; un projet d&#39;assainissement pour rem&eacute;dier aux impacts des m&eacute;taux, du sulfate, du faible pH, des hydrocarbures p&eacute;troliers (PHC) et des hydrocarbures aromatiques polycycliques (HAP) sur l&#39;ancien site Cutler Acid. Le projet consiste &agrave; excaver toutes les zones dont le sol est contamin&eacute;, &agrave; l&#39;exception des zones uniquement touch&eacute;es par un faible pH, qui seront assainies &agrave; l&#39;aide de chaux hydrat&eacute;e, puis transport&eacute;es vers une d&eacute;charge agr&eacute;&eacute;e par le MECP ou une installation de traitement s&eacute;lectionn&eacute;e. Le site contient actuellement environ 82 200 m3 de sol contamin&eacute; qui doit &ecirc;tre excav&eacute; et &eacute;limin&eacute; hors site.

&nbsp;

Les activit&eacute;s physiques comprendront le d&eacute;boisement et l&#39;essouchement, l&#39;installation de ponceaux et de foss&eacute;s, l&#39;excavation du sol contamin&eacute; et l&#39;enl&egrave;vement des d&eacute;bris terrestres (remblai, fondations de maisons en b&eacute;ton et mat&eacute;riaux de construction et de d&eacute;molition tels que b&eacute;ton, briques, bois, pi&egrave;ces m&eacute;talliques de machines, tuyaux m&eacute;talliques, barres d&#39;armature et fils m&eacute;talliques). Une fois l&#39;excavation termin&eacute;e, le site sera remblay&eacute; et restaur&eacute; &agrave; son &eacute;tat naturel, conform&eacute;ment aux esp&egrave;ces v&eacute;g&eacute;tales et herbac&eacute;es indig&egrave;nes de la Premi&egrave;re Nation de Serpent River. Toutes les routes en gravier qui existaient avant l&#39;excavation seront r&eacute;tablies.

Construite entre 1965 et 1967, l&#39;autoroute Bonaventure arrive aujourd&#39;hui &agrave; la fin de sa vie utile. Ainsi, Les Ponts Jacques Cartier et Champlain Incorpor&eacute;e (PJCCI) proc&egrave;dera &agrave; des travaux d&#39;entretien et de r&eacute;fection sur un tron&ccedil;on d&#39;une longueur d&#39;environ 1,1&nbsp;kilom&egrave;tre qui d&eacute;bute &agrave; une centaine de m&egrave;tres au nord-est du pont Cl&eacute;ment et qui se termine aux bretelles d&#39;acc&egrave;s &agrave; l&#39;autoroute 15 sur l&#39;&Icirc;le des S&oelig;urs. 

Des inspections ont r&eacute;v&eacute;l&eacute; certains d&eacute;fauts dans les diff&eacute;rentes structures aux abords du pont Cl&eacute;ment et au niveau de la chauss&eacute;e sur l&#39;&Icirc;le des S&oelig;urs. Les inspections ont aussi r&eacute;v&eacute;l&eacute; certaines d&eacute;ficiences au niveau des ouvrages de drainage et autres &eacute;l&eacute;ments de voirie. Afin d&#39;assurer la p&eacute;rennit&eacute; des infrastructures, des travaux d&#39;entretien et de r&eacute;fection sont jug&eacute;s n&eacute;cessaires. Le pr&eacute;sent projet vise donc &agrave; corriger un ensemble de d&eacute;ficiences et &agrave; augmenter le niveau de s&eacute;curit&eacute; routi&egrave;re en effectuant plusieurs travaux de r&eacute;habilitation de ce tron&ccedil;on de l&#39;autoroute Bonaventure.

Plus sp&eacute;cifiquement, les travaux comprennent principalement, sans s&#39;y limiter&nbsp;:


	R&eacute;fection du pont Cl&eacute;ment ;
	R&eacute;fection compl&egrave;te de la chauss&eacute;e sur le pont Cl&eacute;ment, sur les voies de l&#39;approche sud du Pont cl&eacute;ment ainsi que sur la bretelle provenant du pont Cl&eacute;ment vers la 15S (+- 1100 m. lin) ;
	R&eacute;fection des deux viaducs de l&#39;approche sud sur l&#39;&Icirc;le des S&oelig;urs ;
	R&eacute;fection d&#39;une superstructure ;
	Remplacement de syst&egrave;mes de drainage ;
	R&eacute;fection et remplacement de lampadaires et modifications au r&eacute;seau &eacute;lectrique pour l&#39;installation de luminaires de type DEL.


Les travaux auront lieu durant les saisons estivales 2024 et 2025.

Compte tenu de la nature des travaux, des entraves auront lieu sur le pont Cl&eacute;ment, limitant la circulation &agrave; une voie dans chaque direction.

Le projet pr&eacute;voit un ensemble de mesures de protection de l&#39;environnement, notamment pour la protection de la population d&#39;hirondelles &agrave; front blanc qui niche sous le tablier du pont Cl&eacute;ment.&nbsp;

Ce projet d&#39;entretien et de r&eacute;fection s&#39;inscrit dans la mission de PJCCI qui est d&#39;assurer la mobilit&eacute; des usagers, la s&eacute;curit&eacute;, et la p&eacute;rennit&eacute; des infrastructures en pr&eacute;conisant une gestion syst&eacute;mique selon une approche de d&eacute;veloppement durable.

properties.description_en:
The Proposed Project

&nbsp;

Nibinamik First Nation is proposing the installation of a pre-purchased bridge at winter road Crossing #1, approximately 1.7 km south of the community. This project would improve early access to opening and construction of the winter road since it is the first water crossing. This crossing has proven difficult to maintain as small culverts and fill were used in its initial construction. Overland flooding occurs regularly as the creek exceeds the culvert capacity. Installing a portable bridge would alleviate these challenges and extend the winter road season.

properties.description_fr:
Projet propos&eacute;

&nbsp;

La Premi&egrave;re Nation de Nibinamik propose l&#39;installation d&#39;un pont pr&eacute;achet&eacute; au passage &agrave; niveau n&deg; 1 de la route d&#39;hiver, situ&eacute; &agrave; environ 1,7 km au sud de la communaut&eacute;. Ce projet faciliterait l&#39;acc&egrave;s &agrave; la route d&#39;hiver d&egrave;s son ouverture et pour la construction, puisqu&#39;il s&#39;agit du premier passage &agrave; niveau. L&#39;entretien de ce passage s&#39;av&egrave;re difficile, car sa construction initiale a n&eacute;cessit&eacute; de petits ponceaux et du remblai. Des inondations se produisent r&eacute;guli&egrave;rement lorsque le ruisseau d&eacute;passe la capacit&eacute; des ponceaux. L&#39;installation d&#39;un pont mobile permettrait de rem&eacute;dier &agrave; ces probl&egrave;mes et de prolonger la saison d&#39;utilisation de la route d&#39;hiver.

properties.description_en:
The proposed project will involve the reconstruction of the breakwater structures located on the western side of the Larrys River Small Craft Harbour. The current breakwaters on the western side consist of three separate structures including a rubblemound structure approximately 220 meters (m) in length that extends from the shore on the mainland out to Ram Island. A second breakwater rubblemound structure extends from the east side of Ram Island into the entrance of the harbour and is conjoined to a crib structure with a concrete deck. The three existing breakwater structures have deteriorated to the point whereby major reconstruction is required.&nbsp; It is estimated that the crest level of the remaining western breakwater is approximately 1.0 m above chart datum.&nbsp; During high tide cycles, the western breakwater is currently submerged and water flows into the lee side of the harbour area.

&nbsp;

The reconstruction will involve the full encapsulation of the three existing breakwater structures with layers of rock materials including core, filter and armour stone.&nbsp; The new breakwaters will be raised 3.75 m above chart datum to adapt to the projected sea-level rise and prevent overtopping during storm conditions. This will result in a footprint expansion below high normal tide (HNT) of approximately 3,275 m2.

&nbsp;

The work will be conducted using heavy equipment such as excavators, cranes, front-end loaders, and trucks working from the existing structures. There will be no demolition or removals associated with the construction as all existing structures will remain in-situ and will be completely encapsulated by layers of imported core, filter and armour stone.&nbsp; Rock material will be hauled in and placed directly in the new works starting on the mainland and working out incrementally to Ram Island.

&nbsp;

Construction activities are anticipated to commence in spring 2026 and be completed by the end of March 2027.&nbsp; Project commencement is, however, subject to DFO-SCH operational priorities and funding, as well as the completion of regulatory approval processes, therefore work may be delayed.&nbsp; The scope of the impact assessment (subject to the Impact Assessment Act) will, therefore, be based on the works being completed over a period of 12 months commencing within a period of 5 years following finalization of the assessment.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Larrys River SCH has been developed to support the commercial fishery, which is a main economic driver for the community.&nbsp; The main purpose of this project is to carry out reconstruction of the existing infrastructure so that the harbour can operate safely and&nbsp; continue to serve the fishing industry.

properties.description_fr:
Le projet propos&eacute; comprendra la reconstruction des brise-lames situ&eacute;s du c&ocirc;t&eacute; ouest du port pour petits bateaux de Larrys River. Les brise-lames actuels, situ&eacute;s du c&ocirc;t&eacute; ouest, sont constitu&eacute;s de trois structures distinctes, dont une structure en enrochement d&#39;environ 220 m&egrave;tres de long qui s&#39;&eacute;tend du rivage sur le continent jusqu&#39;&agrave; Ram Island. Un deuxi&egrave;me brise-lames en enrochement s&#39;&eacute;tend du c&ocirc;t&eacute; est de Ram Island jusqu&#39;&agrave; l&#39;entr&eacute;e du port, et il est reli&eacute; &agrave; une structure de caissons munie d&#39;un tablier en b&eacute;ton. Les trois brise-lames existants se sont d&eacute;t&eacute;rior&eacute;s au point o&ugrave; d&#39;importants travaux de reconstruction sont n&eacute;cessaires. On estime que le c&ocirc;t&eacute; du couronnement du brise-lames ouest restant est d&#39;environ 1 m au-dessus du z&eacute;ro des cartes. &Agrave; mar&eacute;e haute, le brise-lames ouest est submerg&eacute; et l&#39;eau s&#39;&eacute;coule du c&ocirc;t&eacute; sous le vent de la zone portuaire.

&nbsp;

Les travaux de reconstruction comprendront l&#39;encapsulation compl&egrave;te des trois brise-lames existants avec des couches de mat&eacute;riaux rocheux, notamment des roches de noyau, des roches de filtration et des pierres de protection. Les nouveaux brise-lames auront une hauteur de 3,75 m au-dessus du z&eacute;ro des cartes afin de tenir compte de la hausse pr&eacute;vue du niveau de la mer et d&#39;emp&ecirc;cher les d&eacute;bordements en cas de temp&ecirc;te. Il en r&eacute;sultera une augmentation d&#39;environ 3 275 m2 de l&#39;empreinte au sol sous le niveau de la mar&eacute;e haute normale.

&nbsp;

Les travaux seront effectu&eacute;s &agrave; l&#39;aide d&#39;&eacute;quipement lourd, comme des excavatrices, des grues, des chargeuses frontales et des camions travaillant &agrave; partir des structures existantes. Aucun travail de d&eacute;molition ou d&#39;enl&egrave;vement ne sera associ&eacute; &agrave; la construction, car toutes les structures existantes resteront en place et seront compl&egrave;tement encapsul&eacute;es &agrave; l&#39;aide de couches de roches de noyau, de roches de filtration et de pierres de protection. Les mat&eacute;riaux rocheux seront transport&eacute;s et directement int&eacute;gr&eacute;s aux nouveaux ouvrages, en partant du continent et en avan&ccedil;ant progressivement jusqu&#39;&agrave; Ram Island.

&nbsp;

Les travaux de construction devraient commencer au printemps 2026 et &ecirc;tre achev&eacute;s d&#39;ici la fin du mois de mars 2027. Le lancement du projet d&eacute;pendra toutefois des priorit&eacute;s op&eacute;rationnelles de la Direction des ports pour petits bateaux de P&ecirc;ches et Oc&eacute;ans Canada (PPB du MPO) et du financement que le programme est en mesure d&#39;obtenir, de m&ecirc;me que des processus d&#39;approbation r&eacute;glementaire. Les travaux pourraient donc &ecirc;tre retard&eacute;s. La port&eacute;e de l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact (assujettie &agrave; la Loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact) reposera donc sur l&#39;ach&egrave;vement des travaux sur une p&eacute;riode de 12 mois commen&ccedil;ant dans les cinq (5) ann&eacute;es suivant la conclusion de l&#39;&eacute;valuation.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Le PPB de Larrys River a &eacute;t&eacute; construit pour soutenir la p&ecirc;che commerciale, qui est l&#39;un des principaux moteurs &eacute;conomiques de la communaut&eacute;. L&#39;objectif principal de ce projet est de reconstruire les infrastructures existantes afin que le port puisse fonctionner de fa&ccedil;on s&eacute;curitaire et continuer &agrave; desservir l&#39;industrie de la p&ecirc;che.

properties.description_en:
As part of the National Capital Commission (NCC) Corporate Priority to develop and implement recreational and animation sites across the National Capital Region, the NCC River House, located at 501 Sir George-&Eacute;tienne Cartier Parkway on the Ottawa River, has been identified as the site for a new year-round recreational infrastructure project. To support this priority and to take advantage of the current infrastructure, the NCC plans to install a floating sauna on the shoreline near the River House.

&nbsp;

To ensure that the sauna&apos;s operations are reliable and safe and to lay the groundwork for future amenities and shoreline activities, the installation of a new electrical service bollard is proposed. This utility will be located approximately 75 metres east of the swim dock area and will connect to the main River House building. It will provide essential power not only for the sauna but also for potential future activities along the waterfront.

&nbsp;

Currently, the lack of electrical infrastructure on the shoreline limits the ability to power new facilities or activities and to provide reliable year-round supply. The proposed electrical infrastructure, as part of the sauna installation, will not only support NCC&apos;s mandate to enhance public offerings, but also comply with operational, safety, and sustainability standards. The new electrical infrastructure will be designed using durable materials suitable for Ottawa&apos;s climate and recurring flood risks associated with the Ottawa River. The design will prioritize easy access for maintenance, minimize environmental impacts, and ensure dependable, year-round service to safeguard both public and operator safety. &nbsp;Project implementation is planned for winter 2025-2026.

&nbsp;

The National Capital Commission must determine whether the proposed electrical upgrades for recreational infrastructure at the NCC River House are likely to cause significant adverse environmental effects under sections 81-91 of the Impact Assessment Act, 2019 and the National Capital Act, 1985. A federal land use, design and transaction approval (FLUDTA) is required for this work.

properties.description_fr:
Une des priorit&eacute;s organisationnelles de la Commission de la capitale nationale (CCN) consiste &agrave; d&eacute;velopper et mettre en &oelig;uvre des lieux de loisirs et d&#39;animation dans la r&eacute;gion de la capitale nationale. La Maison riveraine de la CCN, situ&eacute;e au 501, promenade Sir-George-&Eacute;tienne-Cartier, sur la rivi&egrave;re des Outaouais, a &eacute;t&eacute; choisie comme site pour un nouveau projet d&#39;infrastructure r&eacute;cr&eacute;ative ouvert &agrave; l&apos;ann&eacute;e. Afin de soutenir cette priorit&eacute; et tirer avantage de l&apos;infrastructure existante, la CCN pr&eacute;voit installer un sauna flottant sur la rive de la Maison Riveraine.

&nbsp;

Afin de garantir le fonctionnement fiable et s&eacute;curitaire du sauna et de pr&eacute;parer le terrain pour de futurs am&eacute;nagements et activit&eacute;s riveraines, l&#39;installation d&#39;une nouvelle borne &eacute;lectrique est propos&eacute;e. Cette installation sera d&eacute;ploy&eacute;e &agrave; environ 75 m&egrave;tres &agrave; l&#39;est de la zone de baignade et reli&eacute;e au b&acirc;timent principal de la Maison riveraine. Elle alimentera non seulement le sauna, mais aussi d&#39;&eacute;ventuelles activit&eacute;s le long de la rivi&egrave;re.

&nbsp;

Pr&eacute;sentement, l&#39;absence d&#39;infrastructure &eacute;lectrique sur la rive sud de la rivi&egrave;re des Outaouais limite la capacit&eacute; d&#39;approvisionner en &eacute;nergie de nouvelles installations ou activit&eacute;s et d&#39;assurer une alimentation fiable tout au long de l&#39;ann&eacute;e. L&#39;infrastructure &eacute;lectrique propos&eacute;e dans le cadre de l&#39;installation du sauna permettra non seulement de soutenir le mandat de la CCN, visant &agrave; am&eacute;liorer l&#39;offre publique, mais aussi de se conformer aux normes op&eacute;rationnelles, de s&eacute;curit&eacute; et de durabilit&eacute;. La nouvelle infrastructure &eacute;lectrique sera con&ccedil;ue &agrave; partir de mat&eacute;riaux durables adapt&eacute;s au climat d&#39;Ottawa et aux risques d&#39;inondation r&eacute;currents associ&eacute;s &agrave; la rivi&egrave;re des Outaouais. La conception privil&eacute;giera la facilit&eacute; d&#39;acc&egrave;s pour l&#39;entretien, minimisera les impacts environnementaux et garantira un service fiable tout au long de l&#39;ann&eacute;e afin de pr&eacute;server la s&eacute;curit&eacute; du public et des op&eacute;rateurs. La mise en &oelig;uvre du projet est pr&eacute;vue pour l&#39;hiver 2025-2026.

&nbsp;

La Commission de la capitale nationale doit d&eacute;terminer si les am&eacute;liorations &eacute;lectriques propos&eacute;es pour les infrastructures r&eacute;cr&eacute;atives de la Maison Riveraine de la CCN sont susceptibles d&#39;avoir des effets n&eacute;gatifs importants sur l&#39;environnement en vertu des articles 81 &agrave; 91 de la Loi de 2019 sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation des impacts et de la Loi de 1985 sur la capitale nationale. Une approbation f&eacute;d&eacute;rale de l&apos;utilisation du sol, du design et des transactions immobili&egrave;res (AFUSDTI) est requise pour ces travaux.

L&#39;APM souhaite mettre &agrave; niveau le quai 101 du Port de Montr&eacute;al pour permettre d&#39;assurer la s&eacute;curit&eacute; de navigation des navires empruntant ce quai. Le quai 101 est situ&eacute; sur une partie du lot 1&nbsp;250&nbsp;987 &agrave; Montr&eacute;al-Est.

&nbsp;

Le projet pr&eacute;voit la consolidation d&#39;un caisson du quai, l&#39;approfondissement du fond marin adjacent au quai &agrave; la profondeur requise pour la navigation, l&#39;installation de nouvelles d&eacute;fenses d&#39;accostage, et la r&eacute;fection ponctuelle de la fa&ccedil;ade de quai. 

&nbsp;

Les travaux sont pr&eacute;vus d&eacute;buter au printemps 2026.

properties.description_en:
The Department of National Defence (DND) has proposed a project. This Activity will pertain to three projects to be undertaken in Lielvarde, Latvia, as part of Canadian Armed Forces operations;

1. Apron &amp; Flight Line Infrastructure (apron, helipad permanent office building, 3 x permanent hangars, parking lot, access roads, tent membrane structure on gravel pads);

2. Real Life Support Area Infrastructure (paved loop road and parking lot, gravel pads, ISO structure buildings, tent membrane structure on concrete pads); and

3. Permanent Accommodations Building (up to 304 persons).

properties.description_fr:
Le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale (MDN) a propos&eacute; un projet. Cette activit&eacute; portera sur 3 projets qui seront entrepris &agrave; Lielvarde, en Lettonie, dans le cadre des op&eacute;rations des Forces arm&eacute;es canadiennes;

1. Infrastructure de l&#39;aire de trafic et de la ligne de vol (aire de trafic, immeuble de bureaux permanent pour h&eacute;liport, 3 hangars permanents, parking, routes d&#39;acc&egrave;s, structure de tente en membrane sur dalles de gravier);

2. Infrastructure de la zone de support d&#39;assistance vitale (route en boucle pav&eacute;e et parking, dalles de gravier, b&acirc;timents &agrave; structure ISO, structure de tente en membrane sur dalles en b&eacute;ton); et

3. B&acirc;timent d&#39;h&eacute;bergement permanent (jusqu&#39;&agrave; 304 personnes).

properties.description_en:
The wharf reconstruction project at Camp Cove Small Craft Harbour (SCH) will include the removing of the existing ell (402) and&nbsp; stem (401) wharves as well as new scour protection surrounding the T-wharf (404).

The existing T-wharf (404) cribwork will remain and a 9 m transition ramp at a 5% slope will be built to connect the T-wharf (404) to the stem wharf (401). Scour protection will surround the T-wharf starting on the southeast side to the northwest side stopping at the end of the transition ramp. The existing stem wharf (401) timber cribwork with concrete deck will be completely removed. Silt and organics will be removed to reveal the top of existing rock mattress where 400 mm of thickness will be removed. This process will be duplicated in removing the existing ell wharf (402).

A new crib structure will be built so the ell wharf (402) can be connected to the stem wharf (401). The new timber cribwork for the ell will be approximately 63 m in length by approximately 8 m wide. The existing rock mattress will be used to support a new clear stone rock mattress measuring 400 mm beginning at a chart datum elevation of -2.85 m. Clear stone will be placed at a 1.5: 1 ratio and on the inland side, scour protection using precast concrete blocks measuring 3000 mm x 3000 mm chained together will be placed on the new rock mattress. The crib structure for the ell wharf (402) will be built to an elevation of +6.03 m on the lower slope end of the 300 mm thick concrete deck. The crib will be filled with ballast rock and built with 200 mm x 200 mm treated timber.&nbsp;

A new crib structure will be built so the stem wharf (401) can be connected to the ell (402) and tee wharves (404). It will measure approximately 95 m in length and approximately 8 m wide. The new crib structure will use the remaining existing rock mattress to support 400 mm thick new clear stone placed at a 1.5: 1 ratio. The structure will be built using ballast rock and 200 mm x 200 mm treated timber to an elevation of +6.03 m. A new asphalt approach road will lead onto the stem wharf. The last section of approach road will be supported by corerstone to an elevation of approximately +6.03 m.&nbsp; The approach road and a section of crib #1 of the stem wharf (401) will consist of R-25 road base aggregate at a 1.5: 1 slope starting at El +2.42 m to EL. +6.10 m.&nbsp; The 300 mm thick reinforced concrete deck will be placed at EL + 6.10 m on top of the crib structure.&nbsp;

The wharf&nbsp; reconstruction will consist of the use of heavy equipment such as excavators and haul trucks working from the shore as it is being constructed. Alternatively, an access road, temporary work bridge or barge may be used for heavy equipment to conduct work on the stem and ell sections of the wharf.

properties.description_fr:
Le projet de reconstruction du quai du port pour petits bateaux de Camp Cove comprendra l&apos;enl&egrave;vement des quais en forme d&apos;&eacute;trave (402) et d&apos;&eacute;trave (401) existants ainsi qu&apos;une nouvelle protection contre l&apos;affouillement autour du quai en T (404).

Le quai en T (404) existant sera conserv&eacute; et une rampe de transition de 9 m &agrave; une pente de 5% sera construite pour relier le quai en T (404) au quai d&apos;&eacute;trave (401). Une protection contre l&apos;affouillement entourera le quai en T &agrave; partir du c&ocirc;t&eacute; sud-est jusqu&apos;au c&ocirc;t&eacute; nord-ouest et s&apos;arr&ecirc;tera &agrave; l&apos;extr&eacute;mit&eacute; de la rampe de transition. Le quai d&apos;&eacute;trave existant (401) &agrave; encoffrement en bois avec tablier en b&eacute;ton sera compl&egrave;tement enlev&eacute;. Le limon et les mati&egrave;res organiques seront enlev&eacute;s pour r&eacute;v&eacute;ler le dessus du lit de roches existant, o&ugrave; 400 mm d&apos;&eacute;paisseur seront enlev&eacute;s. Ce processus sera reproduit lors de l&apos;enl&egrave;vement du quai en saillie existant (402).

Une nouvelle structure &agrave; encoffrement sera construite afin que le quai &agrave; claire-voie (402) puisse &ecirc;tre reli&eacute; au quai d&apos;&eacute;trave (401). Le nouvel encoffrement en bois d&apos;&oelig;uvre de l&apos;aile mesurera environ 63 m de longueur sur environ 8 m de largeur. Le lit de roches existant servira &agrave; soutenir un nouveau lit de pierres claires mesurant 400 mm &agrave; partir d&apos;une &eacute;l&eacute;vation du z&eacute;ro des cartes de -2,85 m. Des pierres claires seront plac&eacute;es dans un rapport de 1,5 : 1 et, du c&ocirc;t&eacute; int&eacute;rieur, une protection contre l&apos;affouillement au moyen de blocs de b&eacute;ton pr&eacute;fabriqu&eacute;s mesurant 3 000 mm x 3 000 mm, encha&icirc;n&eacute;s les uns aux autres, sera mise en place sur le nouveau lit de pierre. La structure &agrave; encoffrement du quai en forme d&apos;aile (402) sera construite &agrave; une &eacute;l&eacute;vation de +6,03 m sur l&apos;extr&eacute;mit&eacute; inf&eacute;rieure de la pente du tablier en b&eacute;ton de 300 mm d&apos;&eacute;paisseur. L&apos;encoffrement sera rempli de pierres de ballast et construit avec du bois trait&eacute; de 200 mm x 200 mm.&nbsp;

Une nouvelle structure &agrave; encoffrement sera construite afin que le quai d&apos;&eacute;trave (401) puisse &ecirc;tre reli&eacute; aux quais en saillie (402) et en T (404). Il mesurera environ 95 m de longueur et environ 8 m de largeur. La nouvelle structure de caissons utilisera le lit de pierre restant existant pour supporter de nouvelles pierres claires de 400 mm d&apos;&eacute;paisseur plac&eacute;es selon un rapport de 1,5:1. La structure sera construite avec de la roche de ballast et du bois trait&eacute; de 200 mm x 200 mm &agrave; une &eacute;l&eacute;vation de +6,03 m. Un nouveau chemin d&apos;acc&egrave;s asphalt&eacute; m&egrave;nera au quai d&apos;&eacute;trave. Le dernier tron&ccedil;on de la route d&apos;acc&egrave;s sera support&eacute; par des pierres de carottage jusqu&apos;&agrave; une &eacute;l&eacute;vation d&apos;environ +6,03 m.&nbsp; La route d&apos;acc&egrave;s et une section de l&apos;encoffrement #1 du quai d&apos;&eacute;trave (401) seront constitu&eacute;es de granulats de base de route R-25 &agrave; une pente de 1,5:1 &agrave; partir de El +2,42 m &agrave; EL +6,10 m.&nbsp; Le tablier en b&eacute;ton arm&eacute; de 300 mm d&apos;&eacute;paisseur sera plac&eacute; &agrave; EL + 6,10 m au-dessus de la structure du caisson.&nbsp;

La reconstruction du quai consistera en l&apos;utilisation d&apos;&eacute;quipement lourd, comme des excavatrices et des camions de transport, &agrave; partir de la rive pendant sa construction. Autrement, une route d&apos;acc&egrave;s, un pont de travail temporaire ou une barge peut &ecirc;tre utilis&eacute; pour l&apos;&eacute;quipement lourd afin d&apos;effectuer des travaux sur les sections de l&apos;&eacute;trave et de l&apos;&eacute;trave du quai..

properties.description_en:
Agnico Eagle is proposing the construction, operation, decommissioning and abandonment of an underground gold mine located in the Abitibi-T&eacute;miscamingue region, approximately 15&nbsp;kilometres from downtown Rouyn-Noranda, Quebec. As proposed, the Wasamac Gold Mine Project would have a mine life of 11&nbsp;years and an ore production capacity of 6053&nbsp;tonnes per day. The project would include the operation of an underground mine, the construction of an ore processing plant and related infrastructure, and the development of underground infrastructure for ore and waste rock transportation as well as waste rock, tailings and overburden accumulation areas.

&nbsp;

Please note that the proponent for this project was previously Monarch Gold Corporation (2020 to January&nbsp;21,&nbsp;2021) and then Yamana Gold Inc. (January&nbsp;21,&nbsp;2023 - March 31,&nbsp;2023).

properties.description_fr:
Agnico Eagle propose la construction, l&#39;exploitation, la d&eacute;saffectation et la fermeture d&#39;une mine aurif&egrave;re souterraine, situ&eacute;e &agrave; environ 15 kilom&egrave;tres du centre-ville de Rouyn-Noranda dans la r&eacute;gion de l&#39;Abitibi-T&eacute;miscamingue au Qu&eacute;bec. Tel qu&#39;il est propos&eacute;, le projet minier aurif&egrave;re Wasamac aurait une dur&eacute;e de vie de 11&nbsp;ans et une capacit&eacute; de production de minerai de 6053&nbsp;tonnes par jour. Le projet comprendrait l&#39;exploitation d&#39;une mine souterraine, l&#39;implantation d&#39;une usine de traitement du minerai et d&#39;infrastructures connexes, la mise en place d&#39;infrastructures souterraines d&eacute;di&eacute;es au transport du minerai et du st&eacute;rile ainsi que des aires d&#39;accumulation de st&eacute;riles, de r&eacute;sidus et de mort-terrain.

&nbsp;

Veuillez noter que le promoteur de ce projet &eacute;tait pr&eacute;c&eacute;demment Corporation Aurif&egrave;re Monarques (de 2020 au 21&nbsp;janvier&nbsp;2021) et ensuite Yamana Gold (du 21&nbsp;janvier&nbsp;2021 au 31&nbsp;mars 2023).

properties.description_en:
Whitecap Dakota Nation is proposing a new Water Treatment Plant Upgrade &amp; Wells Project. Work includes new well development, new raw water pipeline, new water treatment plant building and reservoir. Building life is 50 years with other components for wells and treatment estimated to have a 10 year lifespan before replacement of upgrade.&nbsp; The reservoir will be a concrete substructure sized for 861,793 L of potable storage,&nbsp; approximately 800 sq.m. building, new 9.2 L/s raw water system and 6.0 L/s treatment system utilizing bio-membrane filtration.

&nbsp;

Work will require new raw water mains, new distribution mains, new sewer mains, new natural gas and electrical lines to the building.

&nbsp;

Work will include construction of new wells, directional drilling under existing roads and tree areas, topsoil removal to excavate for a new building and backfilling once structure is complete.&nbsp; Total disturbed area to be less than 3500sq.m. The project will also require new raw water mains, new distribution mains, new sewer mains, new natural gas and electrical lines to the building.

&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Whitecap Dakota Nation is proposing a new Water Treatment Plant Upgrade &amp; Wells Project. Work includes new well development, new raw water pipeline, new water treatment plant building and reservoir. Building life is 50 years with other components for wells and treatment estimated to have a 10 year lifespan before replacement of upgrade.&nbsp; The reservoir will be a concrete substructure sized for 861,793 L of potable storage,&nbsp; approximately 800 sq.m. building, new 9.2 L/s raw water system and 6.0 L/s treatment system utilizing bio-membrane filtration.

&nbsp;

Work will require new raw water mains, new distribution mains, new sewer mains, new natural gas and electrical lines to the building.

&nbsp;

Work will include construction of new wells, directional drilling under existing roads and tree areas, topsoil removal to excavate for a new building and backfilling once structure is complete.&nbsp; Total disturbed area to be less than 3500sq.m. The project will also require new raw water mains, new distribution mains, new sewer mains, new natural gas and electrical lines to the building.

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
Signature Aviation is proposing to construct and operate a new helicopter hangar at 4360 Agar Drive, Vancouver International Airport in Richmond, B.C. This new facility is an expansion of their existing hangar facilities at the same address. The proposed hangar&nbsp;&nbsp; building&nbsp; has approximately 2,600 square meters of floor space over one and half floors. The total project area is approximately 4700 m2. The new hangar building will include helicopter storage and maintenance area, as well as office spaces. New facilities will include the new hangar building, new security fence including relocation of primary security line (PSL), parking lot expansion, landscaping, new vehicle lanes and pathways, utilities&nbsp;&nbsp; and site services. The hangar is intended to be used for helicopters dedicated to air ambulance use and will be utilized for aircraft maintenance and storage. Operations will occur on an as needed basis, with air ambulance helicopters dispatched and returning according to demand. The hangar will have capacity for up to three helicopters. Daily aircraft movements will therefore vary as the facility supports emergency and maintenance activities. Full time support staff will be on site, and pilots may also be accommodated on the premises to assist with air ambulance and evacuation procedures as needed.

&nbsp;

The site is currently occupied by pavement (parking lot) and vacant grass lawn.

&nbsp;

Signature Aviation is also planning to construct a fixed-wing hangar located north-east of the helicopter hangar. The two hangars are being assessed as separate projects.

properties.description_fr:
Signature Aviation propose de construire et d&#39;exploiter un nouveau hangar pour h&eacute;licopt&egrave;res au 4360, Agar Drive, &agrave; l&#39;a&eacute;roport international de Vancouver &agrave; Richmond, en Colombie-Britannique. Cette nouvelle installation est une extension des installations de hangars existantes &agrave; la m&ecirc;me adresse. Ce hangar devrait avoir une superficie d&#39;environ 2 600 m&egrave;tres carr&eacute;s, sur un &eacute;tage et demi. La zone d&#39;implantation du projet est d&#39;environ 4 700 m2. Le nouveau b&acirc;timent du hangar inclura une zone d&#39;entretien et d&#39;entreposage des h&eacute;licopt&egrave;res, ainsi que des espaces de bureaux. Ces installations comprendront le nouveau b&acirc;timent du hangar et la nouvelle cl&ocirc;ture de s&eacute;curit&eacute;. Elles n&eacute;cessiteront le d&eacute;placement de la premi&egrave;re ligne de s&ucirc;ret&eacute;, l&#39;agrandissement du stationnement, la r&eacute;alisation de l&#39;am&eacute;nagement paysager, de nouvelles voies et des voies r&eacute;serv&eacute;es aux v&eacute;hicules, des services publics et des services sur place. Le hangar est destin&eacute; aux h&eacute;licopt&egrave;res servant d&#39;ambulances a&eacute;riennes et servira &agrave; l&#39;entretien et l&#39;entreposage des a&eacute;ronefs. Les op&eacute;rations se d&eacute;rouleront en fonction des besoins, et des h&eacute;licopt&egrave;res servant d&#39;ambulances a&eacute;riennes seront d&eacute;p&ecirc;ch&eacute;s selon la demande. Le hangar pourra accueillir jusqu&#39;&agrave; trois h&eacute;licopt&egrave;res. Les mouvements quotidiens des a&eacute;ronefs varieront donc, car l&#39;installation sert aux activit&eacute;s d&#39;urgence et d&#39;entretien. Du personnel de soutien s&#39;y trouvera en tout temps et les pilotes pourront &eacute;galement &ecirc;tre h&eacute;berg&eacute;s sur place pour aider aux proc&eacute;dures d&#39;ambulance a&eacute;rienne et d&#39;&eacute;vacuation, au besoin.

&nbsp;

Le site est actuellement occup&eacute; par une chauss&eacute;e (stationnement) et une pelouse vacante.

&nbsp;

Signature Aviation pr&eacute;voit &eacute;galement construire un hangar pour a&eacute;ronefs &agrave; voilure fixe situ&eacute; au nord-est du hangar pour h&eacute;licopt&egrave;res. Les deux hangars sont &eacute;valu&eacute;s comme des projets distincts.

properties.description_en:
Signature Aviation is proposing to construct and operate a new hangar for fixed wing aircraft located at 4360 Agar Drive, Vancouver International Airport in Richmond, B.C. This facility is an expansion of the existing Signature hangar complex at this location. The new hangar building is proposed to be approximately 3,853 square meters of floor space over one and half floors. The total project area is approximately 13000 m2. The new hangar building will include aircraft maintenance area and storage area, as well as office spaces. New facilities will include the new hangar building, new aircraft apron, construction of security fence including relocation of primary security line (PSL), parking lot expansion, landscaping, new vehicle lanes and pathways, utilities and site services. The hangar is intended as a facility for aircraft storage and maintenance. The hangar is designed to accommodate up to two fixed-wing aircraft at any one time. Aircraft movements will therefore vary from day to day, depending on the scheduling of maintenance and charter flights rather than a fixed timetable.

&nbsp;

The site is currently occupied by paved parking lot and vacant land. 

&nbsp;

Signature Aviation is also planning to construct a helicopter hangar located southwest of the fixed wing hangar. The two hangars are assessed as separate projects.

properties.description_fr:
Signature Aviation propose de construire et d&#39;exploiter un nouveau hangar pour a&eacute;ronefs &agrave; voilure fixe au 4360, Agar Drive, &agrave; l&#39;a&eacute;roport international de Vancouver &agrave; Richmond, en Colombie-Britannique. Cette installation est une extension du complexe de hangars de Signature Aviation existant &agrave; cet endroit. Le nouveau b&acirc;timent du hangar devrait avoir une superficie d&#39;environ 3 853 m&egrave;tres carr&eacute;s, sur un &eacute;tage et demi. La zone d&#39;implantation du projet est d&#39;environ 13 000 m2. Le nouveau b&acirc;timent du hangar inclura une zone d&#39;entretien et d&#39;entreposage des a&eacute;ronefs, ainsi que des espaces de bureaux. Ces installations comprendront le nouveau b&acirc;timent du hangar et la nouvelle aire de trafic des a&eacute;ronefs. Elles n&eacute;cessiteront la construction d&#39;une cl&ocirc;ture de s&eacute;curit&eacute;, le d&eacute;placement de la premi&egrave;re ligne de s&ucirc;ret&eacute;, l&#39;agrandissement du stationnement, la r&eacute;alisation de l&#39;am&eacute;nagement paysager, de nouvelles voies et des voies r&eacute;serv&eacute;es aux v&eacute;hicules, des services publics et des services sur place. Le hangar est con&ccedil;u comme une installation d&#39;entreposage et d&#39;entretien des a&eacute;ronefs et peut accueillir jusqu&#39;&agrave; deux a&eacute;ronefs &agrave; voilure fixe en m&ecirc;me temps. Les mouvements d&#39;a&eacute;ronefs varieront donc d&#39;une journ&eacute;e &agrave; l&#39;autre, en fonction des horaires variables d&#39;entretien et des vols nolis&eacute;s.

&nbsp;

Le site est actuellement occup&eacute; par un stationnement pav&eacute; et un terrain vacant.

&nbsp;

Signature Aviation pr&eacute;voit &eacute;galement construire un hangar pour h&eacute;licopt&egrave;res situ&eacute; au sud-ouest du hangar pour a&eacute;ronefs &agrave; voilure fixe. Les deux hangars sont &eacute;valu&eacute;s comme des projets distincts.

properties.description_en:
EverWind Fuels (EverWind), the Proponent, is proposing to construct and operate the EverWind Strait Crossing Transmission Line, a new 345 kilovolt overhead transmission line that will span the Strait of Canso from Steep Creek, Guysborough County, to the Point Tupper Hydrogen and Ammonia Production Facility (the Facility) in Richmond County. The Project will allow for the transmission of renewable energy generated from select wind farms to be developed by EverWind in the Municipality of the District of Guysborough and St Mary&#39;s, to the Facility.&nbsp;The scope of Transport Canada&#39;s review is limited to the transmission line span crossing the Strait of Canso.

&nbsp;

The transmission crossing span is 1.5 kilometres and requires specialized suspension towers that are approximately 210 metres in height. The suspension towers will be located on private lands on either side of the Strait of Canso. A 75 m midspan clearance has been selected to accommodate sufficient clearance for the air draft of the largest vessels likely to pass through the Strait of Canso. This clearance applies only at the center of the crossing and gradually increases towards each shoreline. The Proponent has also committed to installing transmission line sag monitoring systems.

properties.description_fr:
EverWind Fuels (EverWind), le promoteur, propose de construire et d&#39;exploiter la ligne de transmission EverWind Strait Crossing, une nouvelle ligne a&eacute;rienne de transmission de 345 kilovolts qui traversera le d&eacute;troit de Canso, de Steep Creek (comt&eacute; de Guysborough) jusqu&#39;&agrave; l&#39;installation de production d&#39;hydrog&egrave;ne et d&#39;ammoniac de Point Tupper (&laquo; l&#39;installation &raquo;) dans le comt&eacute; de Richmond. Le projet permettra de transmettre l&#39;&eacute;nergie renouvelable produite par certains parcs &eacute;oliens d&eacute;velopp&eacute;s par EverWind dans la municipalit&eacute; du district de Guysborough et &agrave; St. Mary&#39;s, vers l&#39;installation.&nbsp;La port&eacute;e de l&#39;examen de Transports Canada est limit&eacute;e &agrave; la portion de la ligne de transmission qui traverse le d&eacute;troit de Canso.

&nbsp;

La port&eacute;e de la travers&eacute;e est de 1,5 kilom&egrave;tre et n&eacute;cessite des pyl&ocirc;nes de suspension sp&eacute;cialis&eacute;s d&#39;environ 210 m&egrave;tres de hauteur. Ces pyl&ocirc;nes seront situ&eacute;s sur des terrains priv&eacute;s de chaque c&ocirc;t&eacute; du d&eacute;troit de Canso. Un d&eacute;gagement de 75 m&egrave;tres au centre de la port&eacute;e a &eacute;t&eacute; choisi afin de permettre le passage des plus grands navires susceptibles de traverser le d&eacute;troit de Canso. Ce d&eacute;gagement s&#39;applique uniquement au centre de la travers&eacute;e et augmente progressivement vers chaque rive. Le promoteur s&#39;est &eacute;galement engag&eacute; &agrave; installer des syst&egrave;mes de surveillance de la fl&egrave;che des lignes de transmission.&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
Black Lake First Nation is proposing a roadway upgrades project that will consist of road structure and ditching upgrades to all of the Black Lake First Nation&#39;s roadways, which includes all residential roads within the Black Lake community and the Black Lake First Nation - Stony Lake subdivision.

&nbsp;

The project activities will include excavating/filling existing roadways and ditching to design elevations, application of aggregate and surfacing materials to the road surface, and application of topsoil, seeding, and erosion control blanket to all ditching. Erosion control measures will be installed as required during construction and will remain in place until sufficient vegetation has re-established. All topsoil within the roadway right-of-way to be upgraded will be stripped and temporarily stockpiled for the duration of construction. Following completion of the work, the topsoil will be replaced, the area will be seeded, and an erosion control blanket will be applied across all locations where topsoil replacement and seeding occur.

properties.description_fr:
La Premi&egrave;re Nation Black Lake propose un projet de modernisation des routes qui comprendra la structure routi&egrave;re et la modernisation des foss&eacute;s sur toutes les routes de la Premi&egrave;re Nation Black Lake, incluant toutes les routes r&eacute;sidentielles de la communaut&eacute; de Black Lake ainsi que le lotissement Black Lake First Nation - Stony Lake.

&nbsp;

Les activit&eacute;s du projet comprendront l&#39;excavation/le remplissage des routes existantes et le creusement de foss&eacute;s pour concevoir les &eacute;l&eacute;vations, l&#39;application de mat&eacute;riaux d&#39;agr&eacute;gats et de rev&ecirc;tement sur la surface de la route, ainsi que l&#39;application de terre arable, de semis et de couverture de contr&ocirc;le de l&#39;&eacute;rosion sur tous les foss&eacute;s. Des mesures de contr&ocirc;le de l&#39;&eacute;rosion seront mises en place au besoin pendant la construction et resteront en place jusqu&#39;&agrave; ce qu&#39;une v&eacute;g&eacute;tation suffisante soit r&eacute;tablie. Toute la terre arable &agrave; l&#39;int&eacute;rieur de l&#39;emprise de la route &agrave; moderniser sera d&eacute;cap&eacute;e et temporairement stock&eacute;e pendant la dur&eacute;e des travaux. Apr&egrave;s l&#39;ach&egrave;vement des travaux, la couche arable sera remplac&eacute;e, la zone sera ensemenc&eacute;e, et une couverture de contr&ocirc;le de l&#39;&eacute;rosion sera appliqu&eacute;e &agrave; tous les endroits o&ugrave; le remplacement et le semis de la couche arable auront lieu.

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
Black Lake First Nation is proposing the construction of a lagoon upgrades project. The project includes the construction of a new primary and storage cell to expand the capacity of the existing lagoon. The lagoon site is located approximately 2 km north of the Black Lake First Nation community, and expansion of the new cells will be immediately to the east of the existing cells.

&nbsp;

Construction will consist of expanding to the existing facultative lagoon, which will include construction of a 5.45 ha primary cell and storage cell with 237,800 cu.m. capacity, complete with installation of all interconnecting and release structures. The lagoon upgrade project will continue to use the existing effluent discharge route, which releases to the west of the lagoon and flows approximately 9 km through a creek containing several low-lying, naturally occurring detention-type pond areas before ultimately entering Middle Lake.

properties.description_fr:
La Premi&egrave;re Nation Black Lake propose la construction d&#39;un projet de modernisation de la lagune. Le projet comprend la construction d&#39;une nouvelle cellule primaire et d&#39;une cellule de stockage afin d&#39;augmenter la capacit&eacute; de la lagune existante. Le site du lagon est situ&eacute; &agrave; environ 2 km au nord de la communaut&eacute; des Premi&egrave;res Nations Black Lake, et l&#39;expansion des nouvelles cellules se fera imm&eacute;diatement &agrave; l&#39;est des cellules existantes.

&nbsp;

La construction consistera &agrave; s&#39;&eacute;tendre &agrave; la lagune facultative existante, ce qui comprendra la construction d&#39;une cellule primaire et d&#39;une cellule de stockage de 5,45 ha de 237 800 m&sup3;. avec l&#39;installation de toutes les structures d&#39;interconnexion et de lib&eacute;ration. Le projet de modernisation de la lagune continuera d&#39;utiliser la route existante de rejet des effluents, qui se d&eacute;verse &agrave; l&#39;ouest de la lagune et s&#39;&eacute;coule sur environ 9 km &agrave; travers un ruisseau contenant plusieurs basses zones naturelles de d&eacute;tention avant d&#39;entrer finalement dans le lac Middle.

properties.description_en:
The project proposes upgrades to the TDK Logistics site at 480 Audley Boulevard on Annacis Island in Delta, BC to enhance the existing container storage and distribution facility, as well as add new rail tracks and a new grain transload operation (approximately 100,000 metric tonnes per annum) at the site.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Proposed works comprise the following:&nbsp;&nbsp;


	Demolition of an existing warehouse building&nbsp;
	Reconfiguration of truck gate and container yard, including construction of gate entrance and exit buildings&nbsp;
	Construction of two new rail tracks at the end of the existing&nbsp;Southern Railway of British Columbia (SRY)&nbsp;spur track, to accommodate a total of 20 railcars&nbsp;
	Ground improvement works utilising Rammed Aggregate Pier (RAP) ground densification methods, extending to a depth of approx. 15m&nbsp;
	Installation of mobile grain handling operation (utilising mobile grain conveyors)&nbsp;
	Associated miscellaneous works - utility removals and installations, removal and installation of fencing and lighting installation&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Le projet comprend des mises &agrave; niveau apport&eacute;es au site de TDK Logistics situ&eacute; au 480, boulevard Audley sur l&#39;&icirc;le Annacis &agrave; Delta (C.-B.) visant &agrave; am&eacute;liorer l&#39;installation d&#39;entreposage des conteneurs et de distribution existante, ainsi qu&#39;&agrave; ajouter de nouvelles voies ferroviaires et une nouvelle installation de transbordement de c&eacute;r&eacute;ales (environ 100 000 tonnes m&eacute;triques par an) sur le site.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Les travaux propos&eacute;s comprennent les &eacute;l&eacute;ments suivants :&nbsp;&nbsp;


	D&eacute;molition d&#39;un entrep&ocirc;t existant&nbsp;
	Reconfiguration de la porte pour les camions et du parc de conteneurs, y compris la construction d&#39;une porte d&#39;entr&eacute;e et de sortie&nbsp;
	Construction de deux nouvelles voies ferroviaires &agrave; l&#39;extr&eacute;mit&eacute; de l&#39;embranchement SRY (Southern Railway of British Columbia) afin d&#39;accueillir un total de 20 wagons&nbsp;
	Travaux d&#39;am&eacute;lioration du sol &agrave; l&#39;aide des m&eacute;thodes de densification du sol RAP (Rammed Aggregate Pier), jusqu&#39;&agrave; une profondeur d&#39;environ 15 m&nbsp;
	Mise en place d&#39;une installation mobile de manutention des c&eacute;r&eacute;ales (&agrave; l&#39;aide de convoyeurs de c&eacute;r&eacute;ales mobiles)&nbsp;
	Divers travaux connexes : retrait et installation des services publics, retrait et installation de la cl&ocirc;ture et du syst&egrave;me d&#39;&eacute;clairage&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
Beginning at the southern end of Gatineau Park, the Gatineau Parkway provides direct access to some of the park&#39;s most popular attractions, trails and viewpoints. Unlike the rest of the parkway network, a 2.7-km section of the Gatineau parkway, located between Alexandre-Tach&eacute; Boulevard and the former Gamelin Street, remains open all year. This section is an important access route to Gatineau Park, and for the National Capital Commission&#39;s (NCC) shuttle service to Gatineau Park.&nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Due to the very poor condition of the road surface along this section of the parkway, major rehabilitation is required to ensure continued access of the parkway for its users and the Gatineau Park shuttle service. In addition, there are drainage issues along the parkway. The NCC therefore proposes to complete a partial reconstruction of the road structure to replace non-functional culverts, eliminate drainage issues by installing new concrete curbs, catch basins and drains, repair guardrails installed at the approaches to the Allumeti&egrave;res viaduct, and improve existing road signage along the parkway.&nbsp;Construction is planned to begin in June 2025.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

A characterization of the natural environment in the work and access zones has been carried out, including an inventory of trees that will be impacted by the proposed works. Mitigation measures such as erosion and sediment control, tree protection measures and tree compensation, will be implemented to protect wildlife and their habitat near the work zone.  &nbsp;

&nbsp;

The project is proposed by the NCC, on land under its stewardship (Gatineau Park) as well as on land that is owned by Hydro Qu&eacute;bec and Quebec&#39;s Minist&egrave;re des Transports et de la Mobilit&eacute; durable. The project is subject to a federal land use, design and transaction approval (FLUDTA) under the National Capital Act. Coordination with the Department of Fisheries and Oceans (DFO) is required, as DFO will likely issue a letter of advice under the Fisheries Act for planned work in fish habitat.&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
De l&#39;extr&eacute;mit&eacute; sud du parc de la Gatineau, la promenade de la Gatineau procure un acc&egrave;s direct &agrave; certains des sentiers et points de vue les plus populaires du parc. Contrairement aux autres promenades de ce r&eacute;seau, celle de la Gatineau reste ouverte toute l&#39;ann&eacute;e sur 2,7 km, entre le boulevard Alexandre-Tach&eacute; et l&#39;ancienne rue Gamelin. Ce tron&ccedil;on est une importante voie d&#39;acc&egrave;s au parc de la Gatineau, notamment pour la navette de la Commission de la capitale nationale (CCN) qui y m&egrave;ne.&nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Le rev&ecirc;tement de ce tron&ccedil;on de 2,7 km est en tr&egrave;s mauvais &eacute;tat et n&eacute;cessite une r&eacute;fection importante pour maintenir l&#39;acc&egrave;s &agrave; la promenade et le service de navette. On observe aussi des probl&egrave;mes de drainage le long de la promenade. La CCN se propose donc de reconstruire partiellement cette infrastructure routi&egrave;re, de mani&egrave;re &agrave; remplacer les tuyaux de ponceau non fonctionnels; &agrave; r&eacute;gler le probl&egrave;me de drainage, en installant des bordures en b&eacute;ton, des puisards et des drains; &agrave; r&eacute;parer la glissi&egrave;re install&eacute;e &agrave; l&#39;approche du pont d&#39;&eacute;tagement des Allumetti&egrave;res; et &agrave; am&eacute;liorer la signalisation routi&egrave;re existante le long de la promenade. Le d&eacute;but des travaux est pr&eacute;vu pour juin 2025.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

La caract&eacute;risation du milieu naturel dans les zones de construction et d&#39;acc&egrave;s a &eacute;t&eacute; r&eacute;alis&eacute;e, y compris l&#39;inventaire des arbres que les travaux propos&eacute;s affecteront. Des mesures d&#39;att&eacute;nuation sont pr&eacute;vues pour prot&eacute;ger la faune et la flore &agrave; proximit&eacute; du chantier et leurs habitats, par exemple des contr&ocirc;les pour les s&eacute;diments et contre l&#39;&eacute;rosion, et des mesures de protection ou de compensation pour les arbres.&nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;

La CCN est la proposante du projet, qui se d&eacute;roulera sur un terrain dont elle assure l&#39;intendance (parc de la Gatineau) et sur un terrain qui appartient &agrave; Hydro-Qu&eacute;bec et au minist&egrave;re des Transports et de la Mobilit&eacute; durable. En vertu de la Loi sur la capitale nationale, ce projet est assujetti &agrave; l&#39;obtention d&#39;une approbation f&eacute;d&eacute;rale de l&#39;utilisation du sol, du design et des transactions immobili&egrave;res. La coordination avec le minist&egrave;re des P&ecirc;ches et des Oc&eacute;ans est n&eacute;cessaire, car en vertu de la Loi sur les p&ecirc;ches, il est probable que ce minist&egrave;re &eacute;mette une lettre d&#39;avis pour du travail pr&eacute;vu dans l&#39;habitat du poisson.&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The Proposed Project

This project involves the commercial development of a coffee shop and gas station.&nbsp;Site preparation activities will include geo-technical studies, surveys, and environmental studies.

The Saskatoon Airport Authority permits the lease of the 45th &amp; Airport Holdings Ltd. commercial development on its property and is therefore the lead authority on this project.&nbsp;

Environmental description includes greenfield surrounded by industrial/commercial land.&nbsp;

A subsidiary company of Peter Ballantyne Cree Nation is proposing a commercial and residential development on the Chief Joseph Custer Reserve land within Prince Albert. The first phase of the development involves the installation of the base infrastructure and utilities, including power lines, gas lines, communication access, storm water drains, sewer, roads, curbs. The project will include the clearing of vegetation. The Kistapiskaw Property Development LP is currently working with the City of Prince Albert&#39;s development and building permit approval process.

&nbsp;

Phase 2 of the project includes 3-4 separate buildings and associated parking for office, retail and residential purposes. The proposed residential units include medium density rental properties as well as mixed commercial and residential buildings.

properties.description_fr:
Une filiale de la Nation crie Peter Ballantyne propose un d&eacute;veloppement commercial et r&eacute;sidentiel sur les terres de la r&eacute;serve Chief Joseph Custer &agrave; Prince Albert. La premi&egrave;re phase du d&eacute;veloppement comprend l&#39;installation des infrastructures de la base et des services publics, incluant les lignes &eacute;lectriques, les lignes de gaz, l&#39;acc&egrave;s aux communications, les &eacute;gouts, les &eacute;gouts, les routes et les bordures. Le projet comprendra le d&eacute;frichement de la v&eacute;g&eacute;tation. Le d&eacute;veloppement immobilier Kistapiskaw LP travaille actuellement avec le processus de d&eacute;veloppement et d&#39;approbation des permis de construction de la Ville de Prince Albert.

&nbsp;

La phase 2 du projet comprend 3 &agrave; 4 b&acirc;timents distincts ainsi que des stationnements associ&eacute;s pour des bureaux, des commerces et des r&eacute;sidences. Les unit&eacute;s r&eacute;sidentielles propos&eacute;es comprennent des propri&eacute;t&eacute;s locatives &agrave; densit&eacute; moyenne ainsi que des immeubles mixtes commerciaux et r&eacute;sidentiels.

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
James Smith Cree Nation is proposing to construct a new Aboriginal Headstart on Reserve (AHSOR) and Daycare. The space will house AHSOR and daycare facilities, including space for an Elder/Culture room, storage, offices, and outdoor play area. The kitchen will be shared by the AHSOR and daycare clients and staff. The building is approximately 900 m2, with a parking lot, garage and landscaping to support play area and a fire pit area.

Physical activities will include general building construction activities from foundation installation to HVAC system commissioning. Supporting utilities such as power, communication and water lines to connect to existing subdivision distributions.

&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
La Nation crie James Smith propose de construire un nouveau programme Aboriginal Headstart on Reserve (AHSOR) et une garderie. L&#39;espace abritera l&#39;AHSOR et les garderies, incluant une salle pour les a&icirc;n&eacute;s/culture, du rangement, des bureaux et une aire de jeux ext&eacute;rieure. La cuisine sera partag&eacute;e par l&#39;AHSOR ainsi que par les clients et le personnel de la garderie. Le b&acirc;timent fait environ 900 m2, avec un stationnement, un garage et un am&eacute;nagement paysager pour accueillir une aire de jeux et un foyer.

&nbsp;

Les activit&eacute;s physiques comprendront des activit&eacute;s g&eacute;n&eacute;rales de construction de b&acirc;timents, de l&#39;installation des fondations &agrave; la mise en service des syst&egrave;mes CVC. Soutenir les services publics tels que l&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute;, les communications et les lignes d&#39;eau pour se connecter aux distributions de lotissements existantes.

properties.description_en:
Sawridge First Nation is proposing to build two new homes. The lots require tree clearing (980 m2), road access and&nbsp;additional lot prep.&nbsp;

The buildings will have slab on grade foundations, cisterns, septic and utility tie-ins.&nbsp;

Waste generation will be minimal and disposed of off site. Imported fill is required.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Pearson International Fuel Facilities Corporation (PIFFC) is the owner of fuel storage installations located on Tank Farm Road at YYZ Pearson International Airport in Mississauga, ON that supply jet fuel to the airport.

&nbsp;

As part of this proposed project,&nbsp;PIFFC&nbsp;will decommission the existing fuel storage installations and conduct remediation at the site. The work will consist primarily of dismantling and removing all underground and aboveground fuel storage tanks and all associated piping, equipment, structural foundations and buildings at the site. Environmental remediation work will be completed in conjunction with the decommissioning of these installations.

properties.description_fr:
Pearson International Fuel Facilities Corporation (PIFFC) est le propri&eacute;taire des infrastructures d&#39;un parc de r&eacute;servoirs de carburant situ&eacute; sur la rue Tank Farm &agrave; YYZ a&eacute;roport Pearson de Toronto, qui fournit du carburant d&apos;aviation &agrave; l&apos;a&eacute;roport.

&nbsp;

Dans le cadre du projet propos&eacute;, PIFFC pr&eacute;voit d&eacute;manteler ses installations actuelles de stockage de carburant et r&eacute;alisera des travaux de r&eacute;habilitation.&nbsp; Les travaux comprendront principalement le d&eacute;mant&egrave;lement et l&apos;enl&egrave;vement des r&eacute;servoirs hors sol et souterrains ainsi que l&apos;ensemble des tuyauteries, &eacute;quipements, des bases structurelles, et des b&acirc;timents associ&eacute;s sur le site. Les travaux de r&eacute;habilitation seront r&eacute;alis&eacute;s en parall&egrave;le avec le d&eacute;mant&egrave;lement de ces infrastructures.

properties.description_en:
Lubicon Lake Band is proposing to build a new Administration Building on reserve. The new Administration Building is anticipated to become a central hub for the operations of the Lubicon Lake Band. The facility will provide dedicated space for the Chief and Council, and various offices for multiple community departments. The building will measure approximately 936 square meters. Space for future expansion has been planned. In addition, a FireSmart buffer, parking area, and landscaping have been incorporated into the design.&nbsp;

Supporting infrastructure includes water and sewer connections, electrical and telecommunications services, HVAC systems, parking facilities, access roads, drainage, and landscaping.

Site preparation includes clearing of trees, grubbing, removal of topsoil, on-site equipment maintenance and re-fueling, importing fill and regrading the site. All waste will be removed from the reserve.&nbsp;
&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
La bande du lac Lubicon propose de construire un nouveau b&acirc;timent administratif dans la r&eacute;serve. Ce nouveau b&acirc;timent administratif devrait devenir le centre n&eacute;vralgique des activit&eacute;s de la bande du lac Lubicon. Il comprendra des locaux r&eacute;serv&eacute;s au chef et au conseil, ainsi que divers bureaux pour plusieurs services communautaires. Le b&acirc;timent aura une superficie d&#39;environ 936 m&egrave;tres carr&eacute;s. Un espace a &eacute;t&eacute; pr&eacute;vu pour une expansion future. De plus, une zone tampon FireSmart, un parking et des am&eacute;nagements paysagers ont &eacute;t&eacute; int&eacute;gr&eacute;s &agrave; la conception.&nbsp;

Les infrastructures de soutien comprennent les raccordements &agrave; l&#39;eau et aux &eacute;gouts, les services d&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute; et de t&eacute;l&eacute;communications, les syst&egrave;mes de chauffage, de ventilation et de climatisation, les parkings, les routes d&#39;acc&egrave;s, le drainage et l&#39;am&eacute;nagement paysager.

La pr&eacute;paration du site comprend le d&eacute;boisement, l&#39;essouchement, l&#39;enl&egrave;vement de la couche arable, l&#39;entretien et le ravitaillement en carburant des &eacute;quipements sur place, l&#39;importation de remblai et le nivellement du site. Tous les d&eacute;chets seront retir&eacute;s de la r&eacute;serve.&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
Surrounded by National Capital Commission (NCC) lands, at the junction of Highway 5 and McLaren Road; lot 3,389,956 is a private lot of 210,100 square metres without direct access to a road network. In order to gain access to the propriety, the owner proposes the construction of an access road, starting from McLaren Road, and, using an old forest road, crossing NCC lands - all with the objective of minimizing the environmental impact on the surrounding environment.

&nbsp;

The proposed road would cross lands owned by the NCC and is subject to the federal approval of land use, design and real estate transaction, under the National Capital Law.

&nbsp;

The access road would start on the West side of McLaren Road, between Highway 5 and Oakview Road. It would take an old forest road that is already partly deforested. The width of the path would be 2.4 metres, but with a total width of 6 metres if we include the ditches. At approximately every 100 meters, there would be a widening of the road to allow for the passage of oncoming vehicles. The total road distance to the land of the owner will be 616 metres. The road will be mostly gravel, but with two sections of asphalt, on the slope at the beginning of the road, and on the culvert towards the end of the road.

&nbsp;

The proposed road crosses NCC lands which are not an integral part of Gatineau Park, therefore without public access, but which serve to enrich the biodiversity of the region while allowing an access path for animals between the park and outside of it. The first half of the proposed path passes through mixed forest of mostly hardwood on slightly hilly terrain. The second portion of the path crosses a field, near a wetland and crosses a small stream of about 10-20 cm in diameter towards the end of the path.

&nbsp;

The deforestation of the future path should begin at the end of August 2022. The construction of the road will follow and will be done with heavy machinery while respecting the limits of the road so as not to impact the surrounding ecosystem. The completion date should be before the 2022 winter freeze, but could resume and be finalized in the spring 2023 depending on metrological conditions and construction contingencies.

&nbsp;

There would be about 100 trees, including 10 dead or dying, which will have to be cut to allow the widening of the old forest road. In its second section, the road will pass near a wetland, which must be protected during the work phase to avoid it being impacted. A culvert will then be installed to cross the stream at the end of the road, which will measure 2 metres in diameter, to minimize the impact of the road on the aquatic ecosystem. Stormwater management measures are included in the design of the road. All necessary environmental studies have been completed for this project, and there are no animal or plant species at risk which would potentially be affected by this work. The anticipated environmental effects will be mitigated or even avoided by the implementation of standard and effective mitigation measures.

&nbsp;

Once the road is finished, it will initially serve as an access road to the owner&#39;s land for the construction of a bi-generational house with the possible addition of a small organic farm. In a second phase, the project could expand, and build 2 to 3 rental chalets, still on the land of the owner, for a small-scale agrotourism vision. In any case, to preserve the surrounding ecosystem. the road will remain a private path with limited access.

properties.description_fr:
Enclav&eacute; par les terrains de la Commission de la capitale nationale (CCN), &agrave; la jonction de l&#39;autoroute 5 et du chemin McLaren; le lot 3&nbsp;389 956 est un terrain priv&eacute; de 210 100 m&egrave;tres carr&eacute; sans acc&egrave;s direct &agrave; un r&eacute;seau routier. Dans le but d&#39;avoir acc&egrave;s au terrain, le propri&eacute;taire, propose la construction d&#39;un chemin d&#39;acc&egrave;s, partant du chemin McLaren, et traversant les terrains de la CCN en utilisant un ancien chemin forestier. Le tout avec l&#39;objectif de minimiser l&#39;impact environnemental sur le milieu environnant.

&nbsp;

La route propos&eacute;e, traverserait des terrains appartenant &agrave; la CCN et est assujetti &agrave; une approbation f&eacute;d&eacute;rale de l&#39;utilisation du sol, du design et des transactions immobili&egrave;res en vertu de la Loi sur la capitale nationale.

&nbsp;

Le chemin d&#39;acc&egrave;s d&eacute;buterait du c&ocirc;t&eacute; ouest du chemin McLaren, entre l&#39;autoroute 5 et le chemin Oakview. Il emprunterait un ancien chemin forestier d&eacute;j&agrave; en partie d&eacute;bois&eacute;. La largeur du chemin serait de 2,4 m&egrave;tres, mais avec une largeur totale de 6 m&egrave;tres en incluant les foss&eacute;s. Il y aurait des &eacute;largissements de la route environ tous les 100 m&egrave;tres, permettant le passage de voitures &agrave; contresens. Le tout sur une distance de 616 m&egrave;tres, jusqu&#39;au terrain du propri&eacute;taire. La route sera majoritairement en gravier, mais avec deux portions en bitume, dans la pente du d&eacute;but du chemin, et sur le ponceau vers la fin du chemin.

&nbsp;

La route propos&eacute;e traverse les terrains de la CCN qui ne font pas partie int&eacute;grante du parc de la Gatineau, donc sans acc&egrave;s au public, mais qui servent &agrave; enrichir la biodiversit&eacute; de la r&eacute;gion tout en permettant un chemin d&#39;acc&egrave;s aux animaux entre le parc et l&#39;ext&eacute;rieur de celui-ci. La premi&egrave;re moiti&eacute; du chemin propos&eacute; traverse une for&ecirc;t mixte, principalement de feuillus, avec un terrain l&eacute;g&egrave;rement montagneux. La deuxi&egrave;me portion du chemin traverse une plaine, &agrave; proximit&eacute; d&#39;un milieu humide et traversant vers la fin du chemin un petit ruisseau d&#39;environ 10-20 cm de diam&egrave;tre.

&nbsp;

Le d&eacute;boisement du futur chemin devrait d&eacute;buter fin ao&ucirc;t 2022. La construction de la route suivra et se fera avec de la machinerie lourde en respectant les limites de la route pour ne pas impacter l&#39;&eacute;cosyst&egrave;me environnant. La date d&#39;ach&egrave;vement devrait &ecirc;tre avant le gel de l&#39;hiver 2022, mais pourrait reprendre et se finaliser au printemps 2023 selon les conditions m&eacute;trologiques et les impr&eacute;vus de construction.

&nbsp;

Il y aurait environ 100 arbres, dont 10 de morts ou moribonds, qui devront &ecirc;tre coup&eacute;s pour permettre l&#39;&eacute;largissement de l&#39;ancien chemin forestier. Dans sa deuxi&egrave;me portion, la route passera &agrave; proximit&eacute; d&#39;un milieu humide, qui devra &ecirc;tre prot&eacute;g&eacute; durant la phase des travaux pour ne pas &ecirc;tre impact&eacute;. Il y aura ensuite installation d&#39;un ponceau pour traverser le ruisseau &agrave; la fin du chemin, et qui sera d&#39;un diam&egrave;tre de 2 m&egrave;tres, pour minimiser l&#39;impact de la route sur l&#39;&eacute;cosyst&egrave;me aquatique. Des mesures de gestion des eaux pluviales sont incluses dans la conception de la route. Toutes les &eacute;tudes environnementales n&eacute;cessaires ont &eacute;t&eacute; compl&eacute;t&eacute;es pour le projet, et il n&#39;y a aucune esp&egrave;ces animales ou v&eacute;g&eacute;tales en p&eacute;ril potentiellement touch&eacute;es par ces travaux. Les effets environnementaux anticip&eacute;s seront att&eacute;nu&eacute;s voire &eacute;vit&eacute;s par la mise en place de mesures d&#39;att&eacute;nuation standard et efficaces.

&nbsp;

Une fois la route termin&eacute;e, le chemin servira dans un premier temps comme chemin d&#39;acc&egrave;s au terrain du propri&eacute;taire pour la construction d&#39;une maison bi-g&eacute;n&eacute;rationnelle avec possiblement une fermette en agriculture biologique. Dans une deuxi&egrave;me phase, le projet pourrait s&#39;agrandir, et construire 2 &agrave; 3 chalets locatifs, toujours sur le terrain du propri&eacute;taire, dans une vison agrotouristique &agrave; petite &eacute;chelle. Le chemin resterait dans tous les cas un chemin priv&eacute; avec acc&egrave;s limit&eacute;, pour pr&eacute;server l&#39;&eacute;cosyst&egrave;me environnant.

properties.description_en:
Troilus Mining Corporation&nbsp;is proposing the construction, operation and decommissioning of a new open-pit gold and copper mine located approximately 76 kilometres northwest of the Cree community of Mistissini and approximately 170 kilometres north of Chibougamau, Quebec. As proposed, the Troilus Mining Project would include the mining of two former open pits and two new pits, the reuse of the tailings facility, the development of waste rock and overburden piles, and the construction and operation of a new ore processing plant complex. The project would have a maximum ore production capacity of 50,000 tonnes per day and a 22-year operating life.

&nbsp;

Please note that the proponent for this project was previously&nbsp;Troilus Gold Corp.

properties.description_fr:
Corporation Mini&egrave;re Troilus propose la construction, l&#39;exploitation et la fermeture d&#39;une nouvelle mine &agrave; ciel ouvert d&#39;or et de cuivre situ&eacute;e &agrave; environ 76 kilom&egrave;tres au nord-ouest de la communaut&eacute; crie de Mistissini et &agrave; environ 170 kilom&egrave;tres au nord de Chibougamau, au Qu&eacute;bec. Tel que propos&eacute;, le projet minier Troilus comprendrait l&#39;exploitation de deux anciennes fosses et de deux nouvelles fosses, la r&eacute;utilisation du parc &agrave; r&eacute;sidus, l&#39;am&eacute;nagement de haldes &agrave; st&eacute;riles et &agrave; mort-terrain ainsi que la construction et l&#39;op&eacute;ration d&#39;un nouveau complexe usinier de traitement du minerai. Le projet aurait une capacit&eacute; maximale de production de minerai de 50 000 tonnes par jour et une dur&eacute;e d&#39;exploitation de 22 ans.

&nbsp;

Veuillez noter que le promoteur de ce projet &eacute;tait pr&eacute;c&eacute;demment&nbsp;La soci&eacute;t&eacute; Troilus Gold

properties.description_en:
Peepeekisis Cree Nation is proposing to construct a new wastewater lagoon system for treatment, storage and disposal of the community&#39;s wastewater. The lagoon improvements will be required to service the design population of 1237 people in 2043.

The project consists of the construction of two new cells, a treatment cell of 3.2 ha at full service level and a storage cell with a capacity of 96,800 m3 at full service level. A new approximately 7600 m 150 mm diameter HDPE DR17 forcemain originating at the SPS would be required to convey sewage to a new lagoon at Site 5. The existing pumps at the SPS are not sized appropriately to pump the design flow of 10.2 L/s to Site 5 and would need to be replaced with pumps with larger motors. Associated electrical and ventilation upgrades would be required as part of the pump replacement. A pump station upgrade would include the addition of a separate electrical room with a standby generator to bring the station to modern standards. Vehicle access to the lagoon site will require construction of a new access road, spanning approximately 2400 m. The existing lagoon, main line and pumping station will be decommissioned as part of the project.

&nbsp;

Electrical Distribution Infrastructure - Permit for the whole of&nbsp;Wapachewunak First Nation No. 92D for as long as needed. SaskPower may install and maintain electrical distribution lines and all structures, poles, cables, anchors, pipes, conduits, apparatus and equipment in relation thereto on the above noted reserve. Activities under the blanket permit may include but are not limited to: surveying, affixing, constructing, placing, replacing and repairing, maintaining, operating and removing electrical distribution lines and all structures, poles, wires, cables, anchors, pipes, conduits, apparatus and equipment in relation thereto, and all works necessary or appurtenances ancillary and useful in connection with or incidental to the construction, operation or maintenance of electrical distribution lines.

&nbsp;

SaskPower may use roads and trails for access to and from electrical distribution lines to complete the above-mentioned activities. All garbage and debris generated will be removed and disposed of in an approved receptacle or facility. 

&nbsp;

Distribution facilities may be placed in close proximity to wetlands and drainages, but efforts are made to avoid these features where feasible. Any work near fish-bearing waterways or wetlands will undergo a Department of Oceans and Fisheries (DFO) self-assessment and further review.

properties.description_fr:
Infrastructure de distribution &eacute;lectrique &ndash; permis pour l&#39;ensemble de la Premi&egrave;re Nation Wapachewunak n&deg; 92D aussi longtemps que n&eacute;cessaire. SaskPower peut installer et entretenir des lignes de distribution &eacute;lectrique ainsi que toutes les structures, poteaux, c&acirc;bles, ancres, tuyaux, conduits, appareils et &eacute;quipements qui s&#39;y rapportent sur la r&eacute;serve mentionn&eacute;e ci-dessus. Les activit&eacute;s pr&eacute;vues par le permis global peuvent inclure, sans s&#39;y limiter : l&#39;arpentage, l&#39;installation, la construction, la pose, le remplacement et la r&eacute;paration, l&#39;entretien, l&#39;exploitation et le retrait des lignes de distribution &eacute;lectrique ainsi que toutes les structures, poteaux, fils, c&acirc;bles, ancres, tuyaux, conduits, appareils et &eacute;quipements y aff&eacute;rents, ainsi que tous les travaux n&eacute;cessaires ou accessoires auxiliaires et utiles en lien avec ou accessoires &agrave; la construction, l&#39;exploitation ou l&#39;entretien des lignes de distribution &eacute;lectrique.

&nbsp;

SaskPower peut utiliser des routes et sentiers pour acc&eacute;der aux lignes de distribution &eacute;lectrique et &agrave; en revenir afin de r&eacute;aliser les activit&eacute;s mentionn&eacute;es ci-dessus. Tous les d&eacute;chets et d&eacute;bris g&eacute;n&eacute;r&eacute;s seront enlev&eacute;s et &eacute;limin&eacute;s dans un r&eacute;ceptacle ou une installation approuv&eacute;e. 

&nbsp;

Des installations de distribution peuvent &ecirc;tre install&eacute;es &agrave; proximit&eacute; des zones humides et des bassins versants, mais des efforts sont faits pour &eacute;viter ces caract&eacute;ristiques lorsque cela est possible. Tout travail pr&egrave;s des cours d&#39;eau ou des zones humides &agrave; poissons fera l&#39;objet d&#39;une auto&eacute;valuation et d&#39;un examen approfondi du minist&egrave;re des Oc&eacute;ans et des P&ecirc;ches (DFO).

properties.description_en:
Sturgeon Lake First Nation is proposing the construction of a new Child and Family Service Centre for their CFS agency to provide programs and services for Sturgeon Lake children and families.&nbsp; A five acre site located southeast from the existing Band Office will be home to the new facility. The Administrative Building is projected to have an 1,100 square metre footprint with a gross building area of 1,903 square meters spread over two stories. Vehicular circulation is provided on-site with modest sized driving lanes amidst a large parking lot designed for 62 parking spaces with 3 of those serving people with disabilities. The site is designed to have a dedicated area for deliveries and loading at the rear of the building.&nbsp; An external 260 square metre garage/storage building and fenced compound is also being planned to safely house and store CFS Agency vehicles and equipment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The foundation design will require site excavation to proceed, first removing the topsoil (which will be stockpiled onsite and used for finishing site grades and reseeding activities) and then removing excess soil materials to make way for a concrete foundation that is reinforced and secured by steel helical piles at key loading and weight bearing intervals.&nbsp; The building will be constructed primarily of steel and structural concrete, with finishes consisting of exposed raw wood in specific locations (i.e. cultural room)&nbsp; Exterior finishes are expected to consist of stone accents and metal siding, with steel roof panels. Landscaping will include concrete sidewalks, select platings that consist of plants that are commonly found in this area of the province.

&nbsp;

Site services are to be provided by communal water and sewer systems, with interconnection to existing roadways and walking trails. Crown utilities are already proximate to the development site and will be extended as construction proceeds. It is estimated that this project will take up to 24 months to complete, which is dependent on weather, availability of material and labour, and other risks that are outside of the community&#39;s control.

properties.description_fr:
La Premi&egrave;re Nation de Sturgeon Lake propose la construction d&#39;un nouveau Centre de services &agrave; l&#39;enfance et &agrave; la famille pour leur agence SFC afin d&#39;offrir des programmes et services aux enfants et familles de Sturgeon Lake.&nbsp; Un site de cinq acres situ&eacute; au sud-est du bureau actuel de la bande accueillera la nouvelle installation. Le b&acirc;timent administratif devrait avoir une superficie de 1 100 m&egrave;tres carr&eacute;s avec une superficie brute de 1 903 m&egrave;tres carr&eacute;s r&eacute;partis sur deux &eacute;tages. La circulation des v&eacute;hicules est assur&eacute;e sur place avec des voies de circulation de taille modeste, au milieu d&#39;un grand stationnement con&ccedil;u pour 62 places, dont 3 desservent les personnes handicap&eacute;es. Le site est con&ccedil;u pour avoir une zone d&eacute;di&eacute;e aux livraisons et au chargement &agrave; l&#39;arri&egrave;re du b&acirc;timent.&nbsp; Un garage/entrep&ocirc;t ext&eacute;rieur de 260 m&egrave;tres carr&eacute;s ainsi qu&#39;un complexe cl&ocirc;tur&eacute; sont &eacute;galement pr&eacute;vus pour abriter et entreposer en toute s&eacute;curit&eacute; les v&eacute;hicules et &eacute;quipements de l&#39;Agence CFS.

&nbsp;

La conception de la fondation n&eacute;cessitera une excavation du site pour se poursuivre, en retirant d&#39;abord la couche arable (qui sera stock&eacute;e sur place et utilis&eacute;e pour finir les niveaux du site et les activit&eacute;s de r&eacute;ensemencement), puis en retirant l&#39;exc&egrave;s de mat&eacute;riaux de terre pour faire place &agrave; une fondation en b&eacute;ton renforc&eacute;e et fix&eacute;e par des pieux h&eacute;lico&iuml;daux en acier &agrave; des intervalles cl&eacute;s de charge et de charge.&nbsp; Le b&acirc;timent sera principalement construit en acier et en b&eacute;ton structurel, avec des finitions en bois brut apparent &agrave; des emplacements sp&eacute;cifiques (c.-&agrave;-d. salle culturelle). Les finitions ext&eacute;rieures devraient consister en des accents en pierre et un rev&ecirc;tement m&eacute;tallique, avec des panneaux de toit en acier. L&#39;am&eacute;nagement paysager comprendra des trottoirs en b&eacute;ton, des plaques s&eacute;lectionn&eacute;es compos&eacute;es de plantes que l&#39;on retrouve couramment dans cette r&eacute;gion de la province.

&nbsp;

Les services du site seront assur&eacute;s par des syst&egrave;mes communaux d&#39;eau et d&#39;&eacute;gouts, avec une connexion aux routes et sentiers p&eacute;destres existants. Les services publics de la Couronne sont d&eacute;j&agrave; proches du site de d&eacute;veloppement et seront &eacute;tendus au fur et &agrave; mesure de la construction. On estime que ce projet prendra jusqu&#39;&agrave; 24 mois &agrave; compl&eacute;ter, ce qui d&eacute;pend de la m&eacute;t&eacute;o, de la disponibilit&eacute; des mat&eacute;riaux et de la main-d&#39;&oelig;uvre, ainsi que d&#39;autres risques hors du contr&ocirc;le de la communaut&eacute;.

properties.description_en:
The Lac La Ronge Indian Band Little Red River community is proposing the construction of a water treatment plant and direct distribution system to the residences within the community. The water system will consist of two new groundwater wells, water treatment plant with biological filtration and reverse osmosis treatment system, distribution pumping, distribution piping network and remote reservoir. The capacity of the WTP and equipment will be designed based on a 12 - 15 year lifespan with the ability to expand. The underground piping network will be designed for a 20 year life with distribution pumping equipment designed for 12 year capacities. We will provide a copy of our Feasibility Report containing demand projections and maps for major infrastructure.

&nbsp;

The community currently does not have a potable water treatment plant (WTP) or wastewater treatment lagoon within the reserve or the associated distribution and collection systems and currently rely on truck hauling from Montreal Lake to cisterns at each residence.

properties.description_fr:
La communaut&eacute; de la bande indienne Lac La Ronge Little Red River propose la construction d&#39;une station de traitement de l&#39;eau et d&#39;un syst&egrave;me de distribution directe pour les r&eacute;sidences de la communaut&eacute;. Le syst&egrave;me d&#39;eau comprendra deux nouveaux puits d&#39;eau souterraine, une station de traitement d&#39;eau avec filtration biologique et syst&egrave;me de traitement par osmose inverse, un pompage de distribution, un r&eacute;seau de tuyauterie de distribution et un r&eacute;servoir isol&eacute;. La capacit&eacute; du WTP et de l&#39;&eacute;quipement sera con&ccedil;ue selon une dur&eacute;e de vie de 12 &agrave; 15 ans avec la possibilit&eacute; d&#39;expansion. Le r&eacute;seau de tuyauterie souterraine sera con&ccedil;u pour une dur&eacute;e de vie de 20 ans avec des &eacute;quipements de pompage de distribution con&ccedil;us pour des capacit&eacute;s de 12 ans. Nous fournirons une copie de notre rapport de faisabilit&eacute; contenant des projections de la demande et des cartes pour les infrastructures majeures.

&nbsp;

La communaut&eacute; ne dispose actuellement pas d&#39;usine de traitement d&#39;eau potable (WTP) ni de lagune de traitement des eaux us&eacute;es dans la r&eacute;serve, ni des syst&egrave;mes de distribution et de collecte associ&eacute;s, et d&eacute;pend actuellement du transport par camion du lac Montr&eacute;al jusqu&#39;aux citernes de chaque r&eacute;sidence.

properties.description_en:
The Proposed Project 

&nbsp;

Eabametoong First Nation is proposing the development of a subdivision on the east end of the community&#39;s core to address the community&#39;s ongoing housing crisis. The subdivision will include 266 subdivision lots and 50 rural lots with the project footprint totalling 125.7 ha. Development with be divided into the following 4 phases; Phase 1 - construction of 48 lots, Phase 2 &ndash; construction of 58 lots and 16 rural lots, Phase 3 &ndash; construction of 83 lots and 11 rural lots, and Phase 4 &ndash; construction of 45 lots and 23 rural lots. The scope of work of each phase will include:


	Tree clearing, grubbing and grading the lots;
	Construction of granular driveways and walkways;
	Construction of drainage ditches along the roadways;
	The construction of new roads to lots;
	Extension of the electrification network from the diesel generating station (DGS) to the new lot locations;
	Complete electrical service connections to the lot boundaries;
	Extension of the water distribution network by installing a trunk watermain along the Main Road to the east end development area and watermain along the new road for lots;
	Installation of water service connections to lots from the new water distribution system;
	Construct sanitary sewers, sewage pumping station and associated force main for lots;
	Install sanitary service connections to the lots from the new sanitary collection system.


Infrastructure required includes:


	Access roads in the subdivision, drainage ditching, culverts, telecommunication lines, overhead electrical lines, and water and sewer piping.


Activities involved throughout the project lifecycle includes:&nbsp;


	Tree clearing, land grading, bedrock blasting, road construction and utility installation.


Waste generation may include:


	Excess soil temporarily stockpiled and used for landscaping the residential lots, logs from tree clearing will be piled and made available to community members.


Quarry materials to be used:


	Borrow granular materials wil be utilized for road base construction.
	Borrow sand materials will be utilized for pipe bedding.


&nbsp;

&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Le projet propos&eacute;

&nbsp;

La Premi&egrave;re Nation d&#39;Eabametoong propose l&#39;am&eacute;nagement d&#39;un lotissement &agrave; l&#39;est du centre-ville afin de rem&eacute;dier &agrave; la crise du logement qui s&eacute;vit dans la communaut&eacute;. Ce lotissement comprendra 266 lots et 50 lots ruraux, pour une superficie totale de 125,7 hectares. Le d&eacute;veloppement sera divis&eacute; en quatre phases : phase 1 &ndash; construction de 48 lots, phase 2 &ndash; construction de 58 lots et 16 lots ruraux, phase 3 &ndash; construction de 83 lots et 11 lots ruraux, et phase 4 &ndash; construction de 45 lots et 23 lots ruraux. Les travaux pr&eacute;vus pour chaque phase comprendront :


	D&eacute;boisement, dessouchage et nivellement des lots&nbsp;;
	Construction d&#39;all&eacute;es et de trottoirs en gravier&nbsp;;
	Cr&eacute;ation de foss&eacute;s de drainage le long des voies d&#39;acc&egrave;s&nbsp;;
	Construction de nouvelles routes d&#39;acc&egrave;s aux terrains&nbsp;;
	Extension du r&eacute;seau &eacute;lectrique depuis la centrale diesel jusqu&#39;aux nouveaux lots&nbsp;;
	Raccordements &eacute;lectriques complets aux limites des lots&nbsp;;
	Extension du r&eacute;seau de distribution d&#39;eau par l&#39;installation d&#39;une conduite principale le long de la route principale jusqu&#39;&agrave; la zone d&#39;am&eacute;nagement est et d&#39;une conduite le long de la nouvelle route desservant les lots&nbsp;;
	Raccordements d&#39;eau potable aux lots &agrave; partir du nouveau r&eacute;seau de distribution&nbsp;;
	Construction des &eacute;gouts sanitaires, de la station de pompage des eaux us&eacute;es et de la conduite de refoulement associ&eacute;e pour les lots&nbsp;;
	Raccordements d&#39;eau potable aux terrains &agrave; partir du nouveau r&eacute;seau d&#39;assainissement.


Les infrastructures requises comprennent&nbsp;:


	Voies d&#39;acc&egrave;s au lotissement, foss&eacute;s de drainage, ponceaux, lignes de t&eacute;l&eacute;communications, lignes &eacute;lectriques a&eacute;riennes et r&eacute;seaux d&#39;eau et d&#39;&eacute;gouts.


Les activit&eacute;s pr&eacute;vues tout au long du cycle de vie du projet comprennent&nbsp;:


	D&eacute;boisement, nivellement du terrain, dynamitage de la roche m&egrave;re, construction de routes et installation de services publics.


G&eacute;n&eacute;ration de d&eacute;chets&nbsp;:


	La terre exc&eacute;dentaire sera temporairement entrepos&eacute;e et utilis&eacute;e pour l&#39;am&eacute;nagement paysager des terrains r&eacute;sidentiels. Les billots provenant de la d&eacute;forestation seront empil&eacute;s et mis &agrave; la disposition des r&eacute;sidents.


Mat&eacute;riaux de carri&egrave;re utilis&eacute;s&nbsp;:


	Des mat&eacute;riaux granulaires emprunt&eacute;s seront utilis&eacute;s pour la construction de la fondation routi&egrave;re.
	Du sable d&#39;emprunt sera utilis&eacute; pour le lit de pose des canalisations.


&nbsp;

Stabilisation des berges de la Premi&egrave;re Nation Anishinabe de Roseau River &agrave; : a) le site du cimeti&egrave;re 1, d&#39;une superficie de 2 000 m&sup2; ; et B) le site de l&#39;&eacute;missaire 1 de la rivi&egrave;re Rouge, d&#39;une superficie de 21 600 m&sup2;. La Premi&egrave;re Nation Anishinabe de Roseau River est situ&eacute;e &agrave; la jonction entre le sable de la rivi&egrave;re Rouge et Ginew, au Manitoba, &agrave; environ 15 km au nord de la fronti&egrave;re canado-am&eacute;ricaine. Une section de digue bordant &agrave; l&#39;origine le terrain du cimeti&egrave;re communautaire a &eacute;t&eacute; r&eacute;align&eacute;e derri&egrave;re le terrain du cimeti&egrave;re en r&eacute;ponse &agrave; des ruptures de pente r&eacute;p&eacute;t&eacute;es. La configuration actuelle de la digue comprend huit structures d&#39;&eacute;missaire &agrave; vannes pour &eacute;liminer le ruissellement des eaux de surface du c&ocirc;t&eacute; sec de la digue principale en cas de crue. Cinq des huit vannes d&#39;&eacute;missaire fonctionnent par gravit&eacute; et les trois autres vannes d&#39;&eacute;missaire comprennent des stations de pompage.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
Flying Dust First Nation is proposing the development of a new subdivision to meet the projected housing needs of the community, The proposed subdivision development project will involve the construction of residential lots, complete with underground utility installations, site roadways and ditching, and lot grading. The preferred location is Site 1, which bounds the commercial subdivision that is currently under construction to the north of Highway 55. The subdivision development will be constructed around an existing semi-permanent wetland, which will be preserved and utilized as a storm water retention pond for the development.

Site preparation activities will generally be limited to topsoil stripping. The proposed development area is currently used for agricultural purposes, and no tree clearing will be required during construction. Approximately 100 hectares of ground disturbance will be required for subdivision development. Ground disturbance activities will consist of underground utility installations, roadway construction, and lot grading.&nbsp;

All anticipated waste generation from construction activities will be responsibly handled and disposed of at designated off-reserve facilities. Procedures will also be followed to limit the amounts of waste generated during construction, and mitigate any potential contamination pathways for petroleum products from on-site equipment.

properties.description_fr:
La Premi&egrave;re Nation Flying Dust propose le d&eacute;veloppement d&#39;un nouveau lotissement pour r&eacute;pondre aux besoins immobiliers pr&eacute;vus de la communaut&eacute;. Le projet de lotissement propos&eacute; impliquera la construction de lots r&eacute;sidentiels, comprenant des installations de services publics souterrains, des routes et des foss&eacute;s sur le site, ainsi que le nivellement des lots. L&#39;emplacement privil&eacute;gi&eacute; est le Site 1, qui borde le lotissement commercial actuellement en construction au nord de l&#39;autoroute 55. Le lotissement sera construit autour d&#39;une zone humide semi-permanente existante, qui sera pr&eacute;serv&eacute;e et utilis&eacute;e comme bassin de r&eacute;tention des eaux pluviales pour le projet.

Les activit&eacute;s de pr&eacute;paration du site seront g&eacute;n&eacute;ralement limit&eacute;es au d&eacute;pouillement de la couche arable. La zone de d&eacute;veloppement propos&eacute;e est actuellement utilis&eacute;e &agrave; des fins agricoles, et aucun d&eacute;frichage d&#39;arbres ne sera n&eacute;cessaire pendant la construction. Environ 100 hectares de perturbation du sol seront n&eacute;cessaires pour le d&eacute;veloppement des lotissements. Les activit&eacute;s de perturbation du sol comprendront des installations de services publics souterrains, la construction de routes et le nivellement des lots.&nbsp;

Toute la production de d&eacute;chets pr&eacute;vue lors des activit&eacute;s de construction sera g&eacute;r&eacute;e de fa&ccedil;on responsable et &eacute;limin&eacute;e dans des installations d&eacute;sign&eacute;es hors r&eacute;serve. Des proc&eacute;dures seront &eacute;galement suivies pour limiter la quantit&eacute; de d&eacute;chets g&eacute;n&eacute;r&eacute;s pendant la construction et att&eacute;nuer toute voie potentielle de contamination des produits p&eacute;troliers provenant de l&#39;&eacute;quipement sur place.

properties.description_en:
The G Jetty and Jetty 11 Remediation Project is a proposed marine sediment remediation project at the Department of National Defence Colwood facility in Esquimalt Harbour, British Columbia. The Department of National Defence, which administers Esquimalt Harbour, is implementing a remediation and risk management program in Esquimalt Harbour as part of a long-term strategy to address sediments that have been contaminated by historical industrial activities. Various remediation projects have been or are currently being undertaken in Esquimalt Harbour as part of the remediation and risk management program. The G Jetty and Jetty 11 Remediation Project is the latest project being planned under this program and is being undertaken under the Federal Contaminated Sites Action Plan.

&nbsp;

The G Jetty and Jetty 11 Remediation Project is proposed to include temporary removal of select jetty structures, mechanical dredging and excavation of contaminated marine sediment and debris, processing of dredged sediment and debris to remove unexploded explosive ordnance, stabilization of sediment with leachable metals, potential dewatering of dredged material, in-water transportation of dredged material, offloading/stockpiling/potential treatment of dredged material, upland transportation of dredged material, disposal of dredged material, placement of clean material, and replacement of select jetty structures.

&nbsp;

The purpose of the temporary removal of select jetty structures is to dredge contaminated sediment underneath the jetty structures and to place clean material over the dredged area or to place clean material over areas that will not be dredged to act as remedial cover. Area to be dredged is approximately 5,200 m2.

&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Le projet d&#39;assainissement des jet&eacute;es G et 11 est un projet propos&eacute; d&#39;assainissement des s&eacute;diments marins &agrave; l&#39;installation de Colwood du minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale situ&eacute;e dans le port d&#39;Esquimalt (Colombie-Britannique). Le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale, qui administre le port d&#39;Esquimalt, met en &oelig;uvre un programme de gestion des risques et d&#39;assainissement du port d&#39;Esquimalt dans le cadre d&#39;une strat&eacute;gie &agrave; long terme de traitement des s&eacute;diments qui ont &eacute;t&eacute; contamin&eacute;s par les activit&eacute;s industrielles ant&eacute;rieures. Dans le cadre du programme de gestion des risques et d&#39;assainissement, divers projets d&#39;assainissement ont &eacute;t&eacute; entrepris ou sont pr&eacute;sentement en cours dans le port d&#39;Esquimalt. Le projet d&#39;assainissement des jet&eacute;es G et 11 est le plus r&eacute;cent projet en cours de planification de ce programme et il est entrepris dans le cadre du Plan d&#39;action pour les sites contamin&eacute;s f&eacute;d&eacute;raux.

&nbsp;

On propose d&#39;inclure au projet d&#39;assainissement des jet&eacute;es G et 11 l&#39;enl&egrave;vement temporaire de certaines structures des jet&eacute;es, le dragage m&eacute;canique et l&#39;excavation des s&eacute;diments marins contamin&eacute;s et des d&eacute;bris, le traitement des s&eacute;diments dragu&eacute;s et des d&eacute;bris pour en retirer les munitions explosives non explos&eacute;es, la stabilisation des s&eacute;diments contenant des m&eacute;taux lixiviables, l&#39;ass&egrave;chement potentiel des mat&eacute;riaux dragu&eacute;s, le transport dans l&#39;eau des mat&eacute;riaux dragu&eacute;s, le d&eacute;chargement, la mise en tas et le traitement potentiel des mat&eacute;riaux dragu&eacute;s, le transport sur terre des mat&eacute;riaux dragu&eacute;s, l&#39;&eacute;limination des mat&eacute;riaux dragu&eacute;s, la mise en place de mat&eacute;riaux propres et la remise en place des structures des jet&eacute;es enlev&eacute;es.

&nbsp;

L&#39;enl&egrave;vement temporaire de certaines structures des jet&eacute;es a pour objet la facilitation du dragage des s&eacute;diments contamin&eacute;s se trouvant sous ces structures ainsi que la mise en place de mat&eacute;riaux propres sur la zone dragu&eacute;e ou la mise en place de mat&eacute;riaux propres sur les zones qui ne seront pas dragu&eacute;es, ce qui servira de couverture aux fins d&#39;assainissement. La zone &agrave; draguer mesure approximativement 5 200 m2.

&nbsp;

Le projet vise &agrave; ajouter un b&acirc;timent annexe &agrave; la jet&eacute;e domestique pour accro&icirc;tre la capacit&eacute; de la salle &agrave; bagages et les services offerts aux passagers.

&nbsp;

Pour ce faire, ADM pr&eacute;voit la construction d&#39;un nouveau b&acirc;timent comportant 4 &eacute;tages avec une empreinte au sol d&#39;environ 5&nbsp;200 m2, annex&eacute; au b&acirc;timent existant de l&#39;a&eacute;rogare, &agrave; la jonction de la jet&eacute;e internationale et de la jet&eacute;e domestique.

&nbsp;

Le b&acirc;timent comportera 4 niveaux&nbsp;:


	Sous-sol&nbsp;: entreposage de bagages et salles techniques ;
	Rez-de-chauss&eacute;e&nbsp;: salle &agrave; bagages (quai, carrousels) ;
	Niveau 1&nbsp;: aires d&#39;attente et espaces commerciaux ;
	Niveau 2&nbsp;: salons VIP.


&nbsp;

La construction du b&acirc;timent est pr&eacute;vue d&eacute;buter vers le d&eacute;but de l&#39;ann&eacute;e 2026 tandis que certains travaux pr&eacute;liminaires pour d&eacute;placer certains conduits de services souterrains d&eacute;buteront en octobre 2025.

Le minist&egrave;re de la D&eacute;fense nationale (MDN) a propos&eacute; un projet. Ce projet vise &agrave; r&eacute;pondre aux pr&eacute;occupations en mati&egrave;re de s&eacute;curit&eacute; li&eacute;es au passage de Brightwater Creek au niveau du pont Woods, situ&eacute; dans la zone d&#39;entra&icirc;nement et de tir du d&eacute;tachement de la 17e Escadre &agrave; Dundurn.

Les travaux comprennent les &eacute;l&eacute;ments suivants :


	Le r&eacute;acheminement du cours d&#39;eau en amont et en aval, accompagn&eacute; d&#39;une stabilisation des zones riveraines;
	Le reprofilage du talus;
	L&#39;installation d&#39;un nouveau pont &agrave; trav&eacute;e unique, y compris la structure et les fondations;
	Le placement de rampes d&#39;acc&egrave;s en gravier au nouveau pont;
	
		Raccorder la rampe sud au sentier Woods
		Raccorder la rampe nord &agrave; la route de gravier existante.

properties.description_en:
The Land Base Building will provide children, youth and families in the community with land base skills and cultural teachings.&nbsp; The building will provide space for hunting, trapping, medicine gathering, wild rice harvesting teachings as well as wilderness survival, hunter safety, and other training.&nbsp; The building will also provide space for processing traditional foods and storing equipment for land base training and travel.&nbsp;

It will be a one story building with a mezzanine and adjoining parking lot.&nbsp; The building will be constructed on undeveloped land and comprise an approximate area of 1,300 m2.&nbsp; Sewer and water services for the new development will be provided by a new potable groundwater well and a septic field.&nbsp; A closed-loop geothermal system is also proposed for heating/cooling purposes. Ground mounted solar panels will be utilized as a secondary energy source for the proposed development. A back-up emergency generator supported by a 5,000 L diesel tank will also be included in the proposed development.&nbsp;

Construction is anticipated to commence in late 2025 and be completed by mid-2026.

Indigenous Services Canada will be providing funding for the project.

The Proposed Project

&nbsp;

Eabametoong First Nation is proposing the installation of a 18 m temporary bridge at a winter road crossing #1 located about 9.5 km east of the community. This crossing has been difficult to flood, freeze and maintain in the beginning of the winter road season, as well as the tail end. The proposed temporary bridge would alleviate these challenges and extend the winter road season, including improving early access to opening and construction of the winter road since it is the first crossing. The scope of work will include:


	Tree clearing and grubbing;
	Demolition of current bridge;
	Removal of topsoil;
	Importing of fill;
	Re-grading.


Infrastructure required includes:


	Aggregates, bearing pads, bridge structure and hardware.


Waste generation:


	No significant waste generation is anticipated. No hazardous waste is anticipated to be generated. Any waste will be disposed of at the local landfill.


Quarry materials to be used:


	A mixture of fine to coarse aggregate materials.


&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
Le projet propos&eacute;

&nbsp;

La Premi&egrave;re Nation d&#39;Eabametoong propose l&#39;installation d&#39;un pont temporaire de 18 m au point de passage routier d&#39;hiver n&deg; 1, situ&eacute; &agrave; environ 9,5 km &agrave; l&#39;est de la communaut&eacute;. Ce point de passage est difficile &agrave; entretenir et &agrave; inonder au d&eacute;but et &agrave; la fin de la saison hivernale. Le pont temporaire propos&eacute; permettrait d&#39;att&eacute;nuer ces difficult&eacute;s et de prolonger la saison hivernale, notamment en facilitant l&#39;acc&egrave;s d&egrave;s l&#39;ouverture et la construction de la route d&#39;hiver, puisqu&#39;il s&#39;agit du premier point de passage. Les travaux comprendront&nbsp;:


	D&eacute;boisement et dessouchage&nbsp;;
	D&eacute;molition du pont actuel&nbsp;;
	Enl&egrave;vement de la terre v&eacute;g&eacute;tale&nbsp;;
	Apport de remblai&nbsp;;
	Rectification du terrain.


Infrastructures requises&nbsp;:


	Granulations, semelles d&#39;appui, structure du pont et quincaillerie.


Production de d&eacute;chets&nbsp;:


	Aucune production importante de d&eacute;chets n&#39;est pr&eacute;vue. Aucun d&eacute;chet dangereux ne devrait &ecirc;tre produit. Tous les d&eacute;chets seront &eacute;limin&eacute;s &agrave; la d&eacute;charge locale.


Mat&eacute;riaux de carri&egrave;re utilis&eacute;s&nbsp;:


	Un m&eacute;lange de granulats fins et grossiers.

properties.description_en:
The proposed project will involve the construction of two new conjoining containment cells located in the intertidal zone south of the launching ramp located at the Three Fathom Harbour Small Craft Harbour.&nbsp; The proposed project also involves re-dredging of the historic channel and basin limits of the harbour. The harbour was last dredged in its entirety in 2013 and before that in 2001 which would indicate a twelve (12)-year dredge cycle.

&nbsp;

The proposed new containment cells will include core stone berms placed on the existing substrate with side slopes shaped at 1.5:1 (horizontal to vertical).&nbsp; The first cell will run approximately 60 m between the launching ramp and an existing rock groyne that is orientated perpendicular to the shoreline.&nbsp; The adjacent cell will be constructed on the opposite side (south) of the rock groyne and extend approximately 220 m to the south.&nbsp; A synthetic geotextile layer will then be placed over the prepared core stone slopes to provide filtration and separation.&nbsp; The exterior slopes and tops of the berms will be covered with layers of imported armour stone (500 &ndash; 1,000 kilogram stones) for protection from storm surges.&nbsp; The elevation of the new cells will be 4.0 m above chart datum.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Given the lack of upland in the vicinity of the construction site, the rock materials will likely be hauled in and placed directly in the new works starting on shore and working incrementally between the rock groynes to complete the new rubble mound berms. The construction is expected to be carried out using land-based equipment such as loaders, excavators, and trucks operating from shore. If temporary stockpiling of material is required, the stockpile area will be located at the Small Craft Harbour and coordinated with the Harbour Authority to avoid disruption of fishing activities.

&nbsp;

Dredging is required throughout the channel and basin to remove accumulated sediments in order to provide safer navigational access and maneuverability within the harbour.&nbsp; The last dredging event in 2013 included an area of approximately 18,283 square meters (m2) with a dredge volume of approximately 11,000 cubic meters place measure. This same area will be dredged as part of this proposed project with the same design dredge grade of 2.0 m below chart datum.

&nbsp;

Dredging is expected to be carried out using a combination of land-based equipment (long-reach excavator) and floating plant equipment.&nbsp; Dredge material will be excavated from the basin and loaded by the long reach excavator directly on to dump trucks and then deposited into the new on-site containment cells.&nbsp; Dredging involving floating plant equipment would include a mechanical dredge on a barge with scows that will relay dredge material to where it can be reached from land, removed from the scows and loaded on trucks for transit or deposited directly into the containment cells.

&nbsp;

Construction activities are anticipated to commence in spring 2026 and be completed by the end of March 2027.&nbsp; Project commencement is, however, subject to DFO-SCH operational priorities and funding, as well as the completion of regulatory approval processes, therefore work may be delayed. The scope of the impact assessment (subject to the Impact Assessment Act) will, therefore, be based on the works being completed over a period of 12 months commencing within a period of 5 years following finalization of the assessment.

&nbsp;

Three Fathom Harbour SCH is currently classified by DFO-SCH as a Class &quot;C&quot; fishing harbour and home port to 10 commercial fishing vessels that operate on a seasonal basis. The main purpose of the proposed project is to facilitate dredging of the channel and basin to allow for safe navigation to support the continued viability of the harbour for the commercial fishery and other commercial and recreational sectors.

properties.description_fr:
Le projet propos&eacute; comprendra la construction de deux nouvelles cellules de confinement contigu&euml;s dans la zone intertidale au sud de la rampe de mise &agrave; l&#39;eau situ&eacute;e dans le port pour petits bateaux de Three Fathom Harbour. Le projet propos&eacute; pr&eacute;voit &eacute;galement le dragage du chenal historique et des limites du bassin du port. Le port a &eacute;t&eacute; dragu&eacute; au complet pour la derni&egrave;re fois en 2013, et avant cela en 2001, ce qui indiquerait un cycle de dragage de douze (12) ans.

&nbsp;

Les nouvelles cellules de confinement propos&eacute;es comprendront des bermes en pierres plac&eacute;es sur le substrat existant avec des pentes lat&eacute;rales am&eacute;nag&eacute;es &agrave; 1,5 pour 1 (horizontal par rapport vertical). La premi&egrave;re cellule s&#39;&eacute;tendra sur environ 60 m&egrave;tres entre la rampe de mise &agrave; l&#39;eau et un &eacute;pi de rochers existant qui est orient&eacute; perpendiculairement &agrave; la rive. La cellule adjacente sera construite sur le c&ocirc;t&eacute; oppos&eacute; (sud) de l&#39;&eacute;pi de rochers et s&#39;&eacute;tendra sur environ 220 m&egrave;tres au sud. Une toile g&eacute;otextile synth&eacute;tique sera ensuite plac&eacute;e sur les pentes pr&eacute;par&eacute;es en pierres pour assurer la filtration et la s&eacute;paration. Les pentes ext&eacute;rieures et le sommet des bermes seront recouverts de couches de pierres de protection import&eacute;es (de 500 &agrave; 1 000 kg) afin de les prot&eacute;ger contre les ondes de temp&ecirc;te. L&#39;&eacute;l&eacute;vation des nouvelles cellules sera de 4,0 m&egrave;tres au-dessus du z&eacute;ro des cartes.

&nbsp;

Compte tenu de l&#39;absence de hautes terres &agrave; proximit&eacute; du site des travaux, les mat&eacute;riaux rocheux seront probablement transport&eacute;s et plac&eacute;s directement dans les nouveaux ouvrages, en commen&ccedil;ant par la rive et en travaillant progressivement entre les &eacute;pis de rochers pour achever les nouveaux talus en enrochement. La construction devrait &ecirc;tre r&eacute;alis&eacute;e avec de l&apos;&eacute;quipement bas&eacute; au sol, comme des chargeurs, des excavatrices et des camions utilis&eacute;s &agrave; partir de la rive. Si des mat&eacute;riaux doivent &ecirc;tre stock&eacute;s temporairement, la zone de stockage sera situ&eacute;e dans le port pour petits bateaux et coordonn&eacute;e par l&apos;administration portuaire afin d&apos;&eacute;viter toute perturbation des activit&eacute;s de p&ecirc;che.

&nbsp;

Le dragage est n&eacute;cessaire dans l&#39;ensemble du chenal et du bassin pour enlever les s&eacute;diments accumul&eacute;s afin d&#39;assurer un acc&egrave;s plus s&eacute;curitaire &agrave; la navigation et une meilleure man&oelig;uvrabilit&eacute; &agrave; l&#39;int&eacute;rieur du port. Le dernier dragage effectu&eacute; en 2013 visait une zone d&apos;une superficie d&apos;environ 18 283 m&egrave;tres carr&eacute;s (m2) avec un volume de dragage d&#39;environ 11 000 m&egrave;tres cubes (m3). Cette m&ecirc;me zone sera dragu&eacute;e dans le cadre du projet propos&eacute; avec le m&ecirc;me niveau de dragage de 2,0 m&egrave;tres sous le z&eacute;ro des cartes.

&nbsp;

On pr&eacute;voit que le dragage sera effectu&eacute; au moyen d&apos;une combinaison d&#39;&eacute;quipement terrestre (excavatrice &agrave; longue port&eacute;e) et d&#39;&eacute;quipement flottant. Les d&eacute;blais de dragage seront extraits du bassin et charg&eacute;s par l&#39;excavatrice &agrave; longue port&eacute;e directement dans des camions &agrave; benne, puis d&eacute;pos&eacute;s dans les nouvelles cellules de confinement du site. Le dragage r&eacute;alis&eacute; &agrave; partir d&apos;&eacute;quipement flottant comprendrait une drague m&eacute;canique sur une barge avec des chalands qui relaieraient les d&eacute;blais de dragage jusqu&#39;&agrave; un endroit o&ugrave; ils peuvent &ecirc;tre atteints depuis la terre, retir&eacute;s des chalands et charg&eacute;s sur des camions pour le transport ou d&eacute;pos&eacute;s directement dans les cellules de confinement.

&nbsp;

Les travaux de construction devraient commencer au printemps 2026 et &ecirc;tre achev&eacute;s d&apos;ici la fin du mois de mars 2027. Le lancement du projet d&eacute;pendra toutefois des priorit&eacute;s op&eacute;rationnelles de la Direction des ports pour petits bateaux de P&ecirc;ches et Oc&eacute;ans Canada et du financement que le programme est en mesure d&apos;obtenir, de m&ecirc;me que des processus d&apos;approbation r&eacute;glementaire. Les travaux pourraient donc &ecirc;tre retard&eacute;s. La port&eacute;e de l&apos;&eacute;valuation d&apos;impact (assujettie &agrave; la Loi sur l&apos;&eacute;valuation d&apos;impact) sera donc fond&eacute;e sur les travaux r&eacute;alis&eacute;s sur une p&eacute;riode de douze (12) mois, commen&ccedil;ant dans les cinq (5) ans suivant l&apos;&eacute;tape finale de l&apos;&eacute;valuation.

&nbsp;

Le port pour petits bateaux de Three Fathom Harbour est actuellement class&eacute; par la Direction des ports pour petits bateaux de P&ecirc;ches et Oc&eacute;ans Canada comme un port de p&ecirc;che de classe &laquo; C &raquo; et le port d&#39;attache de dix (10) navires de p&ecirc;che commerciale dont l&apos;exploitation est saisonni&egrave;re. L&#39;objectif principal du projet propos&eacute; est de faciliter le dragage du chenal et du bassin afin de permettre une navigation s&eacute;curitaire et d&#39;assurer la viabilit&eacute; continue du port pour la p&ecirc;che commerciale et d&#39;autres secteurs commerciaux et r&eacute;cr&eacute;atifs.

properties.description_en:
The redevelopment project proposes to turn the&nbsp;existing Coyote Rock Golf Course into Northside Development residential subdivision. The size of the proposed&nbsp;development area is approximately 45 hectares and it is located on Williams Lake IR1 north of&nbsp;Highway 97 and east of Williams Lake.&nbsp; The redevelopment will consist of single-family, medium-density (4-8 attached units with common parking area), and high-density (more than 8 units, more than 2 stories, potential underground parking) building structures.

&nbsp;

The existing Coyote Rock Golf Course includes clubhouse, parking lot, greens and fairways, outhouse shed, utility buildings, golf cart access roads, fences, numerour waterbodies including a pond, several wetlands, Asahal Creek, and seasonal drainage channels.&nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;

An abundance of vegetation, including native, exotic, and invasive species exist within and around&nbsp;the development area.&nbsp;&nbsp;The development area was primarily characterized by manicured golf course greens and fairways&nbsp;interspersed with groves of trees and shrubs.&nbsp; These groves are predominantly comprised of trembling aspen, with Douglas fir, rocky&nbsp;mountain juniper (Juniperus scopulorum), snowberry (Symphoricarpos albus), and roses (Rosa spp.) also&nbsp;abundant within them. There was a single patch of black hawthorn (Crataegus douglasii) north of the approximate center of the property and snowberry patches and common juniper (Juniperus&nbsp;communis) were identified at various locations throughout the development area.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Development of the residential subdivision will involve clearing and grading, placement of stormwater&nbsp;infrastructure and other utilities, and construction of roads, driveways, and buildings.

properties.description_fr:
Le projet de r&eacute;am&eacute;nagement propose de transformer le terrain de golf Coyote Rock existant en lotissement r&eacute;sidentiel Northside Development. La superficie du terrain concern&eacute; est d&#39;environ 45 hectares. Il est situ&eacute; &agrave; Williams Lake IR1, au nord de l&#39;autoroute 97 et &agrave; l&#39;est de Williams Lake. Le r&eacute;am&eacute;nagement comprendra des maisons individuelles, des immeubles de densit&eacute; moyenne (4 &agrave; 8 logements mitoyens avec parking commun) et des immeubles de haute densit&eacute; (plus de 8 logements, plus de 2 &eacute;tages, parking souterrain potentiel).

&nbsp;

Le terrain de golf Coyote Rock comprend un club-house, un parking, des greens et des fairways, des toilettes ext&eacute;rieures, des b&acirc;timents utilitaires, des routes d&#39;acc&egrave;s pour les voiturettes de golf, des cl&ocirc;tures, de nombreux plans d&#39;eau, dont un &eacute;tang, plusieurs zones humides, le ruisseau Asahal et des canaux de drainage saisonniers. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Une v&eacute;g&eacute;tation abondante, comprenant des esp&egrave;ces indig&egrave;nes, exotiques et envahissantes, existe &agrave; l&#39;int&eacute;rieur et autour de la zone de d&eacute;veloppement. &nbsp;La zone de d&eacute;veloppement se caract&eacute;risait principalement par des greens et des fairways de golf soigneusement entretenus, entrecoup&eacute;s de bosquets d&#39;arbres et d&#39;arbustes. Ces bosquets sont principalement compos&eacute;s de peupliers faux-trembles, mais on y trouve &eacute;galement en abondance des sapins de Douglas, des gen&eacute;vriers des Rocheuses (Juniperus scopulorum), des symphoricarpus (Symphoricarpos albus) et des roses (Rosa spp.). Il y avait une seule parcelle d&#39;aub&eacute;pine noire (Crataegus douglasii) au nord du centre approximatif de la propri&eacute;t&eacute;, et des parcelles de symphorique et de gen&eacute;vrier commun (Juniperus communis) ont &eacute;t&eacute; identifi&eacute;es &agrave; divers endroits dans la zone de d&eacute;veloppement.

&nbsp;

Le d&eacute;veloppement du lotissement r&eacute;sidentiel comprendra le d&eacute;frichage et le nivellement, la mise en place d&#39;infrastructures pour les eaux pluviales et d&#39;autres services publics, ainsi que la construction de routes, d&#39;all&eacute;es et de b&acirc;timents.

properties.description_en:
The Quinsam Crossing area is a thriving commercial and industrial hub developed over the past two decades, and has seen significant growth in&nbsp;recent years.&nbsp; The addition of commercial enterprises such as Starbucks, a liquor store, a marijuana dispensary, Finning/Caterpillar, and the Akers Development building has bolstered its appeal.&nbsp; This proposal aims to finalize the last phase of&nbsp;development in this area.


Situated conveniently adjacent to the highway and close to Campbell River, demand for land in this location has remained&nbsp;consistently high.&nbsp; The proposed project seeks to meet this demand by implementing necessary infrastructure, including a new&nbsp;roadway, water, and sanitary sewer along the Brant Drive Alignment, to service existing lots.&nbsp; These lots will be earmarked for the&nbsp;construction of a future hotel, retail spaces, a grocery store, and an office building.&nbsp; Transportation enhancements along Willis Road are slated to improve safety for users of&nbsp;the Quinsam Crossing complex.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

properties.description_fr:
La zone de Quinsam Crossing est un p&ocirc;le commercial et industriel florissant qui s&#39;est d&eacute;velopp&eacute; au cours des deux derni&egrave;res d&eacute;cennies et qui a connu une croissance significative ces derni&egrave;res ann&eacute;es. L&#39;arriv&eacute;e d&#39;entreprises commerciales telles que Starbucks, un magasin d&#39;alcool, un dispensaire de marijuana, Finning/Caterpillar et le b&acirc;timent Akers Development a renforc&eacute; son attrait. Cette proposition vise &agrave; finaliser la derni&egrave;re phase de d&eacute;veloppement de cette zone.


Id&eacute;alement situ&eacute; &agrave; proximit&eacute; de l&#39;autoroute et de Campbell River, la demande de terrains dans cet endroit est rest&eacute;e constante. &nbsp;Le projet propos&eacute; vise &agrave; r&eacute;pondre &agrave; cette demande en mettant en place les infrastructures n&eacute;cessaires, notamment une nouvelle route, un r&eacute;seau d&#39;adduction d&#39;eau et un r&eacute;seau d&#39;&eacute;gouts sanitaires le long de Brant Drive Alignment, afin de desservir les terrains existants. &nbsp;Ces terrains seront r&eacute;serv&eacute;s &agrave; la construction d&#39;un futur h&ocirc;tel, d&#39;espaces commerciaux, d&#39;une &eacute;picerie et d&#39;un immeuble de bureaux. &nbsp;Des am&eacute;liorations des transports le long de Willis Road sont pr&eacute;vues afin d&#39;am&eacute;liorer la s&eacute;curit&eacute; des utilisateurs du complexe Quinsam Crossing.

&nbsp;

Ce projet vise &agrave; fournir une installation de base permanente/g&eacute;n&eacute;rateur de s&eacute;curit&eacute; vitale qui assurera l&#39;alimentation de secours pour toutes les op&eacute;rations de base/gestion de la s&eacute;curit&eacute; vitale dans un avenir pr&eacute;visible. Le g&eacute;n&eacute;rateur permanent propos&eacute; permettrait de renouveler un actif consid&eacute;rablement vieillissant, les g&eacute;n&eacute;rateurs actuels du b&acirc;timent de base ayant pr&egrave;s de 50 ans et d&eacute;passant largement leur dur&eacute;e de vie pr&eacute;vue. De plus, ce projet envisage d&#39;ajouter son propre syst&egrave;me de distribution de carburant pour ne fournir que le g&eacute;n&eacute;rateur de base/s&eacute;curit&eacute; vitale. Cela sera r&eacute;alis&eacute; en se d&eacute;connectant du bunker &agrave; carburant existant de 10 000 litres et en enlevant le r&eacute;servoir de jour existant. Un nouveau r&eacute;servoir de carburant externe mont&eacute; sur socle avec des dispositifs de confinement des d&eacute;versements sera ajout&eacute; &agrave; l&#39;ext&eacute;rieur du b&acirc;timent.

&nbsp;

Une &eacute;tude de faisabilit&eacute; a &eacute;t&eacute; r&eacute;alis&eacute;e pour d&eacute;terminer la taille optimale, l&#39;emplacement et l&#39;architecture du syst&egrave;me du nouveau g&eacute;n&eacute;rateur de base/s&eacute;curit&eacute; vitale et du syst&egrave;me de distribution &eacute;lectrique. L&#39;option recommand&eacute;e d&#39;une unit&eacute; ext&eacute;rieure mont&eacute;e sur socle et &eacute;tanche aux intemp&eacute;ries de 1,0 MW avec stockage de carburant externe mont&eacute; sur socle a &eacute;t&eacute; s&eacute;lectionn&eacute;e. Cela permettra le retrait du g&eacute;n&eacute;rateur de base/s&eacute;curit&eacute; vitale existant de la salle des g&eacute;n&eacute;rateurs, permettant ainsi l&#39;installation d&#39;&eacute;quipements de distribution nouveaux conformes au code.

Taseko Mines Limited propose la construction, l&#39;exploitation et la fermeture d&#39;une nouvelle mine de cuivre &agrave; ciel ouvert situ&eacute;e &agrave; environ 150 kilom&egrave;tres au nord-est de Kamloops, en Colombie-Britannique. Le Projet de cuivre de Yellowhead a &eacute;t&eacute; con&ccedil;u en vue d&#39;une capacit&eacute; de production de 90&thinsp;000 tonnes de minerai par jour (jusqu&#39;&agrave; 32 millions de tonnes par ann&eacute;e) pour une dur&eacute;e de vie de 25 ans. Le projet, qui produirait &eacute;galement de l&#39;or et de l&#39;argent, comprend une nouvelle usine de traitement, une ligne de transport d&#39;&eacute;lectricit&eacute; d&#39;environ 110 kilom&egrave;tres qui se connecterait &agrave; une sous-station existante de BC Hydro pr&egrave;s de 100 Mile House, ainsi qu&#39;une installation de chargement ferroviaire sur un site existant &agrave; Vavenby.

Le Bureau d&#39;&eacute;valuation environnementale de la Colombie-Britannique (BEE) collabore avec l&#39;Agence d&#39;&eacute;valuation d&#39;impact du Canada dans le cadre de l&#39;&eacute;valuation f&eacute;d&eacute;rale du projet. Pour en savoir plus sur le processus du BEE, veuillez visiter EPIC.engage (en anglais seulement).

&nbsp;

properties.description_en:
The Motor Vehicle Test Centre in Blainville, Quebec is a world-class testing ground. The Centre is owned by the Government of Canada and managed by PMG Technologies. It has resources to test vehicles and equipment, including connected and automated technologies.

For safety reasons, a deer fence will be installed on the CEVA site. This will prevent any intrusion of wild animals onto the property and finalize the installation of deer fencing around the site&#39;s periphery, begun in 2016.

Area 2 to be fenced is located opposite the site&#39;s two main stormwater drainage points. The work will include replacing the two culverts.

Work includes:

- Removal of vegetation where necessary (particularly at culverts in zone 2 - zones 8 and 9 have no vegetation);
- Drilling for new fence posts;
- Replacement and installation of fences (zone 2: replacement of 200 m and zones 8-9: installation of 1,100 m);
- Replacement of two existing culverts (HDPE 1.8 m and 3 m).

Machinery traffic will use an existing access road.

Work is scheduled for summer and fall 2025.

properties.description_fr:
Le Centre d&#39;essais pour v&eacute;hicules automobiles situ&eacute; &agrave; Blainville, au Qu&eacute;bec, est un terrain d&#39;essai de classe mondiale. Le Centre appartient au gouvernement du Canada, alors que PMG Technologies en assure la gestion. Il dispose de ressources pour mettre &agrave; l&#39;essai diff&eacute;rents v&eacute;hicules et &eacute;quipements, y compris les technologies de v&eacute;hicules connect&eacute;s et automatis&eacute;s.

Pour des questions de s&eacute;curit&eacute;, des cl&ocirc;tures &agrave; cervid&eacute;s doivent &ecirc;tre install&eacute;es sur le site du CEVA. Ces am&eacute;nagements pr&eacute;viendront l&#39;intrusion potentielle d&#39;animaux sauvages sur la propri&eacute;t&eacute; et compl&eacute;teront l&#39;installation de cl&ocirc;tures &agrave; cervid&eacute;s en p&eacute;riph&eacute;rie du site ayant &eacute;t&eacute; amorc&eacute;e en 2016.

La zone 2 &agrave; cl&ocirc;turer est situ&eacute;e vis-&agrave;-vis des deux exutoires principaux du drainage pluvial du site. Les travaux impliqueront le remplacement des deux ponceaux.

Les travaux incluent :


	L&#39;enl&egrave;vement de la v&eacute;g&eacute;tation lorsque n&eacute;cessaire (surtout &agrave; l&#39;endroit des ponceaux de la zone 2 - les zones 8 et 9 ne comportent pas de v&eacute;g&eacute;tation);
	Les forages pour l&#39;installation des poteaux des nouvelles cl&ocirc;tures;
	Remplacement et installation des cl&ocirc;tures (zone 2 : remplacement de 200m et zones 8-9 : installation de 1100m) ;
	Le remplacement des deux ponceaux existants (PEHD 1,8m et 3m).


La circulation de la machinerie se fera sur un chemin d&#39;acc&egrave;s existant.

Les travaux sont pr&eacute;vus &agrave; l&#39;&eacute;t&eacute; et &agrave; l&#39;automne 2025.

properties.description_en:
Camp Fortune proposes to replace the existing ski run lighting and install new high-efficiency lighting to the Meech chairlift corridor and Meech area trails, including Paradis and North American, which are accessed from the Meech chairlift. Lighting is required for maintenance and night safety access during night skiing operations. &nbsp;

In total, new lighting will be installed at 60 locations, including the installation of 54 new light standards and the installation of six lights on existing chairlift support towers along the Meech chairlift corridor.

The project specifications were designed to reduce excavation and groundworks to the highest extent possible, promote the sustainable re-use of materials wherever possible, and improve the sustainability of night skiing by utilizing high efficiency, dark-sky approved and ecologically sound LED lighting.

Camp Fortune offers a variety of skiing over three peaks. It has 24 runs for different skill levels, seven lifts, and twelve lit runs for skiing at night. The Meech chairlift corridor and the Paradis and North American trails, do not currently offer night skiing; however, the addition of new lighting along these routes will expand Camp Fortune&#39;s night skiing options to include more beginner and intermediate terrain that is currently lacking among the night skiing routes at Camp Fortune. The addition will also provide another chairlift to move skiers around the area, reducing congestion on Pineault and Clifford chairlifts. This will make for a more enjoyable and safer ski experience.

Camp Fortune sits on federal lands in Gatineau Park.&nbsp;

Title: Construction of a Grain Processing (Milling) Facility at 5925 Lyndale Drive, Livonia, New York, USA&nbsp;

Armstrong Milling Companies Limited, a Canadian company, is requesting financing from FCC for the construction of a new grain processing (milling) facility located at 5925 Lyndale Drive, Livonia, New York, USA.&nbsp; The site is approximately 10 acres of vacant agricultural land, requiring installation of site infrastructure for development. The commercial scale milling facility will include a 7,200 square foot stand-alone building, office building and bulk grain storage silos and improvements dedicated to product receiving and shipping.

Contact:&nbsp;

Valuations&nbsp;

Farm Credit Canada&nbsp;

#210, 6700 46 Street&nbsp;

Olds, AB&nbsp;

T4H 0A2&nbsp;

Email: EnvironmentalPolicy@fcc-fac.ca&nbsp;

