properties.description_en:
This project is intended to provide a permanent tenant generator that will provide the backup power for all tenant operations for the foreseeable future. With the implementation of the Lester B. Pearson Rehabilitation project underway, they are a number of newly renovated client spaces looking to add to the existing tenant generator distribution system. The proposed permanent generator would provide extra capacity as well as flexibility, when accommodating back up power connections for other projects, as the existing back up power distribution system does not appear to be easily shut down in order to allow new connections. Additionally, this project is looking to add its own fuel distribution system to supply only the tenant owned generator. This will achieved by disconnecting from the existing 10,000L fuel bunker and removal of the existing day tank. A new pad mounted external fuel tank with spill containment devices will be added exterior to the building. The existing 10,000L fuel bunker will carry on supplying the base building/life safety generators until their replacement is complete.

&nbsp;

A feasibility study was done to determine the optimal size, location and system architecture of the new tenant generator and power distribution system. The recommended option of a 2.5MW exterior pad mounted and weathertight enclosed unit with external pad mounted fuel storage was selected. This will allow the removal of the existing tenant generator from the generator room permitting additional space for new distribution equipment to be installed in a code compliant manner.

properties.description_fr:
Ce projet vise &agrave; fournir un g&eacute;n&eacute;rateur permanent pour les locataires qui assurera l&#39;alimentation de secours pour toutes les op&eacute;rations des locataires dans un avenir pr&eacute;visible. Avec la mise en &oelig;uvre du projet de r&eacute;habilitation Lester B. Pearson pr&eacute;sentement en cours, plusieurs espaces clients r&eacute;cemment r&eacute;nov&eacute;s envisagent de s&#39;ajouter au syst&egrave;me de distribution du g&eacute;n&eacute;rateur des locataires existant. Le g&eacute;n&eacute;rateur permanent propos&eacute; fournirait une capacit&eacute; suppl&eacute;mentaire ainsi que de la flexibilit&eacute; pour permettre des connexions de secours pour d&#39;autres projets, car le syst&egrave;me de distribution de secours existant ne semble pas &ecirc;tre facilement arr&ecirc;table pour permettre de nouvelles connexions. De plus, ce projet envisage d&#39;ajouter son propre syst&egrave;me de distribution de carburant pour approvisionner uniquement le g&eacute;n&eacute;rateur appartenant aux locataires. Cela sera r&eacute;alis&eacute; en se d&eacute;connectant du bunker &agrave; carburant existant de 10 000 litres et en enlevant le r&eacute;servoir de jour existant. Un nouveau r&eacute;servoir de carburant externe mont&eacute; sur socle avec des dispositifs de confinement des d&eacute;versements sera ajout&eacute; &agrave; l&#39;ext&eacute;rieur du b&acirc;timent. Le bunker &agrave; carburant existant de 10 000 litres continuera &agrave; approvisionner les g&eacute;n&eacute;rateurs du b&acirc;timent de base/s&eacute;curit&eacute; vitale jusqu&#39;&agrave; ce que leur remplacement soit complet.

&nbsp;

Une &eacute;tude de faisabilit&eacute; a &eacute;t&eacute; r&eacute;alis&eacute;e pour d&eacute;terminer la taille optimale, l&#39;emplacement et l&#39;architecture du nouveau g&eacute;n&eacute;rateur des locataires et du syst&egrave;me de distribution &eacute;lectrique. L&#39;option recommand&eacute;e d&#39;une unit&eacute; ext&eacute;rieure mont&eacute;e sur socle et &eacute;tanche aux intemp&eacute;ries de 2,5 MW avec stockage de carburant externe mont&eacute; sur socle a &eacute;t&eacute; s&eacute;lectionn&eacute;e. Cela permettra le retrait du g&eacute;n&eacute;rateur des locataires existant de la salle des g&eacute;n&eacute;rateurs, permettant ainsi l&#39;installation d&#39;&eacute;quipements de distribution nouveaux conformes au code.

properties.description_en:
The City of Montr&eacute;al-Est plans to carry out stabilization work on a 100-meter section of the shoreline at H&ocirc;tel-de-Ville Park (Lot 1,250,984), which borders the St. Lawrence River. The project involves removing an unstable retaining wall made of fill and geogrids and replacing it with a mixed stabilization structure.

This structure will combine various techniques, including riprap and phytotechnologies at the base of the slope, naturalization of the shoreline at mid-slope, and greening of the park&#39;s surroundings on the flat area. The project also includes the reconstruction of a pedestrian path at the top of the slope, which currently runs along the stabilization structure, and the installation of flower beds and riparian trees. Finally, vegetative stabilization of the shoreline will be carried out to address the slumping and erosion observed in recent years, which have made the area potentially hazardous to the public and harmful to local wildlife and plant life along this section of the St. Lawrence River shoreline.

H&ocirc;tel-de-Ville Park, developed by and for the City of Montr&eacute;al-Est, is managed by the Montreal Port Authority. The project is fully funded by the City of Montr&eacute;al-Est.


During the construction period, access to the park will remain open to users, except for the southeastern part of the site, which will be closed to ensure public safety during the proposed construction work. The park&#39;s trails and paths will generally remain open during the work, except for the trail that crosses and runs alongside the construction site. Signage, directions, and barricades will be installed on-site.

In general, the planned work includes the following:


	Site mobilization, installation of signage, safety fences, and construction fencing;
	Installation of watercourse protection equipment (sediment barriers, turbidity curtains, etc.);
	Removal of an ornamental fence, excavation of the old stabilization structure in the slope with geogrids, and cleaning of the shoreline (pebble beach);
	Improvement of the existing riprap key and installation of phytotechnologies such as branch mattresses, fascines, cuttings, and natural fiber anti-erosion mats;
	Placement of topsoil, seeding, planting of perennials, grasses, shrubs, and riparian trees;
	Reinstallation of an ornamental fence, reconstruction of the path, restoration and greening of the construction access, and site demobilization.


The work is expected to begin around August 19 and be completed by the end of October 2025. Maintenance, replacement of dead plants, and environmental monitoring of the shoreline will be carried out over a five-year period following the completion of the work.

properties.description_fr:
La Ville de Montr&eacute;al-Est pr&eacute;voit de proc&eacute;der &agrave; des travaux de stabilisation d&#39;une portion de 100&nbsp;m de la berge du parc de l&#39;H&ocirc;tel-de-Ville (Lot&nbsp;1&thinsp;250&thinsp;984) longeant le fleuve Saint-Laurent. Le projet consiste notamment &agrave; effectuer le retrait d&#39;un muret instable compos&eacute; d&#39;un remblai et de g&eacute;ogrilles afin de le remplacer par un ouvrage de stabilisation dit mixte.

Cet ouvrage combinera diff&eacute;rentes techniques, dont l&#39;enrochement et les phytotechnologies en pied de talus, la naturalisation de la rive &agrave; mi-hauteur du talus et le verdissement des abords du parc en replat. Le projet pr&eacute;voit &eacute;galement la r&eacute;fection d&#39;un sentier p&eacute;destre en haut de talus qui longe actuellement l&#39;ouvrage de stabilisation, incluant la mise en place de quelques plates-bandes et d&#39;arbres riverains. Enfin, la stabilisation v&eacute;g&eacute;tale de la berge sera effectu&eacute;e dans le but d&#39;enrayer les ph&eacute;nom&egrave;nes de d&eacute;crochage et d&#39;&eacute;rosion observ&eacute;s ces derni&egrave;res ann&eacute;es qui rendent les lieux potentiellement dangereux pour le public et nuit &agrave; la faune ainsi qu&#39;&agrave; la flore dans ce tron&ccedil;on de la berge du fleuve Saint-Laurent.

Le parc de l&#39;H&ocirc;tel-de-Ville, am&eacute;nag&eacute; par et pour la Ville de Montr&eacute;al-Est, est sous la gestion de l&#39;Administration portuaire de Montr&eacute;al. Le projet est enti&egrave;rement financ&eacute; par la Ville de Montr&eacute;al-Est.


Pendant la p&eacute;riode des travaux, l&#39;acc&egrave;s au parc sera maintenu pour les usagers, sauf en ce qui concerne la partie sud-est du site o&ugrave; l&#39;acc&egrave;s sera interdit afin d&#39;assurer la s&eacute;curit&eacute; du public lors des travaux de construction propos&eacute;s. Les pistes et sentiers du parc pourront demeurer ouverts durant le chantier, sauf le sentier traversant et longeant le site des travaux. Des indications, de la signalisation et des barricades seront install&eacute;es sur les lieux.

De fa&ccedil;on g&eacute;n&eacute;rale, les travaux planifi&eacute;s se r&eacute;sument comme suit&nbsp;:


	Mobilisation du chantier, installation de signalisation, de cl&ocirc;tures de s&eacute;curit&eacute; et de chantier&thinsp;;
	Installation d&#39;&eacute;quipement de protection du cours d&#39;eau (barri&egrave;re &agrave; s&eacute;diment, rideau de turbidit&eacute;, etc.)&nbsp;;
	Retrait d&#39;une cl&ocirc;ture ornementale, excavation de l&#39;ancien ouvrage de stabilisation dans le talus avec des g&eacute;ogrilles et nettoyage de la gr&egrave;ve (plage de galets)&nbsp;;
	Am&eacute;lioration de la cl&eacute; d&#39;enrochement existante et installation de phytotechnologies telles que des matelas de branches, des fagots, des boutures et du matelas anti-&eacute;rosion&thinsp;en fibres naturelles&nbsp;;
	Mise en place de terreau, de semences, plantation de vivaces, de gramin&eacute;es, d&#39;arbustes et d&#39;arbres de type riverain&thinsp;;
	R&eacute;installation d&#39;une cl&ocirc;ture ornementale, reconstruction du sentier, r&eacute;fection et verdissement de l&#39;acc&egrave;s au chantier et d&eacute;mobilisation&thinsp;;


Les travaux devraient d&eacute;buter vers le 19 ao&ucirc;t prochain et &ecirc;tre termin&eacute;s vers la fin octobre 2025. L&#39;entretien, le remplacement de v&eacute;g&eacute;taux morts et le suivi environnemental de la rive seront r&eacute;alis&eacute;s sur une p&eacute;riode de 5&nbsp;ans depuis la fin des travaux.
